INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('376c82ad-ea59-4d30-836a-1d6b9823e5c6', 'q08-36b71b6c', 'STRUCTURED', 'Some students investigated displacement reactions involving three different metals and solutions of their salts. This equation represents one of these reactions: $\mathrm {Z n} (\mathrm {s}) + \mathrm {C u S O} _ {4} (\mathrm {a q}) \rightarrow \mathrm {Z n S O} _ {4} (\mathrm {a q}) + \mathrm {C u} (\mathrm {s})$ This reaction occurs because zinc is more reactive than copper. When a displacement reaction occurs, there is a temperature rise. The bigger the difference in reactivity between the two metals, the bigger the temperature rise.', 10, 3, 900, NULL, 'a1e23540-5a88-4946-9251-f84ea87e44ba', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.666286+00', 'ff8e556a-61de-4675-8145-150da9df0e98');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('3874736b-acae-4e8d-9b92-2d171d049523', 'q09-36b71b6c', 'STRUCTURED', 'AmmoFert Chemicals is a company that manufactures fertilisers. The flow chart shows how the company manufactures a fertiliser called AmmoBoost.', 18, 3, 1620, NULL, 'a1e23540-5a88-4946-9251-f84ea87e44ba', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.666579+00', 'ff8e556a-61de-4675-8145-150da9df0e98');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('367d74bb-2b81-4608-ac5c-222f083c9cf3', 'q10-36b71b6c', 'STRUCTURED', 'Like other metals, iron is malleable and is a good conductor of electricity.', 8, 3, 720, NULL, 'a1e23540-5a88-4946-9251-f84ea87e44ba', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.666929+00', 'ff8e556a-61de-4675-8145-150da9df0e98');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('cafae2cd-df26-42f4-b68d-2f91167812b7', 'q11-36b71b6c', 'STRUCTURED', 'Some students investigated the rate of reaction between sodium thiosulfate solution and hydrochloric acid. The equation for the reaction is $\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \mathrm {S} _ {2} \mathrm {O} _ {3} (\mathrm {a q}) + 2 \mathrm {H C l} (\mathrm {a q}) \rightarrow 2 \mathrm {N a C l} (\mathrm {a q}) + \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} (\mathrm {l}) + \mathrm {S} (\mathrm {s}) + \mathrm {S O} _ {2} (\mathrm {g})$ The precipitate of sulfur makes the reaction mixture go cloudy. The students used this method. Place a mixture of sodium thiosulfate solution and water in a conical flask Add some dilute hydrochloric acid, swirl the mixture and start a timer Place the flask over a black cross marked on a piece of paper Record the time taken for the cross to disappear when viewed from above The students used 10 $ cm^{3} $ of dilute hydrochloric acid in each experiment. They carried out all the experiments at the same temperature. They used different volumes of sodium thiosulfate solution and water in each experiment. They were told to keep the total volume of sodium thiosulfate solution and water constant. The table shows their results.', 1, 3, 90, NULL, 'a1e23540-5a88-4946-9251-f84ea87e44ba', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.667277+00', 'ff8e556a-61de-4675-8145-150da9df0e98');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('018ad585-425f-4695-940d-93fba33a791e', 'q02-0c94e0a6', 'STRUCTURED', 'Rock salt is a mixture of the soluble salt, sodium chloride, and some insoluble impurities. The diagram shows the first three stages of a method used to obtain pure sodium chloride from rock salt. Stage 1 rock salt crushed Stage2 crushed rock salt added to water Stage 3', 9, 3, 810, NULL, '6f6dcde5-b0f9-4081-8cad-3751870bcc51', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:54:39.65332+00', 'f3355321-ea12-48e9-af55-484a9b136cdf');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('66a376e8-3af5-4e64-82d9-490ea315aebf', 'q03-0c94e0a6', 'STRUCTURED', 'Crude oil is a mixture of hydrocarbons.', 1, 3, 90, NULL, '6f6dcde5-b0f9-4081-8cad-3751870bcc51', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:54:39.653928+00', 'f3355321-ea12-48e9-af55-484a9b136cdf');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('557ba27c-556a-40f4-b2fb-fa5742c80024', 'q04-0c94e0a6', 'STRUCTURED', '(a) (i) Explain what is meant by the term covalent bonding. (ii) Draw a dot and cross diagram to show the bonding in a molecule of ethene, $ \mathrm{C_{2} H_{4}} $ Show only the outer electrons.', 11, 3, 990, NULL, '6f6dcde5-b0f9-4081-8cad-3751870bcc51', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:54:39.654336+00', 'f3355321-ea12-48e9-af55-484a9b136cdf');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('3c0a3f02-c8a8-4543-aea2-44a5fc4c9a97', 'q05-0c94e0a6', 'STRUCTURED', 'Hot, molten sulfur reacts with oxygen to form sulfur dioxide gas.', 10, 3, 900, NULL, '6f6dcde5-b0f9-4081-8cad-3751870bcc51', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:54:39.654703+00', 'f3355321-ea12-48e9-af55-484a9b136cdf');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('02995f08-920f-4564-8cb3-5ffdc6fe42e7', 'q09-0c94e0a6', 'STRUCTURED', 'Some metals can be obtained by heating their oxides with carbon.', 12, 3, 1080, NULL, '6f6dcde5-b0f9-4081-8cad-3751870bcc51', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:54:39.656358+00', 'f3355321-ea12-48e9-af55-484a9b136cdf');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('cfb862d0-3b20-4fee-bd46-7427ad34202e', 'q09-0dbea9f5', 'STRUCTURED', 'A student prepares a sample of copper(II) sulfate crystals using this reaction. $\mathrm {C u O (s)} + \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {S O} _ {4} (\mathrm {a q}) \rightarrow \mathrm {C u S O} _ {4} (\mathrm {a q}) + \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} (\mathrm {l})$ He obtains the crystals from the solution formed. He records this information about the reactants he uses. mass of copper(II) oxide = 6.3 g volume of sulfuric acid = 52 $ cm^{3} $ concentration of sulfuric acid = 1.1 mol/dm $ ^{3} $ (i) Calculate the amount, in moles, of copper(II) oxide used. amount of copper(II) oxide = mol (ii) Calculate the amount, in moles, of sulfuric acid used. amount of sulfuric acid = mol (iii) Why is it important for the amount of copper(II) oxide to be greater than the amount of sulfuric acid? (iv) Draw a diagram of the apparatus that the student should use to remove the excess copper(II) oxide from the reaction mixture.', 1, 3, 90, NULL, 'c419145b-b3aa-4dcf-a4d0-76331aa67c55', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.592905+00', '96328c83-0486-4859-be05-7bc0786f088e');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('299183f9-c2a6-4b2f-a11e-1f20402f0c70', 'q11-0dbea9f5', 'STRUCTURED', 'Synthetic polymers are often manufactured from crude oil. The main stages in the manufacture of one of these polymers are shown in this sequence. $\mathrm {c r u d e o i l} \rightarrow \mathrm {f u e l o i l} \rightarrow \mathrm {p r o p e n e} \rightarrow \mathrm {p o l y (p r o p e n e)}$', 1, 3, 90, NULL, 'c419145b-b3aa-4dcf-a4d0-76331aa67c55', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.593604+00', '96328c83-0486-4859-be05-7bc0786f088e');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('52180e80-98e5-44fc-82b6-94d8314052e6', 'q10-9e5d961d', 'STRUCTURED', '(a) The diagram shows the apparatus a teacher uses to determine the formula of an oxide of lead. This is the teacher''s method. Step1 find the mass of the reduction tube Step 2 add some of the lead oxide to the reduction tube Step 3 find the mass of the reduction tube and lead oxide Step 4 pass hydrogen gas over the lead oxide and ignite the hydrogen at the hole Step 5 heat the lead oxide strongly for 10 minutes Step 7 find the new mass of the reduction tube and its contents Step 6 keep passing hydrogen through the reduction tube until the tube and contents are cool (i) Give a reason why hydrogen is passed through the reduction tube until the tube and contents are cool. (ii) Describe what the teacher should do next to make sure all the lead oxide has been reduced to lead.', 1, 3, 90, NULL, '1eb653d1-3323-4300-835b-7a5bff6ef258', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:55:24.291837+00', '37f3d597-4cdc-48f5-9a3d-f877478d7901');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('5710d529-e411-48b2-b9c8-cd68508ccfb3', 'q06-1469520f', 'STRUCTURED', 'This question is about polymers.', 10, 3, 900, NULL, '8acd9ca3-705e-4f95-a18f-b9756a3bb097', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:56:55.657195+00', '7ee2b7fa-a747-4ba0-97b2-38701421b5b3');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('092bca0d-64da-4536-841e-69fdd31564ee', 'q01-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'A student was asked to find the mass of salt dissolved in $ 1 0 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sea water. She was given the following instructions. Step A Weigh an empty evaporating basin Step B Transfer 50 $ cm^{3} $ of sea water into the basin Step C Heat the sea water in the basin until all the water has evaporated Step D Allow the basin and residue to cool Step E Weigh the basin and residue of salt', 9, 3, 810, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.914201+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('af266607-d423-4ad7-a813-db6169e02517', 'q02-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'The diagrams show the reactions of some metals with cold water and with dilute hydrochloric acid. Metals in cold water Metals in dilute hydrochloric acid', 12, 3, 1080, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.914761+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('113b6cb8-516e-4f6b-95d3-f419f8cfd8c2', 'q03-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'When solutions are mixed together, precipitates sometimes form.', 8, 3, 720, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.915158+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('80dd9d90-8370-4c99-9813-c4be270d20d1', 'q04-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'The diagram shows the positions of some elements in the Periodic Table. 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 0', 11, 3, 990, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.915425+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('4d68a13c-0d89-4560-947c-d02fd3ce6c2d', 'q05-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'The apparatus in the diagram is used to collect the oxygen produced by the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide, $ \mathrm{H_{2}O_{2}} $', 1, 3, 90, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.915739+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('61088d7c-f338-44ec-8b45-adae34e906f2', 'q06-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'The element carbon has three common isotopes. These are carbon-12, carbon-13 and carbon-14.', 8, 3, 720, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.916005+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('5d0b6f4a-cfb8-49f7-bb66-2d245bff7f09', 'q07-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'Decane is a hydrocarbon found in crude oil. The diagram shows the structure of a decane molecule.', 1, 3, 90, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.916309+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('da9fb9e6-c5e9-4b44-b2dc-19374ced90dd', 'q09-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'When water is added to a mixture of sand and cement, a reaction takes place between silicon dioxide in the sand and calcium oxide in the cement. The reaction produces a salt called calcium silicate. The equation for the reaction is: $\mathrm {S i O} _ {2} + \mathrm {C a O} \rightarrow \mathrm {C a S i O} _ {3}$', 8, 3, 720, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.916876+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('12287e18-957c-4c1c-9894-506c6dc8b545', 'q08-06a1d491', 'STRUCTURED', 'The equation for a reaction that occurs in the manufacture of nitric acid is $4 \mathrm {N H} _ {3} (\mathrm {g}) + 5 \mathrm {O} _ {2} (\mathrm {g}) \rightleftharpoons 4 \mathrm {N O} (\mathrm {g}) + 6 \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} (\mathrm {g}) \quad \Delta H = - 9 0 0 \mathrm {k J / m o l}$', 15, 3, 1350, NULL, '28ca36dd-381a-4265-9157-a6ac03a313f7', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:52:24.999029+00', 'fc401417-2892-49d8-9f02-160a9222e7bb');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('0abbcc62-e698-4a2c-8bd3-d89f691026d7', 'q10-06a1d491', 'STRUCTURED', 'A teacher discussed with her students whether the boiling points of organic compounds are related to the size of their molecules. The students suggested measuring the boiling points of some organic compounds using this apparatus.', 7, 3, 630, NULL, '28ca36dd-381a-4265-9157-a6ac03a313f7', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:52:24.999715+00', 'fc401417-2892-49d8-9f02-160a9222e7bb');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('ec4ad51e-8695-48d8-8e4c-a776984d85b6', 'q01-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'The diagram represents an atom of an element. Use numbers from the box to complete the table. You may use each number once, more than once or not at all.', 5, 3, 450, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.919797+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('8bc5fa65-d6b9-4dab-a300-612c6b8c485b', 'q08-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'When ammonia gas and hydrogen chloride gas mix, they react together to form a white solid called ammonium chloride. The equation for the reaction is: $\mathrm {N H} _ {3} (\mathrm {g}) + \mathrm {H C l} (\mathrm {g}) \rightarrow \mathrm {N H} _ {4} \mathrm {C l} (\mathrm {s})$ After five minutes, a white ring of solid ammonium chloride formed. A cotton wool pad was soaked in ammonia solution and another was soaked in hydrogen chloride solution. The two pads were then put into opposite ends of a dry glass tube at the same time.', 6, 3, 540, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.916583+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('fde66226-0408-4d94-9480-f22e54b628a0', 'q10-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'When sodium is burned in air, one of the products is a pale yellow solid, X.', 1, 3, 90, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.917121+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('2de89e5e-09ab-4b9d-b08e-b96ecd3ebecd', 'q11-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'A student carried out a series of tests on a solid, M, in order to identify the ions that could be present. The table shows her results.', 10, 3, 900, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.91741+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('5f877ccf-ee6d-4928-9468-ee3da8c1bc1e', 'q12-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', 'Lead can be extracted from lead(II) sulfide, PbS, in two stages. Stage 1: Lead(II) sulfide is heated in air. It reacts with oxygen to produce lead(II) oxide and sulfur dioxide. Stage 2: The lead(II) oxide is then heated in a blast furnace with coke.', 11, 3, 990, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.917678+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('0c58cfea-c3bf-4b41-8e3c-c2f0ae7a17ac', 'q13-6fa6e7ba', 'STRUCTURED', '(a) Crystals of hydrated zinc sulfate, $ \mathrm{Z n S O_{4}. x H_{2} O} $ , contain water of crystallisation. He weighed the empty tube A. He placed a sample of hydrated zinc sulfate crystals in tube A and reweighed it. He heated the tube, allowed it to cool and weighed it again. He repeated this process until two consecutive masses were the same. This is known as ''heating to constant mass''. When hydrated zinc sulfate crystals are heated gently, they decompose according to the following equation: $\mathrm {Z n S O} _ {4}. \mathrm {x H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} \rightarrow \mathrm {Z n S O} _ {4} + \mathrm {x H} _ {2} \mathrm {O}$ The following masses were recorded: $\mathrm {M a s s o f t u b e A} = 1 0. 1 2 \mathrm {g}$ $\mathrm {M a s s o f t u b e A} + \mathrm {Z n S O} _ {4}. \mathrm {x H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} = 1 8. 7 3 \mathrm {g}$ Mass of tube A and $ \mathrm{Z n S O_{4}} $ after heating to constant mass = 14.95 g (i) Calculate the mass of $ \mathrm{Z n S O}_{4} $ formed after heating to constant mass. (ii) Calculate the mass of water collected after heating to constant mass. (iii) The relative formula mass of $ \mathrm{Z n S O_{4}} $ is 161 The relative formula mass of water is 18 Use this information, and your answers to (a)(i) and (a)(ii), to calculate the value of x in the formula $ \mathrm{Z n S O_{4}. x H_{2}O} $ Show your working. A student used the apparatus shown to remove and collect the water of crystallisation from the crystals in order to find the value of x.', 8, 3, 720, NULL, '40d62282-38ae-433b-a37b-8279c0309ed1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:41:17.924032+00', 'c7143310-3faf-4827-8351-a0a20f7a5772');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('5afa8a7d-4dc9-4b23-86c2-e717839e87f8', 'q02-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'Substances can be classified as elements, compounds or mixtures.', 11, 3, 990, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.920235+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('8235e0f6-5c2f-4b76-83c5-43445bab4756', 'q03-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'The diagram shows three pieces of iron. A is a piece of iron. B is a piece of iron with a thin coating of zinc. C is a piece of iron with some of the zinc coating missing.', 7, 3, 630, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.921495+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('2cb10005-1f34-4284-9e36-6be3b7a322e7', 'q04-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'The table shows the formulae of some positive and negative ions. It also shows the formulae of some compounds containing these ions.', 13, 3, 1170, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.922024+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('8ed243c9-77bf-40be-8187-cc9260ac8bff', 'q05-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'The diagram shows a blast furnace used to extract iron from its ore.', 6, 3, 540, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.922287+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('5854888b-a2a8-4bcf-a65c-987d0158c077', 'q06-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'Poly(ethene) is a common polymer. It is obtained from crude oil by fractional distillation, cracking and polymerisation.', 16, 3, 1440, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.922551+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('f152ea19-b2d7-4139-899c-196f048be357', 'q07-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'A student uses the reaction between iron and oxygen in an experiment to find the percentage by volume of oxygen in air. The diagram shows his apparatus.', 1, 3, 90, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.924721+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('468420c1-4282-425a-bc93-d28bac77b05a', 'q08-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'Hydrogen iodide can be manufactured from its elements using this reaction. $\mathrm {H} _ {2} (\mathrm {g}) + \mathrm {I} _ {2} (\mathrm {g}) \rightleftharpoons 2 \mathrm {H I} (\mathrm {g}) \quad \Delta H = - 9 \mathrm {k J / m o l}$ A temperature of $ 5 0 0^{\circ} \mathrm{C} $ a pressure of 4 atm and a platinum catalyst are used in this manufacturing process.', 9, 3, 810, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.925296+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
INSERT INTO public.questions VALUES ('38775529-39ba-44cd-bdec-04d01a9bd0dc', 'q09-8346f04a', 'STRUCTURED', 'Bromine, chlorine and iodine are elements in Group 7 of the Periodic Table.', 15, 3, 1350, NULL, '2748c57d-8f79-4fc8-a1a5-1d3ded9c73b1', 'PAST_PAPER', true, 1, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.925573+00', '4eb869ff-319e-420e-b833-358a7da58b4d');
