 ["14(a)", "Any two from:\nM1 both forward and backwards reactions are occurring\nM2 amounts/concentrations of reactants and products stay the same/pressure(of gas mixture) stays the same\nM3 rate of forward reaction=rate of backwards reaction", "masses for amounts", "are the same", "2"], ["(b)(i)", "M1 increase\nM2(forward) reaction is exothermic/gives out heat\nM2 dep on M1\nIGNORE references to le Chatelier''s principle and to reaction tries to decrease the temperature/equilibrium shifts to right", "reverse reaction is endothermic", "equilibrium shifts to left", "1\n1"], ["(b)(ii)", "M1 increase\nM2 fewer moles/molecules(of gas) on right(hand side)\nM2 dep on M1\nIGNORE references to le Chatelier''s principle and to reaction tries to decrease the pressure/equilibrium shifts to right", "more molecules on left(hand side)", "equilibrium shifts to left", "1\n1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n14(a) | Any two from:\nM1 both forward and backwards reactions are occurring\nM2 amounts/concentrations of reactants and products stay the same/pressure(of gas mixture) stays the same\nM3 rate of forward reaction=rate of backwards reaction | masses for amounts | are the same | 2\n(b)(i) | M1 increase\nM2(forward) reaction is exothermic/gives out heat\nM2 dep on M1\nIGNORE references to le Chatelier''s principle and to reaction tries to decrease the temperature/equilibrium shifts to right | reverse reaction is endothermic | equilibrium shifts to left | 1\n1\n(b)(ii) | M1 increase\nM2 fewer moles/molecules(of gas) on right(hand side)\nM2 dep on M1\nIGNORE references to le Chatelier''s principle and to reaction tries to decrease the pressure/equilibrium shifts to right | more molecules on left(hand side) | equilibrium shifts to left | 1\n1", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(c)(i)", "2CH3OH+O2→2H2CO+2H2O\nM1 formulae\nM2 balancing\nM2 dep on M1\nIGNORE catalyst if on both sides or above arrow\nIGNORE state symbols", "multiples and halves", "", "2"], ["(ii)", "M1-a substance that increases the rate of a reaction\nIGNORE alters the rate and any reference to enzymes\nM2and is chemically unchanged (at the end of the reaction)\nIGNORE references to takes no part in the reaction", "mass does not change without being used up", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "M1 provides an alternative reaction path(way)/route/mechanism\nM2(alternative path has a) lower activation energy\n[Activation energy can be described, e.g. the minimum energy needed (by colliding particles) for reaction to occur]\nMAX1 if any mention of particles gaining energy", "M1 molecules adsorb on/stick to the catalyst\nM2 weakens the bonds in the reactant molecules", "", "1"], ["(d)", "2CH3OH+3O2→2CO2+4H2O\nM1all formulae correct\nM2balanced\nM2dep on M1\nIGNORE state symbols", "multiples and halves\ncorrect equation for methanal for one mark", "", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total", "14"]], "text": "(c)(i) | 2CH3OH+O2→2H2CO+2H2O\nM1 formulae\nM2 balancing\nM2 dep on M1\nIGNORE catalyst if on both sides or above arrow\nIGNORE state symbols | multiples and halves |  | 2\n(ii) | M1-a substance that increases the rate of a reaction\nIGNORE alters the rate and any reference to enzymes\nM2and is chemically unchanged (at the end of the reaction)\nIGNORE references to takes no part in the reaction | mass does not change without being used up |  | 1\n(iii) | M1 provides an alternative reaction path(way)/route/mechanism\nM2(alternative path has a) lower activation energy\n[Activation energy can be described, e.g. the minimum energy needed (by colliding particles) for reaction to occur]\nMAX1 if any mention of particles gaining energy | M1 molecules adsorb on/stick to the catalyst\nM2 weakens the bonds in the reactant molecules |  | 1\n(d) | 2CH3OH+3O2→2CO2+4H2O\nM1all formulae correct\nM2balanced\nM2dep on M1\nIGNORE state symbols | multiples and halves\ncorrect equation for methanal for one mark |  | 2\n |  |  | Total | 14", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000009"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000011"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "f8db3ca9-e5f0-5ee4-a269-0d2adc4f7d78", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:52:06.392946693Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 178, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 5, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Science Double Award (4SC0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel Level 1/Level 2 Certificates", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (KCH0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Science (Double Award) (KSCO) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:52:25.72762+00');
