played", "", "1"], ["M4- IGNORE bond angles", "", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n14(a) | M1- | continuation bonds not going through brackets |  | 1\nM2-any suitable use, eg: |  | just plastic | 1\n· plastic bags |  |  | \n· buckets/bowls |  |  | \n· storage bottles(for food, drinks, chemicals) |  |  | \n· garden furniture |  |  | \n· gas pipes |  |  | \n· rubbish bins |  |  | \n· storage tanks for fuel |  |  | \n· cling film |  |  | \nPlease research any unfamiliar use | polypropene polypropylene |  | 1\nM3- poly(propene) | methyl group attached to any carbon methyl group displayed |  | 1\nM4- IGNORE bond angles |  |  | ", "row_count": 14, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000051", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 51, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(b)", "Any two from\nM1-(many) small molecules/monomers join up\nM2-double bond becomes single bond/it becomes saturated\nM3-increase in mass/chain length/size", "OWTTE\ndouble bond breaks and single bond forms", "", "2"], ["(c)(i)", "inert(ness)\nIGNORE strong bonds/long chains", "unreactive/non-polar", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1-produces greenhouse gases/toxic gases/poisonous gases\nM2-(landfill) uses up land/takes up space\nOR new sites hard to find", "carbon dioxide", "", "1"]], "text": "(b) | Any two from\nM1-(many) small molecules/monomers join up\nM2-double bond becomes single bond/it becomes saturated\nM3-increase in mass/chain length/size | OWTTE\ndouble bond breaks and single bond forms |  | 2\n(c)(i) | inert(ness)\nIGNORE strong bonds/long chains | unreactive/non-polar |  | 1\n(ii) | M1-produces greenhouse gases/toxic gases/poisonous gases\nM2-(landfill) uses up land/takes up space\nOR new sites hard to find | carbon dioxide |  | 1", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000052", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 52, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["15(a)(i)(ii)", "M1-Mr(NaOH)=40", "", "", "1"], ["M2-10(.0)÷M1", "", "", "1"], ["M3-0.25(mol)Correct answer with no working scores3", "", "", "1"], ["M1-0.25x1000÷250", "", "", "1"], ["M2-1(.0)(mol/dm3)Correct answer with no working scores2", "M3 from(a)(i)÷250/0.001for1mark", "", "1"], ["Mark csq throughout", "", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n15(a)(i)(ii) | M1-Mr(NaOH)=40 |  |  | 1\nM2-10(.0)÷M1 |  |  | 1\nM3-0.25(mol)Correct answer with no working scores3 |  |  | 1\nM1-0.25x1000÷250 |  |  | 1\nM2-1(.0)(mol/dm3)Correct answer with no working scores2 | M3 from(a)(i)÷250/0.001for1mark |  | 1\nMark csq throughout |  |  | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000054", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 54, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(b)(i)", "M1-(reading at end)25.20", "red\npipette measures one volume only", "1"], ["M2-(reading at start)1.65", "1"], ["M3-(volume added)23.55", "1"], ["Award 1 mark for correct end and start readings in reverse order", "1"], ["Mark M3 csq on M1 and M2\nPenalise lack of two decimal places once only in a correct answer", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1-(colour at start)yellow", "pipette measures one volume only", "1"], ["M2-orange/pink", "1"], ["(iii)", "different volumes can be measured\n/continuously graduated\n/addition(of acid)can be controlled\n/volume required is not known\nIGNORE references to precision or accuracy", "", ""], ["(c)(i)", "M1-2(.00)x200÷1000", "400 for 1 mark", "1"], ["M2-0.4(0)(mol)\nCorrect final answer with no working scores 2 marks", "1"], ["M1-n(CO2)=0.2(0)/1/2of M2from(c)(i)(mol)", "1"], ["M2-mass(CO2)=8.8(0)(g)/M1x44\nCorrect final answer with no working scores 2 marks", "1"]], "text": "(b)(i) | M1-(reading at end)25.20 | red\npipette measures one volume only | 1\nM2-(reading at start)1.65 | 1\nM3-(volume added)23.55 | 1\nAward 1 mark for correct end and start readings in reverse order | 1\nMark M3 csq on M1 and M2\nPenalise lack of two decimal places once only in a correct answer | 1\n(ii) | M1-(colour at start)yellow | pipette measures one volume only | 1\nM2-orange/pink | 1\n(iii) | different volumes can be measured\n/continuously graduated\n/addition(of acid)can be controlled\n/volume required is not known\nIGNORE references to precision or accuracy |  | \n(c)(i) | M1-2(.00)x200÷1000 | 400 for 1 mark | 1\nM2-0.4(0)(mol)\nCorrect final answer with no working scores 2 marks | 1\nM1-n(CO2)=0.2(0)/1/2of M2from(c)(i)(mol) | 1\nM2-mass(CO2)=8.8(0)(g)/M1x44\nCorrect final answer with no working scores 2 marks | 1", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000055", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 55, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000005", "e000006", "e000007", "e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000019", "e000021", "e000023", "e000026", "e000029", "e000031", "e000033", "e000036", "e000039", "e000042", "e000044", "e000047", "e000050", "e000053", "e000056"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "2f4affa8-3e24-50db-b0a2-25f265b1a519", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:52:07.130123569Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 182, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "June 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 1C Science Double Award (4SC0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Level 1/Level 2 Certificate Chemistry (KCH0) Paper 1C Science (Double Award) (KSC0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications come from Pearson, the world''s leading learning company. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information, please visit our website at www.edexcel.com.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Our website subject pages hold useful resources, support material and live feeds from our subject advisors giving you access to a portal of information. If you have any subject specific questions about this specification that require the help of a subject specialist, you may find our Ask The Expert email service helpful.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "www.edexcel.com/contactus", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2014 Publications Code UG038368 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 1 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 2 = 3 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 3 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 4 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 5 = 11 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 6 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 7 = 4 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 8 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total marks for Question 9 = 11 