ds shown as dot and cross rest of diagram correct", "Accept all dots and all crosses", "1"], ["M2 DEP on M1", "Accept any combination of dots and crosses", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8 | a | i | air | Accept atmosphere | 1\nnatural gas / water / hydrocarbons / alkanes | Accept steam / methane | 1\niron / Fe | Ignore references to promoters such as iron oxide | 1\nany value in range 150-250 | Reject iron with an oxidation state | 1\nC (hydrogen and nitrogen) | If range stated, must be within 150-250 | Reject values in other units | 1\n | b | i | 2(1)(1)2 | Accept multiples and fractions | 1\nall five bonds shown as dot and cross rest of diagram correct | Accept all dots and all crosses | 1\nM2 DEP on M1 | Accept any combination of dots and crosses | 1", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8", "c", "i", "$\\Delta H$ is negative OR enthalpy changes / energy changes / heat changes / values are negative", "", "1"], ["ii", "does not react with oxygen / no oxygen (in equation)", "Accept no combustion / does not burn Accept decomposition", "1"], ["", "d", "i", "C26.112", "N60.914", "H13.01", "0/3 for use of any atomic numbers / division wrong way round / multiplication If division by 28(N) or 2(H), then no M1, but M2 and M3 can score by ECF:28 and 2 gives CNH328 and 1 gives CNH614 and 2 gives CN2H3If any transcription error (eg 21.6 in place of 26.1), then no M1, but M2 and M3 can score by ECF", "1"], ["ii", "ratio is 2.18:4.35:13.0/1:2:6CN2H6", "Accept elements in any order Use of M and H symbols means M3 cannot be awarded", "111"], ["CN2H6", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8 | c | i | $\\Delta H$ is negative OR enthalpy changes / energy changes / heat changes / values are negative |  | 1\nii | does not react with oxygen / no oxygen (in equation) | Accept no combustion / does not burn Accept decomposition | 1\n | d | i | C26.112 | N60.914 | H13.01 | 0/3 for use of any atomic numbers / division wrong way round / multiplication If division by 28(N) or 2(H), then no M1, but M2 and M3 can score by ECF:28 and 2 gives CNH328 and 1 gives CNH614 and 2 gives CN2H3If any transcription error (eg 21.6 in place of 26.1), then no M1, but M2 and M3 can score by ECF | 1\nii | ratio is 2.18:4.35:13.0/1:2:6CN2H6 | Accept elements in any order Use of M and H symbols means M3 cannot be awarded | 111\nCN2H6 |  | 1", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9", "a", "i", "gains oxygen", "Accept increase in oxidation number/state\nIgnore reference to loss of electrons", "1"], ["ii", "SO2+H2O→H2SO3", "Accept 2SO2+O2+2H2O→2H2SO4OR\n2SO2+O2→2SO3ANDSO3+H2O→H2SO4", "1"], ["", "b", "i", "covalent", "Accept sharing electrons\nReject sharing 1 electron\nReject references to ions\nIgnore intermolecular forces\nIgnore simple\nReject giant", "1"], ["ii", "intermolecular forces(of attraction)/forces(of attraction)between moleculesweak/need little(thermal/heat)energy to overcome", "Accept intermolecular bonds", "1"], ["iii", "Mo2O6", "Accept easily overcome\nM2DEP on M1at least partially correct\nIf only answer is weak bonds,then0/2\nIf any reference to breaking covalent/ionic/metallic bonds,then0/2", "1"], ["", "", "", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9 | a | i | gains oxygen | Accept increase in oxidation number/state\nIgnore reference to loss of electrons | 1\nii | SO2+H2O→H2SO3 | Accept 2SO2+O2+2H2O→2H2SO4OR\n2SO2+O2→2SO3ANDSO3+H2O→H2SO4 | 1\n | b | i | covalent | Accept sharing electrons\nReject sharing 1 electron\nReject references to ions\nIgnore intermolecular forces\nIgnore simple\nReject giant | 1\nii | intermolecular forces(of attraction)/forces(of attraction)between moleculesweak/need little(thermal/heat)energy to overcome | Accept intermolecular bonds | 1\niii | Mo2O6 | Accept easily overcome\nM2DEP on M1at least partially correct\nIf only answer is weak bonds,then0/2\nIf any reference to breaking covalent/ionic/metallic bonds,then0/2 | 1\n |  |  |  | 1", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["", "", "", "", "", ""], ["9", "c", "i", "(giant structure of) positive ions\n(surrounded by) delocalised electrons", "Accept cations but not just ions\nReject references to negative ions and molecules\nAccept sea of electrons\nMark independently", "1"], ["(delocalised / sea of) electrons\nmove / flow (through\nstructure) / are mobile (when\nvoltage/potential difference\napplied)", "Ignore free electrons\nIgnore references to carrying\ncharge/current\nM2 DEP on M1\nNo penalty for references to\nmolybdenum atoms or ions / nuclei /\nprotons, but any mention of these\nmoving = 0/2", "1"], ["iii", "layers/sheets/planes/rows\nAND\n(positive)\nions/atoms/particles\nslide (over each other)", "If any reference to\nmolecules/protons/electrons/nuclei, then 0/2", "1"], ["", "Allow\nslip/flow/shift/move/OWTTE in\nplace of slide\nM2 DEP on mention of either layers etc OR ions etc", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n |  |  |  |  | \n9 | c | i | (giant structure of) positive ions\n(surrounded by) delocalised electrons | Accept cations but not just ions\nReject references to negative ions and molecules\nAccept sea of electrons\nMark independently | 1\n(delocalised / sea of) electrons\nmove / flow (through\nstructure) / are mobile (when\nvoltage/potential difference\napplied) | Ignore free electrons\nIgnore references to carrying\ncharge/current\nM2 DEP on M1\nNo penalty for references to\nmolybdenum atoms or ions / nuclei /\nprotons, but any mention of these\nmoving = 0/2 | 1\niii | layers/sheets/planes/rows\nAND\n(positive)\nions/atoms/particles\nslide (over each other) | If any reference to\nmolecules/protons/electrons/nuclei, then 0/2 | 1\n | Allow\nslip/flow/shift/move/OWTTE in\nplace of slide\nM2 DEP on mention of either layers etc OR ions etc | 1", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10", "a", "i", "water", "Accept steam", "1"], ["risk of explosion / to burn excess hydrogen safely", "OWTTE\nIgnore hydrogen is flammable", "1"], ["", "b", "", "heat the solid again\nreweigh to check mass remains constant", "Ignore burning\nIgnore repeat and find mean heat to constant mass=2", "1\n1"], ["", "c", "i", "0.8", "", "1"], ["ii", "0.8÷16\n0.05", "CQ on(i)\nNo ECF for division by 8 or 32\nM2 subsumes M1", "1\n1"], ["iii", "0.05/answer to ii", "", "1"], ["iv", "2.8÷0.05\n56", "CQ on(iii)\nM2 subsumes M1\n0/2 if any mass other than 2.8 used", "1\n1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 | a | i | water | Accept steam | 1\nrisk of explosion / to burn excess hydrogen safely | OWTTE\nIgnore hydrogen is flammable | 1\n | b |  | heat the solid again\nreweigh to check mass remains constant | Ignore burning\nIgnore repeat and find mean heat to constant mass=2 | 1\n1\n | c | i | 0.8 |  | 1\nii | 0.8÷16\n0.05 | CQ on(i)\nNo ECF for division by 8 or 32\nM2 subsumes M1 | 1\n1\niii | 0.05/answer to ii |  | 1\niv | 2.8÷0.05\n56 | CQ on(iii)\nM2 subsumes M1\n0/2 if any mass other than 2.8 used | 1\n1", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000005", "e000006", "e000007", "e000008", "e000009", "e000010"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000021", "e000024", "e000027", "e000029", "e000032", "e000035", "e000040", "e000043", "e000046", "e000048"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "f9b3ad01-e82b-5449-be6d-12a21d9c4188", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:52:49.079237667Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 234, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "June 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 1CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Science Double Award (4SC0) Paper 1CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications come from Pearson, the world''s leading learning company. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information, please visit our website at www.edexcel.com.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Our website subject pages hold useful resources, support material and live feeds from our subject advisors giving you access to a portal of information. If you have any subject specific questions about this specification that require the help of a subject specialist, you may find our Ask The Expert email service helpful.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "www.edexcel.com/contactus", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2014 Publications Code UG038366", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1=8 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2=14 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3 = 12 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6=15 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7 = 16 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 8 = 15 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 9 = 12 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 10 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:10.710377+00');
