source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "relative atomic mass =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000246", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 246, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 9 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000247", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 247, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "10 This question is about the insoluble salt lead(II) bromide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000248", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 248, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) A student uses the precipitation method to prepare lead(II) bromide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000249", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 249, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation for the reaction she uses is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000250", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 250, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Describe how she could use solutions of lead(II) nitrate and sodium bromide to obtain a pure, dry sample of lead(II) bromide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000252", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 252, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The student''s teacher uses this apparatus to electrolyse a pure sample of molten lead(II) bromide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000253", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 253, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The student records these observations.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000255", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 255, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "a small blob of a silvery liquid appears at one electrode", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000256", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 256, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "a brown substance forms at the other electrode", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000257", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 257, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "the lamp stops working soon after the teacher stops heating the lead(II) bromide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000258", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 258, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Which is the correct statement about this electrolysis?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000259", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 259, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A the brown substance is bromide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000260", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 260, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B the products are both elements", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000261", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 261, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C the silvery liquid forms at the positive electrode", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000262", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 262, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D the silvery liquid is molten lead(II) bromide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000263", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 263, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) The student writes this half-equation to show the reaction in which the brown substance forms.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000264", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 264, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Identify the two mistakes in her half-equation.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000266", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 266, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Explain why the lamp stops working after the teacher stops heating the lead(II) bromide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000267", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 267, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 10 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000268", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 268, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "11 A student uses the neutralisation method to make a sample of the soluble salt, sodium sulfate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000269", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 269, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation for the reaction he uses is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000270", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 270, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) He does a titration using these steps to find the ratio of the volumes of reactants needed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000272", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 272, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add 25.0 $ cm^{3} $ solution of dilute sodium hydroxide solution to a conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000273", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 273, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add a few drops of phenolphthalein indicator to the conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000274", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 274, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add dilute sulfuric acid from a burette until the indicator just changes colour", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000275", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 275, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "repeat the experiment until concordant results are obtained", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000276", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 276, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Which piece of apparatus should the student use to add the sodium hydroxide solution?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000277", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 277, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) What colour change would the student see when he neutralises the sodium hydroxide solution?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000278", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 278, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "colour before neutralisation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000279", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 279, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "colour after neutralisation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000280", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 280, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The diagram shows the burette readings in one experiment before and after adding the acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000281", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 281, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use the readings to calculate the volume of acid added, entering all values to the nearest 0.05 $ cm^{3}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000284", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 284, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "burette reading after adding acid ... $ \\mathrm{c m^{3}} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000285", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 285, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "burette reading before adding acid ... $ \\mathrm{c m^{3}} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000286", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 286, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "volume of acid added ... $ \\mathrm{c m^{3}} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000287", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 287, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The student repeats the experiment and records these results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000288", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 288, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The average (mean) volume of acid added should be calculated using only concordant results (those that differ from each other by $ 0. 2 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ or less).", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000290", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 290, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Identify the concordant results by placing ticks ( $ \\checkmark $ ) in the table where appropriate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000291", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 291, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Use your ticked results to calculate the average volume of acid added.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000292", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 292, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) The student uses 200 $ cm^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution of concentration 0.300 mol/dm $ ^{3} $ to prepare a sample of sodium sulfate solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000293", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 293, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "12 A student investigates the rate of the reaction between marble chips (calcium carbonate) and dilute hydrochloric acid. She is given a bottle containing hydrochloric acid labelled 100% She uses this method to find out how changing the concentration of the acid affects the rate of reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000295", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 295, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add some marble chips to a conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000296", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 296, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "pour 50.0 $ cm^{3} $ of dilute hydrochloric acid into the flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000297", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 297, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "place the flask on a balance and start a timer", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000298", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 298, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "record the time taken for the mass of the flask and contents to decrease by 1.0 g", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000299", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 299, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "repeat the experiment using different concentrations of hydrochloric acid", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000300", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 300, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Suggest two features of the marble chips that the student should keep the same to ensure that the results are valid (a fair test).", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000301", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 301, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Why does the mass of the flask and contents decrease during the experiment?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000302", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 302, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The student should have put some cotton wool in the neck of the conical flask after placing the flask on the balance.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000303", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 303, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "How would this improve the accuracy of the results?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000304", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 304, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) The graph shows the student''s results for the decrease in the mass of the flask and contents by 1.0 g.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000305", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 305, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Use the graph to find the time taken for the loss of 1.0 g of mass from the flask when the concentration of acid is 50%.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000307", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 307, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Show on the graph how you obtained your answer.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000308", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 308, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) One of the points on the graph is anomalous. What could have caused this anomalous result?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000309", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 309, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A the concentration of acid was more than 40%", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000310", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 310, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B the loss of mass was greater than 1.0 g", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000311", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 311, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C the mass of marble chips was more than 10 g", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000312", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 312, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D the student started the timer too late", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000313", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 313, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) The results of each experiment can be used to calculate the rate of reaction using the expression", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000314", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 314, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the rate of reaction when the concentration of acid is 50%.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000316", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 316, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(f) The student is given a bottle of hydrochloric acid with a concentration different from that used in the previous experiments. She repeats the investigation using different concentrations of hydrochloric acid. She calculates the rate of reaction for each experiment.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000318", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 318, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows her results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000319", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 319, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Plot these results on the grid and draw a straight line of best fit.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000321", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 321, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(g) The rate of reaction increases as the concentration of the acid increases. Explain this relationship in terms of particles.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000323", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 323, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 12 = 15 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000324", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 324, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "TOTAL FOR PAPER = 120 MARKS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000325", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 325, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000326", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 326, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:11.207596+00');
