t elements in any order", ""], ["Award 3 marks for correct final answer with no working", ""], ["C2H4F2", "Accept elements in any order", "1"], ["Do not accept C2H4Fl2", ""], ["", "", "", "", "Total 15 marks", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5 f i | M1 setting out division of each % by Ar OR evaluation | Award 0/3 if division by any atomic numbers / wrong way up / multiplication used | 3\n36.412 | 6.01 | 57.619 | Do not penalise roundings or minor misreads of % values (eg 56.7 for fluorine) | \nDo not penalise use of Fl in (i) | \n3 | 6 | 3 | If molecular masses used for H and/or F, lose M1 but M2 and M3 can be awarded: using 2 and 38 gives C2H2F using 2 and 19 gives CHF Using 1 and 38 gives C2H4F Working required for these answers | \nM2 subsumes M1 | \nAccept elements in any order | \nAward 3 marks for correct final answer with no working | \nC2H4F2 | Accept elements in any order | 1\nDo not accept C2H4Fl2 | \n |  |  |  | Total 15 marks | ", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6 a", "(A) refinery gases", "", "2"], ["(F) bitumen", "", ""], ["b", "M1(compound/molecule/substance containing) carbon and hydrogen/C and H(atoms/elements)", "Reject atom/element/ion/mixture in place of compound/molecule/substanceReject compound/molecule/substance in place of atom/elementIgnore references to bonds/long chains", "2"], ["M2only", "Accept other terms with same meaning, eg solely/exclusively/justM2 DEP on mention of carbon and hydrogen/C and H and no other element", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 a | (A) refinery gases |  | 2\n(F) bitumen |  | \nb | M1(compound/molecule/substance containing) carbon and hydrogen/C and H(atoms/elements) | Reject atom/element/ion/mixture in place of compound/molecule/substanceReject compound/molecule/substance in place of atom/elementIgnore references to bonds/long chains | 2\nM2only | Accept other terms with same meaning, eg solely/exclusively/justM2 DEP on mention of carbon and hydrogen/C and H and no other element | ", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6 c", "(fuel oil molecules/it/they)", "Accept converse statements about gasoline", "3"], ["M1 have higher boiling points", "Ignore reference to melting points", ""], ["M2 are darker(in colour)", "Ignore stronger/more intense(colours)\nIf specific colours stated, award M2 if valid comparison,eg gasoline is yellow and fuel oil is brown, fuel oil is browner", ""], ["M3 have higher viscosities/are more viscous", "Accept thicker/stickier/flows less easily,etc in place of more viscous\nIf gasoline,accept thinner/runnier/flows more easily,etc in place of less viscous", ""], ["", "Must be a comparison,eg not enough to say fuel oil has a high boiling point unless also a statement that gasoline has a low boiling point\nMAX 2 if no comparison", ""], ["", "Accept reference to fractions near the top/up the column in place of gasoline\nAccept reference to fractions near the bottom/down the column in place of fuel oil", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 c | (fuel oil molecules/it/they) | Accept converse statements about gasoline | 3\nM1 have higher boiling points | Ignore reference to melting points | \nM2 are darker(in colour) | Ignore stronger/more intense(colours)\nIf specific colours stated, award M2 if valid comparison,eg gasoline is yellow and fuel oil is brown, fuel oil is browner | \nM3 have higher viscosities/are more viscous | Accept thicker/stickier/flows less easily,etc in place of more viscous\nIf gasoline,accept thinner/runnier/flows more easily,etc in place of less viscous | \n | Must be a comparison,eg not enough to say fuel oil has a high boiling point unless also a statement that gasoline has a low boiling point\nMAX 2 if no comparison | \n | Accept reference to fractions near the top/up the column in place of gasoline\nAccept reference to fractions near the bottom/down the column in place of fuel oil | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["d iii", "silica / silicon dioxide / SiO2ORalumina / aluminium oxide / Al2O3", "Accept aluminosilicate(s)/ zeolites", "1"], ["M1 C2H4", "Ignore silica oxide and alumina oxide", "2"], ["M2 C3H6", "Award 1 mark for C4H8 and CH2"]], "text": "d iii | silica / silicon dioxide / SiO2ORalumina / aluminium oxide / Al2O3 | Accept aluminosilicate(s)/ zeolites | 1\nM1 C2H4 | Ignore silica oxide and alumina oxide | 2\nM2 C3H6 | Award 1 mark for C4H8 and CH2", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6 e i", "insufficient/lack of air/oxygen OWTTE", "Accept oxygen not in excess\nReject no oxygen", "1"], ["ii", "carbon monoxide/CO", "", "1"], ["iii", "decreases capacity of blood(cells) to carry oxygen\nOR\nstops blood(cells) from carrying oxygen", "Accept CO combines with haemoglobin/forms\ncarboxyhaemoglobin\nAccept CO displaces/replaces oxygen in haemoglobin\nIgnore CO combines with red blood cells\nIgnore references to suffocation/lack of oxygen in lungs\nstopping breathing/gas exchange\nIgnore just affects haemoglobin\nReject destroys 