 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10 a", "M1 volume", "Ignore amount of solution for both, but accept amount in cm3 for M1", "2"], ["M2 concentration", "Reject volume of gases", ""], ["Allow mass of solution", ""], ["Ignore strength\nIgnore temperature/ pressure\nAccept in either order", ""], ["b i\nii", "B", "", "1"], ["D", "", "1"], ["c", "M1 filter (and dry) and weigh solid/A/it\nM2 mass is (still) 1g/mass is unchanged", "Mark M1 and M2 independently", "2"], ["Accept separate/remove solid/A/it from reaction mixture and weigh it", ""], ["Accept reverse argument, eg if it was a reactant, the mass would decrease", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 a | M1 volume | Ignore amount of solution for both, but accept amount in cm3 for M1 | 2\nM2 concentration | Reject volume of gases | \nAllow mass of solution | \nIgnore strength\nIgnore temperature/ pressure\nAccept in either order | \nb i\nii | B |  | 1\nD |  | 1\nc | M1 filter (and dry) and weigh solid/A/it\nM2 mass is (still) 1g/mass is unchanged | Mark M1 and M2 independently | 2\nAccept separate/remove solid/A/it from reaction mixture and weigh it | \nAccept reverse argument, eg if it was a reactant, the mass would decrease | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10 d i", "图10所示图", "M1+M2 all five points plotted to nearest gridline\nPoints at zero and 120 are not essential but must be correct if plotted\nDeduct 1 mark for each error up to max 2", "3"], ["ii", "M1 some indication on graph", "eg vertical line up from 70s\nOR\nhorizontal line to where line from 70s would meet curve\nOR\ncross on graph", "2"], ["", "M2 volume CQ on candidate curve", "Must be an integer(cm3)\nNo marks if original curve used", ""], ["iii", "curve steeper/gradient steeper/greater\nOR\ncurve levels off earlier/curve reaches\n100cm3in shorter time/OWTTE", "Accept line for curve\nAccept graph is steeper", "1"], ["", "", "Accept answers that do not depend on graph but can be obtained from the table of results, eg bigger volume in a shorter time, reaction stopped earlier", ""], ["", "", "Total 12 marks"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 d i | 图10所示图 | M1+M2 all five points plotted to nearest gridline\nPoints at zero and 120 are not essential but must be correct if plotted\nDeduct 1 mark for each error up to max 2 | 3\nii | M1 some indication on graph | eg vertical line up from 70s\nOR\nhorizontal line to where line from 70s would meet curve\nOR\ncross on graph | 2\n | M2 volume CQ on candidate curve | Must be an integer(cm3)\nNo marks if original curve used | \niii | curve steeper/gradient steeper/greater\nOR\ncurve levels off earlier/curve reaches\n100cm3in shorter time/OWTTE | Accept line for curve\nAccept graph is steeper | 1\n |  | Accept answers that do not depend on graph but can be obtained from the table of results, eg bigger volume in a shorter time, reaction stopped earlier | \n |  | Total 12 marks", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["11 a iii", "(pressure) low\nfewer (gas) moles/molecules/particles on left OR\nfewer moles/molecules/particles of reactants OR\nforward reaction produces more moles/molecules/particles", "Accept statement about numbers of moles/molecules,\neg 3 on left and 5 on right\nAccept more (gas) moles/molecules/particles on right\n/ more moles/molecules of products but not just more products\nIgnore references to favouring right hand side/forward direction\n/endothermic reaction/equilibrium shifting to right\n/Le Chatelier''s principle\n/low pressure favours side with more moles\nIgnore references to rate/collisions\nIf answer to(i) is high, no ECF in(ii)\nIf no answer to(i), mark can be awarded in(ii)", "1\n1"], ["b iii", "(temperature) high\n(forward) reaction is endothermic/has positive ΔH value\n/ absorbs heat", "Accept reverse reaction is exothermic/has negative ΔH value/gives out heat\nIgnore favours the endothermic reaction\nIgnore references to rate/collisions\nIf answer to(i) is low, no ECF in(ii)\nIf no answer to(i), mark can be awarded", "1\n1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n11 a iii | (pressure) low\nfewer (gas) moles/molecules/particles on left OR\nfewer moles/molecules/particles of reactants OR\nforward reaction produces more moles/molecules/particles | Accept statement about numbers of moles/molecules,\neg 3 on left and 5 on right\nAccept more (gas) moles/molecules/particles on right\n/ more moles/molecules of products but not just more products\nIgnore references to favouring right hand side/forward direction\n/endothermic reaction/equilibrium shifting to right\n/Le Chatelier''s principle\n/low pressure favours side with more moles\nIgnore references to rate/collisions\nIf answer to(i) is high, no ECF in(ii)\nIf no answer to(i), mark can be awarded in(ii) | 1\n1\nb iii | (temperature) high\n(forward) reaction is endothermic/has positive ΔH value\n/ absorbs heat | Accept reverse reaction is exothermic/has negative ΔH value/gives out heat\nIgnore favours the endothermic reaction\nIgnore references to rate/collisions\nIf answer to(i) is low, no ECF in(ii)\nIf no answer to(i), mark can be awarded | 1\n1", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "", "", ""], ["c", "$\\Delta$H(value)/enthalpy change is small/smaller/less(than for reactions1and3)OR reaction not very exothermic/has lowest enthalpy change", "Accept energy in place of enthalpyAccept closer to zeroReject $\\Delta$H less negative/less exothermic/less heat given outIgnore references to temperature change/pressureIgnore less energy/not a lot of energy needed", "1"]], "text": " |  |  | \nc | $\\Delta$H(value)/enthalpy change is small/smaller/less(than for reactions1and3)OR reaction not very exothermic/has lowest enthalpy change | Accept energy in place of enthalpyAccept closer to zeroReject $\\Delta$H less negative/less exothermic/less heat given outIgnore references to temperature change/pressureIgnore less energy/not a lot of energy needed | 1", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["11 d\ni\nii", "(rate) increases", "Ignore references to yield/equilibrium/chances of collision in(i) and(ii)", "1"], ["Mark M1 and M2 independently", "2"], ["M1 particles closer together", "Accept more particles in a given volume/space/particles have less space/room(to move in)\nIgnore area in place of volume/space\nIgnore references to just numbers of gas moles/molecules", ""], ["M2 particles collide more frequently", "Not just more(successful) collisions\nAccept more(successful) collisions per unit time/per second, etc", ""], ["0/2 if references to particles moving faster/having greater energy\nIf answer to(i) is decreases,no ECF in(ii)\nIf no answer or ignored answer to(i),marks can be awarded", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n11 d\ni\nii | (rate) increases | Ignore references to yield/equilibrium/chances of collision in(i) and(ii) | 1\nMark M1 and M2 independently | 2\nM1 particles closer together | Accept more particles in a given volume/space/particles have less space/room(to move in)\nIgnore area in place of volume/space\nIgnore references to just numbers of gas moles/molecules | \nM2 particles collide more frequently | Not just more(successful) collisions\nAccept more(successful) collisions per unit time/per second, etc | \n0/2 if references to particles moving faster/having greater energy\nIf answer to(i) is decreases,no ECF in(ii)\nIf no answer or ignored answer to(i),marks can be awarded | ", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["11 e", "Accept working by mass ratio OR moles routes\nMass ratios:", "", "3"], ["M1 Mr(CH3OH)=32 AND Mr(CH3COOH)=60", "Award M1 for 32 and 60 seen anywhere, except as the result of incorrect calculations"], ["M2 m(CH3COOH)=64×60/32", "Mark M2 and M3 consequentially on Mr values"], ["M3 120(kg)", ""], ["OR\nMoles:", ""], ["M1 n(CH3OH)=64000÷32=2000(mol)", "Allow working in ''kilomoles'' even if mol given as unit or no unit for intermediate answers, eg64÷32=2(kmol/mol)"], ["M2 n(CH3COOH)=2000(mol)", "CQ on M1"], ["M3 m(CH3COOH)=2000×60=120000g/120(kg)", "CQ on M2"], ["", "Correct final answer with or without working scores 3 marks\nAccept 120000g if unit shown"], ["", "Total 11 marks"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n11 e | Accept working by mass ratio OR moles routes\nMass ratios: |  | 3\nM1 Mr(CH3OH)=32 AND Mr(CH3COOH)=60 | Award M1 for 32 and 60 seen anywhere, except as the result of incorrect calculations\nM2 m(CH3COOH)=64×60/32 | Mark M2 and M3 consequentially on Mr values\nM3 120(kg) | \nOR\nMoles: | \nM1 n(CH3OH)=64000÷32=2000(mol) | Allow working in ''kilomoles'' even if mol given as unit or no unit for intermediate answers, eg64÷32=2(kmol/mol)\nM2 n(CH3COOH)=2000(mol) | CQ on M1\nM3 m(CH3COOH)=2000×60=120000g/120(kg) | CQ on M2\n | Correct final answer with or without working scores 3 marks\nAccept 120000g if unit shown\n | Total 11 marks", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000049", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 49, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000009"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000011", "e000012"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "c8cb1ae9-aba8-5de6-970a-81a03703a8d9", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:52:50.655855905Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 281, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 2, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2015", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Science Double Award (4SC0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Level 1/Level 2 Certificate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (KCHO) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Science (Double Award) (KSCO) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2015 Publications Code UG041123 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2015", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:11.533779+00');
