2 attract (one another)\nM2 dep on M1 | IGNORE metal ions\nALLOW sea of electrons\nIGNORE free electrons\nany refs to ionic bonding, covalent bonding or IMFs scores zero | 2\n(ii) | (delocalised) electrons can flow/move (through structure)/are mobile (when voltage/pd is applied) | IGNORE carry charge | 1", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["13(a)", "$\\mathrm{I}_{2}+\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}\\rightarrow 2\\mathrm{ICl}$", "ACCEPT halves and multiples", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "M1rate of forward reaction=rate of backwards reaction", "ACCEPT both reactions occur at the same rateIGNORE forward reaction=backwards reaction", "2"], ["(ii)", "M2concentrations of reactants/products remain constant", "ACCEPT amounts/masses for concentrationsACCEPT don''t change/stay for remainIGNORE concentrations/amounts of reactants and products are the same/are equalALLOW colour remains constant", ""], ["", "M1equilibrium has shifted to the left/equilibrium has shifted to the ICl side/equilibrium has shifted to the reactants sideORmore ICl has been produced/more reactants have been produced", "IGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle e.g. an increase in temperature favours the endothermic reaction", "2"], ["", "M2an increase in temperature shifts the equilibrium in the endothermic direction", "ACCEPT `therefore the (backward) reaction is endothermic'' for M2if M1has been awarded", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n13(a) | $\\mathrm{I}_{2}+\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}\\rightarrow 2\\mathrm{ICl}$ | ACCEPT halves and multiples | 1\n(b)(i) | M1rate of forward reaction=rate of backwards reaction | ACCEPT both reactions occur at the same rateIGNORE forward reaction=backwards reaction | 2\n(ii) | M2concentrations of reactants/products remain constant | ACCEPT amounts/masses for concentrationsACCEPT don''t change/stay for remainIGNORE concentrations/amounts of reactants and products are the same/are equalALLOW colour remains constant | \n | M1equilibrium has shifted to the left/equilibrium has shifted to the ICl side/equilibrium has shifted to the reactants sideORmore ICl has been produced/more reactants have been produced | IGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle e.g. an increase in temperature favours the endothermic reaction | 2\n | M2an increase in temperature shifts the equilibrium in the endothermic direction | ACCEPT `therefore the (backward) reaction is endothermic'' for M2if M1has been awarded | ", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["14(a)", "Solid", "Amount", "ALLOW values (corrected rounded) from 1 sf up to calculator value", "2", ""], ["KHCO3", "0.080"], ["K2O", "0.059"], ["KOH", "0.099"], ["K2CO3", "0.040"], ["all four correct = 2 marks three correct = 1 mark", "", ""], ["(b)", "M1 equation 3\nM2 the (mole) ratio of KHCO3 to K2CO3/reactant to product is 2:1", "mark csq on amounts given in part(a)", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n14(a) | Solid | Amount | ALLOW values (corrected rounded) from 1 sf up to calculator value | 2 | \nKHCO3 | 0.080\nK2O | 0.059\nKOH | 0.099\nK2CO3 | 0.040\nall four correct = 2 marks three correct = 1 mark |  | \n(b) | M1 equation 3\nM2 the (mole) ratio of KHCO3 to K2CO3/reactant to product is 2:1 | mark csq on amounts given in part(a) | 2", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["15(a)", "Enthalpy change(of reaction)", "ACCEPT heat(energy) change", "1"], ["(b)", "M1 temperature rise=23.5(℃)\nM2 heat produced=200x4.2x23.5\nM3=20000(J) OR 20kJ unit must be given if answer in kJ", "Penalise use of0.725/200.725/199.275g inM2 only\nACCEPT19740/19700(J)\nACCEPT19.74(0)/19.7(00)kJ\nIGNORE sign\nmark consequentially throughout\ncorrect answer(with no working) scores3", "3"], ["(c)(i)", "(the reaction is) exothermic\nOR\ntransfers heat/thermal energy to the surroundings/gives out heat/thermal energy\nOR\ngives out heat", "ACCEPT loses for gives out\nDO NOT ACCEPT just energy\nACCEPT loses for gives out", "1"], ["(ii)", "incomplete combustion/burning(of the butane)\nOR\n(burns in a) limited supply of oxygen/air", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "less heat(energy)/thermal energy produced\nOR\ntemperature rise less(than expected)", "ACCEPT less heat(energy)/thermal energy transferred to the water\nALLOW soot has absorbed some of the heat(energy)/soot has acted as an insulator", "1"], ["(iv)", "heat/energy is lost to the air/beaker/surroundings/water evaporates", "ALLOW beaker is not insulated/has no lid\nALLOW water is not stirred", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n15(a) | Enthalpy change(of reaction) | ACCEPT heat(energy) change | 1\n(b) | M1 temperature rise=23.5(℃)\nM2 heat produced=200x4.2x23.5\nM3=20000(J) OR 20kJ unit must be given if answer in kJ | Penalise use of0.725/200.725/199.275g inM2 only\nACCEPT19740/19700(J)\nACCEPT19.74(0)/19.7(00)kJ\nIGNORE sign\nmark consequentially throughout\ncorrect answer(with no working) scores3 | 3\n(c)(i) | (the reaction is) exothermic\nOR\ntransfers heat/thermal energy to the surroundings/gives out heat/thermal energy\nOR\ngives out heat | ACCEPT loses for gives out\nDO NOT ACCEPT just energy\nACCEPT loses for gives out | 1\n(ii) | incomplete combustion/burning(of the butane)\nOR\n(burns in a) limited supply of oxygen/air |  | 1\n(iii) | less heat(energy)/thermal energy produced\nOR\ntemperature rise less(than expected) | ACCEPT less heat(energy)/thermal energy transferred to the water\nALLOW soot has absorbed some of the heat(energy)/soot has acted as an insulator | 1\n(iv) | heat/energy is lost to the air/beaker/surroundings/water evaporates | ALLOW beaker is not insulated/has no lid\nALLOW water is not stirred | 1", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["16(a)", "to avoid loss of acid (spray) / solution / liquid\nOR\nonly gas/carbon dioxide can escape", "REJECT to avoid CaCO3/solid escaping", "1"], ["(b)", "carbon dioxide / gas\nAND\nescapes / given off / released", "REJECT incorrectly named gas", "1"], ["(c)(i)", "", "", "2"], ["(ii)", "", "M2 dep on M1\nACCEPT ions\nREJECT atoms / molecules\nACCEPT per unit time / per minute\nACCEPT collision frequency increases\nIGNORE any refs to chance of collisions", "3"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n16(a) | to avoid loss of acid (spray) / solution / liquid\nOR\nonly gas/carbon dioxide can escape | REJECT to avoid CaCO3/solid escaping | 1\n(b) | carbon dioxide / gas\nAND\nescapes / given off / released | REJECT incorrectly named gas | 1\n(c)(i) |  |  | 2\n(ii) |  | M2 dep on M1\nACCEPT ions\nREJECT atoms / molecules\nACCEPT per unit time / per minute\nACCEPT collision frequency increases\nIGNORE any refs to chance of collisions | 3", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "edexcel", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000001", "e000002", "e000003", "e000004", "e000005", "e000006", "e000007", "e000008"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000010"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021", "e000022", "e000023", "e000024", "e000025"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "d5191851-8500-5fd7-a4dc-e13a0833cf4a", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:52:51.397880415Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 189, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 9, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2016", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Science Double Award (4SC0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Level 1/Level 2 Certificate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Biology (KCH0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Science (Double Award) (KSCO) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2016", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH0_1C_1606_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2016", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:11.76633+00');
