ls''\nIgnore more easily separated / easier to break\nif any reference to/implication of breaking covalent or ionic bonds scores 0/2\nM1 and M2 indep"], ["M1 (strong) attraction between bonding/shared pair of electrons", "Do not award M2 if reference to only one nucleus"], ["M2 (and) nuclei of (both atoms)\nOR\nM1 bonding/shared pair of electrons\nM2 (strongly) attracted to nuclei (of both atoms)"], ["", "", "Do not award M2 if reference to only one nucleus", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 a | covalent | Ignore references to polar bonding and electron sharing | 1\nb | M1 weak forces (of attraction) between molecules / weak intermolecular forces | Accept bonds for forces for both M1 and M2\nReject atoms for both M1 and M2 | 2\nM2 (therefore) little (thermal/heat) energy required to overcome the forces / separate the molecules | Accept particles for molecules\nAccept correctly named IMF eg van der Waals''\nIgnore more easily separated / easier to break\nif any reference to/implication of breaking covalent or ionic bonds scores 0/2\nM1 and M2 indep\nM1 (strong) attraction between bonding/shared pair of electrons | Do not award M2 if reference to only one nucleus\nM2 (and) nuclei of (both atoms)\nOR\nM1 bonding/shared pair of electrons\nM2 (strongly) attracted to nuclei (of both atoms)\n |  | Do not award M2 if reference to only one nucleus | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["d", "HxCl", "M1 for 2 electrons shared between one H and one Cl\nM2 rest of molecule fully correct\nM2 DEP on M1\nAccept any combination of dots and crosses\nIgnore inner shells of electrons in chlorine\nif overlapping touching/circles are used both electrons must be within the overlapping/touching area\nsymbols do not need to be shown if overlapping touchi