 answer is D\nA is not correct because zinc is the only metal used to galvanise iron\nB is not correct because zinc is the only metal used to galvanise iron\nC is not correct because zinc is the only metal used to galvanise iron"], ["", "", "Total", "6"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n2(a) | M1 oxygen\nM2 water (vapour) | ACCEPT O2\nIGNORE O\nIGNORE air\nACCEPT moisture\nACCEPT H2O\nIf both name and formula given, mark name only | 2\n(b) |  | Item Method |  | 3\n1\n(c)\nD(zinc)\nThe only correct answer is D\nA is not correct because zinc is the only metal used to galvanise iron\nB is not correct because zinc is the only metal used to galvanise iron\nC is not correct because zinc is the only metal used to galvanise iron\n |  | Total | 6", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(a)", "", "", "4"], ["Separation", "Method"], ["to obtain sand from a mixture of sand and water", "filtration"], ["to separate crude oil into its components", "fractional distillation"], ["to obtain pure water from salt water", "simple distillation"], ["", "to obtain ethanol from a mixture of ethanol and water", "fractional distillation", "", ""], ["(b)(i)", "M1(add to)anhydrous/white copper(II)sulfateM2turns blueORM1add to cobalt(II) chloride paper/cobalt chloride paperM2turns pink", "ACCEPTturns copper(II)sulfate from white to blue for 2 marksACCEPTblue cobalt(II) chlorideALLOWanhydrous cobalt(II) chlorideACCEPTturns cobalt(II) chloride from blue to pink for 2 marksM2DEP onM1or near misse.g. just copper(II)sulfateIGNOREany reference to testing with indicators", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(a) |  |  | 4\nSeparation | Method\nto obtain sand from a mixture of sand and water | filtration\nto separate crude oil into its components | fractional distillation\nto obtain pure water from salt water | simple distillation\n | to obtain ethanol from a mixture of ethanol and water | fractional distillation |  | \n(b)(i) | M1(add to)anhydrous/white copper(II)sulfateM2turns blueORM1add to cobalt(II) chloride paper/cobalt chloride paperM2turns pink | ACCEPTturns copper(II)sulfate from white to blue for 2 marksACCEPTblue cobalt(II) chlorideALLOWanhydrous cobalt(II) chlorideACCEPTturns cobalt(II) chloride from blue to pink for 2 marksM2DEP onM1or near misse.g. just copper(II)sulfateIGNOREany reference to testing with indicators | 2", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(b)(ii)", "M1 measure/determine/test its boiling point", "ACCEPT boil it/heat until it boils", "2"], ["M2 100℃", "it boils at 100℃", ""], ["", "ALLOW its boiling point is 100℃ for 1 mark", ""], ["", "ALLOW heat it and it boils at 100℃ for 2 marks", ""], ["OR", "", ""], ["M1 measure/determine/test its freezing point", "ACCEPT freeze it/cool until it freezes it freezes at 0℃", ""], ["M2 0℃", "ALLOW its freezing point is 0℃ for 1 mark", ""], ["", "ALLOW cool it and it freezes at 0℃ for 2 marks", ""], ["OR", "", ""], ["M1 measure/determine/test its density", "ALLOW its density is 1g/cm3for 1 mark", ""], ["M2 1g/cm3", "M2 DEP on M1 throughout", ""], ["", "", "Total", "8"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(b)(ii) | M1 measure/determine/test its boiling point | ACCEPT boil it/heat until it boils | 2\nM2 100℃ | it boils at 100℃ | \n | ALLOW its boiling point is 100℃ for 1 mark | \n | ALLOW heat it and it boils at 100℃ for 2 marks | \nOR |  | \nM1 measure/determine/test its freezing point | ACCEPT freeze it/cool until it freezes it freezes at 0℃ | \nM2 0℃ | ALLOW its freezing point is 0℃ for 1 mark | \n | ALLOW cool it and it freezes at 0℃ for 2 marks | \nOR |  | \nM1 measure/determine/test its density | ALLOW its density is 1g/cm3for 1 mark | \nM2 1g/cm3 | M2 DEP on M1 throughout | \n |  | Total | 8", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)(i)", "B(the number of protons in an atom)", "", "1"], ["The only correct answer is BA is not correct because atomic number is not the number of neutrons in an atomC is not correct because atomic number is not the number of protons plus the number of electrons in an atomD is not correct because atomic number is not the number of protons plus the number of neutrons in an atom", "", ""], ["(ii)", "C(electrons in the outer shell)", "", "1"], ["", "The only correct answer is CA is not correct because the number of protons does not determine chemical propertiesB is not correct because the number of neutrons does not determine chemical propertiesD is not correct because the number of protons and neutrons does not determine chemical properties", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a)(i) | B(the number of protons in an atom) |  | 1\nThe only correct answer is BA is not correct because atomic number is not the number of neutrons in an atomC is not correct because atomic number is not the number of protons plus the number of electrons in an atomD is not correct because atomic number is not the number of protons plus the number of neutrons in an atom |  | \n(ii) | C(electrons in the outer shell) |  | 1\n | The only correct answer is CA is not correct because the number of protons does not determine chemical propertiesB is not correct because the number of neutrons does not determi