 = 7 4 ]", "latex": "[ M _ {\\mathrm {r}} \\mathrm {o f C a (O H)} _ {2} = 7 4 ]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000221", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 221, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {m i n i u m m a s s o f C a (O H) _ {2}} =", "latex": "\\mathrm {m i n i u m m a s s o f C a (O H) _ {2}} =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000222", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 222, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {F e S O} _ {4}. x \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm {F e S O} _ {4} + x \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O}", "latex": "\\mathrm {F e S O} _ {4}. x \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm {F e S O} _ {4} + x \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O}", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000279", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 279, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {m a s s o f F e S O} _ {4} \\mathrm {f o r m e d} =", "latex": "\\mathrm {m a s s o f F e S O} _ {4} \\mathrm {f o r m e d} =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000285", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 285, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "2f82da9d-2256-5899-9b0c-2139ab00285f", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:53:37.414284232Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 368, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "Instructions", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Use black ink or ball-point pen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Fill in the boxes at the top of this page with your name, centre number and candidate number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer all questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer the questions in the spaces provided", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "there may be more space than you need.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Show all the steps in any calculations and state the units.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Some questions must be answered with a cross in a box. If you change your mind about an answer, put a line through the box and then mark your new answer with a cross.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Information", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The total mark for this paper is 120.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The marks for each question are shown in brackets", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "use this as a guide as to how much time to spend on each question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Advice", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Read each question carefully before you start to answer it.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Write your answers neatly and in good English.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Try to answer every question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Check your answers if you have time at the end.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Turn over", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Answer ALL questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "1 Use the Periodic Table on page 2 to help you answer this question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Give the symbol of the element that has an atomic number of 14.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Give the symbol of the element that has a relative atomic mass of 14.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Give the number of the group that contains the noble gases.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Identify the group whose atoms form ions with a charge of +1. (1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A 1", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B 2", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C 6", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D 7", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) Identify the group whose atoms form ions with a charge of $ - 1 $ (1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A 1", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B 2", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C 6", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D 7", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1 = 5 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "2 The diagram shows the arrangement of particles in the three states of matter. Each circle represents a particle.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "X", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Y", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Z", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Use the letters X, Y and Z to give the starting and finishing states of matter for each of the changes in the table.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The first one has been done for you.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(3)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Which of these changes takes place when solid iodine is heated to form iodine gas?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A crystallisation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000049", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 49, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B evaporation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000050", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 50, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "melting", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000051", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 51, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D sublimation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000052", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 52, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2 = 4 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000053", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 53, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000054", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 54, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "3 A student places a few purple crystals at the bottom of a beaker containing some cold water. The crystals start to dissolve.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000055", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 55, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "( a ) State how the appearance of the crystals and the water change as the crystals dissolve. (2)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000057", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 57, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "crystals...", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000058", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 58, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Which process occurs as the crystals dissolve to form a solution?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000059", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 59, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A condensation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000060", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 60, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B crystallisation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000061", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 61, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "diffusion", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000062", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 62, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D melting", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000063", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 63, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The student repeats the experiment using hot water instead of cold water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000064", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 64, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State how the change in the appearance of the water differs when hot water is used instead of cold water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000065", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 65, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Explain, in terms of particles, why the change differs when hot water is used instead of cold water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000066", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 66, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000067", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 67, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "4 The maximum mass of a solid that dissolves in 100g of water at a given temperature is called its solubility.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000068", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 68, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table gives the solubility of potassium nitrate at six different temperatures.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000069", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 69, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Plot the points on the grid and draw a curve of best fit.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000071", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 71, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Extend your curve to find the solubility of potassium nitrate at $ 1 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000073", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 73, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "solubility = g per 100 g of water", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000074", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 74, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Use your graph to find the maximum mass of potassium nitrate that could dissolve in 50g of water at $ 3 5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000075", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 75, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000076", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 76, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "5 Crude oil is a liquid that contains a mixture of many hydrocarbons.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000077", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 77, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The diagram shows a fractionating column used in the distillation of crude oil.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000078", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 78, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The six fractions obtained are shown. One use for each of four of the fractions is also shown.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000079", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 79, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Describe what is done to the crude oil before it enters the fractionating column.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000081", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 81, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) State how the temperature changes from the top of the column to the bottom.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000082", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 82, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Give a use for gasoline and a use for bitumen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000083", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 83, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "gasoline.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000084", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 84, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "bitumen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000085", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 85, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Name the fraction that contains the largest molecules.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000086", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 86, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) State the physical property that allows the different fractions to be collected at different heights in the column.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000087", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 87, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000088", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 88, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "6 This question is about elements in Groups 1 and 7 of the Periodic Table.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000089", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 89, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The diagram shows two ways in which potassium can be converted into potassium chloride.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000090", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 90, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give the names of gas X, colourless solution Y and acid Z.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000092", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 92, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "gas X.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000093", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 93, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "colourless solution Y.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000094", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 94, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "acid Z.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000095", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 95, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) When sodium is burned in iodine gas, sodium iodide is formed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000096", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 96, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Write a chemical equation for the reaction between sodium and iodine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000097", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 97, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give a test to show that an aqueous solution of sodium iodide contains iodide ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000098", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 98, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "test for iodide ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000099", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 99, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "observation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000100", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 100, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000101", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 101, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "7 Copper pyrites is an ore of copper that contains copper, iron and sulfur.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000102", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 102, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The percentage composition by mass of copper pyrites is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000103", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 103, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Cu 34.60% Fe 30.52% S 34.88%", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000104", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 104, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Show, by calculation, that the empirical formula of copper pyrites is $ \\mathrm{C u F e S_{2}} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000105", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 105, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Copper is obtained from copper pyrites in a two-stage process.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000106", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 106, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Stage 1 Copper pyrites is heated in air.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000107", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 107, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Stage 2 The copper(II) sulfide is separated and then heated in air. It reacts with oxygen to form copper and sulfur dioxide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000109", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 109, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State why the sulfur in the reaction in stage 1 is described as being oxidised.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000110", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 110, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Write a chemical equation for the reaction that occurs in stage 2.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000111", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 111, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Sulfur dioxide dissolves in water to form an acidic solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000112", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 112, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Identify the ion that causes this solution to be acidic.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000113", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 113, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) State how litmus paper can be used to show that the solution is acidic.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000114", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 114, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Give two observations that are made when a piece of magnesium ribbon is added to the acidic solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000115", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 115, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000116", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 116, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "8 In an experiment, a student adds a piece of zinc to some dilute hydrochloric acid in a test tube.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000117", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 117, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The student measures the temperature before adding the zinc.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000119", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 119, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "After adding the zinc, he stirs the mixture and measures the highest temperature reached.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000120", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 120, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The diagram shows his results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000121", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 121, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Use the readings to complete the table, giving all values to the nearest $ 0. 5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000124", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 124, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(2)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000125", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 125, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The student wants to find out if there is a relationship between the reactivity of a metal and the temperature rise.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000127", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 127, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "He repeats the experiment four times, using a different metal each time.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000128", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 128, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows his results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000129", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 129, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State three factors that the student should keep constant in each experiment.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000131", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 131, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Using information from the table, state the relationship between the reactivity of a metal and the temperature rise.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000132", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 132, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) State why there is no temperature rise when gold is added to the acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000133", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 133, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 8 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000134", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 134, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "9 The ions present in ionic compounds can be identified using simple tests.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000135", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 135, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "some cations (positive ions) can be identified using a flame test", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000136", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 136, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "some anions (negative ions) can be identified by observing reactions in solutions of the compounds", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000137", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 137, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Table 1 shows the flame test colours for four cations.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000138", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 138, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Table 1", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000140", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 140, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Table 2 shows the results of three tests used to identify anions in solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000141", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 141, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Table 2", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000143", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 143, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use the information in the tables to answer these questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000144", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 144, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) In the tests, compound X gives a red flame and produces effervescence when hydrochloric acid is added.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000145", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 145, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Suggest two possible identities for compound X.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000146", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 146, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) (i) In the tests, compound Y gives a blue flame and produces a yellow colour when methyl orange is added.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000147", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 147, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A student concludes that compound Y is tantalum hydroxide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000148", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 148, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give two reasons why this conclusion may not be correct.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000149", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 149, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Which additional test from Table 2 would show that the only anion in compound Y is the hydroxide ion?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000150", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 150, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) An aqueous solution contains either carbonate ions or hydrogencarbonate ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000151", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 151, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Using only information from the tables, explain how you could decide if the solution contains carbonate or hydrogencarbonate ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000152", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 152, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 9 = 8 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000153", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 153, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "10 A student uses this apparatus to investigate the heat energy released when nitric acid is added to potassium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000154", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 154, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "She uses this method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000156", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 156, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "put $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of potassium hydroxide solution into the polystyrene cup", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000157", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 157, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "measure the temperature of the potassium hydroxide solution", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000158", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 158, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add 5.00 $ cm^{3} $ of nitric acid from the burette", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000159", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 159, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "stir the mixture and measure the highest temperature reached", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000160", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 160, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add further 5.00 $ cm^{3} $ samples of nitric acid, stir and measure the highest temperature reached after each addition", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000161", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 161, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Name the piece of apparatus that should be used to measure the $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of potassium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000162", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 162, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000163", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 163, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The table shows the student''s results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000164", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 164, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) The result for $ 2 0. 0 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of acid is anomalous.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000166", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 166, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Suggest two possible mistakes, other than misreading the thermometer, that the student might have made to produce the anomalous result.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000167", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 167, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Suggest a true value for the temperature when $ 2 0. 0 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of acid is added.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000168", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 168, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) In another experiment, the student records these results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000169", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 169, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the heat energy released using the equation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000171", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 171, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ Q=\\mathrm{t h e a t e n e r g y r e l e a s e d i n J} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000173", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 173, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ m=\\mathrm{m a s s o f t h e m i t u r e i n g} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000174", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 174, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\Delta T=\\mathrm{c h a n g e i n t e m e r t a r e i n} \\mathrm{^{\\circ} C} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000175", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 175, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "[assume mass of $ 1. 0 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of the mixture is $ 1. 0 0 \\mathrm{g} $]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000176", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 176, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "heat energy released =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000177", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 177, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 10 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000178", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 178, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "11 This question is about titanium and its compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000179", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 179, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Titanium is a metal.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000180", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 180, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The diagram shows the arrangement of the particles in titanium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000181", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 181, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State why metals such as titanium are good conductors of electricity.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000183", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 183, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Explain why metals such as titanium are malleable.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000184", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 184, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Titanium(IV) chloride, $ \\mathrm{T i C l_{4}} $ , and titanium(IV) oxide, $ \\mathrm{T i O_{2}} $ , are both covalent compounds. $ \\mathrm{T i C l_{4}} $ is a liquid at room temperature. $ \\mathrm{T i O_{2}} $ is a solid with a high melting point. Explain these properties in terms of the structures of the two compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000185", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 185, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) (i) A mixture of titanium(IV) oxide and carbon reacts with chlorine to form titanium(IV) chloride and carbon dioxide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000186", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 186, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Write a chemical equation for this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000187", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 187, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Titanium(IV) chloride reacts with magnesium to form titanium and magnesium chloride, $ \\mathrm{M g C l_{2}} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000188", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 188, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Write a chemical equation for this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000189", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 189, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "12 A mixture of carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide and hydrogen is known in industry as synthesis gas.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000190", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 190, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Synthesis gas is converted to methanol, $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} O H} $ , by passing it over a heated solid catalyst.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000191", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 191, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equations for the two reactions are", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000192", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 192, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Assume that both reactions reach a position of equilibrium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000194", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 194, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) For reaction 1, predict whether using a high or a low temperature would produce the higher yield of methanol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000195", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 195, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give a reason for your choice.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000196", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 196, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "prediction reason ...", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000197", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 197, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) For reaction 2, predict whether using a high or a low pressure would produce the higher yield of methanol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000198", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 198, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give a reason for your choice.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000199", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 199, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "prediction reason ...", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000200", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 200, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The catalyst increases the rate of both the forward reaction and the backward reaction. Suggest why the catalyst has no effect on the position of equilibrium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000201", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 201, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Reaction 1 can be represented by a reaction profile diagram.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000202", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 202, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Complete the profile by showing the products of the reaction and the enthalpy change, $ \\Delta H $ , for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000204", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 204, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Draw an arrow on the profile to represent the activation energy for the forward reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000205", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 205, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Label this arrow E.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000206", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 206, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) State the effect, if any, of the catalyst on the enthalpy change for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000207", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 207, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "13 Calcium carbonate decomposes when heated. The equation for the reaction is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000208", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 208, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Calculate the maximum mass of CaO that could be obtained when 20 tonnes of $ \\mathrm{C a C O_{3}} $ is decomposed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000210", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 210, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give the unit.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000211", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 211, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Slaked lime, $ \\mathrm{C a ( O H )_{2}} $ forms when water is added to calcium oxide. Give the chemical name of slaked lime.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000214", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 214, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Slaked lime is often added to soil to raise the pH of the soil.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000215", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 215, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A chemist neutralises $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of $ 0. 5 0 0 \\mathrm{m o l} / \\mathrm{d m}^{3} $ hydrochloric acid with slaked lime.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000216", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 216, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Calculate the amount, in moles, of HCl that is neutralised.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000218", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 218, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Calculate the minimum mass, in grams, of $ \\mathrm{C a ( O H )}_{2} $ required to neutralise the HCl.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000220", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 220, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) A clear solution of slaked lime is made by dissolving $ \\mathrm{C a ( O H )_{2}} $ in an excess of water. This solution is left exposed to air. The solution slowly goes milky as a faint white precipitate forms.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000223", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 223, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain why a faint white precipitate forms.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000224", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 224, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 13 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000225", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 225, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "14 The table shows the displayed formulae of six hydrocarbons, Q, R, S, T, U and V.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000226", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 226, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Which two hydrocarbons will instantly decolourise bromine water?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000228", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 228, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A R and V", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000229", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 229, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B Q and U", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000230", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 230, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C S and T", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000231", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 231, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D Q and T", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000232", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 232, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Which two hydrocarbons have the general formula $ C_{n} H_{2 n+2} $?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000233", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 233, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A R and V", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000234", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 234, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B Q and U", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000235", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 235, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C S and T", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000236", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 236, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D Q and T", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000237", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 237, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Which hydrocarbon is an isomer of U?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000238", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 238, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A Q", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000239", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 239, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B R", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000240", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 240, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C T", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000241", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 241, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D V", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000242", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 242, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000243", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 243, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Which two hydrocarbons have the empirical formula $ \\mathrm{C H_{2}}? $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000244", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 244, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A R and V", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000245", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 245, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B Q and S", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000246", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 246, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C Rand S", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000247", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 247, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D T and U", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000248", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 248, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) The substitution reaction between hydrocarbon T and bromine is similar to the reaction between methane and bromine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000249", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 249, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State a condition, other than temperature, that is required for this reaction to take place.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000250", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 250, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Suggest a displayed formula for a possible organic product of the reaction between hydrocarbon T and bromine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000251", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 251, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 14 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000252", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 252, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "15 The flow diagram shows the main stages in an industrial process to manufacture ammonia.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000253", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 253, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Give the name of this industrial process.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000255", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 255, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Identify gases A and B.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000256", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 256, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "gas B.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000257", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 257, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) State the purpose of the condenser.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000258", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 258, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Name the catalyst that is used in the reactor.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000259", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 259, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) Suggest two reasons why the unreacted gases are recycled.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000260", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 260, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(f) The reaction to make ammonia is reversible and can reach a position of equilibrium. The graph shows the percentage yield of ammonia at equilibrium, and at different temperatures and pressures.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000261", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 261, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Percentage yield of ammonia at equilibrium (%)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000262", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 262, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State the conditions of temperature and pressure that would produce the largest percentage yield of ammonia.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000264", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 264, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Find the percentage yield of ammonia at equilibrium, at a pressure of 200 atmospheres and a temperature of $ 4 5 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000265", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 265, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Suggest why, in the industrial process, the percentage yield of ammonia at 200 atmospheres and $ 4 5 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ is only 15%.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000266", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 266, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "16 The mineral rozenite contains crystals of hydrated iron(II) sulfate, $ \\mathrm{F e S O_{4}. x H_{2} O} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000267", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 267, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A student wants to find the value of x.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000268", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 268, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "She uses this apparatus to remove and collect the water of crystallisation from a sample of iron(II) sulfate crystals.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000269", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 269, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "She uses this method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000271", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 271, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "weigh empty tube A to find its mass", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000272", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 272, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "place a sample of hydrated iron(II) sulfate crystals into tube A and reweigh", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000273", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 273, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "heat tube A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000274", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 274, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "allow tube A to cool and reweigh", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000275", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 275, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "repeat the process until the mass no longer changes", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000276", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 276, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Heating until the mass no longer changes is known as heating to constant mass.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000277", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 277, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "When iron(II) sulfate crystals are heated gently, they decompose according to this equation.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000278", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 278, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "These are the student''s results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000280", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 280, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) State why it is necessary to heat the crystals to constant mass.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000282", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 282, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000283", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 283, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) (i) Calculate the mass of $ \\mathrm{F e S O_{4}} $ formed after heating to constant mass.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000284", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 284, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Calculate the mass of water collected in tube B after heating to constant mass.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000286", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 286, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Calculate the value for x in the formula $ \\mathrm{F e S O_{4}. x H_{2} O} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000287", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 287, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give your answer to the nearest whole number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000288", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 288, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ [ M_{r} $ of $ \\mathrm{F e S O_{4}}=1 5 2; M_{r} $ of $ \\mathrm{H_{2} O}=1 8] $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000289", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 289, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) When the student adds the water from tube B to anhydrous copper(II) sulfate, she observes that the mixture gets hot and that there is a colour change from white to blue.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000290", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 290, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain these observations.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000291", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 291, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 16 = 8 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000292", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 292, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "TOTAL FOR PAPER = 120 MARKS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000293", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 293, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000294", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 294, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:56.352477+00');
