d to gain one electron to have a full outer shell", "1"], ["", "ALLOW all their electron configurations end with 7", ""], ["(c)(i)", "Cl2+2NaBr→2NaCl+Br2", "ALLOW fractions/multiples", "1"], ["orange", "IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", ""], ["M1 no reaction as bromine less reactive than chlorine ORA", "", "1"], ["M2 so bromine cannot displace chlorine", "Penalise incorrect use of chloride once only", ""], ["(iv)", "M1 iodide(ions)/I-lose electrons so oxidised", "REJECT reference to iodine instead of iodide", "2"], ["M2 chlorine/Cl2 gains electrons so reduced", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a)(i) | the greater the relative atomic mass the higher the boiling point ORA | ALLOW positive correlation | 1\ndo not (easily) gain/lose/share electrons | ALLOW full outer shell/energy level (of electrons) | 1\n(b) | all have seven/same number of electrons in outer/valence shell/outer energy level | ALLOW all need to gain one electron to have a full outer shell | 1\n | ALLOW all their electron configurations end with 7 | \n(c)(i) | Cl2+2NaBr→2NaCl+Br2 | ALLOW fractions/multiples | 1\norange | IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | \nM1 no reaction as bromine less reactive than chlorine ORA |  | 1\nM2 so bromine cannot displace chlorine | Penalise incorrect use of chloride once only | \n(iv) | M1 iodide(ions)/I-lose electrons so oxidised | REJECT reference to iodine instead of iodide | 2\nM2 chlorine/Cl2 gains electrons so reduced |  | ", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "OR\nM1 iodide(ions)/I-oxidised and chlorine/Cl2reduced\nM2 iodide(ions)/I-lose electrons and chlorine/Cl2gains electrons\nIf incorrect reference to iodine in either or both M1 and M2 MAX 1 mark\nIGNORE both oxidation and reduction occur(in the same reaction)", ""], ["7(d)(i)", "H2+Cl2→2HCl", "ALLOW fractions/multiples\nIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1(beaker A) litmus stays blue/no change to litmus\nM2 hydrogen chloride does not ionise/does not formH+ions/remains as molecules/does not form hydrochloric acid", "ALLOW litmus turns blue\nALLOW does not dissociate\nNo M1 if references to methylbenzene/solution being alkaline or methylbenzene reacting", "4"], ["", "M3(beaker B) litmus turns red\nM4(hydrogen chloride forms) hydrogen ions/H+ions/hydrochloric acid(forms)", "REJECT litmus paper turns red and then bleaches\nIGNORE acidic solution/acid forms", ""]], "text": " | OR\nM1 iodide(ions)/I-oxidised and chlorine/Cl2reduced\nM2 iodide(ions)/I-lose electrons and chlorine/Cl2gains electrons\nIf incorrect reference to iodine in either or both M1 and M2 MAX 1 mark\nIGNORE both oxidation and reduction occur(in the same reaction) | \n7(d)(i) | H2+Cl2→2HCl | ALLOW fractions/multiples\nIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | 1\n(ii) | M1(beaker A) litmus stays blue/no change to litmus\nM2 hydrogen chloride does not ionise/does not formH+ions/remains as molecules/does not form hydrochloric acid | ALLOW litmus turns blue\nALLOW does not dissociate\nNo M1 if references to methylbenzene/solution being alkaline or methylbenzene reacting | 4\n | M3(beaker B) litmus turns red\nM4(hydrogen chloride forms) hydrogen ions/H+ions/hydrochloric acid(forms) | REJECT litmus paper turns red and then bleaches\nIGNORE acidic solution/acid forms | ", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 3, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(a)(i)", "M1 not making a valid conclusion because could also be zinc or aluminium ions/could be any of the three ions", "ACCEPT zinc and aluminium also/all three ions form white precipitates", "2"], ["M2 because not seen effect of adding excess sodium hydroxide OWTTE", "", "2"], ["M1 flame (test)", "ALLOW description of flame test\nIGNORE burn it/heat it\nIGNORE red or orange alone\nM2 dep on M1 or mention of flame in M2", ""], ["(b)(i)", "M1 reheat/heat again (and reweigh)", "Heat to constant mass scores M1 and M2", "2"], ["M2 until constant mass (achieved)", "", "4"], ["(ii)", "M1 mass(H2O)=(6.1-5.2)=0.9(g)", "", ""], ["M2n(AB2)=5.2÷208\nAND\nn(H2O)=0.9÷18", "", ""], ["M3 ratio of AB2to H2O is0.025:0.05:1:2\nM4x=2", "M3 subsumes M2\naccept AB2.2H2O", ""], ["8(c)", "M1 add nitric acid/HNO3", "If incorrect acid or an alkali added then M2 and M3 can be scored", "3"], ["M2 add silver nitrate(solution)/AgNO3", "", ""], ["M3 white precipitate forms", "M3 dep on addition of silver nitrate", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(a)(i) | M1 not making a valid conclusion because could also be zinc or aluminium ions/could be any of the three ions | ACCEPT zinc and aluminium also/all three ions form white precipitates | 2\nM2 because not seen effect of adding excess sodium hydroxide OWTTE |  | 2\nM1 flame (test) | ALLOW description of flame test\nIGNORE burn it/heat it\nIGNORE red or orange alone\nM2 dep on M1 or mention of flame in M2 | \n(b)(i) | M1 reheat/heat again (and reweigh) | Heat to constant mass scores M1 and M2 | 2\nM2 until constant mass (achieved) |  | 4\n(ii) | M1 mass(H2O)=(6.1-5.2)=0.9(g) |  | \nM2n(AB2)=5.2÷208\nAND\nn(H2O)=0.9÷18 |  | \nM3 ratio of AB2to H2O is0.025:0.05:1:2\nM4x=2 | M3 subsumes M2\naccept AB2.2H2O | \n8(c) | M1 add nitric acid/HNO3 | If incorrect acid or an alkali added then M2 and M3 can be scored | 3\nM2 add silver nitrate(solution)/AgNO3 |  | \nM3 white precipitate forms | M3 dep on addition of silver nitrate | ", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "", "If any other incorrect reagent added e.g. barium chloride then only M1 can be scored", ""], ["(d) clip(ii)", "[208-(2x35.5)=]137", "", "1"], ["A is barium/Ba", "ALLOW Ba2+ALLOW ECF from an incorrect calculation if answer is a group 2 metal or d block metal", "1"]], "text": " |  | If any other incorrect reagent added e.g. barium chloride then only M1 can be scored | \n(d) clip(ii) | [208-(2x35.5)=]137 |  | 1\nA is barium/Ba | ALLOW Ba2+ALLOW ECF from an incorrect calculation if answer is a group 2 metal or d block metal | 1", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(a)(i)", "haematite", "ACCEPT any correct ore of iron e.g. magnetite", "1"], ["(ii)M1 to provide oxygen/O2", "IGNORE name of/formula of iron oxide in any oxidation state", ""], ["ALLOW to form CO/CO2", "2"], ["(iii)2Fe2O3+3C→4Fe+3CO2", "ALLOW fractions/multiples", "1"], ["(iv)M1 limestone/calcium carbonate decomposes to form CaO", "ACCEPT CaCO3→CaO+CO2", "3"], ["M2 calcium oxide/CaO reacts with silica/SiO2/sandM3 to form (molten) slag/calcium silicate", "CaO+SiO2→CaSiO3scores M2 and M3", ""], [""], ["1"], ["(b)(i)Aluminium is more reactive than carbon/higher in the reactivity series than carbon ORA", "", "", "1"], ["(ii)Any 4 fromM1(aluminium extracted by) electrolysisM2(aluminium oxide) mixed with/added to cryoliteM3(electrolyte) moltenM4 carbon/graphite electrodes(used)M5 aluminium ions discharged/aluminium formed at negative electrode/cathode", "", "", "4"], ["", "ACCEPT Al3++3e-→Al", ""], ["", "", ""], ["", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(a)(i) | haematite | ACCEPT any correct ore of iron e.g. magnetite | 1\n(ii)M1 to provide oxygen/O2 | IGNORE name of/formula of iron oxide in any oxidation state | \nALLOW to form CO/CO2 | 2\n(iii)2Fe2O3+3C→4Fe+3CO2 | ALLOW fractions/multiples | 1\n(iv)M1 limestone/calcium carbonate decomposes to form CaO | ACCEPT CaCO3→CaO+CO2 | 3\nM2 calcium oxide/CaO reacts with silica/SiO2/sandM3 to form (molten) slag/calcium silicate | CaO+SiO2→CaSiO3scores M2 and M3 | \n\n1\n(b)(i)Aluminium is more reactive than carbon/higher in the reactivity series than carbon ORA |  |  | 1\n(ii)Any 4 fromM1(aluminium extracted by) electrolysisM2(aluminium oxide) mixed with/added to cryoliteM3(electrolyte) moltenM4 carbon/graphite electrodes(used)M5 aluminium ions discharged/aluminium formed at negative electrode/cathode |  |  | 4\n | ACCEPT Al3++3e-→Al | \n |  | \n |  | ", "row_count": 14, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10", "(a)(i)", "swirl flask", "ALLOW shake/swish", "1"], ["IGNORE stir"], ["(ii)", "Ticks under 23.15 22.95 and 23.10", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "M1(23.15+22.95+23.10)÷3M223.07", "correct final answer with no working scores2", "2"], ["If no results ticked in(ii),then only use of two or three concordant titres can score in(iii)"], ["If only one result ticked,M2 can be scored for correctly averaging2 or more titre values."], ["", "M1 CQ on results tickedM2 CQ on correct calculation fromM1Answer toM2 must be correct to2dp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 | (a)(i) | swirl flask | ALLOW shake/swish | 1\nIGNORE stir\n(ii) | Ticks under 23.15 22.95 and 23.10 |  | 1\n(iii) | M1(23.15+22.95+23.10)÷3M223.07 | correct final answer with no working scores2 | 2\nIf no results ticked in(ii),then only use of two or three concordant titres can score in(iii)\nIf only one result ticked,M2 can be scored for correctly averaging2 or more titre values.\n | M1 CQ on results tickedM2 CQ on correct calculation fromM1Answer toM2 must be correct to2dp", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10(b)(i)", "M1 0.02270 x 0.080", "do not penalise missing trailing zeros", "2"], ["OR 22.70x0.0801000", "", ""], ["M2 0.001816/1.816x10-3(mol)", "0.002 scores 1 mark onlyACCEPT 1.816 for 1 markCorrect answer without working scores 2", ""], ["(ii)M2 from(i)x2/0.003632/3.632x10-3(mol)", "", "1"], ["(iii)M1 answer from(ii)÷0.025/0.003632÷0.025", "", "2"], ["ORM1 answer from(ii)x100025", "", ""], ["M2 0.14528/1.4528x10-1(mol/dm3)", "ALLOW ECF only if division by 25 aloneACCEPT any number of sig fig except oneCorrect answer without working scores 2", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10(b)(i) | M1 0.02270 x 0.080 | do not penalise missing trailing zeros | 2\nOR 22.70x0.0801000 |  | \nM2 0.001816/1.816x10-3(mol) | 0.002 scores 1 mark onlyACCEPT 1.816 for 1 markCorrect answer without working scores 2 | \n(ii)M2 from(i)x2/0.003632/3.632x10-3(mol) |  | 1\n(iii)M1 answer from(ii)÷0.025/0.003632÷0.025 |  | 2\nORM1 answer from(ii)x100025 |  | \nM2 0.14528/1.4528x10-1(mol/dm3) | ALLOW ECF only if division by 25 aloneACCEPT any number of sig fig except oneCorrect answer without working scores 2 | ", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10(c)", "M1 heat/boil until crystals form in a sample of solution that has been removed or cooled OWTTE", "ACCEPT heat/boil to produce a (hot) saturated/concentrated solution", "4"], ["", "ACCEPT heat/boil until crystals start to form"], ["", "ALLOW heat/boil to crystallisation point"], ["", "ALLOW (heat/boil to) evaporate some of the water"], ["", "IGNORE references to filtering before heating"], ["M2 cool/leave (the solution) until crystals form", "M2 DEP on M1"], ["M3 filter (to obtain the crystals)", "M3 DEP on crystals having been formed"], ["", "ACCEPT decant/pour off the liquid/(excess) solution"], ["", "IGNORE references to washing crystals"], ["M4 suitable method of drying the crystals", "e.g. place in (warm) oven / leave to dry (in warm place) / use filter paper / kitchen towel"], ["", "REJECT any reference to heating directly with a flame eg Bunsen", ""], ["", "", "If solution heated to dryness or left to evaporate all of the water only 1 mark can be awarded.", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10(c) | M1 heat/boil until crystals form in a sample of solution that has been removed or cooled OWTTE | ACCEPT heat/boil to produce a (hot) saturated/concentrated solution | 4\n | ACCEPT heat/boil until crystals start to form\n | ALLOW heat/boil to crystallisation point\n | ALLOW (heat/boil to) evaporate some of the water\n | IGNORE references to filtering before heating\nM2 cool/leave (the solution) until crystals form | M2 DEP on M1\nM3 filter (to obtain the crystals) | M3 DEP on crystals having been formed\n | ACCEPT decant/pour off the liquid/(excess) solution\n | IGNORE references to washing crystals\nM4 suitable method of drying the crystals | e.g. place in (warm) oven / leave to dry (in warm place) / use filter paper / kitchen towel\n | REJECT any reference to heating directly with a flame eg Bunsen | \n |  | If solution heated to dryness or left to evaporate all of the water only 1 mark can be awarded. | ", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000007"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000020", "e000022", "e000025", "e000028", "e000031", "e000034", "e000037", "e000040", "e000045"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "e95774df-fe5d-5bf3-8be6-3b14888a7c31", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:54:19.208023204Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 75, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2019", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "In Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2019 Publications Code 4CH0_1C_1901_MS All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2019", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 1 = 6 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 2 = 9 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 3 = 15 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 4 = 11 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 5 = 10 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 6=15 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 7 = 14 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 8 = 15 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 10 = 13 mark", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:54:39.574388+00');
