g OWTTE"], ["IGNORE references to leaving for a specified length of time"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3 a | A description/diagram which makes reference to the following points | ALLOW water for solvent throughout | 4\nM1 put (separate) spots of each of the inks on the (pencil) line. OWTTE | If diagram shows solvent above pencil line only M1 and M2 can be scored\nM2 pour some solvent into the bottom of the beaker OWTTE | \nM3 place the paper in the beaker so that the spots are (just) above the level of the solvent OWTTE | DO NOT ALLOW M3 if words and diagram contradict each other\nM4 leave until the solvent has risen up the paper (to the top/near the top and then take paper out) OWTTE | ALLOW leave until inks stopped separating OWTTE\nALLOW leave until spots/dyes stopped moving OWTTE\nIGNORE references to leaving for a specified length of time", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3b", "An explanation which links the following two points", "", ""], ["M1 ink would/might dissolve in the solvent OR pencil would not dissolve in the solvent", "ALLOW water for solvent", ""], ["M2 ink would interfere with/contaminate the results OWTTE", "ALLOW would produce spots/other colours/get mixed up with inks/move up the paper OWTTE", ""], ["OR", "IGNORE smudge/run", ""], ["pencil would not interfere with/contaminate the results OWTTE", "ALLOW pencil would not produce spots/not produce other colours/not get mixed up with the inks/not move up the paper OWTTE", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3b | An explanation which links the following two points |  | \nM1 ink would/might dissolve in the solvent OR pencil would not dissolve in the solvent | ALLOW water for solvent | \nM2 ink 