s one spot and cannot tell about V (as it does not move/is insoluble) | 2\nM2 as they both only form one spot (on the paper)\n |  |  | ACCEPT reference to the other inks/X, Y, Z form more than one spot\nM2 DEP on M1 | ", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3 d", "Working or equation for Rf valueCalculating the Rf valueGiving the answer to 2 significant figures", "", "3"], ["M1 4.36.5", "Award one mark if correct equation for finding Rf value seen", ""], ["M2 0.6615", "ACCEPT any number of sig fig", ""], ["M3 0.66", "must be 2 sig fig", ""], ["0.66 with no working scores 3correct answer given to 3 or more sig fig with no working scores 2M3 subsumes M2can score M2 and M3ECF provided use 4.3 and 6.5 and do a division", ""], ["", "Total15"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3 d | Working or equation for Rf valueCalculating the Rf valueGiving the answer to 2 significant figures |  | 3\nM1 4.36.5 | Award one mark if correct equation for finding Rf value seen | \nM2 0.6615 | ACCEPT any number of sig fig | \nM3 0.66 | must be 2 sig fig | \n0.66 with no working scores 3correct answer given to 3 or more sig fig with no working scores 2M3 subsumes M2can score M2 and M3ECF provided use 4.3 and 6.5 and do a division | \n | Total15", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4 a", "M1(a compound containing the elements/atoms) hydrogen and carbon", "ALLOW molecule/substance for compound", "2"], ["", "REJECT element/atom/mixture for compound"], ["M2 only", "REJECT ions/molecules for elements/atoms"], ["b(i)", "C5H12+8O2→5CO2+6H2O", "ACCEPT other equivalent words eg solely", "2"], ["M1 all formulae correct", "ALLOW fractions/multiples"], ["M2 balancing of correct formulae", "IGNORE state symbols"], ["(ii)", "Any two from", "", "2"], ["M1 carbon monoxide", "ACCEPT correct formulae/symbol"], ["M2 carbon", "ALLOW soot for carbon"], ["(iii)", "reduces/limits capacity of blood to transport oxygen OWTTE", "ACCEPT prevents blood from carrying oxygen OWTTE", "1"], ["", "ACCEPT correct references to haemoglobin eg prevents haemoglobin from carrying oxygen"], ["M1", "", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4 a | M1(a compound containing the elements/atoms) hydrogen and carbon | ALLOW molecule/substance for compound | 2\n | REJECT element/atom/mixture for compound\nM2 only | REJECT ions/molecules for elements/atoms\nb(i) | C5H12+8O2→5CO2+6H2O | ACCEPT other equivalent words eg solely | 2\nM1 all formulae correct | ALLOW fractions/multiples\nM2 balancing of correct formulae | IGNORE state symbols\n(ii) | Any two from |  | 2\nM1 carbon monoxide | ACCEPT correct formulae/symbol\nM2 carbon | ALLOW soot for carbon\n(iii) | reduces/limits capacity of blood to transport oxygen OWTTE | ACCEPT prevents blood from carrying oxygen OWTTE | 1\n | ACCEPT correct references to haemoglobin eg prevents haemoglobin from carrying oxygen\nM1 |  | 2", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["b(iv)", "Chemical structure of b(iv)", "", ""], ["", "M2\nChemical structure of M2", "in either order", ""], ["c(i)(ii)(iii)", "CnH2n\n(contains a carbon to carbon) double bond", "ALLOW (contains a carbon to carbon) multiple bond", "1"], ["A description linking the following two points", "", "1"], ["M1 add bromine water/solutionM2 (bro