up the reaction OWTTE", "IGNORE references to equilibrium", "1"], ["(b)", "$2\\text{NO}+\\text{O}_{2}\\rightarrow 2\\text{NO}_{2}$", "IGNORE references to lowering the activation energy", "1"], ["(c)(i)", "calculate $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{NO}_{2}$ and $\\text{HNO}_{3}$calculate the amount, in moles, of $\\text{NO}_{2}$calculate the amount, in moles, of $\\text{HNO}_{3}$calculate the mass in tonnes of $\\text{HNO}_{3}$Example calculationM1 $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{NO}_{2}=46$ $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{HNO}_{3}=63$M2 $n(\\text{NO}_{2})=11.5\\times 10^{6}\\div 46$ OR 250 000 (mol)M3 $n(\\text{HNO}_{3})=\\frac{2\\times 250000}{3}$ OR 167 000 / 170 000ALLOW working in megamoles i.e. 11.5÷46 OR 0.25ALLOW ECF from incorrect Mr of $\\text{NO}_{2}$calculator answer 166666.66ALLOW working in megamoles i.e. $\\frac{2\\times 0.25}{3}$ OR 0.167 / 0.17ALLOW ECF from M2M4 (167 000 x 63 g)=10.5 (tonnes)10.5 (tonnes) with no working scores 4ACCEPT 10.7 (if 170 000 used)ALLOW ECF from M3ALLOW ECF from incorrect $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{HNO}_{3}$can be (re)used in stage 2 / to make more nitrogen dioxide (in stage 2) / can be used to make more nitric acidIGNORE can be recycled/reused unless qualified", "4"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10(a)(i) | $4\\text{NH}_{3}+5\\text{O}_{2}\\rightleftharpoons 4\\text{NO}+6\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}$ | ACCEPT multiples and fractions | 1\n(ii) | reversible (reaction) | ACCEPT reaction that goes both ways / both forwards and backwards reactions occur | \n(iii) | to increase the rate of the reaction / to speed up the reaction OWTTE | IGNORE references to equilibrium | 1\n(b) | $2\\text{NO}+\\text{O}_{2}\\rightarrow 2\\text{NO}_{2}$ | IGNORE references to lowering the activation energy | 1\n(c)(i) | calculate $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{NO}_{2}$ and $\\text{HNO}_{3}$calculate the amount, in moles, of $\\text{NO}_{2}$calculate the amount, in moles, of $\\text{HNO}_{3}$calculate the mass in tonnes of $\\text{HNO}_{3}$Example calculationM1 $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{NO}_{2}=46$ $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{HNO}_{3}=63$M2 $n(\\text{NO}_{2})=11.5\\times 10^{6}\\div 46$ OR 250 000 (mol)M3 $n(\\text{HNO}_{3})=\\frac{2\\times 250000}{3}$ OR 167 000 / 170 000ALLOW working in megamoles i.e. 11.5÷46 OR 0.25ALLOW ECF from incorrect Mr of $\\text{NO}_{2}$calculator answer 166666.66ALLOW working in megamoles i.e. $\\frac{2\\times 0.25}{3}$ OR 0.167 / 0.17ALLOW ECF from M2M4 (167 000 x 63 g)=10.5 (tonnes)10.5 (tonnes) with no working scores 4ACCEPT 10.7 (if 170 000 used)ALLOW ECF from M3ALLOW ECF from incorrect $M_{\\mathrm{r}}$ of $\\text{HNO}_{3}$can be (re)used in stage 2 / to make more nitrogen dioxide (in stage 2) / can be used to make more nitric acidIGNORE can be recycled/reused unless qualified | 4", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10(d)", "calculate the amount, in moles, of copper(II) nitratecalculate the theoretical yield, in moles, of copper(II) nitratecalculate the percentage yieldExample calculationM1nCu(NO3)2formed=15.3÷187.5OR0.0816M2theoreticalnCu(NO3)2=0.200÷2OR0.100M3(% yield)=(0.0816x100)/(0.100)81.6(%)40.8 scores2Alternative methodcalculate the theoretical yield, in moles, of copper(II) nitratecalculate the theoretical mass of copper nitrate that should be formedcalculate the percentage yieldExample calculationM1theoreticalnCu(NO3)2=0.200÷2OR0.100M2theoretical mass of copper nitrate=0.1x187.5=18.75M3(% yield)=(15.3/18.75)x100=81.6(%)81.6(%) with no working scores3 marksTotal12", "ALLOW0.0823ACCEPT82(%)Mark M3 CSQ on M1and M240.8 scores2ALLOW18.8ACCEPT82(%)Mark M3 CSQ on M1and M240.8 scores281.6(%) with no working scores3 marks", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10(d) | calculate the amount, in moles, of copper(II) nitratecalculate the theoretical yield, in moles, of copper(II) nitratecalculate the percentage yieldExample calculationM1nCu(NO3)2formed=15.3÷187.5OR0.0816M2theoreticalnCu(NO3)2=0.200÷2OR0.100M3(% yield)=(0.0816x100)/(0.100)81.6(%)40.8 scores2Alternative methodcalculate the theoretical yield, in moles, of copper(II) nitratecalculate the theoretical mass of copper nitrate that should be formedcalculate the percentage yieldExample calculationM1theoreticalnCu(NO3)2=0.200÷2OR0.100M2theoretical mass of copper nitrate=0.1x187.5=18.75M3(% yield)=(15.3/18.75)x100=81.6(%)81.6(%) with no working scores3 marksTotal12 | ALLOW0.0823ACCEPT82(%)Mark M3 CSQ on M1and M240.8 scores2ALLOW18.8ACCEPT82(%)Mark M3 CSQ on M1and M240.8 scores281.6(%) with no working scores3 marks | ", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000002", "e000003"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000005"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000007", "e000008"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "e00b7ce5-edd6-5241-bf38-037bbb19f88e", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:54:21.555631562Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 110, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2020 Publications Code 4CH1_1C_msc_2020305 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:54:40.361231+00');
