sium | 1\n(ii) | He | ACCEPT helium | 1\n(iii) | Br | ACCEPT bromine\nREJECT bromide | 1\n(iv) | Na and Cl | ACCEPT sodium and chlorine\nREJECT chloride | 1\n(b) | 2.8.1 | ACCEPT 2,8,1 or 281\nALLOW diagram of atom showing correct electron configuration. | 1\nTotal 5", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(a)", "molecular formula", "C3H6", "ACCEPT propyleneACCEPT N or other letters e.g. x", "4"], ["name of this alkene", "propene"], ["empirical formula", "CH2"], ["general formula", "CnH2n", "ACCEPT multiple bondREJECT bromineREJECT bromideALLOW turns colourlessIGNORE clearM2 dep M1 or near miss", "12"], ["displayed formula", "H H HI I IH-C=C-C-HI"], ["b)i)", "1 mark for each correct answer(contains a carbon carbon) double bond", "1"], ["ii)", "M1 add bromine waterM2 decolourises/changes to colourless", "2"], ["(c)i)", "CH4+Cl2→CH3Cl+HCl", "ACCEPT multiples", "1"], ["(ii)", "D SubstitutionA is incorrect as it is not an addition reactionB is incorrect as it is not a decomposition reactionC is incorrect as it is not a neutralisation reaction", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "Ultraviolet radiation/light", "ACCEPT UV/ultraviolet rays", "1"], ["(d)i)", "M1(isomers have) the same molecular formulaM2(but) different structural/displayed formulae", "ALLOW different structuresALLOW different arrangement of atoms", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(a) | molecular formula | C3H6 | ACCEPT propyleneACCEPT N or other letters e.g. x | 4\nname of this alkene | propene\nempirical formula | CH2\ngeneral formula | CnH2n | ACCEPT multiple bondREJECT bromineREJECT bromideALLOW turns colourlessIGNORE clearM2 dep M1 or near miss | 12\ndisplayed formula | H H HI I IH-C=C-C-HI\nb)i) | 1 mark for each correct answer(contains a carbon carbon) double bond | 1\nii) | M1 add bromine waterM2 decolourises/changes to colourless | 2\n(c)i) | CH4+Cl2→CH3Cl+HCl | ACCEPT multiples | 1\n(ii) | D SubstitutionA is incorrect as it is not an addition reactionB is incorrect as it is not a decomposition reactionC is incorrect as it is not a neutralisation reaction |  | 1\n(iii) | Ultraviolet radiation/light | ACCEPT UV/ultraviolet rays | 1\n(d)i) | M1(isomers have) the same molecular formulaM2(but) different structural/displayed formulae | ALLOW different structuresALLOW different arrangement of atoms | 2", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "M1", "H H\n| | |\nH-C-C-H\n| | |\nCl Cl", "2"], ["M2", "Cl H\n| | |\nH-C-C-H\n| | |\nCl H", "Total\n14"]], "text": "(ii) | M1 | H H\n| | |\nH-C-C-H\n| | |\nCl Cl | 2\nM2 | Cl H\n| | |\nH-C-C-H\n| | |\nCl H | Total\n14", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4", "(a)", "2H2O2→2H2O+(1)O2", "ALLOW multiples and fractions", "1"], ["(b)", "Relights a glowing splint/spill", "", "1"], ["(c)", "Speeds up/increases rate of the reaction", "IGNORE references to lowering activation energy", "1"], ["(d)", "(i)", "All points plotted correctly", "ALLOW ± half a square", "1"], ["(ii)", "Point at 8 minutes circled", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "Smooth curve of best fit", "", "1"], ["(iv)", "took the reading too soon/before 8 minutes", "ACCEPT misread the volume(of oxygen)", "1"], ["(v)", "M1 vertical line on graph drawn to curve from 3 mins", "", "2"], ["M2 value obtained from candidate''s graph", "Expected value 29 or 30cm3ALLOW ± half a square", ""]], "text": " | Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4 | (a) | 2H2O2→2H2O+(1)O2 | ALLOW multiples and fractions | 1\n(b) | Relights a glowing splint/spill |  | 1\n(c) | Speeds up/increases rate of the reaction | IGNORE references to lowering activation energy | 1\n(d) | (i) | All points plotted correctly | ALLOW ± half a square | 1\n(ii) | Point at 8 minutes circled |  | 1\n(iii) | Smooth curve of best fit |  | 1\n(iv) | took the reading too soon/before 8 minutes | ACCEPT misread the volume(of oxygen) | 1\n(v) | M1 vertical line on graph drawn to curve from 3 mins |  | 2\nM2 value obtained from candidate''s graph | Expected value 29 or 30cm3ALLOW ± half a square | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4", "(e)(i)", "M1 curve drawn on graph that is less steep than curve of student''s results.", "", "2"], ["M2 curve levels off at 40cm3", "ALLOW±halfa square", ""], ["(ii)", "An explanation that links the following three points", "", "3"], ["M1 reaction is slower", "ACCEPT particles are further apart / less crowded", ""], ["M2 fewer particles/molecules (in the same volume)", "ACCEPT less frequent collisions\nIGNORE less chance of a collision", ""], ["M3 fewer collisions per unit time", "", "Total 14"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4 | (e)(i) | M1 curve drawn on graph that is less steep than curve of student''s results. |  | 2\nM2 curve levels off at 40cm3 | ALLOW±halfa square | \n(ii) | An explanation that links the following three points |  | 3\nM1 reaction is slower | ACCEPT particles are further apart / less crowded | \nM2 fewer particles/molecules (in the same volume) | ACCEPT less frequent collisions\nIGNORE less chance of a collision | \n