ng scores179.98 or 80 with no working scores2", "3"], ["(ii)", "same electron configuration", "ALLOW same(total)number of electronsIGNORE same number of electrons in the outer shellIGNORE references to same number of protons", "1"], ["(c)(i)", "An explanation that links the following three pointsM1 the order of reactivity is chlorine(most), bromine and iodine(least)M2 chlorine(is most reactive because it) displaces bromine and iodine/oxidises bromide and iodide(ions)/reacts with sodium bromide and sodium iodideM3 bromine(is less reactive than chlorine since it) only displaces iodine/only oxidises iodide(ions)/only reacts with sodium iodide", "ACCEPT bromine is only displaced by chlorine and iodine is displaced by chlorine and bromine scoresM2 and M3ALLOW chlorine has two reactions,bromine has one reaction and iodine no reactions for1 mark out of M2 and M3Deduct1 mark forincorrect use of ine", "3"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(a) | M1 solidM2 dark grey/black |  | 2\n(b)(i) | Example calculationM1(51×79)+(49×81)OR7998M27998÷100M380.0 | 80.0 with no working scores379.9 with no working scores179.98 or 80 with no working scores2 | 3\n(ii) | same electron configuration | ALLOW same(total)number of electronsIGNORE same number of electrons in the outer shellIGNORE references to same number of protons | 1\n(c)(i) | An explanation that links the following three pointsM1 the order of reactivity is chlorine(most), bromine and iodine(least)M2 chlorine(is most reactive because it) displaces bromine and iodine/oxidises bromide and iodide(ions)/reacts with sodium bromide and sodium iodideM3 bromine(is less reactive than chlorine since it) only displaces iodine/only oxidises iodide(ions)/only reacts with sodium iodide | ACCEPT bromine is only displaced by chlorine and iodine is displaced by chlorine and bromine scoresM2 and M3ALLOW chlorine has two reactions,bromine has one reaction and iodine no reactions for1 mark out of M2 and M3Deduct1 mark forincorrect use of ine | 3", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)(iii)", "", "and ide e.g. bromine displaces iodide", "1"], ["bromine cannot displace itself / bromine does not react with sodium bromide OWTTE", "ALLOW there would be no reaction", "2"], ["M1 bromine is reduced and iodide (ions)/I- is oxidised", "Deduct 1 mark for mention of iodine (ions) being oxidised or losing electrons", ""], ["M2 bromine gains electrons and iodide (ions)/I- loses electrons", "", ""], ["ORM1 bromine gains electrons so is reducedM2 iodide (ions)/I- loses electrons so is oxidised", "REJECT iodine (ions) loses electrons so is oxidised", ""]], "text": "(ii)(iii) |  | and ide e.g. bromine displaces iodide | 1\nbromine cannot displace itself / bromine does not react with sodium bromide OWTTE | ALLOW there would be no reaction | 2\nM1 bromine is reduced and iodide (ions)/I- is oxidised | Deduct 1 mark for mention of iodine (ions) being oxidised or losing electrons | \nM2 bromine gains electrons and iodide (ions)/I- loses electrons |  | \nORM1 bromine gains electrons so is reducedM2 iodide (ions)/I- loses electrons so is oxidised | REJECT iodine (ions) loses electrons so is oxidised | ", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(a)", "M1(propane/it) contains hydrogen and carbon(atoms)", "REJECT carbon and hydrogen molecules", "2"], ["M2 only", "M2 is dependent on mention of just carbon and hydrogen in M1", ""], ["(b)(i)", "carbon monoxide", "ALLOW CO", "1"], ["it decreases the capacity of the blood to transport oxygen OWTTE", "ALLOW carbon monoxide binds to haemoglobin", "1"], ["(c)", "M1(strong electrostatic) attraction between(bonding) pair of electrons", "", "2"], ["M2(and) nuclei(of both atoms)", "REJECT nucleus", ""], ["OR", "", ""], ["M1(bonding) pair of electrons", "REJECT nucleus", ""], ["M2 attracted to nuclei", "0 marks if reference to intermolecular forces between atoms", ""], ["(d)", "An explanation that links the following three points", "", "3"], ["M1(crude oil) produces more long chain hydrocarbons than can be used directly OWTTE", "ALLOW less demand for long chain hydrocarbons", ""], ["M2 shorter chain alkanes are more flammable/more useful as fuels", "ALLOW shorter chain alkanes/hydrocarbons are more useful", ""], ["M3 alkenes are used to make polymers/plastics", "", ""], ["(e)(i)", "M1C3H7Br", "", "2"], ["M2HBr", "ALLOW polysubstituted product if correct balancing number in front of Br2and HBr", ""], ["(ii)", "substitution", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(a) | M1(propane/it) contains hydrogen and carbon(atoms) | REJECT carbon and hydrogen molecules | 2\nM2 only | M2 is dependent on mention of just carbon and hydrogen in M1 | \n(b)(i) | carbon monoxide | ALLOW CO | 1\nit decreases the capacity of the blood to transport oxygen OWTTE | ALLOW carbon monoxide binds to haemoglobin | 1\n(c) | M1(strong electrostatic) attraction between(bonding) pair of electrons |  | 2\nM2(and) nuclei(of both atoms) | REJECT nucleus | \nOR |  | \nM1(bonding) pair of electrons | REJECT nucleus | \nM2 attracted to nuclei | 0 marks if reference to intermolecular forces between atoms | \n(d) | An explanation that links the following three points |  | 3\nM1(crude oil) produces more long chain hydrocarbons than can be used directly OWTTE | ALLOW less demand for long chain hydrocarbons | \nM2 shorter chain alkanes are more flammable/more useful as fuels | ALLOW shorter chain alkanes/hydrocarbons are more useful | \nM3 alkenes are used to make polymers/plastics |  | \n(e)(i) | M1C3H7Br |  | 2\nM2HBr | ALLOW polysubstituted product if correct balancing number in front of Br2and HBr | \n(ii) | substitution |  | 1", "row_count": 17, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10(a)(i)(ii)(iii)", "curve of best fit", "REJECT dot to dot line", "1"], ["M1 lines shown on graph", "ALLOW extra point on curve at 7 carbon atoms", "2"], ["M2 value correctly read from graph (expected value between 97 and 103℃)", "ACCEPT value to $\\pm1^{\\circ}C$", ""], ["An explanation that links the following three points", "", "3"], ["M1 the boiling point increases as the number of carbons/the chain length increases", "ALLOW boiling point increases as the $M_r$ increases", ""], ["M2 because the intermolecular forces (of attraction) get strongerM3 and therefore take more energy to overcome / break", "REJECT directly proportionalM3 dep on M2Any mention of breaking covalent bonds does not score M2 or M3", ""], ["(b)", "M1 same molecular formula", "", "2"], ["M2 different displayed / structural formulae", "ALLOW different structures/different arrangement of atoms", ""], ["(c)(i)(ii)", "M1 82.8÷12or6.917.2÷1or17.2", "0 marks if upside down calculation or use of atomic numbers", "2"], ["M2 (divide by smallest to give) 1:2.5 which is 2:5", "ACCEPT alternative methods", ""], ["$C_{4}H_{10}$", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10(a)(i)(ii)(iii) | curve of best fit | REJECT dot to dot line | 1\nM1 lines shown on graph | ALLOW extra point on curve at 7 carbon atoms | 2\nM2 value correctly read from graph (expected value between 97 and 103℃) | ACCEPT value to $\\pm1^{\\circ}C$ | \nAn explanation that links the following three points |  | 3\nM1 the boiling point increases as the number of carbons/the chain length increases | ALLOW boiling point increases as the $M_r$ increases | \nM2 because the intermolecular forces (of attraction) get strongerM3 and therefore take more energy to overcome / break | REJECT directly proportionalM3 dep on M2Any mention of breaking covalent bonds does not score M2 or M3 | \n(b) | M1 same molecular formula |  | 2\nM2 different displayed / structural formulae | ALLOW different structures/different arrangement of atoms | \n(c)(i)(ii) | M1 82.8÷12or6.917.2÷1or17.2 | 0 marks if upside down calculation or use of atomic numbers | 2\nM2 (divide by smallest to give) 1:2.5 which is 2:5 | ACCEPT alternative methods | \n$C_{4}H_{10}$ |  | 1", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(d)", "M1 moles of CO2=7 or X=7", "ALLOW ecf from incorrect values of X and Y", "3"], ["M2 moles of H2O=8 or Y=8"], ["M3 balancing number=11 or Z=11"]], "text": "(d) | M1 moles of CO2=7 or X=7 | ALLOW ecf from incorrect values of X and Y | 3\nM2 moles of H2O=8 or Y=8\nM3 balancing number=11 or Z=11", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["11", "(a)", "(i)", "glowing splint relights", "REJECT burning splint", "1"], ["A description that refers to the following three points", "", "3"], ["M1 filter out manganese(IV) oxide/solid", "", ""], ["M2 leave to dry", "", ""], ["", "(b)", "(i)", "M1 280÷120", "", "2"], ["M2 2.33", "ALLOW ecf from M1", ""], ["", "ALLOW any number of significant figures except 1", ""], ["An explanation that links the following three points", "", "3"], ["M1 the concentration of hydrochloric acid is greatest", "ALLOW the surface area of zinc is greatest", ""], ["", "ALLOW greatest number of/more particles(of hydrochloric acid/zinc)", ""], ["M2 therefore there are more collisions", "", "2"], ["(iii)", "", "M3 per unit time", "More frequent collisions scores M2 and M3", ""], ["", "Max 1 if incorrect reference to energy", ""], ["M1 curve above original and starts at 0", "", ""], ["M2 curve goes flat at same volume(410cm3)", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n11 | (a) | (i) | glowing splint relights | REJECT burning splint | 1\nA description that refers to the following three points |  | 3\nM1 filter out manganese(IV) oxide/solid |  | \nM2 leave to dry |  | \n | (b) | (i) | M1 280÷120 |  | 2\nM2 2.33 | ALLOW ecf from M1 | \n | ALLOW any number of significant figures except 1 | \nAn explanation that links the following three points |  | 3\nM1 the concentration of hydrochloric acid is greatest | ALLOW the surface area of zinc is greatest | \n | ALLOW greatest number of/more particles(of hydrochloric acid/zinc) | \nM2 therefore there are more collisions |  | 2\n(iii) |  | M3 per unit time | More frequent collisions scores M2 and M3 | \n | Max 1 if incorrect reference to energy | \nM1 curve above original and starts at 0 |  | \nM2 curve goes flat at same volume(410cm3) |  | ", "row_count": 16, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(iv)", "M1 greater surface area\nM2 more collisions per unit time/more frequent collisions", "", "2"], ["(c)", "M1 $8.46\\times10^{-3}$ mol of zinc\nM2 therefore $1.69\\times10^{-2}$ mol hydrochloric acid needed(which is less than $2.50\\times10^{-2}$ mol)\nOR\nM1 $1.25\\times10^{-2}$ mol of zinc are needed\nM2 therefore 0.8(13)g of zinc is needed(and there is only 0.55g)", "ALLOW any number of sig figs including one e.g.0.008 moles of zinc,therefore 0.016 moles of acid needed scores M1 and M2", "2"], ["15 marks"]], "text": "(iv) | M1 greater surface area\nM2 more collisions per unit time/more frequent collisions |  | 2\n(c) | M1 $8.46\\times10^{-3}$ mol of zinc\nM2 therefore $1.69\\times10^{-2}$ mol hydrochloric acid needed(which is less than $2.50\\times10^{-2}$ mol)\nOR\nM1 $1.25\\times10^{-2}$ mol of zinc are needed\nM2 therefore 0.8(13)g of zinc is needed(and there is only 0.55g) | ALLOW any number of sig figs including one e.g.0.008 moles of zinc,therefore 0.016 moles of acid needed scores M1 and M2 | 2\n15 marks", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021", "e000032"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "571678af-1b7e-58f9-be5b-93038ef1581c", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:55:04.764801722Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 51, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2021", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 1C and Science (Double Award) (4SD0) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2021", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_1C_2101_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2021", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response,the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "12 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:55:23.833032+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('364817b6-d2d4-491c-8a54-bd3b88cda453', '20626212-9afd-50b6-b9ce-d4391cb7e4c9', '1.0', 1, 'QUESTION_PAPER', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-1c-2021janr/QP.md', 'QP.md', 'text/markdown', '2b7d591fa30eb959b5d68425e2967eebab790da7124e12d6c1163255df1ecd1c', 'SHA-256', 1, 205, 195, 14, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 12:55:05.419022+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-1c-2021janr/QP.md", "checksum": "2b7d591fa30eb959b5d68425e2967eebab790da7124e12d6c1163255df1ecd1c", "fileName": "QP.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information"], ["Candidate surname", "Other names"], ["Centre Number Candidate Number"], ["Pearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)"], ["Monday 11 January 2021"], ["Morning (Time: 2 hours)", "Paper Reference 4CH1/1CR 4SD0/1CR"], ["Chemistry\nUnit: 4CH1\nScience (Double Award) 4SD0\nPaper: 1CR"], ["You must have:\nCalculator, ruler", "Total Marks"]], "text": "Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information\nCandidate surname | Other names\nCentre Number Candidate Number\nPearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)\nMonday 11 January 2021\nMorning (Time: 2 hours) | Paper Reference 4CH1/1CR 4SD0/1CR\nChemistry\nUnit: 4CH1\nScience (Double Award) 4SD0\nPaper: 1CR\nYou must have:\nCalculator, ruler | Total Marks", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7Li lithium3", "9Be beryllium4", "Key", "4He helium2"], ["23Na sodium11", "24Mg magnesium12", "relative atomic mass atomic symbol atomic (proton) number", "20Ne neon10"], ["39K potassium19", "40Ca calcium20", "45Sc scandium21", "4