roduced | ALLOW carbon dioxide comes from carbonate(reacting/decomposing)\nM2 showing metal carbonate has reacted/decomposed | IGNORE qualifiers eg light\n(ii)CuCO3→CuO+CO2 | ALLOW products in either order", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(f)(i)", "M1 the lower the metal is(in the reactivity series)", "ALLOW the less reactive a metal is", "2"], ["M2 the more easily the(metal) carbonate reacts/decomposes", "ALLOW the more easily the(metal) carbonate produces carbon dioxide", ""], ["", "ALLOW references to the less time the(metal) carbonate takes to react/decompose", ""], ["", "ALLOW references to the faster the(metal) carbonate reacts/decomposes", ""], ["", "ACCEPT reverse arguments", ""], ["(ii)", "repeat (the investigation) using different/other/more(metal) carbonates", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(f)(i) | M1 the lower the metal is(in the reactivity series) | ALLOW the less reactive a metal is | 2\nM2 the more easily the(metal) carbonate reacts/decomposes | ALLOW the more easily the(metal) carbonate produces carbon dioxide | \n | ALLOW references to the less time the(metal) carbonate takes to react/decompose | \n | ALLOW references to the faster the(metal) carbonate reacts/decomposes | \n | ACCEPT reverse arguments | \n(ii) | repeat (the investigation) using different/other/more(metal) carbonates |  | 1", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)(i)", "Zn+2HCl→ZnCl2+H2", "", "2"], ["M1 all symbols and formulae correct", "", ""], ["M2 correctly balanced", "M2 DEP M1", ""], ["(ii)", "lighted splint (produces squeaky) pop", "", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "52(cm3)", "ALLOW 51.5-52.5", "1"], ["M1 vertical line from 15cm3 acid to graph line", "ALLOW extra point drawn at 15cm3", "2"], ["M2 volume hydrogen from graph multiplied by 2", "ALLOW 68-70", ""], ["OR\nM1 vertical line from 30cm3 acid to graph line\nM2 volume hydrogen from graph", "ALLOW extra point drawn at 30cm3\nALLOW 68-70", ""], ["(c)", "explanation linking", "", "3"], ["M1 more (acid) particles/(hydrogen) ions/H+ in same volume", "REJECT molecules once only\nALLOW particles are closer together", ""], ["M2 more (successful) collisions per second/unit time", "ACCEPT more frequent collisions\nIGNORE more chance/probability of collision", ""], ["M3 rate increases", "ALLOW reaction is faster/speeds up", ""], ["", "MAX 1 if refer to particles moving faster/having more energy", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a)(i) | Zn+2HCl→ZnCl2+H2 |  | 2\nM1 all symbols and formulae correct |  | \nM2 correctly balanced | M2 DEP M1 | \n(ii) | lighted splint (produces squeaky) pop |  | 1\n(b)(i) | 52(cm3) | ALLOW 51.5-52.5 | 1\nM1 vertical line from 15cm3 acid to graph line | ALLOW extra point drawn at 15cm3 | 2\nM2 volume hydrogen from graph multiplied by 2 | ALLOW 68-70 | \nOR\nM1 vertical line from 30cm3 acid to graph line\nM2 volume hydrogen from graph | ALLOW extra point drawn at 30cm3\nALLOW 68-70 | \n(c) | explanation linking |  | 3\nM1 more (acid) particles/(hydrogen) ions/H+ in same volume | REJECT molecules once only\nALLOW particles are closer together | \nM2 more (successful) collisions per second/unit time | ACCEPT more frequent collisions\nIGNORE more chance/probability of collision | \nM3 rate increases | ALLOW reaction is faster/speeds up | \n | MAX 1 if refer to particles moving faster/having more energy | ", "row_count": 14, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": nu