 unit structureM2 extension bonds, brackets and n | 2", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(c)(i)", "M1 calculation of mass of octaneM2 calculation of Mr of C8H18 and CO2M3 link between mass/mol C8H18 and mass/mol CO2M4 calculation of mass CO2 in gM5 calculation of mass CO2 in kgExample calculation:M1 50x700=35000(g)M2 Mr of C8H18=114 and Mr CO2=44M3 114g C8H18 produces(8x44=)352(g)CO2M4 35000g C8H18 produces35000x352114=108070.2(g)CO2M5=108(kg)Alternative method using mol:M1 50x700=35000(g)M2 Mr of C8H18=114 and Mr CO2=44M3 n(C8H18)=35000=307.0175mol114so n(CO2)=8x307.0175=2456.14molM4 mass CO2=2456.14x44=108070.2(g)M5=108(kg)MARK CSQ in both methodscorrect answer without working scores5", "5", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(c)(i) | M1 calculation of mass of octaneM2 calculation of Mr of C8H18 and CO2M3 link between mass/mol C8H18 and mass/mol CO2M4 calculation of mass CO2 in gM5 calculation of mass CO2 in kgExample calculation:M1 50x700=35000(g)M2 Mr of C8H18=114 and Mr CO2=44M3 114g C8H18 produces(8x44=)352(g)CO2M4 35000g C8H18 produces35000x352114=108070.2(g)CO2M5=108(kg)Alternative method using mol:M1 50x700=35000(g)M2 Mr of C8H18=114 and Mr CO2=44M3 n(C8H18)=35000=307.0175mol114so n(CO2)=8x307.0175=2456.14molM4 mass CO2=2456.14x44=108070.2(g)M5=108(kg)MARK CSQ in both methodscorrect answer without working scores5 | 5 | ", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "global warming/climate change", "IGNORE greenhouse effect", "1"]], "text": "(ii) | global warming/climate change | IGNORE greenhouse effect | 1", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(a)", "to keep out of contact/prevent reaction with air/oxygen/water/moisture", "ALLOW they react with air/oxygen/water/moisture", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "similarity: both fizz/move on surface/produce flame difference caesium: faster/more violent reaction", "ALLOW both melt/form a ball/produce a gas/produce hydrogen/form an alkaline solutionACCEPT reverse argument for potassiumALLOW caesium explodes", "2"], ["(ii)", "2Cs+2H2O→2CsOH+H2M1 all symbols/formulae correctM2 correctly balanced", "ACCEPT fractions and multiplesM2 DEP M1", "2"], ["(c)(i)", "a lid/cover", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "explanation linking eitherM1 stir solutionM2 to obtain more accurate(maximum) temperatureORM1 measure temperature of sodium hydroxideM2 to check if different to/same as temperature of(hydrochloric) acid", "ALLOW reference to even temperature throughout/heat evenly distributed OWTTE", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(a) | to keep out of contact/prevent reaction with air/oxygen/water/moisture | ALLOW they react with air/oxygen/water/moisture | 1\n(b)(i) | similarity: both fizz/move on surface/produce flame difference caesium: faster/more violent reaction | ALLOW both melt/form a ball/produce a gas/produce hydrogen/form an alkaline solutionACCEPT reverse argument for potassiumALLOW caesium explodes | 2\n(ii) | 2Cs+2H2O→2CsOH+H2M1 all symbols/formulae correctM2 correctly balanced | ACCEPT fractions and multiplesM2 DEP M1 | 2\n(c)(i) | a lid/cover |  | 1\n(ii) | explanation linking eitherM1 stir solutionM2 to obtain more accurate(maximum) temperatureORM1 measure temperature of sodium hydroxideM2 to check if different to/same as temperature of(hydrochloric) acid | ALLOW reference to even temperature throughout/heat evenly distributed OWTTE | 2", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(d)(i)", "M1 correct temperature change/△T", "", "3"], ["M2 correct substitution into Q=mxcx△T", "", ""], ["M3 correct evaluation", "", ""], ["Example calculation:", "", ""], ["M1△T=(26.5-19.9)OR6.6", "", ""], ["M2Q=100x4.2x6.6", "M2ECF M1", ""], ["M3=2800(J)", "M3ECF M2", ""], ["", "IGNORE any sign\nALLOW2770,2772", ""], ["", "correct answer without working scores3", ""], ["(ii)M1answer toM3from(i)÷0.05", "", "2"], ["", "", ""], ["", "M2correct evaluation inkJ/mol with negative sign", "", ""], ["", "expected answer", "", ""], ["", "M12800÷0.05OR56000(J)", "2770gives55400\n2772gives55440", ""], ["", "M2-56(kJ/mol)", "negative sign required\nACCEPT-55.4\nACCEPT-55.44\nACCEPT-55", ""], ["", "", "correct answer without working scores2", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(d)(i) | M1 correct temperature change/△T |  | 3\nM2 correct substitution into Q=mxcx△T |  | \nM3 correct evaluation |  | \nExample calculation: |  | \nM1△T=(26.5-19.9)OR6.6 |  | \nM2Q=100x4.2x6.6 | M2ECF M1 | \nM3=2800(J) | M3ECF M2 | \n | IGNORE any sign\nALLOW2770,2772 | \n | correct answer without working scores3 | \n(ii)M1answer toM3from(i)÷0.05 |  | 2\n |  | \n | M2correct evaluation inkJ/mol with negative sign |  | \n | expected answer |  | \n | M12800÷0.05OR56000(J) | 2770gives55400\n2772gives55440 | \n | M2-56(kJ/mol) | negative sign required\nACCEPT-55.4\nACCEPT-55.44\nACCEPT-55 | \n |  | correct answer without working scores2 | ", "row_count": 17, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10", "(a)(i)", "neutralisation", "ALLOW acid - base", "1"], ["(ii)", "acid donates proton(s)/base accepts proton(s)", "ALLOW metal oxide for base", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "(ii)", "description including", "", "5"], ["M1 appropriate use of at least three named pieces of apparatus", "", ""], ["AND any four of the following points", "", ""], ["M2 add copper(II) carbonate to (dilute sulfuric) acid (a spatula/little at a time and stir after each addition)", "", ""], ["M3 until no more effervescence", "ALLOW until no more reacts/dissolves", ""], ["M4 filter (to remove excess copper(II) carbonate/to obtain (copper(II) sulfate) solution)", "ALLOW until in excess", ""], ["M5 heat/warm filtrate/(copper(II) sulfate) solution until crystals start to appear (solution saturated) OWTTE", "", ""], ["M6 filter to obtain (the saturated) solution", "IGNORE if continue and prepare crystals instead of saturated solution", ""], ["(b)(ii)", "(ii)", "M1 calculation of actual mass of crystals obtained", "", "3"], ["M2 division by expected mass of crystals (6.4) and multiplication by 100 to convert to percentage", "", ""], ["M3 correct to 1 dp", "", ""], ["Example calculation", "", ""], ["M1 (6.40-1.80=) 4.6(0)", "", ""], ["M2 (% yield=) 4.6 x100 OR 71.875 (%) 6.4", "M2 ECF M1", ""], ["", "M3 = 71.9 (%)", "M3 DEP M2", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 | (a)(i) | neutralisation | ALLOW acid - base | 1\n(ii) | acid donates proton(s)/base accepts proton(s) | ALLOW metal oxide for base | 1\n(b)(i) | (ii) | description including |  | 5\nM1 appropriate use of at least three named pieces of apparatus |  | \nAND any four of the following points |  | \nM2 add copper(II) carbonate to (dilute sulfuric) acid (a spatula/little at a time and stir after each addition) |  | \nM3 until no more effervescence | ALLOW until no more reacts/dissolves | \nM4 filter (to remove excess copper(II) carbonate/to obtain (copper(II) sulfate) solution) | ALLOW until in excess | \nM5 heat/warm filtrate/(copper(II) sulfate) solution until crystals start to appear (solution saturated) OWTTE |  | \nM6 filter to obtain (the saturated) solution | IGNORE if continue and prepare crystals instead of saturated solution | \n(b)(ii) | (ii) | M1 calculation of actual mass of crystals obtained |  | 3\nM2 division by expected mass of crystals (6.4) and multiplication by 100 to convert to percentage |  | \nM3 correct to 1 dp |  | \nExample calculation |  | \nM1 (6.40-1.80=) 4.6(0) |  | \nM2 (% yield=) 4.6 x100 OR 71.875 (%) 6.4 | M2 ECF M1 | \n | M3 = 71.9 (%) | M3 DEP M2 | ", "row_count": 18, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10(c)(i)", "M1 find percentage of water", "", "3"], ["M2 divide each percentage by Mr to find number of moles", "", ""], ["M3 divide each answer by smallest to find ratio and value of x", "", ""], ["Expected calculation:", "", ""], ["M1(79%)CaSO421%H2O", "", ""], ["M279(=0.58)13621(=1.17)18", "", ""], ["M30.580.581.17=1:2", "", ""], ["so x=2", "correct answer without working scores3", ""], ["(ii) description including", "", "2"], ["", "M1 do a flame test", "ALLOW description of flame test", ""], ["", "M2 orange-red flame", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10(c)(i) | M1 find percentage of water |  | 3\nM2 divide each percentage by Mr to find number of moles |  | \nM3 divide each answer by smallest to find ratio and value of x |  | \nExpected calculation: |  | \nM1(79%)CaSO421%H2O |  | \nM279(=0.58)13621(=1.17)18 |  | \nM30.580.581.17=1:2 |  | \nso x=2 | correct answer without working scores3 | \n(ii) description including |  | 2\n | M1 do a flame test | ALLOW description of flame test | \n | M2 orange-red flame |  | ", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000019", "e000021", "e000024", "e000026", "e000029", "e000032", "e000035", "e000042", "e000045", "e000046"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "7411fed8-4143-54d4-ba83-d72bca490e08", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:55:05.481953530Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 91, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2021", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 1CR and Science (Double Award) (4SD0) Paper 1CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2021 Publications Code 4CH1_1CR_2101_MS All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2021", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1=6)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2=7)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3=13)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4=9)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5=12)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6=12)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7=8)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 9=13)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 10=15)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for paper = 110 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:55:24.026776+00');
