rrow2NO$", "ALLOW fractions and multiples", "1"], ["", "IGNORE state symbols, even if incorrect", ""], ["the reaction has a high activation energy/E_{a}$", "ACCEPT to give the reactants enough energy to react", "1"], ["", "ACCEPT a lot of energy is required to break the bonds in the reactants", ""], ["(iii)", "acid rain", "ALLOW nitrogen is unreactive", ""], ["", "ACCEPT references to respiratory problems", "1"], ["", "ALLOW a specific harmful effect of acid rain", ""], ["", "ALLOW references to smog", ""], ["", "ALLOW references to greenhouse gases/global warming/climate change", ""], ["(b)(i)", "M1 catalyst provides an alternative reaction route/ pathway", "", "2"], ["M2 with lower activation energy", "", ""], ["M1 particles/molecules are closer together", "ACCEPT more particles in a smaller volume/space", "3"], ["M2 therefore more collisions", "more frequent collisions scores M2 and M3", ""], ["(ii)", "M3 per unit time", "any reference to increasing energy max=1", ""], ["", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a)(i) | $N_{2}+O_{2}\\rightarrow2NO$ | ALLOW fractions and multiples | 1\n | IGNORE state symbols, even if incorrect | \nthe reaction has a high activation energy/E_{a}$ | ACCEPT to give the reactants enough energy to react | 1\n | ACCEPT a lot of energy is required to break the bonds in the reactants | \n(iii) | acid rain | ALLOW nitrogen is unreactive | \n | ACCEPT references to respiratory problems | 1\n | ALLOW a specific harmful effect of acid rain | \n | ALLOW references to smog | \n | ALLOW references to greenhouse gases/global warming/climate change | \n(b)(i) | M1 catalyst provides an alternative reaction route/ pathway |  | 2\nM2 with lower activation energy |  | \nM1 particles/molecules are closer together | ACCEPT more particles in a smaller volume/space | 3\nM2 therefore more collisions | more frequent collisions scores M2 and M3 | \n(ii) | M3 per unit time | any reference to increasing energy max=1 | \n |  | ", "row_count": 16, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(c)(i)", "M1 one pair of electrons between the nitrogen and each hydrogen\nM2 two non-bonding electrons on the nitrogen\n图示", "M2 dep on M1", "2"], ["(ii)", "M1 (electrostatic) attraction between nuclei\nM2 and shared pair(s) of electrons\nOR\nM1 (electrostatic) attraction between shared pair(s) of electrons\nM2 and nuclei (of both atoms)", "nuclei must be plural\nALLOW bonding pair(s) of electrons", "2"], ["(iii)", "M1 forces between molecules/intermolecular forces (of attraction) are weak\nM2 and therefore require little energy to overcome", "ALLOW intermolecular bonds are weak\nIGNORE less energy\nMention of breaking covalent bonds = 0", ""], ["", "", "", "14"]], "text": "(c)(i) | M1 one pair of electrons between the nitrogen and each hydrogen\nM2 two non-bonding electrons on the nitrogen\n图示 | M2 dep on M1 | 2\n(ii) | M1 (electrostatic) attraction between nuclei\nM2 and shared pair(s) of electrons\nOR\nM1 (electrostatic) attraction between shared pair(s) of electrons\nM2 and nuclei (of both atoms) | nuclei must be plural\nALLOW bonding pair(s) of electrons | 2\n(iii) | M1 forces between molecules/intermolecular forces (of attraction) are weak\nM2 and therefore require little energy to overcome | ALLOW intermolecular bonds are weak\nIGNORE less energy\nMention of breaking covalent bonds = 0 | \n |  |  | 14", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(a)", "Any six from:", "", "6"], ["M1 add barium carbonate (one spatula at a time) to the acid", "", ""], ["M2 until the bar