OW ECF from(iv)ALLOW ECF fromM1as long as answer is nearest Group2 metal", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a) | M1(put the carbonate in the boiling tube) and the limewater in the test tube |  | 4\nM2heat the carbonate and time how long it takes for the limewater to turn cloudy OWTTE |  | \nM3repeat with the same mass/amount/number of moles of another carbonate | ACCEPT repeat with another carbonate using same volume of limewater OWTTE | \nM4(the carbonate which decomposes the fastest) will turn the limewater cloudy in the least time | To score M4 reference to limewater turning cloudy must be mentioned at least once somewhere in answer | \n(b)(i) | to prevent loss of solid/XCO3/carbonate/XO | ALLOW so only carbon dioxide/gas can escape | 1\n0.05 |  | 1\n0.05 | ALLOW ECF from(ii) | 1\nM17.40÷0.05M2148 | correct answer with or without working scores2ALLOW ECF from(iii) | 2\nM1Arof metal=148-60OR88M2metal is strontium/Sr | If(iv)correct strontium/Sr scores2without workingALLOW ECF from(iv)ALLOW ECF fromM1as long as answer is nearest Group2 metal | 2", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)", "M1 shared pair(s) of electronsM2 attracted to(two) nuclei", "REJECT nucleus.Must be plural for M2M2 dep on mention of electrons in M1", "2"], ["(b)", "a pair of electrons in each bond and no non-bonding electrons.", "ALLOW dots, crosses or any combination", "1"], ["(c)(i)", "Any one fromM1 oxygen is a smaller atom/particle than siliconM2 each(atom of) oxygen forms two bonds(to silicon atoms)", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1 silicon dioxide has a giant(covalent) structureM2(in melting silicon dioxide) strong/many covalent bonds(need to be broken)M3(in melting silicon hydride) weak intermolecular forces(of attraction need to be overcome/broken)M4 more(thermal/heat) energy is needed to break the(covalent) bonds(in SiO2) than break/overcome the intermolecular forces(in SiH4)", "ALLOW description of covalent bonds as long as strong/many mentionedALLOW weak intermolecular bondsMax 2 if contradictions/references to incorrect forces/particles", "4"], ["(d)", "SiH4+2O2→SiO2+2H2Oall formula correct and equation correctly balanced", "IGNORE state symbolsALLOW multiples and fractions", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a) | M1 shared pair(s) of electronsM2 attracted to(two) nuclei | REJECT nucleus.Must be plural for M2M2 dep on mention of electrons in M1 | 2\n(b) | a pair of electrons in each bond and no non-bonding electrons. | ALLOW dots, crosses or any combination | 1\n(c)(i) | Any one fromM1 oxygen is a smaller atom/particle than siliconM2 each(atom of) oxygen forms two bonds(to silicon atoms) |  | 1\n(ii) | M1 silicon dioxide has a giant(covalent) structureM2(in melting silicon dioxide) strong/many covalent bonds(need to be broken)M3(in melting silicon hydride) weak intermolecular forces(of attraction need to be overcome/broken)M4 more(thermal/heat) energy is needed to break the(covalent) bonds(in SiO2) than break/overcome the intermolecular forces(in SiH4) | ALLOW description of covalent bonds as long as strong/many mentionedALLOW weak intermolecular bondsMax 2 if contradictions/references to incorrect forces/particles | 4\n(d) | SiH4+2O2→SiO2+2H2Oall formula correct and equation correctly balanced | IGNORE state symbolsALLOW multiples and fractions | 1", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "Any five from", "", "5"], ["M1 fractional distillation", "", ""], ["M2 crude oil heated/vapourised", "ALLOW boiled", ""], ["M3 reference to (fractionating) column/tower", "", ""], ["M4 which is hotter at the bottom than at the top", "ALLOW reference to temperature gradient ALLOW the hydrocarbons/gases/vapours cool as they rise up the column", ""], ["M5 shorter hydrocarbons/chains/molecules have lower boiling point (and rise higher/towards the top)", "ACCEPT reverse argument", ""], ["M6 fractions/hydrocarbons/gases/vapours/kerosene condense(s) at (levels depending on) their boiling points OWTTE", "ALLOW correct reference to position of kerosene fraction below refinery gases and gasoline fractions or above diesel and fuel oil fractions", ""], ["(b)(i)", "C8H18", "", "1"], ["Any four from", "", "4"], ["M1 fractional distillation/crude oil produces more long-chain hydrocarbons than can be used (directly)", "ALLOW short(er) chain hydrocarbons are in higher demand/more useful than long(er) chain hydrocarbons ORA", ""], ["M2 cracking produces short chain alkanes", "ALLOW cracking changes long(er) chain hydrocarbons into short(er) chain hydrocarbons", ""], ["M3 short chain alkanes/hydrocarbons are more flammable/can be used as fuels", "", ""], ["M4 cracking produces alkene(s)", "IGNORE named alkene", ""], ["M5 alkenes can be used to make polymers", "ALLOW named alkene forming (named) polymer e.g. ethene can be used to make poly(ethene)/polymer", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | Any five from |  | 5\nM1 fractional distillation |  | \nM2 crude oil heated/vapourised | ALLOW boiled | \nM3 reference to (fractionating) column/tower |  | \nM4 which is hotter at the bottom than at the top | ALLOW reference to temperature gradient ALLOW the hydrocarbons/gases/vapours cool as they rise up the column | \nM5 shorter hydrocarbons/chains/molecules have lower boiling point (and rise higher/towards the top) | ACCEPT reverse argument | \nM6 fractions/hydrocarbons/gases/vapours/kerosene condense(s) at (levels depending on) their boiling points OWTTE | ALLOW correct reference to position of kerosene fraction below refinery gases and gasoline fractions or above diesel and fuel oil fractions | \n(b)(i) | C8H18 |  | 1\nAny four from |  | 4\nM1 fractional distillation/crude oil produces more long-chain hydrocarbons than can be used (directly) | ALLOW short(er) chain hydrocarbons are in higher demand/more useful than long(er) chain hydrocarbons ORA | \nM2 cracking produces short chain alkanes | ALLOW cracking changes long(er) chain hydrocarbons into short(er) chain hydrocarbons | \nM3 short chain alkanes/hydrocarbons are more flammable/can be used as fuels |  | \nM4 cracking produces alkene(s) | IGNORE named alkene | \nM5 alkenes can be used to make polymers | ALLOW named alkene forming (named) polymer e.g. ethene can be used to make poly(ethene)/polymer | ", "row_count": 15, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(c)", "A Addition\nThe only correct answer is A because the reaction between an alkene and a halogen forming a halogenoalkane is addition.\nB is not the correct answer since this reaction is not combustion.\nC is not the correct answer since this reaction is not decomposition.\nD is not the correct answer since this reaction is not substitution.", "", "1"], ["(d)(i)", "M1 single bond between the two carbons and single bonds to three hydrogens and one chlorine\nM2 two extension bonds and n\nM1 they are inert/unreactive\nM2 (so) they are non-biodegradable/do not (naturally) break down/decompose (in landfill sites)\nOR\nM1 when burned\nM2 they produce toxic fumes", "n can be anywhere after brackets\nextension bonds do not have to go through brackets\nM2 dep on M1\nALLOW take long time to break down (so landfill sites may fill up)", "2"]], "text": "(c) | A Addition\nThe only correct answer is A because the reaction between an alkene and a halogen forming a halogenoalkane is addition.\nB is not the correct answer since this reaction is not combustion.\nC is not the correct answer since this reaction is not decomposition.\nD is not the correct answer since this reaction is not substitution. |  | 1\n(d)(i) | M1 single bond between the two carbons and single bonds to three hydrogens and one chlorine\nM2 two extension bonds and n\nM1 they are inert/unreactive\nM2 (so) they are non-biodegradable/do not (naturally) break down/decompose (in landfill sites)\nOR\nM1 when burned\nM2 they produce toxic fumes | n can be anywhere after brackets\nextension bonds do not have to go through brackets\nM2 dep on M1\nALLOW take long time to break down (so landfill sites may fill up) | 2", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(a)(i)", "zinc+copper(II)sulfate→zinc sulfate+copper", "REJECT copper(II)as a productACCEPT zinc(II)sulfate", "1"], ["(ii)", "polystyrene is an insulator/ prevents heat loss", "ALLOW to prevent the cup falling over", "1"], ["(iii)", "zinc is more reactive/higher in the reactivity series than copper", "ALLOW reverse argument", "1"], ["(iv)", "M1 temperature rise=28.6℃M2(75×4.2×28.6=)9009", "correct answer without working scores2ALLOW9010/9000IGNORE any signALLOW ECF from M1", "2"], ["(b)(i)", "M1800÷1000OR0.8(kJ)M20.65÷65OR0.01(mol)M30.8÷0.01=-80(kJ/mol)ORM10.65÷65OR0.01(mol)M2800÷0.01OR80000(J/mol)M3-80(kJ/mol)", "correct answer without working scores3ALLOW ECF but answer must have a-sign80/+80 scores2", "3"], ["(ii)", "M1zinc/Zn is oxidised because loses electronsM2silver ion(s)/Ag+reduced because gain electronsORM1zinc/Zn is oxidised and silver ion(s)/Ag+reducedM2zinc/Zn loses electrons and silver ion(s)/Ag+gain electrons", "", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(a)(i) | zinc+copper(II)sulfate→zinc sulfate+copper | REJECT copper(II)as a productACCEPT zinc(II)sulfate | 1\n(ii) | polystyrene is an insulator/ prevents heat loss | ALLOW to prevent the cup falling over | 1\n(iii) | zinc is more reactive/higher in the reactivity series than copper | ALLOW reverse argument | 1\n(iv) | M1 temperature rise=28.6℃M2(75×4.2×28.6=)9009 | correct answer without working scores2ALLOW9010/9000IGNORE any signALLOW ECF from M1 | 2\n(b)(i) | M1800÷1000OR0.8(kJ)M20.65÷65OR0.01(mol)M30.8÷0.01=-80(kJ/mol)ORM10.65÷65OR0.01(mol)M2800÷0.01OR80000(J/mol)M3-80(kJ/mol) | correct answer without working scores3ALLOW ECF but answer must have a-sign80/+80 scores2 | 3\n(ii) | M1zinc/Zn is oxidised because loses electronsM2silver ion(s)/Ag+reduced because gain electronsORM1zinc/Zn is oxidised and silver ion(s)/Ag+reducedM2zinc/Zn loses electrons and silver ion(s)/Ag+gain electrons |  | 2", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(a)(i)", "M1 copper(II) sulfate(solution)", "ALLOW copper sulfate", "2"], ["M2 shortest time taken to turn colourless", "ALLOW gave greatest increase in rate OWTTE ALLOW made reaction happen fastest OWTTE", ""], ["M1 a catalyst provides an alternative pathway", "M2 dep on M1", ""], ["(ii)", "M2 of lower activation energy", "Any reference to increasing energy/speed of particles scores 0", "2"], ["An explanation with following four points", "", "4"], ["(b)(i)", "M1 the rate of reaction increases/the reaction is faster/the reaction speeds up", "", ""], ["M2 because the particles gain(kinetic) energy/move faster", "", ""], ["M3 there are more collisions per unit time", "ACCEPT more frequent collisions OWTTE", ""], ["M4 more of the collisions are successful/more collisions/particles have energy greater than the activation energy", "No M4 if refer to lower activation energy", ""], ["", "there are more frequent successful collisions scores M3 and M4", ""], ["(ii)", "M1 fewer particles per unit volume", "ALLOW particles less tightly packed/particles further apart", "2"], ["M2(hence) fewer collisions per unit time", "ALLOW decrease in the frequency of collisions between particles", ""], ["", "Any reference to changing energy/speed of particles scores 0", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(a)(i) | M1 copper(II) sulfate(solution) | ALLOW copper sulfate | 2\nM2 shortest time taken to turn colourless | ALLOW gave greatest increase in rate OWTTE ALLOW made reaction happen fastest OWTTE | \nM1 a catalyst provides an alternative pathway | M2 dep on M1 | \n(ii) | M2 of lower activation energy | Any reference to increasing energy/speed of particles scores 0 | 2\nAn explanation with following four points |  | 4\n(b)(i) | M1 the rate of reaction increases/the reaction is faster/the reaction speeds up |  | \nM2 because the particles gain(kinetic) energy/move faster |  | \nM3 there are more collisions per unit time | ACCEPT more frequent collisions OWTTE | \nM4 more of the collisions are successful/more collisions/particles have energy greater than the activation energy | No M4 if refer to lower activation energy | \n | there are more frequent successful collisions scores M3 and M4 | \n(ii) | M1 fewer particles per unit volume | ALLOW particles less tightly packed/particles further apart | 2\nM2(hence) fewer collisions per unit time | ALLOW decrease in the frequency of collisions between particles | \n | Any reference to changing energy/speed of particles scores 0 | ", "row_count": 14, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10", "(a)(i)", "measuring cylinder / burette / pipette", "ALLOW syringe", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1 and M2 all the points correct ± half a square", "If only one plotting error scores M1", "2"], ["(iii)", "2 straight lines of best fit, ignoring the anomalous point", "Left line does not have to go through/use (0.0,10.0) if point has not been plotted", "1"], ["(iv)", "as the volume of sulfuric acid increases the (electrical) conductivity decreases", "IGNORE references to gradient/slope/correlation", "1"], ["(v)", "(the student) forgot to stir the mixture", "ALLOW any reference to adding less acid/lower volume (than should have done) OWTTE", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "(ii)", "M1 barium sulfate has a (giant) ionic structure OR has ionic bonding", "", "3"], ["M2 ionic substances do not conduct when solid", "ALLOW only conduct when dissolved/molten ALLOW in solid ions cannot move", ""], ["M3 water has covalent bonding and covalent compounds do not (usually) conduct electricity", "ALLOW water does not conduct because it is covalent", ""], ["(ii)", "filtration OR filtering", "IGNORE explanations of why covalent do not conduct", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 | (a)(i) | measuring cylinder / burette / pipette | ALLOW syringe | 1\n(ii) | M1 and M2 all the points correct ± half a square | If only one plotting error scores M1 | 2\n(iii) | 2 straight lines of best fit, ignoring the anomalous point | Left line does not have to go through/use (0.0,10.0) if point has not been plotted | 1\n(iv) | as the volume of sulfuric acid increases the (electrical) conductivity decreases | IGNORE references to gradient/slope/correlation | 1\n(v) | (the student) forgot to stir the mixture | ALLOW any reference to adding less acid/lower volume (than should have done) OWTTE | 1\n(b)(i) | (ii) | M1 barium sulfate has a (giant) ionic structure OR has ionic bonding |  | 3\nM2 ionic substances do not conduct when solid | ALLOW only conduct when dissolved/molten ALLOW in solid ions cannot move | \nM3 water has covalent bonding and covalent compounds do not (usually) conduct electricity | ALLOW water does not conduct because it is covalent | \n(ii) | filtration OR filtering | IGNORE explanations of why covalent do not conduct | 1", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(11)(a)(i)", "M1WO3(s)+3H2(g)", "ALLOW upper case", "2"], ["M2W(s)+3H2O(g or I)", "", "1"], ["heat again to constant mass OWTTE", "", "3"], ["M1(mass of tungsten=)1.84g", "", "3"], ["AND(mass of oxygen=)0.48g", "", ""], ["M2(moles of tungsten)=1.84or0.01184", "", ""], ["AND(moles of oxygen)=0.48or0.0316", "M2 subsumes M1ALLOW M2 ECF from incorrect masses", ""], ["(14)(iv)", "M3 therefore ratio is1:3", "M3 dep on M2ALLOW ECF from incorrect M2 only if does give1:3when rounded", "1"], ["Any one from", "", ""], ["M1 use a safety screen", "ALLOW heat proof/safety gloves", ""], ["M2 position the class some distance from the apparatus OWTTE", "ALLOW tie back hair", ""], ["(b)", "Example calculation", "correct answer without working scores3ALLOW any number of significant figures≥2 throughout", "3"], ["M1 moles of tungsten oxide=(2784×106÷232)=12000000", "ALLOW other correct methodsALLOW working in megamoles", ""], ["M2 maximum mass of tungsten=(12000000×184)=2208000000g OR2208tonnes", "ALLOW ECF M1×184", ""], ["M3 mass of tungsten(considering73.5% yield)=(73.5×2208÷100)=1622.88(tonnes)", "ALLOW ECF from M2", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(11)(a)(i) | M1WO3(s)+3H2(g) | ALLOW upper case | 2\nM2W(s)+3H2O(g or I) |  | 1\nheat again to constant mass OWTTE |  | 3\nM1(mass of tungsten=)1.84g |  | 3\nAND(mass of oxygen=)0.48g |  | \nM2(moles of tungsten)=1.84or0.01184 |  | \nAND(moles of oxygen)=0.48or0.0316 | M2 subsumes M1ALLOW M2 ECF from incorrect masses | \n(14)(iv) | M3 therefore ratio is1:3 | M3 dep on M2ALLOW ECF from incorrect M2 only if does give1:3when rounded | 1\nAny one from |  | \nM1 use a safety screen | ALLOW heat proof/safety gloves | \nM2 position the class some distance from the apparatus OWTTE | ALLOW tie back hair | \n(b) | Example calculation | correct answer without working scores3ALLOW any number of significant figures≥2 throughout | 3\nM1 moles of tungsten oxide=(2784×106÷232)=12000000 | ALLOW other correct methodsALLOW working in megamoles | \nM2 maximum mass of tungsten=(12000000×184)=2208000000g OR2208tonnes | ALLOW ECF M1×184 | \nM3 mass of tungsten(considering73.5% yield)=(73.5×2208÷100)=1622.88(tonnes) | ALLOW ECF from M2 | ", "row_count": 16, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000007"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021", "e000022", "e000024", "e000026", "e000028", "e000030", "e000032", "e000034", "e000037", "e000039", "e000041", "e000043", "e000045"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "240b0052-eb0f-58a9-9406-5a5e9af6a653", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:55:50.414663255Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 78, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 1CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Question Paper Log Number P70946A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_1CR_2206_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 1 = 6 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 2 = 8 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 3 = 9 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 4 = 12 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 5 = 11 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 6 = 9 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 7 = 15 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 8 = 10 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 9 = 10 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 10 = 10 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question 11 = 10 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:56:10.406976+00');
