xide has a giant ionic structure.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000175", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 175, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain why lithium oxide has a high melting point.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000176", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 176, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 8 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000177", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 177, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "9 This question is about substances that contain covalent bonds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000178", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 178, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The diagram represents a molecule of oxygen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000179", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 179, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Describe the forces of attraction in a covalent bond.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000181", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 181, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The table shows the boiling points of three Group 7 elements.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000182", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 182, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain the trend in the boiling points.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000184", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 184, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(3)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000185", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 185, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Graphite is a naturally-occurring form of carbon.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000186", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 186, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain why graphite is soft and conducts electricity.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000187", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 187, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Refer to structure and bonding in your answer.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000188", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 188, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "(Total for Question 9 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000189", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 189, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "10 A student uses this apparatus to record the maximum temperature in the reaction between solutions of hydrochloric acid and sodium hydroxide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000190", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 190, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the student''s method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000192", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 192, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add $ 2 5 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of hydrochloric acid to the beaker", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000193", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 193, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add $ 2 5 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution to the beaker", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000194", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 194, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "stir the mixture", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000195", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 195, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "record the maximum temperature reached", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000196", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 196, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Name a suitable piece of apparatus to add $ 2 5 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of solution to the beaker.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000197", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 197, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Before the reaction, both solutions have a temperature of $ 2 1. 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000198", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 198, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The heat energy change, Q, for the reaction is 2880 J.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000199", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 199, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Calculate the theoretical maximum temperature reached by the mixture, which has a mass of 50 g.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000200", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 200, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "[specific heat capacity of mixture, c = 4.2 J/g/ $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000201", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 201, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "temperature =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000202", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 202, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give a reason why the maximum temperature recorded by the student is lower than the theoretical maximum temperature calculated.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000203", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 203, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) In the reaction, 0.0500 mol of hydrochloric acid completely react.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000204", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 204, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the molar enthalpy change, $ \\Delta H $ , in kilojoules per mole of hydrochloric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000205", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 205, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Include a sign in your answer.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000206", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 206, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 10 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000207", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 207, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "11 This question is about the reaction between magnesium and dilute nitric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000208", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 208, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) A student reacts dilute nitric acid with an excess of magnesium powder as a first step in the preparation of dry crystals of hydrated magnesium nitrate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000209", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 209, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000210", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 210, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Explain why it is important that magnesium is in excess.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000212", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 212, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) The student adds 0.75 g of magnesium to 0.025 mol of nitric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000213", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 213, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the mass of magnesium, in grams, that remains at the end of the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000214", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 214, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "[for magnesium, $ A_{\\mathrm{r}}=2 4 $]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000215", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 215, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Describe how the student can obtain dry crystals of hydrated magnesium nitrate from the mixture at the end of the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000216", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 216, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The student repeats the experiment and records the volume of hydrogen gas collected.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000217", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 217, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The graph shows the student''s results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000218", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 218, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Volume of hydrogen in $ \\mathrm{c m^{3}} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000219", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 219, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use the graph to calculate the rate of reaction, in $ \\mathrm{c m^{3} / s} $ , at t=40s.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000221", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 221, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Show your working on the graph.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000222", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 222, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000225", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 225, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "12 This question is about hydrated compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000226", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 226, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Crystals of hydrated barium chloride $ \\mathrm{(B a C I_{2}. x H_{2} O)} $ contain water of crystallisation.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000227", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 227, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A student uses this apparatus to remove and collect the water from some crystals.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000228", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 228, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the student''s method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000230", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 230, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Step 1 record mass of tube A when empty", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000231", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 231, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Step 2 place a sample of hydrated barium chloride crystals in tube A and record new mass", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000232", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 232, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Step 3 heat tube A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000233", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 233, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Step 4 allow tube A to cool and record mass", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000234", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 234, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Repeat steps 3 and 4 until the mass recorded in step 4 is constant.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000235", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 235, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "These are the student''s results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000236", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 236, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) (i) Give a reason why the student repeats steps 3 and 4 until the mass is constant.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000240", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 240, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Calculate the mass of $ \\mathrm{B a C l_{2}} $ that forms in tube A.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000241", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 241, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Calculate the mass of water lost.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000242", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 242, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) Determine the value of x in $ \\mathrm{B a C l_{2}. x H_{2}O} $ Show your working.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000243", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 243, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Describe a physical test to show that the water in tube B is pure.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000245", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 245, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "QUESTION 12 CONTINUES ON NEXT PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000246", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 246, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) A sample containing 0.02 mol of hydrated copper(II) sulfate is heated using the same apparatus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000247", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 247, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The products of the reaction are anhydrous copper(II) sulfate and water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000248", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 248, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000249", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 249, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give the meaning of the symbol $ \\rightleftharpoons $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000251", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 251, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Describe how the reaction can be used to show that a liquid contains water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000252", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 252, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Calculate the maximum number of water molecules in tube B after the sample of hydrated copper(II) sulfate has completely reacted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000253", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 253, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "One mole of any substance contains $ 6\\times1 0^{2 3} $ particles.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000254", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 254, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "maximum number of molecules =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000255", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 255, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 12 = 13 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000256", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 256, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "TOTAL FOR PAPER=110 MARKS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000257", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 257, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:56:55.415473+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('6ef60b42-3bea-44d6-83bb-7b2717859188', 'f9058f52-19bf-5939-bbad-483392b87d5b', '1.0', 1, 'MARK_SCHEME', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-1c-2023jan/MS.md', 'MS.md', 'text/markdown', 'ae2c92fc8f406ca9613bae3b31276799de21636fd7d3d6b189dbf30851031485', 'SHA-256', 1, 32, 32, 14, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 12:56:34.480565+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-1c-2023jan/MS.md", "checksum": "ae2c92fc8f406ca9613bae3b31276799de21636fd7d3d6b189dbf30851031485", "fileName": "MS.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["1(a)(i)", "particles should be close together and should fill from the bottom of the box, most particles should touch with a minimum of 2 random rows of particles", "ALLOW particles filling the whole box\nIGNORE the size of the particles\nREJECT a regular arrangement", "1"], ["(ii)", "solid", "", "1"], ["(b)", "solid to liquid melting\nsolid to gas sublimation", "ALLOW subliming", "2"], ["(c)", "An explanation that links the two points.\nM1(particles/molecules have) more(kinetic) energy\nM2 can overcome/break the(intermolecular) forces/forces(between water molecules)", "ALLOW hot water has more(kinetic) energy\nALLOW(particles/molecules) move faster\nIGNORE vibrate more\nALLOW can overcome/break thebonds(between water molecules)OR to break away from one another OR to escape more easily\nIGNORE references to collisions,activation energy or rate of reaction", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n1(a)(i) | particles should be close together and should fill from the bottom of the box, most particles should touch with a minimum of 2 random rows of particles | ALLOW particles filling the whole box\nIGNORE the size of the particles\nREJECT a regular arrangement | 1\n(ii) | solid |  | 1\n(b) | solid to liquid melting\nsolid to gas sublimation | ALLOW subliming | 2\n(c) | An explanation that links the two points.\nM1(particles/molecules have) more(kinetic) energy\nM2 can overcome/break the(intermolecular) forces/forces(between water molecules) | ALLOW hot water has more(kinetic) energy\nALLOW(particles/molecules) move faster\nIGNORE vibrate more\nALLOW can overcome/break thebonds(between water molecules)OR to break away from one another OR to escape more easily\nIGNORE references to collisions,activation energy or rate of reaction | 2", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["2(a)", "B(Cl2)\nA is not the correct answer as the symbol O is for atoms of oxygen not molecules\nC is not the correct answer as HCl is a compound\nD is not the correct answer as H2O is a compound", "", "1"], ["(b)", "C(filtration)\nA is not the correct answer as crystallisation is not used to separate an insoluble solid from a liquid\nB is not the correct answer as evaporation will not separate an insoluble solid from a liquid\nD is not the correct answer as simple distillation is used to separate a solvent from a solution", "", "1"], ["(c)", "fractional distillation", "REJECT distillation\nREJECT simple distillation", "1"], ["(d)(i)", "D(X(s)→X(aq))\nA is not the correct answer as(l) is not the correct final state symbol\nB is not the correct answer as(g) Is not the final state symbol\nC is not the correct answer as the state symbols are the wrong way round", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "C(diffusion)\nA is not the correct answer as boiling does not occur in the beaker\nB is not the correct answer as condensing does not occur in the beaker\nD is not the correct answer as sublimation does not occur in the beaker", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "M1 potassium/K+M2 sulfate/SO42-", "potassium sulfate scores 2K2SO4 scores 2KSO4 alone scores 1ALLOW in either orderIf name correct ignore incorrect formula", "2"], ["Total for question=7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n2(a) | B(Cl2)\nA is not the correct answer as the symbol O is for atoms of oxygen not molecules\nC is not the correct answer as HCl is a compound\nD is not the correct answer as H2O is a compound |  | 1\n(b) | C(filtration)\nA is not the correct answer as crystallisation is not used to separate an insoluble solid from a liquid\nB is not the correct answer as evaporation will not separate an insoluble solid from a liquid\nD is not the correct answer as simple distillation is used to separate a solvent from a solution |  | 1\n(c) | fractional distillation | REJECT distillation\nREJECT simple distillation | 1\n(d)(i) | D(X(s)→X(aq))\nA is not the correct answer as(l) is not the correct final state symbol\nB is not the correct answer as(g) Is not the final state symbol\nC is not the correct answer as the state symbols are the wrong way round |  | 1\n(ii) | C(diffusion)\nA is not the correct answer as boiling does not occur in the beaker\nB is not the correct answer as condensing does not occur in the beaker\nD is not the correct answer as sublimation does not occur in the beaker |  | 1\n(iii) | M1 potassium/K+M2 sulfate/SO42- | potassium sulfate scores 2K2SO4 scores 2KSO4 alone scores 1ALLOW in either orderIf name correct ignore incorrect formula | 2\nTotal for question=7", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3", "(a)(i)", "argon/Ar", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "C(nitrogen)\nA is not correct because nitrogen is more abundant than carbon dioxide methane or oxygen\nB is not correct because nitrogen is more abundant than methane\nD is not correct because nitrogen is more abundant than oxygen", "", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "(hydrated) iron(III) oxide", "REJECT other oxidation states", "1", ""], ["(neon) has a full outer shell(of electrons)", "ALLOW Fe2O3\nIGNORE iron oxide", "1", ""], ["(iii)", "M1 75-30 OR 45(mm)\nM2(45÷75×100)=60(%)", "ALLOW(neon) is unreactive/inert/has 8 electrons in the outer shell\nALLOW(neon) does not lose or gain(or share) electrons", "2"], ["Total for question=6"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3 | (a)(i) | argon/Ar |  | 1\n(ii) | C(nitrogen)\nA is not correct because nitrogen is more abundant than carbon dioxide methane or oxygen\nB is not correct because nitrogen is more abundant than methane\nD is not correct because nitrogen is more abundant than oxygen |  | 1\n(b)(i) | (hydrated) iron(III) oxide | REJECT other oxidation states | 1 | \n(neon) has a full outer shell(of electrons) | ALLOW Fe2O3\nIGNORE iron oxide | 1 | \n(iii) | M1 75-30 OR 45(mm)\nM2(45÷75×100)=60(%) | ALLOW(neon) is unreactive/inert/has 8 electrons in the outer shell\nALLOW(neon) does not lose or gain(or share) electrons | 2\nTotal for question=6", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "M1 baseline has been drawn in ink", "ALLOW baseline is not drawn in pencil", "4"], ["M2 and will therefore interfere with / contaminate the results", "ALLOW will move up the paper / will get mixed up with A / will produce other colours / affect results / will smudge / ink is soluble", ""], ["M3 the water level is above A/the baseline", "ALLOW water level is too high / A is under water", ""], ["M4 and therefore A will mix with/dissolve in the water", "ALLOW A will wash off the paper\nIGNORE references to lid", ""], ["(b)(i)", "M1 one spot about 1/4 of the way between the baseline and the top of the paper / solvent front and one spot about 1/2 way", "ALLOW answers that show solvent front", "2"], ["M2 the lower spot labelled yellow and the higher spot labelled blue", "", ""], ["(ii)the blue food colouring/it is more soluble (in water) ORA as long as yellow food colouring is referred to", "IGNORE blue colour/it travels further up the paper", "1"], ["Total for question = 7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | M1 baseline has been drawn in ink | ALLOW baseline is not drawn in pencil | 4\nM2 and will therefore interfere with / contaminate the results | ALLOW will move up the paper / will get mixed up with A / will produce other colours / affect results / will smudge / ink is soluble | \nM3 the water level is above A/the baseline | ALLOW water level is too high / A is under water | \nM4 and therefore A will mix with/dissolve in the water | ALLOW A will wash off the paper\nIGNORE references to lid | \n(b)(i) | M1 one spot about 1/4 of the way between the baseline and the top of the paper / solvent front and one spot about 1/2 way | ALLOW answers that show solvent front | 2\nM2 the lower spot labelled yellow and the higher spot labelled blue |  | \n(ii)the blue food colouring/it is more soluble (in water) ORA as long as yellow food colouring is referred to | IGNORE blue colour/it travels further up the paper | 1\nTotal for question = 7", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)(i)(ii)", "copper", "ALLOW Cu\nREJECT copper(II)/Cu2+", "1"], ["magnesium cannot displace itself", "ALLOW magnesium does not react with magnesium sulfate/magnesium ions/Mg2+\nIGNORE magnesium does not react with magnesium/itself", "1"], ["magnesium/Mg\naluminium/Al\nX\ncopper/Cu", "ALLOW 1 mark if aluminium and X are swapped.\nIf copper(II) instead of copper 1 mark only", "2"], ["(b)(i)(ii)", "zinc/iron", "ALLOW all other valid answers", "1"], ["(c)", "An explanation that links the two points\nM1 magnesium/Mg(is the reducing agent)\nM2 magnesium/Mg donates electrons(causing Al3+ions to be reduced)", "ALLOW magnesium/Mg gives(away)/loses electrons(causing Al3+to be reduced)/Al3+gains electrons\nNo M2 if reference to aluminium/Al instead of aluminium ions/Al3+\nIGNORE Mg is oxidised\nM2 dep on M1", "2"], ["Total for question=7 marks"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a)(i)(ii) | copper | ALLOW Cu\nREJECT copper(II)/Cu2+ | 1\nmagnesium cannot displace itself | ALLOW magnesium does not react with magnesium sulfate/magnesium ions/Mg2+\nIGNORE magnesium does not react with magnesium/itself | 1\nmagnesium/Mg\naluminium/Al\nX\ncopper/Cu | ALLOW 1 mark if aluminium and X are swapped.\nIf copper(II) instead of copper 1 mark only | 2\n(b)(i)(ii) | zinc/iron | ALLOW all other valid answers | 1\n(c) | An explanation that links the two points\nM1 magnesium/Mg(is the reducing agent)\nM2 magnesium/Mg donates electrons(causing Al3+ions to be reduced) | ALLOW magnesium/Mg gives(away)/loses electrons(causing Al3+to be reduced)/Al3+gains electrons\nNo M2 if reference to aluminium/Al instead of aluminium ions/Al3+\nIGNORE Mg is oxidised\nM2 dep on M1 | 2\nTotal for question=7 marks", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)", "B( chloroethene)\nA is not correct as the monomer has a double bond\nC is not correct as the monomer has two carbons\nD is not correct as the monomer has two carbons", "", "1"], ["(b)", "Chemical structure of a monomer", "Extension bonds do not need to go through the brackets", "1"], ["(c)", "M1(Mr of chloroethene)=62.5\nM22490000÷62.5=39840", "", "2"], ["(d)", "A discussion which refers to any 4 of the following points\nM1 polymers/poly(propene) will remain in landfill indefinitely OWTTE\nM2(as they) are inert/unreactive/do not biodegrade/do not decompose\nM3 burning produces greenhouse gases/CO2\nM4 reference to climate change/global warming\nM5 burning produces toxic gases", "ALLOW reference to running out of landfill sites OWTTE\nALLOW carbon monoxide/CO/hydrogen chloride/HCl\nMax 3 if any reference to the ozone layer", "4"], ["(e)", "M11:1:3/31800÷10600\nM2CHCl3", "ALLOW other evidence of working\nALLOW the atoms in any order\nAnswer of CHCl3 without working scores 2", "2"], ["Total for question=10"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a) | B( chloroethene)\nA is not correct as the monomer has a double bond\nC is not correct as the monomer has two carbons\nD is not correct as the monomer has two carbons |  | 1\n(b) | Chemical structure of a monomer | Extension bonds do not need to go through the brackets | 1\n(c) | M1(Mr of chloroethene)=62.5\nM22490000÷62.5=39840 |  | 2\n(d) | A discussion which refers to any 4 of the following points\nM1 polymers/poly(propene) will remain in landfill indefinitely OWTTE\nM2(as they) are inert/unreactive/do not biodegrade/do not decompose\nM3 burning produces greenhouse gases/CO2\nM4 reference to climate change/global warming\nM5 burning produces toxic gases | ALLOW reference to running out of landfill sites OWTTE\nALLOW carbon monoxide/CO/hydrogen chloride/HCl\nMax 3 if any reference to the ozone layer | 4\n(e) | M11:1:3/31800÷10600\nM2CHCl3 | ALLOW other evidence of working\nALLOW the atoms in any order\nAnswer of CHCl3 without working scores 2 | 2\nTotal for question=10", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "X contains oxygen/OH", "ALLOW hydrocarbons only contain hydrogen and carbon (atoms)\nREJECT oxygen molecules or hydrogen and carbon molecules", "1"], ["(b)", "W", "", "1"], ["(c)", "V", "", "1"], ["(d)", "CH2=CHCH2CH3", "ALLOW CH2CHCH2CH3", "1"], ["(e)", "M1 same molecular formula\nM2 different displayed/structural formulae", "ALLOW same numbers of C and H atoms\nALLOW different arrangement of atoms", "2"], ["(f)(i)", "C4H10+Br2→C4H9Br+HBr\nM1 C4H9Br as product\nM2 rest of the equation correct", "ALLOW polysubstitution\nM2 dep on M1", "2"], ["(ii)", "C(substitution)\nA is not the correct answer because alkanes do not undergo addition reactions\nB is not the correct answer as this is not a combustion reaction\nD is not the correct answer as this reaction is not thermal decomposition", "", "1"], ["(g)", "A description that refers to any 3 from\nM1 nitrogen and oxygen(from air)\nM2 react at the high temperatures(in a car engine)\nM3 forming oxides of nitrogen\nM4 which react with/dissolve in water forming nitric acid/HNO3/acid rain", "REJECT mention of petrol contains nitrogen for M1 only\nM2 dep on mention of nitrogen and oxygen\nALLOW NOx or named oxides of nitrogen\nM4 dep on M3", "3"], ["Total for question=12"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | X contains oxygen/OH | ALLOW hydrocarbons only contain hydrogen and carbon (atoms)\nREJECT oxygen molecules or hydrogen and carbon molecules | 1\n(b) | W |  | 1\n(c) | V |  | 1\n(d) | CH2=CHCH2CH3 | ALLOW CH2CHCH2CH3 | 1\n(e) | M1 same molecular formula\nM2 different displayed/structural formulae | ALLOW same numbers of C and H atoms\nALLOW different arrangement of atoms | 2\n(f)(i) | C4H10+Br2→C4H9Br+HBr\nM1 C4H9Br as product\nM2 rest of the equation correct | ALLOW polysubstitution\nM2 dep on M1 | 2\n(ii) | C(substitution)\nA is not the correct answer because alkanes do not undergo addition reactions\nB is not the correct answer as this is not a combustion reaction\nD is not the correct answer as this reaction is not thermal decomposition |  | 1\n(g) | A description that refers to any 3 from\nM1 nitrogen and oxygen(from air)\nM2 react at the high temperatures(in a car engine)\nM3 forming oxides of nitrogen\nM4 which react with/dissolve in water forming nitric acid/HNO3/acid rain | REJECT mention of petrol contains nitrogen for M1 only\nM2 dep on mention of nitrogen and oxygen\nALLOW NOx or named oxides of nitrogen\nM4 dep on M3 | 3\nTotal for question=12", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8", "(a)(i)", "M1 NaCl", "Penalise once only for incorrect case or superscript numbers", "3"], ["M2 MgCl2", "ALLOW symbols reversed e.g. N2Mg3", ""], ["M3 Mg3N2", "ALLOW correct charges on ions e.g Mg2+(Cl-)2", ""], ["(ii) magnesium oxide", "Spelling must be correct", "1"], ["(iii) 83", "IGNORE units", "1", ""], ["(b)(i)", "(ii)", "M1 lithium changes (from 2.1) to 2", "ALLOW (two) lithium (atoms) lose one electron", "2"], ["M2 oxygen changes (from 2.6) to 2.8", "ALLOW oxygen (atom) gains two electrons", ""], ["An explanation that links the three points", "No marks if mention of sharing electrons", ""], ["M1 strong (electrostatic) forces of attraction", "ALLOW strong ionic bonds", ""], ["(ii)", "M2 between oppositely charged ions", "IGNORE more energy", ""], ["M3 which require a lot of energy to break", "0 marks if any mention of covalent bonds, intermolecular forces or molecules", ""], ["Total for question = 10"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8 | (a)(i) | M1 NaCl | Penalise once only for incorrect case or superscript numbers | 3\nM2 MgCl2 | ALLOW symbols reversed e.g. N2Mg3 | \nM3 Mg3N2 | ALLOW correct charges on ions e.g Mg2+(Cl-)2 | \n(ii) magnesium oxide | Spelling must be correct | 1\n(iii) 83 | IGNORE units | 1 | \n(b)(i) | (ii) | M1 lithium changes (from 2.1) to 2 | ALLOW (two) lithium (atoms) lose one electron | 2\nM2 oxygen changes (from 2.6) to 2.8 | ALLOW oxygen (atom) gains two electrons | \nAn explanation that links the three points | No marks if mention of sharing electrons | \nM1 strong (electrostatic) forces of attraction | ALLOW strong ionic bonds | \n(ii) | M2 between oppositely charged ions | IGNORE more energy | \nM3 which require a lot of energy to break | 0 marks if any mention of covalent bonds, intermolecular forces or molecules | \nTotal for question = 10", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(a)", "M1(electrostatic) attraction between nuclei\nM2 and shared pair(s) of electrons\nOR\nM1(electrostatic) attraction between shared pair(s) of electrons\nM2 and nuclei", "must be plural\nmust be plural", "2"], ["(b)", "An explanation that links any 3 from\nM1 the boiling points increase(down the group/from F to Br)\nM2 because the intermolecular forces get stronger\nM3 as(molecular) mass/size/number of electrons/(electron) shells increases\nM4 so more energy needed to separate the molecules/break the intermolecular forces", "No M2,M3 or M4 if any mention of breaking covalent/ionic bonds", "3"], ["(c)", "An explanation that links any five from\nM1 the structure is in layers\nM2 there are weak forces between the layers(of atoms)\nM3 which can slide(over one another making it soft)\nM4 each carbon/atom makes three covalent bonds\nM5(one) delocalised electron(per carbon/atom)\nM6(delocalised) electrons flow/move/are mobile(to conduct electricity)", "ALLOW sheets/rows\nREJECT intermolecular forces/molecules/ions\nREJECT ionic bonds\nREJECT molecules/ions", "5"], ["Total for question=10"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(a) | M1(electrostatic) attraction between nuclei\nM2 and shared pair(s) of electrons\nOR\nM1(electrostatic) attraction between shared pair(s) of electrons\nM2 and nuclei | must be plural\nmust be plural | 2\n(b) | An explanation that links any 3 from\nM1 the boiling points increase(down the group/from F to Br)\nM2 because the intermolecular forces get stronger\nM3 as(molecular) mass/size/number of electrons/(electron) shells increases\nM4 so more energy needed to separate the molecules/break the intermolecular forces | No M2,M3 or M4 if any mention of breaking covalent/ionic bonds | 3\n(c) | An explanation that links any five from\nM1 the structure is in layers\nM2 there are weak forces between the layers(of atoms)\nM3 which can slide(over one another making it soft)\nM4 each carbon/atom makes three covalent bonds\nM5(one) delocalised electron(per carbon/atom)\nM6(delocalised) electrons flow/move/are mobile(to conduct electricity) | ALLOW sheets/rows\nREJECT intermolecular forces/molecules/ions\nREJECT ionic bonds\nREJECT molecules/ions | 5\nTotal for question=10", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["10", "(a)(i)", "measuring cylinder", "ALLOW burette/pipette/syringe\nREJECT gas syringe", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "M1 Q=m×c×ΔT\nM2 ΔT=2880÷(50×4.2)\nM3 ΔT=13.7(1)℃\nM4(maximum temp=13.7(1)+21.(0)=)34.7(℃)", "M2 subsumes M1\nALLOW ecf from M3\nALLOW any number of sig fig except1inM3andM4\nCorrect answer without working scores4", "4"], ["", "(b)(ii)", "thermal energy/heat lost(to the atmosphere/surroundings)", "IGNORE energy lost", "1"], ["", "(b)(iii)", "M12880÷1000OR2.880kJ\nM22.880÷0.05(00)\nM3-57.6kJ/mol\nOR\nM12880÷0.05(00)OR57600J\nM257600÷1000\nM3-57.6kJ/mol", "ALLOW ecf from M1\nALLOW any number of sig fig except1inM3\nALLOW ecf from M1\nALLOW any number of sig fig except1inM3\nCorrect answer without working scores3", "3"], ["Total for question=9"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 | (a)(i) | measuring cylinder | ALLOW burette/pipette/syringe\nREJECT gas syringe | 1\n(b)(i) | M1 Q=m×c×ΔT\nM2 ΔT=2880÷(50×4.2)\nM3 ΔT=13.7(1)℃\nM4(maximum temp=13.7(1)+21.(0)=)34.7(℃) | M2 subsumes M1\nALLOW ecf from M3\nALLOW any number of sig fig except1inM3andM4\nCorrect answer without working scores4 | 4\n | (b)(ii) | thermal energy/heat lost(to the atmosphere/surroundings) | IGNORE energy lost | 1\n | (b)(iii) | M12880÷1000OR2.880kJ\nM22.880÷0.05(00)\nM3-57.6kJ/mol\nOR\nM12880÷0.05(00)OR57600J\nM257600÷1000\nM3-57.6kJ/mol | ALLOW ecf from M1\nALLOW any number of sig fig except1inM3\nALLOW ecf from M1\nALLOW any number of sig fig except1inM3\nCorrect answer without working scores3 | 3\nTotal for question=9", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(ii)", "M1 so all the nitric acid reacts/is neutralised", "", "2"], ["AND", "", ""], ["M2 therefore the solution only contains magnesium nitrate", "ALLOW so the excess magnesium can be removed by filtration", ""], ["OR", "", ""], ["M3 if acid is still present it will contaminate the crystals OWTTE", "", ""], ["M1 moles of Mg that reacts = 0.0250÷2 OR 0.0125", "", "3"], ["M2 mass of Mg that reacts = 0.0125×24 OR 0.3(g)", "ALLOW M1×24", ""], ["M3 mass of Mg remaining = 0.45(g)", "ALLOW 0.75-M2", ""], ["OR", "", ""], ["M1 moles of Mg = 0.0250÷2 OR 0.0125", "", ""], ["M2 moles of Mg remaining = 0.75÷24-0.0125 OR 0.03125-0.0125 OR 0.01875", "ALLOW 0.03125-M1", ""], ["(iii)", "M3 mass of Mg remaining (=0.01875×24)=0.45(g)", "ALLOW M2×24\nCorrect answer without working scores 3\n0.15(g) scores 2", ""], ["M1 filter off the excess magnesium", "", "5"], ["M2 heat the solution until crystals first start to form", "ALLOW heat until the solution is saturated/heat until crystals form on the end of a glass rod/heat to evaporate some of the water", ""], ["M3 leave the solution to cool (and crystallise)", "", ""], ["M4 pour/filter off excess liquid (to obtain crystals)", "IGNORE washing", ""], ["M5 leave (crystals) to dry", "ALLOW any method of drying that avoids excess heat e.g. filter paper, a desiccator, a warm oven", ""], ["", "If heated to dryness only M1 can be scored", ""], ["", "If solution is not heated only M1,M4 and M5 can be scored", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(ii) | M1 so all the nitric acid reacts/is neutralised |  | 2\nAND |  | \nM2 therefore the solution only contains magnesium nitrate | ALLOW so the excess magnesium can be removed by filtration | \nOR |  | \nM3 if acid is still present it will contaminate the crystals OWTTE |  | \nM1 moles of Mg that reacts = 0.0250÷2 OR 0.0125 |  | 3\nM2 mass of Mg that reacts = 0.0125×24 OR 0.3(g) | ALLOW M1×24 | \nM3 mass of Mg remaining = 0.45(g) | ALLOW 0.75-M2 | \nOR |  | \nM1 moles of Mg = 0.0250÷2 OR 0.0125 |  | \nM2 moles of Mg remaining = 0.75÷24-0.0125 OR 0.03125-0.0125 OR 0.01875 | ALLOW 0.03125-M1 | \n(iii) | M3 mass of Mg remaining (=0.01875×24)=0.45(g) | ALLOW M2×24\nCorrect answer without working scores 3\n0.15(g) scores 2 | \nM1 filter off the excess magnesium |  | 5\nM2 heat the solution until crystals first start to form | ALLOW heat until the solution is saturated/heat until crystals form on the end of a glass rod/heat to evaporate some of the water | \nM3 leave the solution to cool (and crystallise) |  | \nM4 pour/filter off excess liquid (to obtain crystals) | IGNORE washing | \nM5 leave (crystals) to dry | ALLOW any method of drying that avoids excess heat e.g. filter paper, a desiccator, a warm oven | \n | If heated to dryness only M1 can be scored | \n | If solution is not heated only M1,M4 and M5 can be scored | ", "row_count": 20, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(b)", "M1 tangent drawn(at 40s)\nM2 change in volume of hydrogen÷change in time\nM3 correct answer between2.75and3.75(cm3/s)inclusive", "If no tangent drawn allow1mark for240÷40=6(cm3/s)", "3"], ["Total for question=13"]], "text": "(b) | M1 tangent drawn(at 40s)\nM2 change in volume of hydrogen÷change in time\nM3 correct answer between2.75and3.75(cm3/s)inclusive | If no tangent drawn allow1mark for240÷40=6(cm3/s) | 3\nTotal for question=13", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["12(a)(i)(ii)(iii)(iv)", "to make sure all the water is given off/evaporates", "ALLOW to make sure the reaction is complete", "1"], ["5.2(0g)", "", "1"], ["0.9(0g)", "", "1"], ["M1 moles of BaCl2=5.2÷208OR0.025", "ALLOW ecf from(ii)", "3"], ["M2 moles ofH2O=0.9÷18OR0.05(0)M30.05(0)÷0.025=2", "ALLOW ecf fromM1andM2as long as the answer is an integerCorrect answer without working scores3", ""], ["(b)", "M1(measure the) boiling point", "ALLOW freezing point", "2"], ["M2100℃", "ALLOW0℃for freezing point", ""], ["(c)(i)(ii)(iii)", "reversible", "ALLOW the reaction goes in both directionsIGNORE equilibrium", "1"], ["M1add water to anhydrous copper sulfate", "ALLOW white copper sulfate", "2"], ["M2which turns(from white)to blue", "M2dep on mention of anhydrous/white copper sulfateMax1mark if incorrect starting colour", ""], ["M1moles ofwater=0.02x5OR0.1M2molecules ofwater=6x10^{22}$", "ALLOW ecf fromM1Correct answer without working scores21.2x10^{22}scores1", "2"], ["Total for question=13"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n12(a)(i)(ii)(iii)(iv) | to make sure all the water is given off/evaporates | ALLOW to make sure the reaction is complete | 1\n5.2(0g) |  | 1\n0.9(0g) |  | 1\nM1 moles of BaCl2=5.2÷208OR0.025 | ALLOW ecf from(ii) | 3\nM2 moles ofH2O=0.9÷18OR0.05(0)M30.05(0)÷0.025=2 | ALLOW ecf fromM1andM2as long as the answer is an integerCorrect answer without working scores3 | \n(b) | M1(measure the) boiling point | ALLOW freezing point | 2\nM2100℃ | ALLOW0℃for freezing point | \n(c)(i)(ii)(iii) | reversible | ALLOW the reaction goes in both directionsIGNORE equilibrium | 1\nM1add water to anhydrous copper sulfate | ALLOW white copper sulfate | 2\nM2which turns(from white)to blue | M2dep on mention of anhydrous/white copper sulfateMax1mark if incorrect starting colour | \nM1moles ofwater=0.02x5OR0.1M2molecules ofwater=6x10^{22}$ | ALLOW ecf fromM1Correct answer without working scores21.2x10^{22}scores1 | 2\nTotal for question=13", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000003", "e000004"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000018", "e000031"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "f9058f52-19bf-5939-bbad-483392b87d5b", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:56:34.480565383Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 142, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question = 6", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question = 13", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:56:55.557364+00');
