(repeat) until there is no further change in mass", "", "2"], ["An explanation that links the following two points", "ACCEPT steam", ""], ["M1 to cool the (water) vapour", "", "2"], ["M2 so it condenses / forms liquid/water", "", ""], ["(iii)", "(iii)", "A description that refers to the following two points", "", "2"], ["M1 heat (the water) / measure the boiling point", "ALLOW find the freezing point /melting point?", ""], ["M2 (if it) boils at 100℃ (it is pure water) / boiling point is 100℃", "REJECT evaporate", ""], ["", "ALLOW freezes / melts at 0℃", ""], ["", "", "IGNORE chemical test even if incorrect", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9 | (a)(i) | B4 |  | 1\nA is incorrect as there are not 3 different elements in Na2SO4.7H2O\nC is incorrect as there are not 5 different elements in Na2SO4.7H2O\nD is incorrect as there are not 10 different elements in Na2SO4.7H2O |  | 1\n(ii) | D28\nA is incorrect as there is not a total of 10 atoms in Na2SO4.7H2O\nB is incorrect as there is not a total of 22 atoms in Na2SO4.7H2O\nC is incorrect as there is not a total of 27 atoms in Na2SO4.7H2O |  | 1\n(b)(i) | (ii) | A description that refers to the following two points |  | 2\nM1 heat the sodium sulfate (again) | ACCEPT ‘heat to constant mass’ for both marks | \nM2 (repeat) until there is no further change in mass |  | 2\nAn explanation that links the following two points | ACCEPT steam | \nM1 to cool the (water) vapour |  | 2\nM2 so it condenses / forms liquid/water |  | \n(iii) | (iii) | A description that refers to the following two points |  | 2\nM1 heat (the water) / measure the boiling point | ALLOW find the freezing point /melting point? | \nM2 (if it) boils at 100℃ (it is pure water) / boiling point is 100℃ | REJECT evaporate | \n | ALLOW freezes / melts at 0℃ | \n |  | IGNORE chemical test even if incorrect |  | ", "row_count": 15, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "eleme