ent=1.3÷65=0.02(mol)(which is more than 0.0018,so zinc is in excess)", "", ""], ["OR", "", ""], ["M1 amount of zinc=1.3÷65=0.02(mol)", "", ""], ["M2 amount of HCl that can react=2x0.02=0.04(mol)(which is greater than 0.0036,so zinc is in excess)", "", ""], ["(ii)", "M1 curve starting at origin and steeper than curve AM2 curve levelling off at same volume as curve A/at40cm3", "", "2"], ["(b)(i)", "(i)", "An explanation that links any of the following four points", "", "4"], ["M1 curve B is less steep(than curve A)", "", ""], ["M2(because) the particles have less kinetic energy", "ALLOW particles move more slowly", ""], ["M3so there are fewer successful collisions per unit time/less frequent successful collisions", "ACCEPT less frequent collisions that exceed activation energy", ""], ["M4so rate of reaction is slower/reaction takes longer to complete", "", ""], ["M5no change in reacting quantities,so final volume is unchanged", "ACCEPT reverse argument throughout", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n10 | (a)(i) | M1 0.0036 moles of HCl react with 0.0018 moles of Zn |  | 2\nM2 mass of Zn that reacts is 0.0018 x 65=0.117(g)(which is less than 1.3g,so zinc is in excess) | ALLOW 0.234g is less than 1.3g,so zinc in excess for(1) | \nOR |  | \nM1 moles of zinc that can react with 0.0036 moles of HCl=0.0036/2=0.0018(mol) |  | \nM2 moles of Zn present=1.3÷65=0.02(mol)(which is more than 0.0018,so zinc is in excess) |  | \nOR |  | \nM1 amount of zinc=1.3÷65=0.02(mol) |  | \nM2 amount of HCl that can react=2x0.02=0.04(mol)(which is greater than 0.0036,so zinc is in excess) |  | \n(ii) | M1 curve starting at origin and steeper than curve AM2 curve levelling off at same volume as curve A/at40cm3 |  | 2\n(b)(i) | (i) | An explanation that links any of the following four points |  | 4\nM1 curve B is less steep(than curve A) |  | \nM2(because) the particles have less kinetic energy | ALLOW particles move more slowly | \nM3so there are fewer successful collisions per unit time/less frequent successful collisions | ACCEPT less frequent collisions that exceed activation energy | \nM4so rate of reaction is slower/reaction takes longer to complete |  | \nM5no change in reacting quantities,so final volume is unchanged | ACCEPT reverse argument throughout | ", "row_count": 16, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "An explanation that links two of the following points\nM1 only half the moles (of hydrochloric acid) used / (hydrochloric acid) concentration is halved\nM2 (so) only half the volume/20cm3 of hydrogen/gas produced\nM3 hydrochloric acid is less concentrated so curve is less steep", "If M1 and M2 are not scored, allow (1) mark for the idea that less HCl produces less hydrogen", "2"], ["(c)", "A description that refers to the following two points\nM1 (a catalyst) provides an alternative pathway/route\nM2 with a lower activation energy", "IGNORE general statements about catalysts increasing rate / not being used up", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total 12"]], "text": "(ii) | An explanation that links two of the following points\nM1 only half the moles (of hydrochloric acid) used / (hydrochloric acid) concentration is halved\nM2 (so) only half the volume/20cm3 of hydrogen/gas produced\nM3 hydrochloric acid is less concentrated so curve is less steep | If M1 and M2 are not scored, allow (1) mark for the idea that less HCl produces less hydrogen | 2\n(c) | A description that refers to the following two points\nM1 (a catalyst) provides an alternative pathway/route\nM2 with a lower activation energy | IGNORE general statements about catalysts increasing rate / not being used up | 2\n |  |  | Total 12", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000003", "e000004"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "485eb8fc-8e49-56ae-87b9-500322907307", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:56:35.972303008Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 92, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 4, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 1C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Question Paper Log Number P71950A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_1C_2306_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:56:56.199762+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('4fb2b7ef-edd6-4fee-9cac-63862a8f10f4', 'c98f5542-e243-59b9-af1b-93357fe393ff', '1.0', 1, 'QUESTION_PAPER', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-1c-2023junr/QP.md', 'QP.md', 'text/markdown', '0f3d75d3b6c6247a72c152679f82bdc9c70380a9b907ff386ee2b358c6c7fb1e', 'SHA-256', 1, 235, 218, 13, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 12:56:36.608692+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-1c-2023junr/QP.md", "checksum": "0f3d75d3b6c6247a72c152679f82bdc9c70380a9b907ff386ee2b358c6c7fb1e", "fileName": "QP.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information"], ["Candidate surname", "Other names"], ["Centre Number", "Candidate Number"], ["Pearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)"], ["Monday 22 May 2023"], ["Morning (Time: 2 hours)", "Paper reference", "4CH1/1CR 4SD0/1CR"], ["Chemistry\nUNIT: 4CH1\nScience (Double Award) 4SD0\nPAPER: 1CR"], ["You must have:\nCalculator, ruler", "Total Marks"]], "text": "Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information\nCandidate surname | Other names\nCentre Number | Candidate Number\nPearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)\nMonday 22 May 2023\nMorning (Time: 2 hours) | Paper reference | 4CH1/1CR 4SD0/1CR\nChemistry\nUNIT: 4CH1\nScience (Double Award) 4SD0\nPAPER: 1CR\nYou must have:\nCalculator, ruler | Total Marks", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7 Li lithium 3", "9 Be beryllium 4", "Key", "4 He helium 2"], ["23 Na sodium 11", "24 Mg magnesium 12", "relative atomic mass atomic symbol atomic (proton) number", "20 Ne neon 10"], ["39 K potassium 19", "40 Ca calcium 20", "45