tional", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n4(a)(i)(ii) | poly(ethene) | polyethene/ polythene/ polyethylene |  | 1\ncracking |  |  | 1\n(b)(i)(ii) | M1-bar labelled 9 |  |  | 1\nM2-drawn to correct height |  |  | 1\n(boiling point/it) increases as number of carbon atoms increases | ORA as one goes up,the other goes up positive correlation | (directly) proportional | 1", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["4(c)", "A/buried underground becauseAny two from:M1(plastics) do not produce carbon dioxide/carbon emissions/toxic/poisonous gasesIGNORE harmful/dangerous/polluting gases/sulfur dioxideM2(plastics) do not contribute to global warming/climate change/greenhouse effect/acid rainM3Does not pollute the soil/cause damage to the soilIGNORE references to effect on wildlife/habitats/costORB/burned becauseM1(burning) space in landfill not taken up/does not cause landfill sites toget filled up/will not run out of space for landfillsM2 it provides heat/can be used to generate electricityIGNORE just provides energy", "ORAcarbon monoxide/nitrogen dioxide/hydrogen chloride/chlorine/formulae", "References to ozone layer forM2 only", "11OR11"], ["", "", "", "Total", "7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n4(c) | A/buried underground becauseAny two from:M1(plastics) do not produce carbon dioxide/carbon emissions/toxic/poisonous gasesIGNORE harmful/dangerous/polluting gases/sulfur dioxideM2(plastics) do not contribute to global warming/climate change/greenhouse effect/acid rainM3Does not pollute the soil/cause damage to the soilIGNORE references to effect on wildlife/habitats/costORB/burned becauseM1(burning) space in landfill not taken up/does not cause landfill sites toget filled up/will not run out of space for landfillsM2 it provides heat/can be used to generate electricityIGNORE just provides energy | ORAcarbon monoxide/nitrogen dioxide/hydrogen chloride/chlorine/formulae | References to ozone layer forM2 only | 11OR11\n |  |  | Total | 7", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["5(a)(i)(ii)(iii)", "unsaturated", "", "", "1"], ["M1-(unsaturated) colourless\nIGNORE clear/transparent/looks like water", "no colour", "discoloured", "1"], ["M2-(saturated) orange", "yellow/brown and any combination", "any other colour either on its own or in combination with an accepted colour", "1"], ["addition", "", "", "1"], ["(b)(i)(ii)(iii)", "A", "", "", "1"], ["C and D", "C,D", "C or D", "1"], ["each colouring has a different mixture/combination/patterns of dyes", "Spots/dots for dyes", "", "1"], ["IGNORE references to different heights/distances and solubilities.", "", "", ""], ["", "", "", "Total", "7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n5(a)(i)(ii)(iii) | unsaturated |  |  | 1\nM1-(unsaturated) colourless\nIGNORE clear/transparent/looks like water | no colour | discoloured | 1\nM2-(saturated) orange | yellow/brown and any combination | any other colour either on its own or in combination with an accepted colour | 1\naddition |  |  | 1\n(b)(i)(ii)(iii) | A |  |  | 1\nC and D | C,D | C or D | 1\neach colouring has a different mixture/combination/patterns of dyes | Spots/dots for dyes |  | 1\nIGNORE references to different heights/distances and solubilities. |  |  | \n |  |  | Total | 7", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["6(a)", "(giant) ionic\nIGNORE three-dimensional / lattice", "", "any other answer", "1"], ["(b)", "M1 and M3 can be scored from labelled diagrams\nsodium:\nM1-positive ions/cations/Na+and(delocalised/sea of) electrons\nIGNORE metal ions\nM2-(electrostatic) forces/attraction between positive ions/cations/Na+and(delocalised) electrons\nIGNORE references to metallic bonding\nsodium chloride:\nM3-positive and negative ions/cations and anions/Na+andCl- (ions)\nM4-electrostatic forces/attraction between (oppositely charged/positive and negative) ions/cations and anions/Na+andCl-IGNORE references to ionic bonding\ncomparison:\nM5-forces in Na are weaker(than forces in NaCl) can be awarded even if an incorrect description of the forces has been given.\n[standalone]", "Sodium / metal ions\noppositely charged ions\nchlorine ions if stated as being negative", "atoms/molecules nuclei\nintermolecular forces\natoms/molecules nuclei\nintermolecular forces\nreference to covalent loses M4", "1\n1\n1\n1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n6(a) | (giant) ionic\nIGNORE three-dimensional / lattice |  | any other answer | 1\n(b) | M1 and M3 can be scored from labelled diagrams\nsodium:\nM1-positive ions/cations/Na+and(delocalised/sea of) electrons\nIGNORE metal ions\nM2-(electrostatic) forces/attraction between positive ions/cations/Na+and(delocalised) electrons\nIGNORE references to metallic bonding\nsodium chloride:\nM3-positive and negative ions/cations and anions/Na+andCl- (ions)\nM4-electrostatic forces/attraction between (oppositely charged/positive and negative) ions/cations and anions/Na+andCl-IGNORE references to ionic bonding\ncomparison:\nM5-forces in Na are weaker(than forces in NaCl) can be awarded even if an incorrect description of the forces has been given.\n[standalone] | Sodium / met