"1"], ["silver sulfate", "silver", "", "", "2"], ["potassium nitrate", "", "oxygen", "potassium nitrate", ""], ["", "", "", "", ""], ["(b)(i)", "platinum", "carbon/graphite copper/silver/gold/titanium", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "to increase its (electrical) conductivity/to make it a (better)(electrical) conductor/to lower its (electrical) resistance\nIGNORE references to carrying current/charge/adds hydrogen ions", "to increase the concentration/number of ions", "", "1"], ["(c)(i)", "Moles/amount of hydrogen (produced) = 2x moles/amount of oxygen (produced)\nIGNORE explanations based on forming water\n(some of the) oxygen dissolves in water/acid", "number of molecules of hydrogen (produced) is twice that of oxygen\n(some of the) oxygen reacts with the (carbon) electrode/to form CO2 (which then dissolves)", "explanations based on atoms\noxygen reacts with water/(sulfuric) acid", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1 - number of faradays = 482500 or 5\nM2 - n(H2)=1/2xM1or2.5\nFinal answer on its own without working scores 2", "", "Incorrect units", "1\n1"], ["", "", "", "Total", "9"], ["", "", "", "Total for paper", "60"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n7(a) | Solution | Negative electrode | Positive electrode | Substance left | correct formulae throughout | O for oxygen | 1\nsilver sulfate | silver |  |  | 2\npotassium nitrate |  | oxygen | potassium nitrate | \n |  |  |  | \n(b)(i) | platinum | carbon/graphite copper/silver/gold/titanium |  | 1\n(ii) | to increase its (electrical) conductivity/to make it a (better)(electrical) conductor/to lower its (electrical) resistance\nIGNORE references to carrying current/charge/adds hydrogen ions | to increase the concentration/number of ions |  | 1\n(c)(i) | Moles/amount of hydrogen (produced) = 2x moles/amount of oxygen (produced)\nIGNORE explanations based on forming water\n(some of the) oxygen dissolves in water/acid | number of molecules of hydrogen (produced) is twice that of oxygen\n(some of the) oxygen reacts with the (carbon) electrode/to form CO2 (which then dissolves) | explanations based on atoms\noxygen reacts with water/(sulfuric) acid | 1\n(ii) | M1 - number of faradays = 482500 or 5\nM2 - n(H2)=1/2xM1or2.5\nFinal answer on its own without working scores 2 |  | Incorrect units | 1\n1\n |  |  | Total | 9\n |  |  | Total for paper | 60", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "edexcel", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000001", "e000002", "e000003", "e000004"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006", "e000007", "e000008"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000010", "e000011", "e000023", "e000024", "e000025", "e000026", "e000027", "e000028", "e000029"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "d43d38fe-1078-53fb-96ca-86dd38c818c6", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:58:06.031575368Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 97, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 2, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2013", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "International GCSE Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel Level 1/Level 2 Certificate Chemistry (KCH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications come from Pearson, the world''s leading learning company. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk for our BTEC qualifications. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "If you have any subject specific questions about this specification that require the help of a subject specialist, you can speak directly to the subject team at Pearson. Their contact details can be found on this link: www.edexcel.com/teachingservices.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "You can also use our online Ask the Expert service at www.edexcel.com/ask. You will need an Edexcel username and password to access this service.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2013 Publications Code UG037093 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2013", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Further copies of this publication are available from Edexcel Publications, Adamsway, Mansfield, Notts, NG18 4FN", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Telephone 01623 467467", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Fax 01623 450481", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Email publication.orders@edexcel.com", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Order Code UG037093 Summer 2013", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "For more information on Edexcel qualifications, please visit our website www.edexcel.com", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Education Limited. Registered company number 872828 with its registered office at Edinburgh Gate, Harlow, Essex CM20 2JE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:58:26.312297+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('5cabf8fa-9227-4c90-aca6-416b54eeb726', '2c4bb314-2c6d-521b-afde-836cb2da220c', '1.0', 1, 'QUESTION_PAPER', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2013junr/QP.md', 'QP.md', 'text/markdown', '7eb1bfb34dfe99dc354d05583fa4b65e1265938f7deece6ee6507f33a09438b8', 'SHA-256', 1, 118, 116, 9, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 12:58:06.638272+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2013junr/QP.md", "checksum": "7eb1bfb34dfe99dc354d05583fa4b65e1265938f7deece6ee6507f33a09438b8", "fileName": "QP.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Write your name here"], ["Surname", "Other names"], ["Centre Number", "Candidate Number"], ["Edexcel\nInternational GCSE", ""], ["Chemistry"], ["Unit: 4CH0\nPaper: 2CR"], ["Monday 10 June 2013 – Afternoon\nTime: 1 hour"], ["Paper Reference\n4CH0/2CR"], ["You must have:\nRuler\nCalculator"], ["Total Marks"]], "text": "Write your name here\nSurname | Other names\nCentre Number | Candidate Number\nEdexcel\nInternational GCSE | \nChemistry\nUnit: 4CH0\nPaper: 2CR\nMonday 10 June 2013 – Afternoon\nTime: 1 hour\nPaper Reference\n4CH0/2CR\nYou must have:\nRuler\nCalculator\nTotal Marks", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7 Li", "9 Be"], ["3 Lithium", "4 Beryllium"], ["23 Na Sodium", "24 Mg Magnesium"], ["39 K Potassium", "40 Ca Calcium"], ["86 Rb Rubidium", "88 Sr Strontium"], ["133 Cs Caesium", "137 Ba Banum"], ["223 Fr Francium", "226 Ra Radium"]], "text": "7 Li | 9 Be\n3 Lithium | 4 Beryllium\n23 Na Sodium | 24 Mg Magnesium\n39 K Potassium | 40 Ca Calcium\n86 Rb Rubidium | 88 Sr Strontium\n133 Cs Caesium | 137 Ba Banum\n223 Fr Francium | 226 Ra Radium", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 2, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Substance", "Mixture", "Letter"], ["sand", "sand and water", ""], ["solid copper(II) sulfate", "aqueous copper(II) sulfate", ""], ["red food dye", "mixture of food dyes", ""], ["kerosene", "crude oil", ""]], "text": "Substance | Mixture | Letter\nsand | sand and water | \nsolid copper(II) sulfate | aqueous copper(II) sulfate | \nred food dye | mixture of food dyes | \nkerosene | crude oil | ", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 3, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "Au\nNaCN\nO2\nH2O", "NaCN\nNaCN\nNaCN\nNaCN", "Au\nH2O\nAu\nH2O"], ["Compound, element or mixture", "", "", ""]], "text": " | Au\nNaCN\nO2\nH2O | NaCN\nNaCN\nNaCN\nNaCN | Au\nH2O\nAu\nH2O\nCompound, element or mixture |  |  | ", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Statement", "Fractional distillation", "Cracking"], ["Crude oil is heated", "√", ""], ["A catalyst may be used", "", ""], ["Alkenes are formed", "", ""], ["Decomposition reactions occur", "", ""], ["Fuels are obtained", "", ""], ["Separation is the main purpose", "", ""]], "text": "Statement | Fractional distillation | Cracking\nCrude oil is heated | √ | \nA catalyst may be used |  | \nAlkenes are formed |  | \nDecomposition reactions occur |  | \nFuels are obtained |  | \nSeparation is the main purpose |  | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000069", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 3, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 69, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["reaction is"], ["C2H4(g)+H2O(g)→C2H5OH(g)"], ["(i) Identify the catalyst and state the temperature used in this process."], ["(2)"], ["Catalyst"], ["Temperature"], ["(ii) A 20 mol sample of ethanol was produced using this reaction."], ["Deduce the amount, in moles, of ethene needed and the volume, in dm3, that this amount of ethene would occupy at room temperature and pressure."], ["Assume that all of the ethene is converted into ethanol and that the molar volume of ethene is 24 dm3 at rtp."], ["(3)"], ["Amount of ethene mol"], ["Volume of ethene"], ["Volume = dm3"], ["(Total for Question 5 = 19 marks)"]], "text": "reaction is\nC2H4(g)+H2O(g)→C2H5OH(g)\n(i) Identify the catalyst and state the temperature used in this process.\n(2)\nCatalyst\nTemperature\n(ii) A 20 mol sample of ethanol was produced using this reaction.\nDeduce the amount, in moles, of ethene needed and the volume, in dm3, that this amount of ethene would occupy at room temperature and pressure.\nAssume that all of the ethene is converted into ethanol and that the molar volume of ethene is 24 dm3 at rtp.\n(3)\nAmount of ethene mol\nVolume of ethene\nVolume = dm3\n(Total for Question 5 = 19 marks)", "row_count": 14, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000081", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 81, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "Positive electrode", "Negative electrode"], ["Mass of electrode before electrolysis in g", "8.78", "7.95"], ["Mass of electrode after electrolysis in g", "8.46", "8.25"]], "text": " | Positive electrode | Negative electrode\nMass of electrode before electrolysis in g | 8.78 | 7.95\nMass of electrode after electrolysis in g | 8.46 | 8.25", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000098", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "colu