e/ammonia solution(names or formulae)\nIf reagent incorrect,then0/3\nIf reagent missing,then thenM2andM3can be awarded\nIf near miss(eg ammonia hydroxide)thenM2andM3can be awarded", "1"], ["green precipitate", "Ⅰignore qualifiers such as light/pale/dark\nAccept solid/suspension/ppt(e)in place of precipitate\nReject all other colours\nⅠignore names and formulae even if incorrect", "1"], ["brown precipitate", "Ⅰignore qualifiers such as light/pale/dark/rusty/foxy/orange\nAccept red-brown\nAccept solid/suspension/ppt(e)in place of precipitate\nReject all other colours\nⅠignore names and formulae even if incorrect\nIf both colours correct,penalise missing precipitate once only\nDo not awardM2orM3for two correct observations in the wrong order\nⅠignore references to bubbles etc", "1"], ["", "", "Total", "8"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(c) | (add) sodium hydroxide(solution)/NaOH | Any groupⅠhydroxide/ammonium hydroxide/barium or calcium hydroxide/ammonia solution(names or formulae)\nIf reagent incorrect,then0/3\nIf reagent missing,then thenM2andM3can be awarded\nIf near miss(eg ammonia hydroxide)thenM2andM3can be awarded | 1\ngreen precipitate | Ⅰignore qualifiers such as light/pale/dark\nAccept solid/suspension/ppt(e)in place of precipitate\nReject all other colours\nⅠignore names and formulae even if incorrect | 1\nbrown precipitate | Ⅰignore qualifiers such as light/pale/dark/rusty/foxy/orange\nAccept red-brown\nAccept solid/suspension/ppt(e)in place of precipitate\nReject all other colours\nⅠignore names and formulae even if incorrect\nIf both colours correct,penalise missing precipitate once only\nDo not awardM2orM3for two correct observations in the wrong order\nⅠignore references to bubbles etc | 1\n |  | Total | 8", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "bubbles/fizzing/effervescence", "Accept gas given off/evolved/formed/producedAccept hydrogen gasIgnore identity of gas", "2"], ["sodium moves/darts/floats", "Accept equivalents such as shoots/skimsAccept dissolves", ""], ["sodium gets smaller/disappears", "Do not apply list principleAssume that it=sodiumIgnore flames/sparksAny two for1each", ""], ["(b)Do not apply list principle", "Assume that it=sodium", "1"], ["(c)i", "hydrogen/H2", "IgnoreH", "1"], ["K+", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | bubbles/fizzing/effervescence | Accept gas given off/evolved/formed/producedAccept hydrogen gasIgnore identity of gas | 2\nsodium moves/darts/floats | Accept equivalents such as shoots/skimsAccept dissolves | \nsodium gets smaller/disappears | Do not apply list principleAssume that it=sodiumIgnore flames/sparksAny two for1each | \n(b)Do not apply list principle | Assume that it=sodium | 1\n(c)i | hydrogen/H2 | IgnoreH | 1\nK+ |  | 1", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(d)", "Na is 2.8.1\nK is 2.8.8.1", "Accept other punctuation and no punctuation and diagrams in place of full stops\nIf neither of M1 and M2 scored, allow potassium has more(electron) shells(or numbers of shells stated)/energy levels for1mark?", "1\n1"], ["outer/valence electron/outer shell\n/electron lost inK further from nucleus/protons", "Ignore potassium further from nucleus", "1"], ["less attracted by nucleus", "Accept(electron)more easily removed/lost/less energy needed to remove(electron)\nAccept potassium more willing to lose electron\nIf no reference to nucleus or protons,then neitherM3norM4can be awarded\nA correct reference to nucleus/protons is needed beforeM3andM4can be awarded\nIgnore references to shielding\nAccept reverse arguments for sodium inM3andM4", "1"], ["", "Total", "9"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(d) | Na is 2.8.1\nK is 2.8.8.1 | Accept other punctuation and no punctuation and diagrams in place of full stops\nIf neither of M1 and M2 scored, allow potassium has more(electron) shells(or numbers of shells stated)/energy levels for1mark? | 1\n1\nouter/valence electron/outer shell\n/electron lost inK further from nucleus/protons | Ignore potassium further from nucleus | 1\nless attracted by nucleus | Accept(electron)more easily removed/lost/less energy needed to remove(electron)\nAccept potassium more willing to lose electron\nIf no reference to nucleus or protons,then neitherM3norM4can be awarded\nA correct reference to nucleus/protons is needed beforeM3andM4can be awarded\nIgnore references to shielding\nAccept reverse arguments for sodium inM3andM4 | 1\n | Total | 9", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)", "Statement", "Fractional distillation", "Cracking", "1 mark for each line correct", "5"], ["Crude oil is heated", "(√)", ""], ["A catalyst may be used", "", "√"], ["Alkenes are formed", "", "√"], ["Decomposition reactions occur", "", "√"], ["Fuels are obtained", "√", "√"], ["Separation is the main purpose", "√", ""], ["(b)i", "C5H12", "Accept H12C5", "1"], ["ii", "H H H H H\n| | | | |\nH-C-C-C-C-C-C-H\n| | | | |\nH H H H H", "Accept H12C5", "1"], ["iii", "C5H12", "", "1"], ["iv", "pentane", "Accept x and other letters in place of n\nAccept answers like CnH2n+2\nIgnore 2(n+1)", ""], ["v", "CnH2n+2", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a) | Statement | Fractional distillation | Cracking | 1 mark for each line correct | 5\nCrude oil is heated | (√) | \nA catalyst may be used |  | √\nAlkenes are formed |  | √\nDecomposition reactions occur |  | √\nFuels are obtained | √ | √\nSeparation is the main purpose | √ | \n(b)i | C5H12 | Accept H12C5 | 1\nii | H H H H H\n| | | | |\nH-C-C-C-C-C-C-H\n| | | | |\nH H H H H | Accept H12C5 | 1\niii | C5H12 |  | 1\niv | pentane | Accept x and other letters in place of n\nAccept answers like CnH2n+2\nIgnore 2(n+1) | \nv | CnH2n+2 |  | 1", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5", "(c)i", "(products)", "2", "2", "", "1"], ["(oxygen)", "3", "", "M1 and M2 independent", "1"], ["", "ii", "4 electrons shared between 2 (carbon) atoms", "Ignore inner electrons even if wrong", "1"], ["4 electron pairs between 2C and 4H atoms", "Ignore number of hydrogen atoms", "1"], ["", "(d)i", "phosphoric acid/H3PO4any value in range 250-350℃", "Accept all permutations of dots and crossesIgnore intersecting circlesAccept H atoms at all anglesAt least one C or one H atom must be labelled-max1 if notMax1 if more than2C atomsMax1 if wrong number of electrons in outer shell of any atom", ""], ["ii", "20(mol)M1×24480(dm3)", "Ignore concentrated/diluteAccept value without unitAccept 523-623KMarks independent", "11"], ["", "", "", "", "Accept 480000cm3If M1 incorrect but 480 is final answer, then only M3 can be awardedIf no answer to amount of ethene, then20×24=480 scores M2 and M3", "11"], ["", "", "", "", "", "Total", "19"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5 | (c)i | (products) | 2 | 2 |  | 1\n(oxygen) | 3 |  | M1 and M2 independent | 1\n | ii | 4 electrons shared between 2 (carbon) atoms | Ignore inner electrons even if wrong | 1\n4 electron pai