s\n |  |  |  |  |  | \n4 | e |  | M1 | volume of alkali CQ on where lines cross | Accept answer to nearest gridline to min 1 dp | 1\n |  |  | M2 | maximum temperature CQ on where lines cross | Accept answer to nearest gridline to min 1 dp | 1\n |  |  |  |  | Penalise missing dp once only If both values correct but in wrong order, award 1/2 0/2 if lines do not cross | \n |  |  |  |  |  | \n | f | i | M1 | 0.650×0.025 |  | 1\n |  |  | M2 | 0.01625/0.0163 | 16.25 scores 1/2 Accept 0.016 and 0.0162 | 1\n |  |  |  |  |  | \n |  | ii | M1 | 0.0325 | CQ on fi | 1\n |  |  |  |  |  | \n |  | iii | M1 | 0.0325×1000/0.500 | CQ on fii | 1\n |  |  | M2 | 65(cm3) | If M1 wrong because×1000 missing then award M2 by ECF | 1\n |  |  |  |  | Penalise failure to use 1000 once only in i and iii Do not penalise rounding of intermediate answers and consequent final answer eg 65.2 | \n |  |  |  |  | If final answer obtained by use of $ \\frac{V_{1}M_{1}}{n_{1}}=\\frac{V_{2}M_{2}}{n_{2}} $ both marks may be awarded in iii | \n |  |  |  |  |  | \nTOTAL |  |  |  | 18", "row_count": 17, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["5", "a", "", "", "cross in box C (fractional distillation)", "", "1"], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["", "b", "", "M1", "larger molecules in crude oil", "Accept longer (chains)/bigger Mr in place of largerAccept molecules in crude oil have wide range of sizes AND molecules in kerosene have similar sizes", "4"], ["", "", "", "M2", "more covalent bonds in crude oil (molecules)/bonds have different strengths", "Accept no difference/same type of covalent bondingReject references to double bonds in kerosene", ""], ["", "", "", "M3", "crude oil has higher viscosity", "Accept less runny/less thick", ""], ["", "", "", "M4", "correct reference to other difference-eg crude oil darker colourcrude oil harder to ignitecrude oil burns with a smokier flamecrude oil has a higher boiling point/wider range of boiling points", "", ""], ["", "", "", "", "", "Any three points from fourAccept converse statements for (molecules in) kerosene", ""], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["", "c", "i", "", "C9H20", "Accept H20C9", "1"], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["", "", "ii", "", "pentane", "", "1"], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["", "", "iii", "", "C=CHCH", "Ignore bond anglesIgnore dot and cross diagramIgnore non-displayed formulae", "1"]], "text": "Question number |  | Answer | Notes | Marks\n |  |  |  |  |  | \n5 | a |  |  | cross in box C (fractional distillation) |  | 1\n |  |  |  |  |  | \n | b |  | M1 | larger molecules in crude oil | Accept longer (chains)/bigger Mr in place of largerAccept molecules in crude oil have wide range of sizes AND molecules in kerosene have similar sizes | 4\n |  |  | M2 | more covalent bonds in crude oil (molecules)/bonds have different strengths | Accept no difference/same type of covalent bondingReject references to double bonds in kerosene | \n |  |  | M3 | crude oil has higher viscosity | Accept less runny/less thick | \n |  |  | M4 | correct reference to other difference-eg crude oil darker colourcrude oil harder to ignitecrude oil burns with a smokier flamecrude oil has a higher boiling point/wider range of boiling points |  | \n |  |  |  |  | Any three points from fourAccept converse statements for (molecules in) kerosene | \n |  |  |  |  |  | \n | c | i |  | C9H20 | Accept H20C9 | 1\n |  |  |  |  |  | \n |  | ii |  | pentane |  | 1\n |  |  |  |  |  | \n |  | iii |  | C=CHCH | Ignore bond anglesIgnore dot and cross diagramIgnore non-displayed formulae | 1", "row_count": 15, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["5", "d", "", "M1M2", "C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1", "M1 for 4 correct atoms joined to 2 C atoms(ignore C=C and extra atoms joined to C)Accept Cl in any position of fourM2 for all 7 bonds correct provided that continuation bonds are shown but have no atoms attachedCl2in place of Cl but otherwise correct scoresM2 but not M1Ignore brackets and any subscript", "11"], ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["", "e", "i", "", "(in condensation polymerisation)a small molecule/H2O/HCl is (also) formed/lost/releasedORtwo(different) monomers/more than one product", "Accept converse statement for addition polymerisationeg(only) one product formed/ no atoms are lost/gained", "1", ""], ["", "", "", "", "", "If no reference to type of polymerisation, assume that condensation is referred to", "", ""], ["", "", "ii", "M1", "breakdown/decomposition", "Ignore wear away/rot", "1", ""], ["", "", "", "M2", "by bacteria/microbes/micro-organisms", "Accept biologically/naturallyM2 dep on M1 or near miss", "1", ""], ["", "", "iii", "", "inert(ness)", "Accept unreactive/non-polarIgnore strong bonds/long chains", "1", ""], ["TOTAL", "", "", "", "", "13"]], "text": "Question number |  | Answer | Notes | Marks\n |  |  |  |  |  |  | \n5 | d |  | M1M2 | C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1C1 | M1 for 4 correct atoms joined to 2 C atoms(ignore C=C and extra atoms joined to C)Accept Cl in any position of fourM2 for all 7 bonds correct provided that continuation bonds are shown but have no atoms attachedCl2in place of Cl but otherwise correct scoresM2 but not M1Ignore brackets and any subscript | 11\n |  |  |  |  |  |  | \n | e | i |  | (in condensation polymerisation)a small molecule/H2O/HCl is (also) formed/lost/releasedORtwo(different) monomers/more than one product | Accept converse statement for addition polymerisationeg(only) one product formed/ no atoms are lost/gained | 1 | \n |  |  |  |  | If no reference to type of polymerisation, assume that condensation is referred to |  | \n |  | ii | M1 | breakdown/decomposition | Ignore wear away/rot | 1 | \n |  |  | M2 | by bacteria/microbes/micro-organisms | Accept biologically/naturallyM2 dep on M1 or near miss | 1 | \n |  | iii |  | inert(ness) | Accept unreactive/non-polarIgnore strong bonds/long chains | 1 | \nTOTAL |  |  |  |  | 13", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [{"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_1_1789063936755.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_1_1789063936755.png", "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "figure", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000005"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000007", "e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "e6476629-7410-535c-8220-4251b62c70a0", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:58:07.322502967Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 74, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "International GCSE Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel Level 1/Level 2 Certificates Chemistry (KCH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:58:26.593807+00');
