ron(s) to Fe3+/zinc is oxidised/zinc increases its oxidation number", "Accept Fe3+gains electron(s)/is reduced/oxidation number decreases\nIgnore Fe3+converted to Fe2+/Zn converted to Zn2+Reject iron/Fe gains electrons\nM2 DEP on M1", "1\n1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 | a |  | brown precipitate | Accept usual alternatives for precipitate\nIgnore qualifiers such as dark/light\nIgnore red(dish)/orange/rust(y)\nReject other colours\nIgnore all names and formulae | 1\n | b | i | ammonium/NH4+gas given off is ammonia/NH3 | If name and formula given, both must be correct\nAccept gas given off is alkaline\nIf name and formula given, both must be correct\nM2 DEP on M1 or near miss | 1\n1\n |  | ii | sulfate/SO42- | If name and formula given, both must be correct | 1\n | c |  | Zn/zinc(atom)\n(it) loses(2) electrons/gives electron(s) to Fe3+/zinc is oxidised/zinc increases its oxidation number | Accept Fe3+gains electron(s)/is reduced/oxidation number decreases\nIgnore Fe3+converted to Fe2+/Zn converted to Zn2+Reject iron/Fe gains electrons\nM2 DEP on M1 | 1\n1", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7", "a", "i", "Any two of\n·(same) general formula\n·same/similar chemical properties /behaviour/characteristics\nOR same/similar reactions\n·gradation/gradual change/trend/increase/decrease in physical properties\n·same functional group\n·(successive) members differ by CH2\nH H\nI I\nH-C-C-O-H\nI I\nH H", "Apply list principle\nIgnore specific general formula\nIgnore specific chemical properties, eg combustion\nIgnore trend etc. in chemical properties\nAccept reference to specific physical property, eg boiling point\nReject same/similar physical properties\nIgnore differ by Mr=14\nAll atoms and bonds must be shown\nOH group can be in any position\nIgnore bond angles", "2"], ["", "", "ii", "", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7 | a | i | Any two of\n·(same) general formula\n·same/similar chemical properties /behaviour/characteristics\nOR same/similar reactions\n·gradation/gradual change/trend/increase/decrease in physical properties\n·same functional group\n·(successive) members differ by CH2\nH H\nI I\nH-C-C-O-H\nI I\nH H | Apply list principle\nIgnore specific general formula\nIgnore specific chemical properties, eg combustion\nIgnore trend etc. in chemical properties\nAccept reference to specific physical property, eg boiling point\nReject same/similar physical properties\nIgnore differ by Mr=14\nAll atoms and bonds must be shown\nOH group can be in any position\nIgnore bond angles | 2\n |  | ii |  |  | 1", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7", "b", "", "batch process slower\n/continuous process faster\nbatch process less pure\n/continuous process purer\nbatch process uses\nrenewable/sustainable/non-finite resources\nresources that do not run out\nAND\ncontinuous process uses finite resources\nOR\nunambiguous reference to one process\n(eg only the batch process uses renewable resources)", "Accept batch process slow\nAND continuous process fast\nAccept batch process gives impure product\nAND continuous process gives pure product\nIgnore references to yield\nAccept OWTTE, eg sugar used in batch process can be grown again, crude oil is not being replaced\nIgnore uses plant material for renewable and uses crude oil for finite\nAccept references to fermentation/sugars in place of batch, and hydration/ethene in place of continuous", "1\n1\n1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7 | b |  | batch process slower\n/continuous process faster\nbatch process less pure\n/continuous process purer\nbatch process uses\nrenewable/sustainable/non-finite resources\nresources that do not run out\nAND\ncontinuous process uses finite resources\nOR\nunambiguous reference to one process\n(eg only the batch process uses renewable resources) | Accept batch process slow\nAND continuous process fast\nAccept batch process gives impure product\nAND continuous process gives pure product\nIgnore references to yield\nAccept OWTTE, eg sugar used in batch process can be grown again, crude oil is not being replaced\nIgnore uses plant material for renewable and uses crude oil for finite\nAccept references to fermentation/sugars in place of batch, and hydration/ethene in place of continuous | 1\n1\n1", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["", "", "", "", "", ""], ["7", "c", "i", "3600×1000180=20000(mol)", "CQ on M120000 with or without working scores2 marks20 mol scores1/2", "11"], ["(c)(i)×2/40000(mol)", "", "11"], ["(c)(ii)×24=960000dm3", "Correct or consequential answer with or without working scores2 marks", "11"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n |  |  |  |  | \n7 | c | i | 3600×1000180=20000(mol) | CQ on M120000 with or without working scores2 marks20 mol scores1/2 | 11\n(c)(i)×2/40000(mol) |  | 11\n(c)(ii)×24=960000dm3 | Correct or consequential answer with or without working scores2 marks | 11", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8", "a", "i", "high / higher (temperature) because (forward) reaction is endothermic / absorbs heat", "Accept reverse reaction is exothermicAccept reaction shifts in endothermic direction/favours the endothermic reaction (more)Ignore references to Le Chatelier''s principle", "1"], ["ii", "low / lower (pressure) because more moles/molecules (of gas) on RHS/products side/hydrogen side", "Accept fewer moles/molecules on LHSAccept 2 mol on LHS and 4 mol on RHSAccept particles in place of moleculesAccept shift to side with more molesIgnore references to Le Chatelier''s principle", "1"], ["", "b", "", "provides an alternative route/pathway/mechanism with lower activation energyOR(gas) molecules adsorb/stick to surface of catalyst(covalent) bonds in molecules weakened", "Ignore just a route/pathIf no reference to activation energy, then accept references to energy if qualified by idea of being needed to start the reactionMAX 1 if any reference to particles gaining energy or moving more quickly", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8 | a | i | high / higher (temperature) because (forward) reaction is endothermic / absorbs heat | Accept reverse reaction is exothermicAccept reaction shifts in endothermic direction/favours the endothermic reaction (more)Ignore references to Le Chatelier''s principle | 1\nii | low / lower (pressure) because more moles/molecules (of gas) on RHS/products side/hydrogen side | Accept fewer moles/molecules on LHSAccept 2 mol on LHS and 4 mol on RHSAccept particles in place of moleculesAccept shift to side with more molesIgnore references to Le Chatelier''s principle | 1\n | b |  | provides an alternative route/pathway/mechanism with lower activation energyOR(gas) molecules adsorb/stick to surface of catalyst(covalent) bonds in molecules weakened | Ignore just a route/pathIf no reference to activation energy, then accept references to energy if qualified by idea of being needed to start the reactionMAX 1 if any reference to particles gaining energy or moving more quickly | 2", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8", "c", "i", "CO+H2O=CO2+H2", "M1 for all formulae correctM2 for balancing AND reversible arrowIgnore state symbolsM2 DEP on M1", "2"], ["ii", "(carbon/it) gains/reacts with oxygen/oxygen is added", "Accept oxygen atom/moleculeAccept increase in oxidation numberAccept actual oxidation numbers if correct(+2 to+4)Reject oxide ionIgnore references to gain or loss of electrons", "1"], ["iii", "K2CO3+CO2+H2O→2KHCO3", "M1 for all formulae correct and on the correct sidesM2 for balancingM2 DEP on M1", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8 | c | i | CO+H2O=CO2+H2 | M1 for all formulae correctM2 for balancing AND reversible arrowIgnore state symbolsM2 DEP on M1 | 2\nii | (carbon/it) gains/reacts with oxygen/oxygen is added | Accept oxygen atom/moleculeAccept increase in oxidation numberAccept actual oxidation numbers if correct(+2 to+4)Reject oxide ionIgnore references to gain or loss of electrons | 1\niii | K2CO3+CO2+H2O→2KHCO3 | M1 for all formulae correct and on the correct sidesM2 for balancingM2 DEP on M1 | 2", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000007", "e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021", "e000023", "e000026", "e000028", "e000032", "e000035", "e000037", "e000041", "e000044"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "b27e3724-c846-5220-b8d7-52376dca347c", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:58:08.023667398Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 193, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 2, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "June 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Certificate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (KCHO) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications come from Pearson, the world''s leading learning company. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information, please visit our website at www.edexcel.com.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Our website subject pages hold useful resources, support material and live feeds from our subject advisors giving you access to a portal of information. If you have any subject specific questions about this specification that require the help of a subject specialist, you may find our Ask The Expert email service helpful.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "www.edexcel.com/contactus", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "June 2014 Publications Code UG038305", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2014", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1=3 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2=4 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 8 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7 = 11 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 8 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:58:26.788247+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('b6d8d758-8554-461a-aca3-8739e1561567', '7a337178-d58f-5b51-8355-63df0327ca7c', '1.0', 1, 'QUESTION_PAPER', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2014junr/QP.md', 'QP.md', 'text/markdown', '682b67c88046c069c57b11ea4d6a03d3c4c8aaa7bb90a9fcbb91beeac9254da7', 'SHA-256', 1, 187, 183, 11, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 12:58:47.825426+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2014junr/QP.md", "checksum": "682b67c88046c069c57b11ea4d6a03d3c4c8aaa7bb90a9fcbb91beeac9254da7", "fileName": "QP.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Write your name here"], ["Surname", "Other names"], ["Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "Centre Number", "Candidate Number"], ["Chemistry\nUnit: 4CH0\nPaper: 2CR"], ["Tuesday 10 June 2014 – Afternoon\nTime: 1 hour", "Paper Reference\n4CH0/2CR"], ["You must have:\nCalculator", "Total Marks"]], "text": "Write your name here\nSurname | Other names\nPearson Edexcel International GCSE | Centre Number | Candidate Number\nChemistry\nUnit: 4CH0\nPaper: 2CR\nTuesday 10 June 2014 – Afternoon\nTime: 1 hour | Paper Reference\n4CH0/2CR\nYou must have:\nCalculator | Total Marks", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7 Li", "9 Be"], ["3 Lithium", "4 Beryllium"], ["23 Na Sodium", "24 Mg Magnesium"], ["39 K Potassium", "40 Ca Calcium"], ["86 Rb Rubidium", "88 Sr Strontium"], ["133 Cs Caesium", "137 Ba Banum"], ["223 Fr Francium", "226 Ra Radium"]], "text": "7 Li | 9 Be\n3 Lithium | 4 Beryllium\n23 Na Sodium | 24 Mg Magnesium\n39 K Potassium | 40 Ca Calcium\n86 Rb Rubidium | 88 Sr Strontium\n133 Cs Caesium | 137 Ba Banum\n223 Fr Francium | 226 Ra Radium", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "el