 q})", "latex": "\\mathrm {P b} \\left(\\mathrm {N O} _ {3}\\right) _ {2} (\\mathrm {a q}) + \\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \\mathrm {S O} _ {4} (\\mathrm {a q}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {P b S O} _ {4} (\\mathrm {s}) + 2 \\mathrm {N a N O} _ {3} (\\mathrm {a q})", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000140", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 140, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {H} - \\mathrm {C} - \\mathrm {H} + 2 \\mathrm {O} = \\mathrm {O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm {O} = \\mathrm {C} = \\mathrm {O} + 2 \\mathrm {H} - \\mathrm {O} - \\mathrm {H}", "latex": "\\mathrm {H} - \\mathrm {C} - \\mathrm {H} + 2 \\mathrm {O} = \\mathrm {O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm {O} = \\mathrm {C} = \\mathrm {O} + 2 \\mathrm {H} - \\mathrm {O} - \\mathrm {H}", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000177", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 177, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "7a337178-d58f-5b51-8355-63df0327ca7c", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:58:47.825425517Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 232, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "Instructions", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Use black ink or ball-point pen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Fill in the boxes at the top of this page with your name, centre number and candidate number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer all questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer the questions in the spaces provided", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "there may be more space than you need.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Show all the steps in any calculations and state the units.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Some questions must be answered with a cross in a box. If you change your mind about an answer, put a line through the box and then mark your new answer with a cross.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Information", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The total mark for this paper is 60.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The marks for each question are shown in brackets", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "use this as a guide as to how much time to spend on each question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Read each question carefully before you start to answer it.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Advice", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Keep an eye on the time.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Write your answers neatly and in good English.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Try to answer every question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Check your answers if you have time at the end.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "THE PERIODIC TABLE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Answer ALL questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "1 Neon is an element with atomic number 10.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Which sub-atomic particles are present in the nucleus of a neon atom?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A electrons and neutrons", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B electrons and protons", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C electrons and neutrons and protons", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D neutrons and protons", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Use words from the box to complete the sentences about the particles in a neon atom. Each word may be used once, more than once or not at all.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The particles with the smallest mass are ...", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "An atom of neon has no overall charge because it contains equal numbers of ... and ...", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The chemical properties of neon depend on the number of ... in the outer shell.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) What is the electronic configuration of a neon atom?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A 2.8", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B 2.2.6", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C 2.8.8", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D 2.8.8.2", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Neon has two main isotopes that can be represented as $ ^{2 0} \\mathrm{N e} $ and $ ^{2 2} \\mathrm{N e}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Explain, with reference to sub-atomic particles, what is meant by the term isotopes.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) The relative atomic mass of neon is 20.2", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "How does this information support the fact that a sample of neon contains more $ ^{20} $Ne than $ ^{22} $Ne?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) Neon belongs to the family of noble gases and is inert.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) What is meant by the term inert?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Why are noble gases inert?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "2 This question is about the reactions of some metals and their compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) A student adds a sample of four metals R, S, T and U separately to water and to dilute sulfuric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows the observations in each experiment.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State two properties of the metals that the student should keep the same in all of the experiments in order to compare their reactivity.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000050", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 50, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Which is the least reactive metal?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000051", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 51, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A metal R", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000052", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 52, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B metal S", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000053", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 53, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C metal T", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000054", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 54, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D metal U", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000055", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 55, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Which gas forms during the reactions with dilute sulfuric acid?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000056", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 56, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A carbon dioxide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000057", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 57, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B hydrogen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000058", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 58, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C oxygen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000059", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 59, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D sulfur dioxide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000060", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 60, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The student carries out a test to show that the solution formed when metal U reacts with dilute sulfuric acid contains sulfate ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000061", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 61, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use words from the box to complete the sentence about this test.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000062", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 62, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Each word may be used once, more than once or not at all.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000063", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 63, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "He adds a ... and observes", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000065", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 65, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "the formation of a ...", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000066", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 66, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The student observes a lilac colour in a flame test on a small sample of a different metal compound.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000067", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 67, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Which metal ions cause the formation of this colour?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000068", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 68, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A copper", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000069", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 69, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B magnesium", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000070", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 70, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C potassium", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000071", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 71, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D zinc", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000072", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 72, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000073", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 73, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "3 The thermite reaction is used on railways to produce molten iron for joining rails together. The diagram shows how this is done.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000074", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 74, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation for this thermite reaction is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000076", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 76, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) What does this reaction show about the reactivity of iron compared to the reactivity of aluminium?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000078", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 78, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Why is this reaction described as displacement?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000079", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 79, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) State two reasons why the term oxidation applies to aluminium in this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000080", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 80, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Although the thermite reaction is exothermic, it only begins after a lot of heat energy is supplied.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000081", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 81, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "How is this heat energy supplied?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000082", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 82, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3 = 5 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000083", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 83, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "4 (a) Ethanol can be manufactured by two different processes.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000084", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 84, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Process 1 sucrose $ \\xrightarrow[]{stage1} $ glucose $ \\xrightarrow[]{stage2} $ ethanol", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000085", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 85, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Process 2 ethene $ \\longrightarrow $ ethanol", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000086", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 86, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) What is the general name for compounds such as sucrose and glucose?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000087", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 87, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) What type of reaction occurs in stage 2?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000088", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 88, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) What is the catalyst used in stage 2?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000089", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 89, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) What type of reaction occurs in process 2?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000090", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 90, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The table shows the displayed formulae of four organic compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000091", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 91, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Ethanol and compound D are members of the homologous series of alcohols.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000093", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 93, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) The first member of this homologous series is methanol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000094", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 94, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Draw the displayed formula of methanol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000095", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 95, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Suggest the name of compound D.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000096", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 96, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) In industry, the conversion of propene to compound D uses the same conditions as those used in the conversion of ethene to ethanol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000097", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 97, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Identify a suitable catalyst and temperature for these conversions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000098", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 98, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "catalyst", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000099", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 99, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "temperature ... °C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000100", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 100, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Ethene and acetylene can both be used for welding metals.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000101", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 101, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equations for the reactions of these gases in welding are", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000102", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 102, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "ethene acetylene", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000103", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 103, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "One problem with using hydrocarbons as fuels is incomplete combustion.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000106", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 106, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Incomplete combustion is a bigger problem with ethene than with acetylene. Suggest why.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000107", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 107, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) One of the gases produced during incomplete combustion is dangerous to humans. Identify this gas and explain how it is dangerous.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000108", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 108, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) Ethene can be used to ripen bananas.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000109", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 109, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Bananas are placed in a large container and ethene is added. The ethene can be added in two different ways.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000110", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 110, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) In method 1, ethene is stored under pressure and passed through a pipe into the container.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000112", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 112, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Suggest one risk in using this method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000113", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 113, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) In method 2, the generator contains a known quantity of ethanol that is slowly decomposed to ethene using a catalyst.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000114", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 114, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Write a chemical equation for this decomposition.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000115", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 115, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 14 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000116", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 116, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "5 Solutions of lead(II) nitrate and sodium sulfate react together to form the insoluble salt lead(II) sulfate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000117", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 117, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) A student wrote this plan to prepare a pure dry sample of lead(II) sulfate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000118", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 118, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step1 pour some lead(II) nitrate solution into a beaker", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000119", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 119, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step 2 add sodium sulfate solution until the reaction is complete", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000120", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 120, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step3 filter the mixture", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000121", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 121, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step4 heat the filtrate to evaporate some of the water", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000122", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 122, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step 5 cool the filtrate and remove the crystals", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000123", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 123, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) How will the student know when the reaction in step 2 is complete?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000124", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 124, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Which compound could the student use in this preparation instead of sodium sulfate?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000125", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 125, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A lead(II) hydroxide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000126", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 126, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B nitric acid", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000127", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 127, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C sodium hydroxide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000128", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 128, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D sulfuric acid", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000129", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 129, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) State why the student should not have included steps 4 and 5 in his plan.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000130", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 130, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) Suggest replacement steps to obtain a pure dry sample of lead(II) sulfate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000131", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 131, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step 4", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000132", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 132, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step 5", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000133", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 133, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(v) Lead(II) carbonate cannot be used instead of lead(II) nitrate in this preparation. This is because lead(II) carbonate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000134", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 134, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A contains ionic bonding", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000135", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 135, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B has a high relative formula mass", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000136", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 136, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C is insoluble in water", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000137", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 137, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D is toxic", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000138", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 138, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The equation for the reaction in the student''s plan is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000139", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 139, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Deduce the amount of each reactant needed to form 0.150 mol of lead(II) sulfate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000141", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 141, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\mathrm{P b} \\left( \\mathrm{N O}_{3} \\right)_{2} $ mol", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000142", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 142, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\mathrm{N a}_{2} \\mathrm{S O}_{4} $ mol", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000143", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 143, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) What volume of $ 0. 5 0 0 \\mathrm{m o l} / \\mathrm{d m}^{3} $ lead(II) nitrate solution is needed to form 0.150 mol of lead(II) sulfate?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000144", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 144, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "volume =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000145", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 145, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000146", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 146, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "6 A student does some experiments to find the heat energy released when natural gas burns.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000147", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 147, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "She uses this apparatus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000148", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 148, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The diagram shows the thermometer readings in one of her experiments.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000150", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 150, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use these readings to complete the table, entering all values to the nearest 0.1 $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000152", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 152, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The student repeats the experiment three times.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000154", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 154, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows her results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000155", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 155, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Calculate the amount, in moles, at room temperature and pressure, of methane burned in experiment 1.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000157", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 157, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Assume that natural gas contains only methane.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000158", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 158, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(The volume of 1 mol of a gas at room temperature and pressure is $ 2 4 0 0 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000159", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 159, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) The quantity of heat energy released in experiment 1 is 29200 J.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000160", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 160, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the molar enthalpy change, in kJ/mol, for the combustion of methane.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000161", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 161, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "molar enthalpy change = ... kJ/mol", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000162", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 162, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) The temperature rise in experiment 2 is $ 4 1. 2 \\mathrm{~} ^ {\\circ} \\mathrm{C}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000163", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 163, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the heat energy change in experiment 2 using the expressio heat energy change = volume of water $ \\times $ 4.2 $ \\times $ temperature change (in J) (in $ cm^{3} $) (in $ ^{\\circ} C $)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000164", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 164, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "heat energy change = ... J", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000165", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 165, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) The student uses the results from experiment 3 to calculate the molar enthalpy change, in kJ/mol, for the combustion of methane.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000166", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 166, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "She compares her value with the value in a data book.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000167", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 167, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Which is the best explanation for the large difference between these two values?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000169", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 169, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B not all of the heat energy is transferred to the water", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000170", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 170, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A natural gas contains other gases that release heat energy when burned", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000171", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 171, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C some of the water evaporates during the experiment", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000172", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 172, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D the student measures the gas by volume instead of by mass", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000173", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 173, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The student uses a table of average bond energies to calculate another value for the molar enthalpy of combustion of methane.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000174", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 174, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation for the combustion can be shown using displayed formulae.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000176", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 176, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Use values from the table to calculate the energy taken in when the bonds in the reactants are broken.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000178", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 178, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "energy taken in = ... kJ", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000179", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 179, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Use values from the table to calculate the energy given out when the bonds in the products are formed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000180", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 180, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "energy given out = ... kJ", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000181", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 181, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Use your answers to (i) and (ii) to calculate the molar enthalpy change for the combustion of methane.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000182", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 182, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "molar enthalpy change = kJ/mol", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000183", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 183, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6 = 15 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000184", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 184, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "TOTAL FOR PAPER=60 MARKS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000185", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 185, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000186", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 186, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:08.696469+00');
