lostM2potassium hydroxide dissolves(very/too)slowly", "water evaporates potassium hydroxide does not completely dissolve potassium hydroxide is impure less than3g of potassium hydroxide is used more than50cm3of water is used", "2", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n5(a) | M1温度after | 27.1 |  | one trailing zero | more than one trailing zero | 3\nM2温度before | 18.8\nM3温度change | (+)8.3\nRecorded temperatures correct but in wrong order scores1 forM1和M2M3csq onM1和M2\n(b) | M1heat(energy)/thermal energy lost(to the atmosphere)ignore just energy lostM2potassium hydroxide dissolves(very/too)slowly | water evaporates potassium hydroxide does not completely dissolve potassium hydroxide is impure less than3g of potassium hydroxide is used more than50cm3of water is used | 2 | ", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["6(a)", "Element", "Arrangement of electrons in atom", "Arrangement of electrons in ion", "Charge on ion", "K(1)+/K+1S2-/S-2positive for potassium and negative for sulfide for 1 mark", "3"], ["", "", "2.8.8", "(1)+/+1"], ["", "", "2.8.8", "2-/-2"], ["M1- both arrangements correctM2- charge on potassium ionM3- charge on sulfide ion"], ["(b)(i)(ii)", "ions move/travel (to the electrodes)M1(electrostatic) forces (of attraction) between (oppositely charged) ionsM2 are (relatively) strongM3 large amount of energy required to overcome the forces / separate the ions from the latticeM2 dep on mention of forces (of attraction) or bondsMention of covalent bonds or intermolecular forces no M1", "ions are free to move / ions are mobileionic bonding / ionic bondsbreak the bonds", "13"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n6(a) | Element | Arrangement of electrons in atom | Arrangement of electrons in ion | Charge on ion | K(1)+/K+1S2-/S-2positive for potassium and negative for sulfide for 1 mark | 3\n |  | 2.8.8 | (1)+/+1\n |  | 2.8.8 | 2-/-2\nM1- both arrangements correctM2- charge on potassium ionM3- charge on sulfide ion\n(b)(i)(ii) | ions move/travel (to the electrodes)M1(electrostatic) forces (of attraction) between (oppositely charged) ionsM2 are (relatively) strongM3 large amount of energy required to overcome the forces / separate the ions from the latticeM2 dep on mention of forces (of attraction) or bondsMention of covalent bonds or intermolecular forces no M1 | ions are free to move / ions are mobileionic bonding / ionic bondsbreak the bonds | 13", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "H2S2O7+H2O→2H2SO4", "multiples and fractions", "", "1"], ["(b)", "M132(of S)→80(of SO3)(tonnes or g)\nM2mass of SO3=80\nM3=200(tonnes)\nM2csq on M1\nM3csq on M2\nCorrect answer with no working scores 3", "M1n(S)=(n(SO3))=80x106/32(mol)(=2500000(000(g))\nM2mass of SO3=M1x80(=2000000(000(g))\nM3=M2÷106/200(tonnes)", "", "3"], ["(c)", "M164(g)(of SO2) reacts with 12(dm3)(ofO2)\nM2(64 tonnes) reacts 12x106(dm3)OR1.2x107(dm3)\nM2csq on M1\nCorrect answer with no working scores 2", "M1n(SO2)=64x106/64(mol)(=106mol)\nM2M1/2x24/1.2x107(dm3)\nOR\nM1mass of oxygen\naccept1.2x1010cm3", "", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n7(a) | H2S2O7+H2O→2H2SO4 | multiples and fractions |  | 1\n(b) | M132(of S)→80(of SO3)(tonnes or g)\nM2mass of SO3=80\nM3=200(tonnes)\nM2csq on M1\nM3csq on M2\nCorrect answer with no working scores 3 | M1n(S)=(n(SO3))=80x106/32(mol)(=2500000(000(g))\nM2mass of SO3=M1x80(=2000000(000(g))\nM3=M2÷106/200(tonnes) |  | 3\n(c) | M164(g)(of SO2) reacts with 12(dm3)(ofO2)\nM2(64 tonnes) reacts 12x106(dm3)OR1.2x107(dm3)\nM2csq on M1\nCorrect answer with no working scores 2 | M1n(SO2)=64x106/64(mol)(=106mol)\nM2M1/2x24/1.2x107(dm3)\nOR\nM1mass of oxygen\naccept1.2x1010cm3 |  | 2", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["8", "M1- add (aqueous) chlorine to (aqueous) KBr", "yellow / brown", "red", "5"], ["M2-(solution) turns orange", "red-brown / orange", "yellow", ""], ["M3- add (aqueous) bromine to (aqueous) KI", "correct ionic equations", "", ""], ["M4-(solution) turns brown", "accept Cl2+2KI→I2+2KCl if chlorine is added to potassium iodide", "", ""], ["M5- Cl2+2KBr→Br2+2KCl OR Br2+2KI→I2+2KBr", "", "", ""], ["Ignore state symbols", "", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n8 | M1- add (aqueous) chlorine to (aqueous) KBr | yellow / brown | red | 5\nM2-(solution) turns orange | red-brown / orange | yellow | \nM3- add (aqueous) bromine to (aqueous) KI | correct ionic equations |  | \nM4-(solution) turns brown | accept Cl2+2KI→I2+2KCl if chlorine is added to potassium iodide |  | \nM5- Cl2+2KBr→Br2+2KCl OR Br2+2KI→I2+2KBr |  |  | \nIgnore state symbols |  |  | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["8", "M1- add (aqueous) bromine to (aqueous) KCl", "", "", "5"], ["M2- no change", "orange/ yellow/brown solution/colour produced only if it is clear that no reaction has occurred", "red", ""], ["M3- add (aqueous) iodine to (aqueous) KBr", "", "yellow", ""], ["M4- no change/ no change", "brown/ red-brown/orange solution/colour produced only if it is clear that no reaction has occurred", "", ""], ["If this route is chosen then M5 cannot be scored", "", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n8 | M1- add (aqueous) bromine to (aqueous) KCl |  |  | 5\nM2- no change | orange/ yellow/brown solution/colour produced only if it is clear that no reaction has occurred | red | \nM3- add (aqueous) iodine to (aqueous) KBr |  | yellow | \nM4- no change/ no change | brown/ red-brown/orange solution/colour produced only if it is clear that no reaction has occurred |  | \nIf this route is chosen then M5 cannot be scored |  |  | ", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Accept", "Reject", "Marks"], ["9(a)(i)", "shifts to left", "moves in the endothermic direction\nshifts to the side of the reactants\nOWTTE", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "shifts to the right", "", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "impossible to know which shift is greater / impossible to know which change has the greater effect", "moves in the exothermic direction\nshifts to the side of the products\nOWTTE\nshifts to the side with fewer (gas) moles/molecules\nOWTTE\nthe (two) effects are opposing one another", "", ""], ["(b)", "M1- greater proportion of NO2\nM2-(increase of) temperature has a greater effect than\n(increase of) pressure", "more NO2 present\nequilibrium shifts to left", "", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Accept | Reject | Marks\n9(a)(i) | shifts to left | moves in the endothermic direction\nshifts to the side of the reactants\nOWTTE |  | 1\n(ii) | shifts to the right |  |  | 1\n(iii) | impossible to know which shift is greater / impossible to know which change has the greater effect | moves in the exothermic direction\nshifts to the side of the products\nOWTTE\nshifts to the side with fewer (gas) moles/molecules\nOWTTE\nthe (two) effects are opposing one another |  | \n(b) | M1- greater proportion of NO2\nM2-(increase of) temperature has a greater effect than\n(increase of) pressure | more NO2 present\nequilibrium shifts to left |  | 2", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "edexcel", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000001", "e000002", "e000003", "e000004"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006", "e000007", "e000008"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000010", "e000011"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000023", "e000026", "e000031", "e000033", "e000035", "e000037", "e000039"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "ed36b1ae-5eef-5a3f-8063-a643f291d15b", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:58:48.513455237Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 109, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2015", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Certificate in Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications come from Pearson, the world''s leading learning company. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information, please visit our website at www.edexcel.com.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Our website subject pages hold useful resources, support material and live feeds from our subject advisors giving you access to a portal of information. If you have any subject specific questions about this specification that require the help of a subject specialist, you may find our Ask The Expert email service helpful.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "www.edexcel.com/contactus", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2015 Publications Code UG040458 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2015", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 4 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 10 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 7 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 6 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 5 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 5 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 5 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:09.171532+00');
