abelled or unlabelled)M2 for(vertical)line connecting the two horizontal lines AND labelled ΔH(ignore sign)Ignore all arrow headsIgnore curves for energy profiles including activation energy", "2"], ["", "", "", "", "", "Total 11 marks"]], "text": "Question number |  | Answer | Notes | Marks\n | c | i | M1M2 | 24000.048x100050 | Accept 50.0 and 50.00Award 1 mark for 50 000Award 2 marks for 50 000 if units changed toJ/mol on answer lineIgnore signsCorrect answer with no working scores2 | 2\n | c | ii |  | Energy lithium iodide+waterΔH lithium iodide solution | Mark M1 and M2 independentlyM1 for horizontal line drawn below(labelled or unlabelled)M2 for(vertical)line connecting the two horizontal lines AND labelled ΔH(ignore sign)Ignore all arrow headsIgnore curves for energy profiles including activation energy | 2\n |  |  |  |  | Total 11 marks", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6", "a", "", "too reactive / very reactiveORhigh in the reactivity series", "Accept words with equivalent meaningeg highly", "1"], ["", "b", "i", "B (stage 2)", "", "1"], ["", "", "ii", "calcium chloride / CaCl2", "If both name and formula given, markname only", "1"], ["", "", "iii", "(they / the ions) are mobile", "Accept free to moveAccept move to electrodes(allow even ifincorrect electrodes)Accept ions break free from lattice/crystalNot just freeAllow they/ions are delocalisedIgnore references to conduction", "1"], ["", "", "iv", "2Cl-→Cl2+2e(-)", "Accept 2Cl-→2e(-)→Cl2", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 | a |  | too reactive / very reactiveORhigh in the reactivity series | Accept words with equivalent meaningeg highly | 1\n | b | i | B (stage 2) |  | 1\n |  | ii | calcium chloride / CaCl2 | If both name and formula given, markname only | 1\n |  | iii | (they / the ions) are mobile | Accept free to moveAccept move to electrodes(allow even ifincorrect electrodes)Accept ions break free from lattice/crystalNot just freeAllow they/ions are delocalisedIgnore references to conduction | 1\n |  | iv | 2Cl-→Cl2+2e(-) | Accept 2Cl-→2e(-)→Cl2 | 1", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6", "c", "i", "M1M2", "Correct calculation of $ M_{r} $ ($ MgCl_{2} $ )M1 x 2", "Sample calculation:M1=95M2=190(kg)Accept 190000gM2 CQ on M1 when M1 is a genuine attempt to calculate $ M_{r} $ ($ MgCl_{2} $ )Correct answer with no working scores2", "2"], ["", "c", "", "Award 2 marks for 4000Award 1 mark if one error", "2000 (wrong ratio for Mg and electrons)4 (working in grams instead of kilograms)", "2"]], "text": "Question number |  | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 | c | i | M1M2 | Correct calculation of $ M_{r} $ ($ MgCl_{2} $ )M1 x 2 | Sample calculation:M1=95M2=190(kg)Accept 190000gM2 CQ on M1 when M1 is a genuine attempt to calculate $ M_{r} $ ($ MgCl_{2} $ )Correct answer with no working scores2 | 2\n | c |  | Award 2 marks for 4000Award 1 mark if one error | 2000 (wrong ratio for Mg and electrons)4 (working in grams instead of kilograms) | 2", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6", "d", "", "M1", "Mix magnesium oxide and sulfuric acid(and heat)", "If heated to dryness,no M4 or M5Allow place in a warm oven(to evaporate the excess water) to form crystals", "5"], ["M2", "Use excess MgO"], ["M3", "Filter(before heating to remove some water)"], ["M4", "Heat(the solution) to remove some water/for a short period of time"], ["M5", "Leave to crystallise"]], "text": "Question number |  | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 | d |  | M1 | Mix magnesium oxide and sulfuric acid(and heat) | If heated to dryness,no M4 or M5Allow place in a warm oven(to evaporate the excess water) to form crystals | 5\nM2 | Use excess MgO\nM3 | Filter(before heating to remove some water)\nM4 | Heat(the solution) to remove some water/for a short period of time\nM5 | Leave to crystallise", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 5, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "edexcel", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000001", "e000002", "e000003", "e000004", "e000005"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000007"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000009", "e000010"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "2514b013-6d3a-5028-b8c3-edfd1301f48d", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:58:49.208501152Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 65, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2015", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Certificate Chemistry (KCH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chemistry (4CHO) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2015 Publications Code UG041072 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2015", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:09.364594+00');
