this test.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000088", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 88, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3 = 9 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000089", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 89, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000090", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 90, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "4 A student investigates electrolysis using this apparatus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000091", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 91, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The student electrolyses KCl(aq) and collects samples of any gases formed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000093", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 93, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Complete the following diagram to show how to assemble the apparatus. Label the diagram to show the potassium chloride solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000094", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 94, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The table shows the half-equation for the reaction at one electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000096", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 96, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Complete the table to show the half-equation for the reaction at the other electrode and the polarity (+ or -) of each electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000097", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 97, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Describe a test to show that the gas collected is hydrogen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000099", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 99, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000100", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 100, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "5 Potassium and lithium are Group 1 metals that exist as isotopes.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000101", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 101, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) (i) Complete the table of information about two isotopes of potassium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000102", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 102, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) A sample of lithium has this percentage composition by mass.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000104", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 104, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use this information to calculate the relative atomic mass of lithium. Give your answer to one decimal place.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000106", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 106, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "relative atomic mass of lithium=", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000107", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 107, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) A reaction occurs when a small piece of potassium is added to water in a trough. State two observations that could be made during the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000108", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 108, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) A few drops of phenolphthalein are added to the liquid in the trough at the end of the reaction. A colour change occurs.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000109", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 109, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State the final colour of the liquid in the trough.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000110", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 110, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give the formula of the ion formed during the reaction that causes this colour change.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000111", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 111, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) The electronic configurations of lithium and potassium are Li 2,1 K 2,8,8,1", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000112", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 112, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain why potassium is more reactive than lithium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000113", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 113, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 11 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000114", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 114, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "6 Lithium hydroxide (LiOH) and lithium peroxide $ \\left( \\mathrm{L i}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2} \\right) $ have been used in spacecraft to remove the carbon dioxide astronauts breathe out.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000115", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 115, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equations for the reactions with carbon dioxide are", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000116", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 116, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Explain, with reference to these equations, two advantages of using lithium peroxide rather than lithium hydroxide, to remove carbon dioxide from the air in a spacecraft.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000119", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 119, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) (i) Calculate the mass of lithium hydroxide needed to react with 100 g of carbon dioxide. $ [ M_{r} $ of $ \\mathrm{L i O H}=2 4 ] $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000120", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 120, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Calculate the volume of carbon dioxide, at room temperature and pressure, removed by 100 g of lithium peroxide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000121", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 121, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "[M $ _{r} $ of $ \\mathrm{L i}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}=4 6 $]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000122", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 122, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Assume that one mole of gas has a volume of 24000 $ cm^{3} $ at rtp.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000123", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 123, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "7 This question is about the laboratory preparation of salts.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000124", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 124, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) A student writes this plan for preparing a sample of hydrated magnesium sulfate crystals.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000125", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 125, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step1 Pour about 100 $ cm^{3} $ of dilute nitric acid into a 250 $ cm^{3} $ beaker.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000126", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 126, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step 2 Add a solution of magnesium carbonate to the acid until there is no more effervescence.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000127", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 127, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "step 3 Heat the solution until all of the water has boiled off.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000128", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 128, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This plan will not succeed because there is one mistake in each step. Identify the mistake in each of the steps.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000129", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 129, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Another student uses the following plan to prepare a sample of ammonium hydrogenphosphate, formed in this reaction between aqueous ammonia and dilute phosphoric acid", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000130", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 130, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "use a pipette to transfer 25.0 $ cm^{3} $ of phosphoric acid to a conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000132", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 132, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add 3 drops of indicator", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000133", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 133, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "use a burette to add aqueous ammonia until the indicator just changes colour permanently", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000134", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 134, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) The diagram shows the burette readings in one experiment before and after adding aqueous ammonia.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000135", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 135, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use the readings to complete the table, entering all values to the nearest 0.05 $ cm^{3}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000138", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 138, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) In another titration, the student made a mistake. After he filled the burette, he noticed that the space between the tap of the burette and the tip contained air. After adding the aqueous ammonia, he noticed that it now contained liquid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000140", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 140, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain how, if at all, this mistake affects the calculated volume of aqueous ammonia added.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000141", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 141, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) He repeats the experiment until he obtains concordant results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000142", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 142, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows the results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000143", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 143, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Concordant results are those volumes that differ from each other by 0.20 $ cm^{3} $ or less.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000145", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 145, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Identify the concordant results by placing ticks ( $ \\checkmark $ ) in the table where appropriate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000146", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 146, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Use the concordant results to calculate the average (mean) volume of aqueous ammonia added.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000147", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 147, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "average volume of aqueous ammonia = ... $ \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000148", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 148, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) The student then mixed the volumes of aqueous ammonia and phosphoric acid found in the titration.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000149", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 149, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Describe how to use the method of crystallisation to obtain a pure dry sample of the salt from this mixture.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000150", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 150, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7 = 14 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000151", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 151, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "TOTAL FOR PAPER = 60 MARKS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000152", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 152, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000153", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 153, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Every effort has been made to contact copyright holders to obtain their permission for the use of copyright material. Pearson Education Ltd. will, if notified, be happy to rectify any errors or omissions and include any such rectifications in future editions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000154", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 154, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:55.775706+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('1ab38c26-1eff-4a79-975d-c4b4fb6e924f', 'd677a959-1285-5cd8-afcc-e9f44438314a', '1.0', 1, 'MARK_SCHEME', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2016junr/MS.md', 'MS.md', 'text/markdown', '1cb8718120203461cd919a520fe2e5ee18ed47ac7278bf3c7e6ad1afea1b5ed2', 'SHA-256', 1, 28, 28, 10, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 12:59:34.382405+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2016junr/MS.md", "checksum": "1cb8718120203461cd919a520fe2e5ee18ed47ac7278bf3c7e6ad1afea1b5ed2", "fileName": "MS.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["1 a\nb", "A", "(the crystal dissolves)", "", "1"], ["A", "(it is all blue)", "", "1"], ["c i\nii", "4", "", "", "1"], ["21", "", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n1 a\nb | A | (the crystal dissolves) |  | 1\nA | (it is all blue) |  | 1\nc i\nii | 4 |  |  | 1\n21 |  |  | 1", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["2 a", "M1 oxygen/air", "ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{O_{2}} $ but not O", "2"], ["M2 water(vapour)/moisture", "ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{H_{2}O} $ IGNORE steam"], ["b", "(hydrated) iron(III) oxide", "ACCEPT iron oxide/ferric oxide REJECT ferrous oxide and iron with other oxidation numbers IGNORE iron trioxide ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{Fe_{2}O_{3}} $ (.xH2O) IGNORE all other formulae If both name and formula given mark name only", "1"], ["c", "M1 (galvanising)", "bucket/car body/railway bridge", "DO NOT AWARD M3 for car body/railway bridge if already scored for M1", "3"], ["M2 (oiling)", "bicycle chain/car engine"], ["M3 (painting)", "car body/railway bridge"], ["d", "M1 zinc corrodes/oxidises/reacts in preference to iron", "REJECT zinc rusts IGNORE reference to sacrificial protection ACCEPT for M1 zinc atoms react with iron(II) ions", "2"], ["M2 (because) zinc is more reactive than iron/zinc (atoms) lose electrons more readily (than do iron atoms)", "ACCEPT for M2 iron(II) ions are converted to iron atoms"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n2 a | M1 oxygen/air | ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{O_{2}} $ but not O | 2\nM2 water(vapour)/moisture | ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{H_{2}O} $ IGNORE steam\nb | (hydrated) iron(III) oxide | ACCEPT iron oxide/ferric oxide REJECT ferrous oxide and iron with other oxidation numbers IGNORE iron trioxide ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{Fe_{2}O_{3}} $ (.xH2O) IGNORE all other formulae If both name and formula given mark name only | 1\nc | M1 (galvanising) | bucket/car body/railway bridge | DO NOT AWARD M3 for car body/railway bridge if already scored for M1 | 3\nM2 (oiling) | bicycle chain/car engine\nM3 (painting) | car body/railway bridge\nd | M1 zinc corrodes/oxidises/reacts in preference to iron | REJECT zinc rusts IGNORE reference to sacrificial protection ACCEPT for M1 zinc atoms react with iron(II) ions | 2\nM2 (because) zinc is more reactive than iron/zinc (atoms) lose electrons more readily (than do iron atoms) | ACCEPT for M2 iron(II) ions are converted to iron atoms", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3 a", "C (nitrogen)", "", "1"], ["b", "A (argon)", "", "1"], ["c", "M1 (formula) CuO\nM2 (colour) black", "ACCEPT correct formula as a product of an equation. The equation need not be balanced\nIGNORE names\nIGNORE brown\nREJECT all other colours", "2"], ["d i\nii\niii", "C (dilute hydrochloric acid)\nA (calcium carbonate)\nin a (gas) syringe / downward delivery in air", "ALLOW downward delivery", "1\n1\n1"], ["e i", "CO2(g)+Ca(OH)2(aq)→CaCO3(s)+H2O(l)", "ACCEPT upper case letters\nIGNORE words", "1"], ["e ii", "white precipitate forms / liquid goes milky/cloudy", "ACCEPT usual alternatives for precipitate", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3 a | C (nitrogen) |  | 1\nb | A (argon) |  | 1\nc | M1 (formula) CuO\nM2 (colour) black | ACCEPT correct formula as a product of an equation. The equation need not be balanced\nIGNORE names\nIGNORE brown\nREJECT all other colours | 2\nd i\nii\niii | C (dilute hydrochloric acid)\nA (calcium carbonate)\nin a (gas) syringe / downward delivery in air | ALLOW downward delivery | 1\n1\n1\ne i | CO2(g)+Ca(OH)2(aq)→CaCO3(s)+H2O(l) | ACCEPT upper case letters\nIGNORE words | 1\ne ii | white precipitate forms / liquid goes milky/cloudy | ACCEPT usual alternatives for precipitate | 1", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4 a", "potassium chloride solution\nbattery", "M1 both bungs inserted AND electrodes connected to battery\nM2 both tubes inverted over electrodes\nM3 solution placed in the voltameter and labelled as potassium chloride/KCl(aq)\nFor M3, ignore all three liquid levels, except that the level in the voltameter must be above the bottoms of both tubes if present", "3"], ["b", "Polarity Equation", "M1 for $2\\text{Cl}^{-}\\rightarrow\\text{Cl}_{2}+2\\text{e}^{(-)}$\nACCEPT $2\\text{Cl}^{-}-2\\text{e}^{(-)}\\rightarrow\\text{Cl}_{2}$", "2"], ["-(ve)", "$(2\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}+2\\text{e}^{-}\\rightarrow\\text{H}_{2}+2\\text{OH}^{-})$", "M2 for -(ve) in top row AND +(ve) in bottom row\nACCEPT negative and positive\nIGNORE cathode and anode", ""], ["+(ve)", "$2\\text{Cl}^{-}\\rightarrow\\text{Cl}_{2}+2\\text{e}^{(-)}$", "", ""], ["c", "burns with a pop/squeak\nOR\nuse burning/lit spill/use flame to see if pop/squeak", "Must be reference to test and result\nReference to spill/match with no indication of flame is not enough\nACCEPT splint for spill\nREJECT reference to glowing spill/splint\nIgnore flame extinguished\n''Squeaky pop test'' alone is not sufficient", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4 a | potassium chloride solution\nbattery | M1 both bungs inserted AND electrodes connected to battery\nM2 both tubes inverted over electrodes\nM3 solution placed in the voltameter and labelled as potassium chloride/KCl(aq)\nFor M3, ignore all three liquid levels, except that the level in the voltameter must be above the bottoms of both tubes if present | 3\nb | Polarity Equation | M1 for $2\\text{Cl}^{-}\\rightarrow\\text{Cl}_{2}+2\\text{e}^{(-)}$\nACCEPT $2\\text{Cl}^{-}-2\\text{e}^{(-)}\\rightarrow\\text{Cl}_{2}$ | 2\n-(ve) | $(2\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}+2\\text{e}^{-}\\rightarrow\\text{H}_{2}+2\\text{OH}^{-})$ | M2 for -(ve) in top row AND +(ve) in bottom row\nACCEPT negative and positive\nIGNORE cathode and anode | \n+(ve) | $2\\text{Cl}^{-}\\rightarrow\\text{Cl}_{2}+2\\text{e}^{(-)}$ |  | \nc | burns with a pop/squeak\nOR\nuse burning/lit spill/use flame to see if pop/squeak | Must be reference to test and result\nReference to spill/match with no indication of flame is not enough\nACCEPT splint for spill\nREJECT reference to glowing spill/splint\nIgnore flame extinguished\n''Squeaky pop test'' alone is not sufficient | 1", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5 a iii", "Atomic number", "Mass number", "Number of protons", "Number of neutrons", "M1 for 19 protons in top row AND atomic number of 19M2 for 20 neutrons in top rowM3 for mass number of 41ACCEPT(6×7.4)+(7×92.6)100Answer must be to 1 dpCorrect final answer without working scores 2 marks", "3"], ["", "", "19", "20", "2"], ["19", "41", "", "", ""], ["M1(6×0.074)+(7×0.926)M2=6.9", ""], ["b", "any two from\n• effervescence/fizzing/bubbles\n• potassium moves/darts/floats\n• potassium leaves white trail\n• potassium forms into a ball\n• potassium becomes smaller/disappears\n• (lilac) flame", "ACCEPT(hydrogen) gas given off/evolved/formed/producedIGNOREname of gasACCEPTmeltsACCEPTdissolvesIGNOREcolour of flame/explodes", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5 a iii | Atomic number | Mass number | Number of protons | Number of neutrons | M1 for 19 protons in top row AND atomic number of 19M2 for 20 neutrons in top rowM3 for mass number of 41ACCEPT(6×7.4)+(7×92.6)100Answer must be to 1 dpCorrect final answer without working scores 2 marks | 3\n |  | 19 | 20 | 2\n19 | 41 |  |  | \nM1(6×0.074)+(7×0.926)M2=6.9 | \nb | any two from\n• effervescence/fizzing/bubbles\n• potassium moves/darts/floats\n• potassium leaves white trail\n• potassium forms into a ball\n• potassium becomes smaller/disappears\n• (lilac) flame | ACCEPT(hydrogen) gas given off/evolved/formed/producedIGNOREname of gasACCEPTmeltsACCEPTdissolvesIGNOREcolour of flame/explodes | 2", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5 c iii", "pink", "ALLOW red\nIGNORE purple", "1"], ["OH-/HO-", "", "1"], ["d", "M1 potassium loses its outer/valence electron more easily/readily", "", "2"], ["M2 because it is further from (the attraction of) nucleus (and therefore less strongly attracted to the nucleus)", "IGNORE references to more shells/larger atomic radius/more shielding/more screening"], ["ACCEPT reverse arguments as long as it is clear that lithium is being considered"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5 c iii | pink | ALLOW red\nIGNORE purple | 1\nOH-/HO- |  | 1\nd | M1 potassium loses its outer/valence electron more easily/readily |  | 2\nM2 because it is further from (the attraction of) nucleus (and therefore less strongly attracted to the nucleus) | IGNORE references to more shells/larger atomic radius/more shielding/more screening\nACCEPT reverse arguments as long as it is clear that lithium is being considered", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6 a", "M1 twice as much/more carbon dioxide removed(per mole reacted)", "", "2"], ["M2 produces oxygen(for breathing)", "ACCEPT reverse arguments for bothM1andM2eg lithium hydroxide removes lessCO2and does not produce oxygen scores2IGNORE references to the need to remove water in reaction1"], ["b i", "M1n(CO2)=100OR2.27(27...)(mol)", "", "3"], ["M2n(LiOH)=answer toM1x2OR4.54(54...)(mol)", ""], ["M3m(LiOH)=(answer toM3x24)=110(g)", "ACCEPT any number of sig figs except oneeg109/109.1/109.09/109.0909..."], ["OR", "Award3marksforcorrectfinalanswerwithoutworking"], ["M148(g)reactswith44(g)", "108.96(from2.27)scores3marks"], ["M2x(g)reactswith100(g)", "110.4(from2.3)scores3marks"], ["M3x=110(g)", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 a | M1 twice as much/more carbon dioxide removed(per mole reacted) |  | 2\nM2 produces oxygen(for breathing) | ACCEPT reverse arguments for bothM1andM2eg lithium hydroxide removes lessCO2and does not produce oxygen scores2IGNORE references to the need to remove water in reaction1\nb i | M1n(CO2)=100OR2.27(27...)(mol) |  | 3\nM2n(LiOH)=answer toM1x2OR4.54(54...)(mol) | \nM3m(LiOH)=(answer toM3x24)=110(g) | ACCEPT any number of sig figs except oneeg109/109.1/109.09/109.0909...\nOR | Award3marksforcorrectfinalanswerwithoutworking\nM148(g)reactswith44(g) | 108.96(from2.27)scores3marks\nM2x(g)reactswith100(g) | 110.4(from2.3)scores3marks\nM3x=110(g) | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6 b ii", "M1 $n(\\mathrm{Li}_{2}\\mathrm{O}_{2})=\\frac{100}{46}=2.17(3913...)$ mol(= $n\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$)", "ACCEPT any number of sig figs except one eg 52170,52174,52173.9,etcAward 3 marks for correct final answer without working52080(from 2.17) scores 3 marks52800/53000(from 2.2) scores 3 marks", "3"], ["M2 volume of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ answer to M1 $\\times$ 24000"], ["M3 $= 52000(\\mathrm{cm}^{3})$"], [""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 b ii | M1 $n(\\mathrm{Li}_{2}\\mathrm{O}_{2})=\\frac{100}{46}=2.17(3913...)$ mol(= $n\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$) | ACCEPT any number of sig figs except one eg 52170,52174,52173.9,etcAward 3 marks for correct final answer without working52080(from 2.17) scores 3 marks52800/53000(from 2.2) scores 3 marks | 3\nM2 volume of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ answer to M1 $\\times$ 24000\nM3 $= 52000(\\mathrm{cm}^{3})$\n", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7 a", "M1(step 1)nitric acid", "ACCEPTsulfuric acid should be used", "3"], ["M2(step 2)magnesium carbonate is insoluble/magnesium carbonate does not form a solution", "REJECTthe use of reagents that would not work, eg magnesium chloride"], ["M3(step 3)boiling off all the water(will not produce a hydrated salt)"], ["7 b i", "M1(after)", "23.80", "If both readings are correct but in the wrong order, award 1 mark forM1andM2", "3"], ["M2(before)", "2.15", "M3CQ on the values given forM1andM2\nPenalise missing trailing zeros once only"], ["M3(volume added)", "21.65"], ["b ii", "M1(the calculated)volume will be higher", "", "2"], ["M2because it includes the air(contained in the tip of the burette)", "M2dep onM1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7 a | M1(step 1)nitric acid | ACCEPTsulfuric acid should be used | 3\nM2(step 2)magnesium carbonate is insoluble/magnesium carbonate does not form a solution | REJECTthe use of reagents that would not work, eg magnesium chloride\nM3(step 3)boiling off all the water(will not produce a hydrated salt)\n7 b i | M1(after) | 23.80 | If both readings are correct but in the wrong order, award 1 mark forM1andM2 | 3\nM2(before) | 2.15 | M3CQ on the values given forM1andM2\nPenalise missing trailing zeros once only\nM3(volume added) | 21.65\nb ii | M1(the calculated)volume will be higher |  | 2\nM2because it includes the air(contained in the tip of the burette) | M2dep onM1", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["c i", "ticks in columns 2 and 4", "", "1"], ["ii", "M1 26.45+26.25/2", "CQ on any combination of ticked results", ""], ["", "", "If no results are ticked then M1 can only be awarded if the values from columns 2 and 4 are averaged", ""], ["", "", "If only one column ticked then no marks can be awarded in(c)(ii)", "2"], ["", "M2 26.35(cm3)", "CQ on results averagedAnswers should be to 2dp, except trailing zero not needed", ""], ["", "", "Correct final answer without working scores 2", ""]], "text": "c i | ticks in columns 2 and 4 |  | 1\nii | M1 26.45+26.25/2 | CQ on any combination of ticked results | \n |  | If no results are ticked then M1 can only be awarded if the values from columns 2 and 4 are averaged | \n |  | If only one column ticked then no marks can be awarded in(c)(ii) | 2\n | M2 26.35(cm3) | CQ on results averagedAnswers should be to 2dp, except trailing zero not needed | \n |  | Correct final answer without working scores 2 | ", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7 d", "M1", "heat/boil until crystals form in a sample of solution that has been removed(and cooled)", "ACCEPT heat/boil to produce a(hot) saturated/concentrated solutionACCEPT heat until crystals start/begin to formALLOW(heat/boil to) evaporate some of the waterALLOW heat/boil to crystallisation pointIGNORE references to filtering before heating", "3"], ["M2", "leave(the solution) to cool(so that crystals form)", "M2 dep onM1"], ["M3", "filter(to obtain crystals)ANDsuitable method of drying crystals", "ACCEPT decant/pour off the liquid/(excess)solution for filtereg place in(warm) oven/leave to dry(in warm place)/use filter paper/use kitchen towelREJECT any reference to heating directly with a flame,eg with a BunsenIGNORE reference to washing crystalsM3 dep onM1If M1 not scored then award1 mark out of3 for leaving the solution until the water evaporates fully"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7 d | M1 | heat/boil until crystals form in a sample of solution that has been removed(and cooled) | ACCEPT heat/boil to produce a(hot) saturated/concentrated solutionACCEPT heat until crystals start/begin to formALLOW(heat/boil to) evaporate some of the waterALLOW heat/boil to crystallisation pointIGNORE references to filtering before heating | 3\nM2 | leave(the solution) to cool(so that crystals form) | M2 dep onM1\nM3 | filter(to obtain crystals)ANDsuitable method of drying crystals | ACCEPT decant/pour off the liquid/(excess)solution for filtereg place in(warm) oven/leave to dry(in warm place)/use filter paper/use kitchen towelREJECT any reference to heating directly with a flame,eg with a BunsenIGNORE reference to washing crystalsM3 dep onM1If M1 not scored then award1 mark out of3 for leaving the solution until the water evaporates fully", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000004"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006", "e000007"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "d677a959-1285-5cd8-afcc-e9f44438314a", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:59:34.382404796Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 90, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2016", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2016 Publications Code 4CH0_2CR_1606_MS All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2016", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:55.876534+00');
