acted", "1"], ["", "", "Total", "7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a)(i) | M10.080 mol of HCl react with 0.040 mol of MgCO3 | ACCEPT any method involving correct ratios of moles, egHCl to MgCO3 is 2:10.08 to 0.05 is 2:1.25 | 2\nM20.050>0.040 | ACCEPT correct calculations involving masses | 2\n(ii) | M1n(CO2)=1/2x0.08(0)OR0.04(0)M2vol(CO2)=(0.04(0)x24000)=960(cm3)ORM1×24000 correctly evaluated | Correct answer with no working scores21920(cm3) scores1 mark | \n(b)(i) | M1Mr(MgCl2.6H2O)=203M2% yield=((5.5÷(203×0.050))×100=54 | M2CSQ onM1ACCEPT any number of significant figures except one(eg reject50)Calculator value is54.1871921182REJECT answers>100 | 2\n(ii) | Any one of:some of the crystals remained in the filtrate(after cooling and filtration)the solution was not allowed to cool for long enough(for complete crystallisation)magnesium carbonate is impure | IGNORE references to side reactionsREJECT not all of the magnesium carbonate reacted | 1\n |  | Total | 7", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(a)", "M1rate of forward reaction=rate of backward reaction", "IGNOREforward reaction=backward reaction", "2"], ["M2concentrations of reactants/products remain/stay constant", "ACCEPTamounts/masses for concentrationsACCEPTdo not change for remain constantALLOWcolour remains constantALLOWpressure remains constantIGNOREconcentrations/amounts of reactants and products are the same/are equal", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(a) | M1rate of forward reaction=rate of backward reaction | IGNOREforward reaction=backward reaction | 2\nM2concentrations of reactants/products remain/stay constant | ACCEPTamounts/masses for concentrationsACCEPTdo not change for remain constantALLOWcolour remains constantALLOWpressure remains constantIGNOREconcentrations/amounts of reactants and products are the same/are equal | ", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(b)(i)", "Number of moles\nOR\nTime\ncross drawn on either curve just where it becomes horizontal", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1 curve starts at 0,0 and has the general shape shown\nM2 curve becomes horizontal at approximately the same time as the original curve\nM3 curve finishes below original curve", "M2 and M3 DEP on M1 or near miss (eg curve does not start at exactly 0,0)", "3"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(b)(i) | Number of moles\nOR\nTime\ncross drawn on either curve just where it becomes horizontal |  | 1\n(ii) | M1 curve starts at 0,0 and has the general shape shown\nM2 curve becomes horizontal at approximately the same time as the original curve\nM3 curve finishes below original curve | M2 and M3 DEP on M1 or near miss (eg curve does not start at exactly 0,0) | 3", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(c)", "M1 equilibrium has shifted to the left/equilibrium has shifted to the NO2 side/equilibrium has shifted to the reactants side", "IGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle eg an increase in temperature favours the reaction that reduces the temperature", "2"], ["OR more NO2 has been produced/more reactants have been produced", "ACCEPT (forward) reaction is exothermic", ""], ["M2 (therefore) backward reaction is endothermic", "", ""], ["", "", "Total", "8"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(c) | M1 equilibrium has shifted to the left/equilibrium has shifted to the NO2 side/equilibrium has shifted to the reactants side | IGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle eg an increase in temperature favours the reaction that reduces the temperature | 2\nOR more NO2 has been produced/more reactants have been produced | ACCEPT (forward) reaction is exothermic | \nM2 (therefore) backward reaction is endothermic |  | \n |  | Total | 8", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [{"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_2_1789064008864.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_2_1789064008864.png", "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "figure", "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Mark Scheme (Results) January 2017", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000002", "e000003"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "3225cbae-c9a2-569f-8acc-9c1e84a10e55", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:59:35.004986380Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 76, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 5, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results) January 2017", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "International GCSE Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel Certificate in Chemistry (KCH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2017 Publications Code 4CH0_2C_1701_MS All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2017", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:56.184732+00');
