"ACCEPT same number of electrons\nIGNORE same atomic number", "2"], ["M2(different) number of neutrons", "IGNORE relative atomic mass\nIGNORE different mass number"], ["", "", "Total", "5"]], "text": "(b) | M1(same) number of protons | ACCEPT same number of electrons\nIGNORE same atomic number | 2\nM2(different) number of neutrons | IGNORE relative atomic mass\nIGNORE different mass number\n |  | Total | 5", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["2(a)", "M1 bubbles(of gas)/effervescence", "ACCEPT fizzing", "2"], ["M2 magnesium disappears/magnesium gets smaller", "ACCEPT magnesium dissolves", ""], ["ALLOW solid for magnesium", ""], ["IGNORE reference to movement", ""], ["IGNORE reference to temperature change", ""], ["(b) increases", "ACCEPT gets hotter", "1"], ["(c) magnesium+(dilute)sulfuric acid→magnesium sulfate+hydrogen", "ALLOW chemical equationIf both word and chemical equation given mark word equation only", "1"], ["", "", "Total", "4"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n2(a) | M1 bubbles(of gas)/effervescence | ACCEPT fizzing | 2\nM2 magnesium disappears/magnesium gets smaller | ACCEPT magnesium dissolves | \nALLOW solid for magnesium | \nIGNORE reference to movement | \nIGNORE reference to temperature change | \n(b) increases | ACCEPT gets hotter | 1\n(c) magnesium+(dilute)sulfuric acid→magnesium sulfate+hydrogen | ALLOW chemical equationIf both word and chemical equation given mark word equation only | 1\n |  | Total | 4", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(a)", "M1(A) hydrochloric acid/HCl(aq)\nM2(B) calcium carbonate/marble\n/limestone/chalk/CaCO3", "If both name and formula given, both must be correct.\nState symbol not needed, but penalise if incorrect\nIf both name and formula given, both must be correct", "2"], ["(b)", "(gas) syringe/downward delivery(in air)", "ACCEPT upward displacement of air", "1"], ["(c)(i)", "orange/yellow", "ACCEPT yellow-orange\nIGNORE shades or qualifiers,e.g. light", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1(name) carbonic acid\nM2(formula)H2CO3", "ALLOW as the only product of an equation", "2"], ["", "Total", "", "6"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(a) | M1(A) hydrochloric acid/HCl(aq)\nM2(B) calcium carbonate/marble\n/limestone/chalk/CaCO3 | If both name and formula given, both must be correct.\nState symbol not needed, but penalise if incorrect\nIf both name and formula given, both must be correct | 2\n(b) | (gas) syringe/downward delivery(in air) | ACCEPT upward displacement of air | 1\n(c)(i) | orange/yellow | ACCEPT yellow-orange\nIGNORE shades or qualifiers,e.g. light | 1\n(ii) | M1(name) carbonic acid\nM2(formula)H2CO3 | ALLOW as the only product of an equation | 2\n | Total |  | 6", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "hydrogen AND carbon", "ACCEPT in either order\nACCEPT C and H\nif both names and symbols given, mark name only", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "(a mixture of)\ncompounds/hydrocarbons/substances with similar boiling points", "REJECT elements\nREJECT same boiling points\nALLOW references to condense at similar temperatures\nALLOW references to similar carbon chain length\nIGNORE references to other physical properties e.g. viscosity\nIGNORE references to similar chemical properties", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | hydrogen AND carbon | ACCEPT in either order\nACCEPT C and H\nif both names and symbols given, mark name only | 1\n(b)(i) | (a mixture of)\ncompounds/hydrocarbons/substances with similar boiling points | REJECT elements\nREJECT same boiling points\nALLOW references to condense at similar temperatures\nALLOW references to similar carbon chain length\nIGNORE references to other physical properties e.g. viscosity\nIGNORE references to similar chemical properties | ", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(b)(ii)", "M1 vaporise/heat the crude oil", "ALLOW boil\nIGNORE distil\nIGNORE references to temperature", "3"], ["M2 pass vapour/gas into a (fractionating) column/tower", "", ""], ["M3 vapours/gases/fractions/hydrocarbons/substances condense at different heights/levels/points", "ALLOW collected for condense\nALLOW lower boiling point/more volatile substances\ncondense/collected higher up\nAND\nhigher boiling point/less volatile substances condense/collected lower down", ""], ["", "ALLOW shorter chain substances condense/collected higher up\nAND\nlonger chain substances condense/collected lower down\nIGNORE reference to melting points\nIf reference to cracking only M1 can be scored", ""]], "text": "Question | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(b)(ii) | M1 vaporise/heat the crude oil | ALLOW boil\nIGNORE distil\nIGNORE references to temperature | 3\nM2 pass vapour/gas into a (fractionating) column/tower |  | \nM3 vapours/gases/fractions/hydrocarbons/substances condense at different heights/levels/points | ALLOW collected for condense\nALLOW lower boiling point/more volatile substances\ncondense/collected higher up\nAND\nhigher boiling point/less volatile substances condense/collected lower down | \n | ALLOW shorter chain substances condense/collected higher up\nAND\nlonger chain substances condense/collected lower down\nIGNORE reference to melting points\nIf reference to cracking only M1 can be scored | ", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question", "Answer", "Notes", "marks"], ["4(c)(i)(ii)", "bitumengasoline", "", "11"], ["(d)(i)(ii)", "carbon monoxide(it is) poisonous/(it is) toxic/(it) reduces the capacity of the blood to carry oxygen", "ACCEPT COIf both name and formula given, mark name onlyACCEPT correct references to haemoglobin/carboxyhaemoglobinIGNORE references to suffocation", "11"], ["", "", "Total", "9"]], "text": "Question | Answer | Notes | marks\n4(c)(i)(ii) | bitumengasoline |  | 11\n(d)(i)(ii) | carbon monoxide(it is) poisonous/(it is) toxic/(it) reduces the capacity of the blood to carry oxygen | ACCEPT COIf both name and formula given, mark name onlyACCEPT correct references to haemoglobin/carboxyhaemoglobinIGNORE references to suffocation | 11\n |  | Total | 9", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)(i)(ii)", "46.6(g)as temperature increases, solubility decreases", "Ignore trailing zeros e.g. accept 46.60ACCEPT reverse argumentIGNORE any reference to inverse proportionalityREJECT reference to (direct) proportionalityALLOW references to negative correlation", "11"], ["(b)", "M1 use a fume cupboardM2 (because) ammonia is toxic/poisonous", "ALLOW carry out in a well-ventilated areaIGNORE reference to lab coats/goggles/(gas) masks/glovesIGNORE do not inhale fumesIGNORE dangerous/harmful/irritant", "2"], ["(c)", "water evaporates (more quickly)/ammonia escapes (as it is less soluble in hot water)", "ALLOW (ammonia) solution evaporatesIGNORE ammonia evaporates", "1"], ["(d)", "measure the pH (of the solution using universal indicator or pH meter)OR titrate with acid", "", "1"], ["", "", "Total", "6"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a)(i)(ii) | 46.6(g)as temperature increases, solubility decreases | Ignore trailing zeros e.g. accept 46.60ACCEPT reverse argumentIGNORE any reference to inverse proportionalityREJECT reference to (direct) proportionalityALLOW references to negative correlation | 11\n(b) | M1 use a fume cupboardM2 (because) ammonia is toxic/poisonous | ALLOW carry out in a well-ventilated areaIGNORE reference to lab coats/goggles/(gas) masks/glovesIGNORE do not inhale fumesIGNORE dangerous/harmful/irritant | 2\n(c) | water evaporates (more quickly)/ammonia escapes (as it is less soluble in hot water) | ALLOW (ammonia) solution evaporatesIGNORE ammonia evaporates | 1\n(d) | measure the pH (of the solution using universal indicator or pH meter)OR titrate with acid |  | 1\n |  | Total | 6", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)", "M1(method 1)zymase", "ACCEPT yeast", "2"], ["M2(method 2)phosphoric acid/H3PO4", "If both name and formula given, mark name only", ""], ["(b)", "M1company A chooses method 1/fermentation AND company B chooses method 2/ethene with steam/hydration", "", "4"], ["M2company A has(access to)a supply of sugar(cane)/glucose", "", ""], ["M3company B can obtain ethene from crude oil/an oil refinery", "", ""], ["M4company A does not need pure ethanol/company B does need pure ethanol", "IGNORE company A only needs a dilute solution of ethanolIGNORE references to batch/continuous processes", ""], ["(c)(i)", "Chemical structure", "M1one correct repeat unit drawn with continuation bonds e.g.HCCHnor-CH2-CH2-M2rest of diagram correct ie brackets and balanced using n", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a) | M1(method 1)zymase | ACCEPT yeast | 2\nM2(method 2)phosphoric acid/H3PO4 | If both name and formula given, mark name only | \n(b) | M1company A chooses method 1/fermentation AND company B chooses method 2/ethene with steam/hydration |  | 4\nM2company A has(access to)a supply of sugar(cane)/glucose |  | \nM3company B can obtain ethene from crude oil/an oil refinery |  | \nM4company A does not need pure ethanol/company B does need pure ethanol | IGNORE company A only needs a dilute solution of ethanolIGNORE references to batch/continuous processes | \n(c)(i) | Chemical structure | M1one correct repeat unit drawn with continuation bonds e.g.HCCHnor-CH2-CH2-M2rest of diagram correct ie brackets and balanced using n | 2", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "C12H26", "ALLOW n in any position after bracket but not before M2 DEP M1", ""], ["(iii)", "crude oil is a finite/limited resource OR ethanol can be made from sugar (cane)/glucose which is a renewable resource", "ALLOW crude oil is non-renewable IGNORE reference to high/increasing demand for ethene", ""], ["", "", "Total", "10"]], "text": "(ii) | C12H26 | ALLOW n in any position after bracket but not before M2 DEP M1 | \n(iii) | crude oil is a finite/limited resource OR ethanol can be made from sugar (cane)/glucose which is a renewable resource | ALLOW crude oil is non-renewable IGNORE reference to high/increasing demand for ethene | \n |  | Total | 10", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "M1 polystyrene is a better insulator", "ALLOW polystyrene is an insulator", "2"], ["M2 so less heat(energy)/thermal energy is transferred/lost to the surroundings/atmosphere/air", "REJECT no heat loss to the surroundings", ""], ["(b)", "M1(before)18.6(0℃)", "one mark for correct answers in the wrong order", "2"], ["M2(after)22.8(0℃)", "Ignore trailing zeros e.g. accept 18.60", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | M1 polystyrene is a better insulator | ALLOW polystyrene is an insulator | 2\nM2 so less heat(energy)/thermal energy is transferred/lost to the surroundings/atmosphere/air | REJECT no heat loss to the surroundings | \n(b) | M1(before)18.6(0℃) | one mark for correct answers in the wrong order | 2\nM2(after)22.8(0℃) | Ignore trailing zeros e.g. accept 18.60 | ", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(c)(i)", "Highest temperature of mixture in $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $\nvolume of aqueous sodium hydroxide in $ \\mathrm{cm}^{3} $\nM1 and M2 all points plotted correctly to the nearest gridline\nM3 best fit straight line through first 3 points drawn with the aid of a ruler\nM4 best fit straight line through last 3 points drawn with the aid of a ruler", "deduct one mark for each incorrectly plotted point\nALLOW M3 and M4 even if lines do not intersect\nPenalise lack of use of a ruler once only", "4"]], "text": "Question | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(c)(i) | Highest temperature of mixture in $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $\nvolume of aqueous sodium hydroxide in $ \\mathrm{cm}^{3} $\nM1 and M2 all points plotted correctly to the nearest gridline\nM3 best fit straight line through first 3 points drawn with the aid of a ruler\nM4 best fit straight line through last 3 points drawn with the aid of a ruler | deduct one mark for each incorrectly plotted point\nALLOW M3 and M4 even if lines do not intersect\nPenalise lack of use of a ruler once only | 4", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(c)(ii)", "M1(sodium hydroxide) expected value37-38cm3", "mark CSQ on candidates graphread to nearest gridline", "2"], ["M2(hydrochloric acid)(100-M1) expected value63-62cm3"], ["(iii)", "sodium hydroxide(has the greater concentration because)", "ALLOW hydrochloric acidhas the lower concentration because the volume of hydrochloric acid required is more(than the volume of hydrochloric acid required)", "2"], ["M1 sodium hydroxide and hydrochloric acid react in a1:1(molar) ratio"], ["M2 the volume of sodium hydroxide required is less(than the volume of hydrochloric acid required)"], ["", "", "Total", "12"]], "text": "Question | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(c)(ii) | M1(sodium hydroxide) expected value37-38cm3 | mark CSQ on candidates graphread to nearest gridline | 2\nM2(hydrochloric acid)(100-M1) expected value63-62cm3\n(iii) | sodium hydroxide(has the greater concentration because) | ALLOW hydrochloric acidhas the lower concentration because the volume of hydrochloric acid required is more(than the volume of hydrochloric acid required) | 2\nM1 sodium hydroxide and hydrochloric acid react in a1:1(molar) ratio\nM2 the volume of sodium hydroxide required is less(than the volume of hydrochloric acid required)\n |  | Total | 12", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(ii)", "M1 0.02350x0.0200", "do not penalise missing trailing zeros", "2"], ["M2 0.000470/4.70x10-4(mol)", "0.0005 scores 1/2", ""], ["", "ACCEPT 0.47 for 1 mark\nCorrect answer without working scores 2", ""], ["M1 M2 from(i)÷0.0250/(0.000470)÷0.0250", "do not penalise missing trailing zeros", "2"], ["M2 0.0188(mol/dm3)", "ACCEPT any number of sig fig except one", ""], ["OR", "Correct answer without working scores 2", ""], ["M1 M2 from(i)x1000/25", "", ""], ["M2 0.0188(mol/dm3)", "", ""], ["OR", "", ""], ["M1(23.5÷25.0)x0.0200", "", ""], ["M2 0.0188(mol/dm3)", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(ii) | M1 0.02350x0.0200 | do not penalise missing trailing zeros | 2\nM2 0.000470/4.70x10-4(mol) | 0.0005 scores 1/2 | \n | ACCEPT 0.47 for 1 mark\nCorrect answer without working scores 2 | \nM1 M2 from(i)÷0.0250/(0.000470)÷0.0250 | do not penalise missing trailing zeros | 2\nM2 0.0188(mol/dm3) | ACCEPT any number of sig fig except one | \nOR | Correct answer without working scores 2 | \nM1 M2 from(i)x1000/25 |  | \nM2 0.0188(mol/dm3) |  | \nOR |  | \nM1(23.5÷25.0)x0.0200 |  | \nM2 0.0188(mol/dm3) |  | ", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["8(b)", "M1heat/boil until crystals form in a sample of solution that has been removed and cooled", "ACCEPT heat/boil to produce a (hot) saturated/concentrated solution\nACCEPT heat/boil until crystals start/begin to form\nALLOW (heat/boil to) evaporate some of the water\nALLOW heat/boil to crystallisation point\nIGNORE references to filtering before heating", "4"], ["M2cool/leave (the solution) until crystals have formed", "M2 DEP on M1", ""], ["M3filter (to remove the crystals)\nAND\nwash with (a little deionised/distilled) water", "ACCEPT decant/pour off the liquid/(excess solution)", ""], ["M4suitable method of drying the crystals", "M3 dep on crystals having been formed\ne.g. place in (warm) oven / leave to dry (in warm place) / use filter paper / use kitchen towel\nREJECT any reference to heating directly with a flame, e.g. with a Bunsen\nIf M1 not scored then award 1 mark out of 4 for leaving the solution until the water evaporates fully OR for evaporating solution to dryness", ""], ["", "Total", "8"]], "text": "8(b) | M1heat/boil until crystals form in a sample of solution that has been removed and cooled | ACCEPT heat/boil to produce a (hot) saturated/concentrated solution\nACCEPT heat/boil until crystals start/begin to form\nALLOW (heat/boil to) evaporate some of the water\nALLOW heat/boil to crystallisation point\nIGNORE references to filtering before heating | 4\nM2cool/leave (the solution) until crystals have formed | M2 DEP on M1 | \nM3filter (to remove the crystals)\nAND\nwash with (a little deionised/distilled) water | ACCEPT decant/pour off the liquid/(excess solution) | \nM4suitable method of drying the crystals | M3 dep on crystals having been formed\ne.g. place in (warm) oven / leave to dry (in warm place) / use filter paper / use kitchen towel\nREJECT any reference to heating directly with a flame, e.g. with a Bunsen\nIf M1 not scored then award 1 mark out of 4 for leaving the solution until the water evaporates fully OR for evaporating solution to dryness | \n | Total | 8", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [{"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_2_1789069493392.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_2_1789069493392.png", "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "figure", "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000002", "e000003"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000008"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "4f3e8b3c-78e8-5005-b586-cbe9d600cb5e", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:59:36.377187186Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 75, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2017", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:56.490595+00');
