, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)(i)", "C3H8O", "Penalise incorrect use of lowercase letters and subscriptsALLOW symbols in any order e.g. C3OH8REJECT C3H7OH", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1(correct as X) only contains single bondsM2(not correct as X) contains oxygen/OM3 hydrocarbon contains hydrogen/H and carbon/C only", "ALLOW no double bondsREJECT if they say it is unsaturatedIGNORE O2ALLOW(not correct as X) is an alcoholREJECT if they say it is a hydrocarbonREJECT hydrogen and carbon molecules", "3"], ["(b)", "Any one from:·have a general formula·successive members differ by CH2·trends in physical properties·same functional group", "IGNORE reference to chemical properties", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a)(i) | C3H8O | Penalise incorrect use of lowercase letters and subscriptsALLOW symbols in any order e.g. C3OH8REJECT C3H7OH | 1\n(ii) | M1(correct as X) only contains single bondsM2(not correct as X) contains oxygen/OM3 hydrocarbon contains hydrogen/H and carbon/C only | ALLOW no double bondsREJECT if they say it is unsaturatedIGNORE O2ALLOW(not correct as X) is an alcoholREJECT if they say it is a hydrocarbonREJECT hydrogen and carbon molecules | 3\n(b) | Any one from:·have a general formula·successive members differ by CH2·trends in physical properties·same functional group | IGNORE reference to chemical properties | 1", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(c)(i)", "catalyst", "ALLOW description of effect of catalyst e.g. to speed up the reaction/ to lower the activation energy\nIGNORE to dehydrate compound X", "1"], ["(ii)", "insoluble (in water)", "IGNORE reference to density\nALLOW (only) slightly soluble in water", "1"], ["(iii)", "contains air", "ALLOW contains oxygen\nIGNORE contains other gases", "1"], ["(iv)", "M1", "IGNORE bond angles\nALLOW H-O-H", ""], ["(v)", "M2 H2O\npropene", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(c)(i) | catalyst | ALLOW description of effect of catalyst e.g. to speed up the reaction/ to lower the activation energy\nIGNORE to dehydrate compound X | 1\n(ii) | insoluble (in water) | IGNORE reference to density\nALLOW (only) slightly soluble in water | 1\n(iii) | contains air | ALLOW contains oxygen\nIGNORE contains other gases | 1\n(iv) | M1 | IGNORE bond angles\nALLOW H-O-H | \n(v) | M2 H2O\npropene |  | 1", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)", "", "All three names must be correct", "1"], ["Fe", "iron", "", ""], ["Cr", "chromium", "", ""], ["O", "oxygen", "", ""], ["(b)(i)", "Cr2O3+2Al→Al2O3+2CrM1Al2O3M2 completely correct equation", "", "2"], ["(ii)", "M1 aluminium more reactive(than chromium)M2 as aluminium displaces chromium", "ORAALLOW aluminium higher in the reactivity series(than chromium)ALLOW aluminium removes the oxygen from chromium", "2"], ["(iii)", "Any two fromM1(redox means both) reduction and oxidation taking place(at same time)M2 chromium reduced and aluminium oxidisedM3 chromium(reduced as) loses oxygen and aluminium(oxidised as) gains oxygen", "ACCEPT chromium oxideACCEPT chromium oxideACCEPT chromium ions gain electrons(so reduced) and aluminium loses electrons(so oxidised)ALLOW answer in terms of oxidation number changes", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a) |  | All three names must be correct | 1\nFe | iron |  | \nCr | chromium |  | \nO | oxygen |  | \n(b)(i) | Cr2O3+2Al→Al2O3+2CrM1Al2O3M2 completely correct equation |  | 2\n(ii) | M1 aluminium more reactive(than chromium)M2 as aluminium displaces chromium | ORAALLOW aluminium higher in the reactivity series(than chromium)ALLOW aluminium removes the oxygen from chromium | 2\n(iii) | Any two fromM1(redox means both) reduction and oxidation taking place(at same time)M2 chromium reduced and aluminium oxidisedM3 chromium(reduced as) loses oxygen and aluminium(oxidised as) gains oxygen | ACCEPT chromium oxideACCEPT chromium oxideACCEPT chromium ions gain electrons(so reduced) and aluminium loses electrons(so oxidised)ALLOW answer in terms of oxidation number changes | 2", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(c)(i)", "M1 mol(Cr)=0.13/52=0.0025M2 vol H2=answer to M1x24=M3 0.06(0)dm3", "accept 60cm3If incorrect moles ofH2e.g.0.0025has been multiplied or divided by2,ECF toM3,i.e.0.03or0.12would score2marks", "3"], ["(ii)", "Any two fromM1(sample of) chromium impureM2 gas leakage(from apparatus)/some gas escaped(before the bung was inserted)M3 not enough/less than0.13g chromium used/did not use excess acidM4 reaction not allowed to go to completion/the volume was measured before reaction endedM5 some gas dissolved in the acid/solution", "", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(c)(i) | M1 mol(Cr)=0.13/52=0.0025M2 vol H2=answer to M1x24=M3 0.06(0)dm3 | accept 60cm3If incorrect moles ofH2e.g.0.0025has been multiplied or divided by2,ECF toM3,i.e.0.03or0.12would score2marks | 3\n(ii) | Any two fromM1(sample of) chromium impureM2 gas leakage(from apparatus)/some gas escaped(before the bung was inserted)M3 not enough/less than0.13g chromium used/did not use excess acidM4 reaction not allowed to go to completion/the volume was measured before reaction endedM5 some gas dissolved in the acid/solution |  | 2", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)(i)", "(24+16)=40", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "Li+andF-", "both needed", "1"], ["(b)", "Any four fromM1 strong(electrostatic)forces/attractionM2 between oppositely charged ionsM3 a large amount of energy needed to overcome attraction/break down lattice/break bondsM4(MgO higher melting point as) greater charge onMg2+(thanLi+)/greater charge onO2-(thanF-)M5EITHERso stronger attraction/forces/bonds(inMgO)ORmore(thermal/heat)energy required to overcome attraction/break down lattice/break the bonds(inMgO)/ORAMAX2if any reference to intermolecular forces/covalent bonding/electron sharing/molecules/metallic bonding", "ACCEPT strong(ionic)bondsMust be a comparison to gain M5MAX2if any reference to intermolecular forces/covalent bonding/electron sharing/molecules/metallic bonding", "4"], ["(c)", "M1(when)solid ions in fixed positions/don''t move/only vibrateM2(when)molten or in solution ions can move/mobile", "IGNORE electronsALLOW atomsREJECT electrons/atomsMAX1if mention of sharing of electrons/covalent bonding", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a)(i) | (24+16)=40 |  | 1\n(ii) | Li+andF- | both needed | 1\n(b) | Any four fromM1 strong(electrostatic)forces/attractionM2 between oppositely charged ionsM3 a large amount of energy needed to overcome attraction/break down lattice/break bondsM4(MgO higher melting point as) greater charge onMg2+(thanLi+)/greater charge onO2-(thanF-)M5EITHERso stronger attraction/forces/bonds(inMgO)ORmore(thermal/heat)energy required to overcome attraction/break down lattice/break the bonds(inMgO)/ORAMAX2if any reference to intermolecular forces/covalent bonding/electron sharing/molecules/metallic bonding | ACCEPT strong(ionic)bondsMust be a comparison to gain M5MAX2if any reference to intermolecular forces/covalent bonding/electron sharing/molecules/metallic bonding | 4\n(c) | M1(when)solid ions in fixed positions/don''t move/only vibrateM2(when)molten or in solution ions can move/mobile | IGNORE electronsALLOW atomsREJECT electrons/atomsMAX1if mention of sharing of electrons/covalent bonding | 2", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)(i)", "M1 oxidation is loss of electronsM2 chloride ions/Cl- lose electrons (so oxidised)", "REJECT chlorine/Cl/Cl2 loses electronsALLOW chloride loses electrons", "2"], ["(ii)", "2H2O+2e-→2OH-+H2M1 all correct speciesM2 correctly balancingM2 dep on M1", "ACCEPT multiples", "2"], ["(b)", "Cl2+2NaOH→NaCl+NaOCl+H2O", "ACCEPT multiples", "1"], ["(c)(i)", "M1 monomers join together/ double bonds broken(in monomers)M2 to form a long chain(molecule)/large molecule", "ALLOW link/add in place of join", "2"], ["(ii)", "[H]C[H]C[nH2]M1 correct repeat structureM2 brackets and continuation bonds and n", "No M1 if more than 1 repeat unit shownACCEPT n anywhere after the brackets but not beforeREJECT any structure with a double bond for both marks", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a)(i) | M1 oxidation is loss of electronsM2 chloride ions/Cl- lose electrons (so oxidised) | REJECT chlorine/Cl/Cl2 loses electronsALLOW chloride loses electrons | 2\n(ii) | 2H2O+2e-→2OH-+H2M1 all correct speciesM2 correctly balancingM2 dep on M1 | ACCEPT multiples | 2\n(b) | Cl2+2NaOH→NaCl+NaOCl+H2O | ACCEPT multiples | 1\n(c)(i) | M1 monomers join together/ double bonds broken(in monomers)M2 to form a long chain(molecule)/large molecule | ALLOW link/add in place of join | 2\n(ii) | [H]C[H]C[nH2]M1 correct repeat structureM2 brackets and continuation bonds and n | No M1 if more than 1 repeat unit shownACCEPT n anywhere after the brackets but not beforeREJECT any structure with a double bond for both marks | 2", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000008"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000010"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000021", "e000023", "e000025", "e000030", "e000032", "e000034"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "8bc45e9f-9a99-57e0-bd8e-0fbe78e3cb1d", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T12:59:37.089444256Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 53, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2018", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "In Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 6 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 8 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 6 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 12 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 8 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total 9 marks", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 12:59:56.701823+00');
