largest temperature rise/increase", "ECF on temperature changes recorded in table\nACCEPT(because it produces the) largest temperature change\nIGNORE reaches the highest final temperature", "2"], ["(c)", "C(exothermic)\nA is incorrect as decomposition is not the name given to reactions that release heat energy\nB is incorrect as endothermic reactions take in heat energy\nD is incorrect as reduction is not the name given to reactions that release heat energy", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n2(a) |  | All three must be correct\nIGNORE trailing zeroes | 1\nW | \nX | (+)10.3\nY | (+)15.9\nZ | (+)11.1\n(b) | M1 fuel Y\nM2(because it produces the) largest temperature rise/increase | ECF on temperature changes recorded in table\nACCEPT(because it produces the) largest temperature change\nIGNORE reaches the highest final temperature | 2\n(c) | C(exothermic)\nA is incorrect as decomposition is not the name given to reactions that release heat energy\nB is incorrect as endothermic reactions take in heat energy\nD is incorrect as reduction is not the name given to reactions that release heat energy | 1", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Mark"], ["3(a)(i)", "Burette reading after", "(20.80)", "Mark M2 CQ on M1If the answers are in the wrong order allow 1 mark", "2"], ["Burette reading before", "3.15"], ["Volume of acid added", "17.65"], ["M1 3.15M2 17.65"], ["(b)(i)", "", "All three columns must contain ticks", "1"], ["Volume of acid added", "26.25", "25.10", "25.75", "25.30", "25.20"], ["", "Concordant results", "", "√", "", "√", "√", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Mark\n3(a)(i) | Burette reading after | (20.80) | Mark M2 CQ on M1If the answers are in the wrong order allow 1 mark | 2\nBurette reading before | 3.15\nVolume of acid added | 17.65\nM1 3.15M2 17.65\n(b)(i) |  | All three columns must contain ticks | 1\nVolume of acid added | 26.25 | 25.10 | 25.75 | 25.30 | 25.20\n | Concordant results |  | √ |  | √ | √ |  | ", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Mark"], ["3(b)(ii)", "25.2(0)", "CQ on any combination of ticked results rounded correctlyIf no results are ticked then the mark can only be awarded for 25.2(0)If only one column ticked then no mark can be awarded in(b)(ii)ALLOW any number of figures after the decimal point,but answer must be given to at least one decimal place", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Mark\n3(b)(ii) | 25.2(0) | CQ on any combination of ticked results rounded correctlyIf no results are ticked then the mark can only be awarded for 25.2(0)If only one column ticked then no mark can be awarded in(b)(ii)ALLOW any number of figures after the decimal point,but answer must be given to at least one decimal place | 1", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "C(fluorine)\nA is incorrect as bromine is not the most reactive element. It is not as reactive as fluorine\nB is incorrect as chlorine is not the most reactive element. It is not as reactive as fluorine\nD is incorrect as iodine is the least reactive element of the four", "", "1"], ["(b)", "D(iodine)\nA is incorrect as bromine is a liquid at room temperature\nB is incorrect as chlorine is a gas at room temperature\nC is incorrect as fluorine is a gas at room temperature", "", "1"], ["(c)", "D(iodine)\nA is incorrect as bromine is brown and not as dark as iodine, which is dark grey\nB is incorrect as chlorine is pale green\nC is incorrect as fluorine is pale yellow", "", "1"], ["(d)", "M1 Σ(bonds broken) = 436+193\nOR 629(kJ/mol)\nM2 Σ(bonds made) = 2×366\nOR 732(kJ/mol)\nM3 ΔH=-103(kJ/mol)\nOR\nM1-M2 evaluated correctly with the correct sign", "IGNORE any signs in M1 and M2\nnegative sign required\n-103 with or without working scores 3\n(+)103 with or without working scores 2", "3"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | C(fluorine)\nA is incorrect as bromine is not the most reactive element. It is not as reactive as fluorine\nB is incorrect as chlorine is not the most reactive element. It is not as reactive as fluorine\nD is incorrect as iodine is the least reactive element of the four |  | 1\n(b) | D(iodine)\nA is incorrect as bromine is a liquid at room temperature\nB is incorrect as chlorine is a gas at room temperature\nC is incorrect as fluorine is a gas at room temperature |  | 1\n(c) | D(iodine)\nA is incorrect as bromine is brown and not as dark as iodine, which is dark grey\nB is incorrect as chlorine is pale green\nC is incorrect as fluorine is pale yellow |  | 1\n(d) | M1 Σ(bonds broken) = 436+193\nOR 629(kJ/mol)\nM2 Σ(bonds made) = 2×366\nOR 732(kJ/mol)\nM3 ΔH=-103(kJ/mol)\nOR\nM1-M2 evaluated correctly with the correct sign | IGNORE any signs in M1 and M2\nnegative sign required\n-103 with or without working scores 3\n(+)103 with or without working scores 2 | 3", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)(i)", "Yeast", "ALLOWzymaseIGNOREenzyme(s)", "1"], ["(ii)", "(C12H22O11+H2O\\rightarrow)2C6H12O6", "ACCEPTmultiples andfractionsIGNOREstate symbolseven if incorrect", "1"], ["(iii)", "C6H12O6\\rightarrow2C2H5OH+2CO2", "ACCEPTmultiples andfractionsIGNOREstate symbolseven if incorrectALLOWC2H6Ofor ethanol", "1"], ["(iv)", "C(fractional distillation)A is incorrect as you couldnot obtain ethanol by crystallisationB is incorrect as you couldnot obtain ethanol by filtrationD is incorrect as simpledistillation is not the mosteffective way to obtainethanol", "", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a)(i) | Yeast | ALLOWzymaseIGNOREenzyme(s) | 1\n(ii) | (C12H22O11+H2O\\rightarrow)2C6H12O6 | ACCEPTmultiples andfractionsIGNOREstate symbolseven if incorrect | 1\n(iii) | C6H12O6\\rightarrow2C2H5OH+2CO2 | ACCEPTmultiples andfractionsIGNOREstate symbolseven if incorrectALLOWC2H6Ofor ethanol | 1\n(iv) | C(fractional distillation)A is incorrect as you couldnot obtain ethanol by crystallisationB is incorrect as you couldnot obtain ethanol by filtrationD is incorrect as simpledistillation is not the mosteffective way to obtainethanol |  | 1", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(b)(i)", "phosphoric acid", "ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{H_{3}PO_{4}} $ If both name and formula given, mark name only\nREJECT phosphorus acid\nIGNORE reference to concentration", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1 300( $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $)", "ACCEPT any temperature, or range of temperatures, between 250 and 350 inclusive\nACCEPT temperatures in other units provided unit is given", "2"], ["", "M2 60-70(atm)", "ACCEPT any pressure or range of pressures between 60 and 70 inclusive\nACCEPT pressures in other units provided unit is given e.g. $ 6 \\times10^{6} $ Pa to $ 7 \\times10^{6} $ Pa", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(b)(i) | phosphoric acid | ACCEPT $ \\mathrm{H_{3}PO_{4}} $ If both name and formula given, mark name only\nREJECT phosphorus acid\nIGNORE reference to concentration | 1\n(ii) | M1 300( $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $) | ACCEPT any temperature, or range of temperatures, between 250 and 350 inclusive\nACCEPT temperatures in other units provided unit is given | 2\n | M2 60-70(atm) | ACCEPT any pressure or range of pressures between 60 and 70 inclusive\nACCEPT pressures in other units provided unit is given e.g. $ 6 \\times10^{6} $ Pa to $ 7 \\times10^{6} $ Pa | ", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(c)(i)", "dehydration", "ACCEPT(thermal) decomposition/elimination", "1"], ["(ii)", "(to act as a) catalyst", "ACCEPTto increase the rate of reaction\nIGNOREto lower the activation energy\nIGNOREreferences to increased surface area", "1"], ["(d)(i)", "(contains a carbon to carbon) double bond/C=C", "ALLOWmultiple bond", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1(from) orange", "ACCEPTbrown/yellow or any combination of orange/brown/yellow e.g. orange-brown\nREJECTred", "2"], ["", "M2(to) colourless", "IGNOREclear\nALLOWdecolourised\nREJECTdiscoloured\nAward 1 mark for two correct answers in wrong order", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(c)(i) | dehydration | ACCEPT(thermal) decomposition/elimination | 1\n(ii) | (to act as a) catalyst | ACCEPTto increase the rate of reaction\nIGNOREto lower the activation energy\nIGNOREreferences to increased surface area | 1\n(d)(i) | (contains a carbon to carbon) double bond/C=C | ALLOWmultiple bond | 1\n(ii) | M1(from) orange | ACCEPTbrown/yellow or any combination of orange/brown/yellow e.g. orange-brown\nREJECTred | 2\n | M2(to) colourless | IGNOREclear\nALLOWdecolourised\nREJECTdiscoloured\nAward 1 mark for two correct answers in wrong order | ", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)(i)", "M1 the equilibrium shifts to the left(as temperature increases)", "ALLOW the reaction moves in the backwards direction OWTTE\nIGNORE changes in amounts of reactants and products e.g. less phosgene/more CO and Cl2 produced", "2"], ["M2(because the forward)\nreaction is exothermic/releases heat(energy)/releases thermal energy", "ACCEPT(because the) backward reaction is endothermic/takes in heat(energy)/takes in thermal energy\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle, eg favours the reaction that tries to reduce the temperature/favours the backward reaction\nM2 dep on M1 correct or missing", ""], ["(ii)\nM1(yield) increases/the amount of phosgene increases\nM2as there are fewer moles/molecules(of gas) on the right", "ACCEPTthere are fewer moles/molecules of product\nACCEPTreverse argument\nALLOW particles\nREJECTatoms\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle, eg favours the reaction with more moles(of gas)\nM2dep on M1", "2"], ["(b)", "COCl2+H2O→2HCl+CO2", "ACCEPTmultiples and fractions\nIGNOREstate symbols even if incorrect", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a)(i) | M1 the equilibrium shifts to the left(as temperature increases) | ALLOW the reaction moves in the backwards direction OWTTE\nIGNORE changes in amounts of reactants and products e.g. less phosgene/more CO and Cl2 produced | 2\nM2(because the forward)\nreaction is exothermic/releases heat(energy)/releases thermal energy | ACCEPT(because the) backward reaction is endothermic/takes in heat(energy)/takes in thermal energy\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle, eg favours the reaction that tries to reduce the temperature/favours the backward reaction\nM2 dep on M1 correct or missing | \n(ii)\nM1(yield) increases/the amount of phosgene increases\nM2as there are fewer moles/molecules(of gas) on the right | ACCEPTthere are fewer moles/molecules of product\nACCEPTreverse argument\nALLOW particles\nREJECTatoms\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s principle, eg favours the reaction with more moles(of gas)\nM2dep on M1 | 2\n(b) | COCl2+H2O→2HCl+CO2 | ACCEPTmultiples and fractions\nIGNOREstate symbols even if incorrect | 1", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(c)", "M1 both bond pairs for C-Cl correctM2 bond pairs for C=O correctM3 all non-bonded electrons correct", "ACCEPT any combination of dots and crossesIGNORE inner shells even if incorrectM3 dep on M1 and M2 correct", "3"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(c) | M1 both bond pairs for C-Cl correctM2 bond pairs for C=O correctM3 all non-bonded electrons correct | ACCEPT any combination of dots and crossesIGNORE inner shells even if incorrectM3 dep on M1 and M2 correct | 3", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "carbon dioxide/gas escapes(from the crucible)/is given off/is lost/is released", "REJECT incorrectly named gas\nIGNORE carbon dioxide is formed\nREJECT references to evaporation", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "to check that the magnesium carbonate has fully decomposed", "ALLOW to make sure all(the magnesium carbonate) has reacted/the reaction is complete OWTTE\nALLOW to make sure allthe gas/carbon dioxide has been given off\nIGNORE the reaction has stopped", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1(expt)1\nM2(because the) mass is not constant(after heating for 15 minutes)/mass at 15 minutes is different from the mass at 10 minutes\nOR\nthe mass is still changing(after heating for 15 minutes)", "ALLOW weight for mass\nM2 dep on M1", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | carbon dioxide/gas escapes(from the crucible)/is given off/is lost/is released | REJECT incorrectly named gas\nIGNORE carbon dioxide is formed\nREJECT references to evaporation | 1\n(b)(i) | to check that the magnesium carbonate has fully decomposed | ALLOW to make sure all(the magnesium carbonate) has reacted/the reaction is complete OWTTE\nALLOW to make sure allthe gas/carbon dioxide has been given off\nIGNORE the reaction has stopped | 1\n(ii) | M1(expt)1\nM2(because the) mass is not constant(after heating for 15 minutes)/mass at 15 minutes is different from the mass at 10 minutes\nOR\nthe mass is still changing(after heating for 15 minutes) | ALLOW weight for mass\nM2 dep on M1 | 2", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["8(a)", "M1 0.0968x0.1(00)", "", "2"], ["OR 0.0968x1001000", "", ""], ["M2 0.00968(mol)", "ACCEPT 0.0097REJECT 0.01ALLOW 9.68/9.7 for 1 markCorrect final answer without working scores both marks", ""], ["(b)", "M1 0.29÷58", "", "2"], ["M2 0.005(0)(mol)", "Correct final answer without working scores both marks", ""], ["(c)", "M1 Yes(he used the right amount of magnesium hydroxide)/no he used too much(magnesium hydroxide)", "", "2"], ["M2 1molMg(OH)2reacts with/neutralises 2molHCl", "ACCEPT He needs 0.00484mol(Mg(OH)2)", ""], ["OR 0.005molMg(OH)2reacts with/neutralises0.01molHCl", "", ""], ["OR 0.00968molHClreactswith/is neutralised by0.00484molMg(OH)2", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n8(a) | M1 0.0968x0.1(00) |  | 2\nOR 0.0968x1001000 |  | \nM2 0.00968(mol) | ACCEPT 0.0097REJECT 0.01ALLOW 9.68/9.7 for 1 markCorrect final answer without working scores both marks | \n(b) | M1 0.29÷58 |  | 2\nM2 0.005(0)(mol) | Correct final answer without working scores both marks | \n(c) | M1 Yes(he used the right amount of magnesium hydroxide)/no he used too much(magnesium hydroxide) |  | 2\nM2 1molMg(OH)2reacts with/neutralises 2molHCl | ACCEPT He needs 0.00484mol(Mg(OH)2) | \nOR 0.005molMg(OH)2reacts with/neutralises0.01molHCl |  | \nOR 0.00968molHClreactswith/is neutralised by0.00484molMg(OH)2 |  | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(a)(i)", "M1(⇌)(the reaction is) reversible", "ACCEPT reaction goes both ways/both forward and backward reactions can occur", "2"], ["M2(ΔH)(molar) enthalpy change(of reaction)", "ACCEPT heat(energy) change/thermal energy change", ""], ["", "IGNORE enthalpy alone", ""], ["", "REJECT temperature change", ""], ["(ii)", "vanadium(V) oxide/vanadium pentoxide", "ACCEPT vanadium oxide", "1"], ["(iii)", "M1(temperature)450(℃)", "ACCEPT any temperature,or range of temperatures,between400to500inclusive", "2"], ["M2(pressure)2(atm)", "ACCEPT temperature in other units provided unit is given", ""], ["", "ACCEPT any pressure,or range of pressures,between1and5(atm)inclusive", ""], ["", "ACCEPT pressure in other units provided unit is givene.g.1x105to5x105Pa", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(a)(i) | M1(⇌)(the reaction is) reversible | ACCEPT reaction goes both ways/both forward and backward reactions can occur | 2\nM2(ΔH)(molar) enthalpy change(of reaction) | ACCEPT heat(energy) change/thermal energy change | \n | IGNORE enthalpy alone | \n | REJECT temperature change | \n(ii) | vanadium(V) oxide/vanadium pentoxide | ACCEPT vanadium oxide | 1\n(iii) | M1(temperature)450(℃) | ACCEPT any temperature,or range of temperatures,between400to500inclusive | 2\nM2(pressure)2(atm) | ACCEPT temperature in other units provided unit is given | \n | ACCEPT any pressure,or range of pressures,between1and5(atm)inclusive | \n | ACCEPT pressure in other units provided unit is givene.g.1x105to5x105Pa | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["9(b)(i)", "a(corrosive)mist/cloud/fog/spray/fumes(of sulfuric acid)would be formed(above the mixture)", "ACCEPTthe reactiongenerates a lot of/too much heat/istooxothermicACCEPTthe mixturegets very/too hot/formssteamIGNOREveryoxothermicIGNOREtoo dangerous/explosive", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1(step3)H2SO4+SO3H2S2O7", "ACCEPTmultiples", "2"], ["", "M2(step4)H2S2O7+H2O2H2SO4", "ACCEPTmultiplesandfractions", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n9(b)(i) | a(corrosive)mist/cloud/fog/spray/fumes(of sulfuric acid)would be formed(above the mixture) | ACCEPTthe reactiongenerates a lot of/too much heat/istooxothermicACCEPTthe mixturegets very/too hot/formssteamIGNOREveryoxothermicIGNOREtoo dangerous/explosive | 1\n(ii) | M1(step3)H2SO4+SO3H2S2O7 | ACCEPTmultiples | 2\n | M2(step4)H2S2O7+H2O2H2SO4 | ACCEPTmultiplesandfractions | ", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["(c)", "Any two from:", "", "2"], ["M1 manufacture of/making detergents/soaps", "If they have not mentioned manufacture or making give MAX 1 for two correct uses."], ["M2 manufacture of/making fertilisers", "IGNORE used to manufacture sulphuric acid in the Contact Process"], ["M3 manufacture of/making paints/pigments/dyes", ""], ["M4 manufacture of/making polymers/plastics/fibres", ""], ["M5 pickling of steel/cleaning metals", ""], ["M6 manufacture of/making explosives", ""], ["M7 manufacture of/making paper", ""], ["", "M8 in car batteries/battery acid", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n(c) | Any two from: |  | 2\nM1 manufacture of/making detergents/soaps | If they have not mentioned manufacture or making give MAX 1 for two correct uses.\nM2 manufacture of/making fertilisers | IGNORE used to manufacture sulphuric acid in the Contact Process\nM3 manufacture of/making paints/pigments/dyes | \nM4 manufacture of/making polymers/plastics/fibres | \nM5 pickling of steel/cleaning metals | \nM6 manufacture of/making explosives | \nM7 manufacture of/making paper | \n | M8 in car batteries/battery acid |  | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 1, "title": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000003", "e000004"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000020", "e000022", "e000025", "e000027", "e000031", "e000034", "e000036", "e000038", "e000042"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "eeaf9c56-f211-5c7c-a9a8-e37822342420", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:00:18.963528757Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 100, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 2, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 1, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2018", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH0) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2018 Publications Code 4CH0_2C_1806_MS All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2018", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 1 = 6", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 2 = 4", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 3 =4", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 4 = 6", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 5 = 12", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 6 = 8", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Question 7 = 4", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_