nd products remains constant scores 1 mark independently of M1 but\nREJECT concentrations of the reactants and products are equal/the same", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(b)(i)", "An explanation that links together the following two points:\nM1 (the position of) equilibrium has moved to the left", "ALLOW (position of) equilibrium has shifted in backwards direction\nALLOW (position of) equilibrium has shifted towards the $ \\mathrm{N_{2}O_{4}} $ /reactants (side)\nALLOW increasing pressure shifts (position of) equilibrium in direction that produces fewer moles (of gas)\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s Principle eg increasing pressure favours the side that has fewer moles of gas / increasing pressure favours the backwards reaction", "2"], ["", "M2 because there are fewer moles/molecules (of gas) on the left", "ALLOW particles\nREJECT atoms\nALLOW because there are fewer moles of $ \\mathrm{N_{2}O_{4}} $ (than $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $)\nALLOW because there are fewer moles of reactant (than product)\nACCEPT reverse argument", ""], ["(ii)", "the concentration of $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ has increased", "ALLOW molecules/particles of $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ are closer together\nALLOW molecules/particles of $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ are in a smaller volume\nREJECT more $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ produced", "1"]], "text": "(b)(i) | An explanation that links together the following two points:\nM1 (the position of) equilibrium has moved to the left | ALLOW (position of) equilibrium has shifted in backwards direction\nALLOW (position of) equilibrium has shifted towards the $ \\mathrm{N_{2}O_{4}} $ /reactants (side)\nALLOW increasing pressure shifts (position of) equilibrium in direction that produces fewer moles (of gas)\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s Principle eg increasing pressure favours the side that has fewer moles of gas / increasing pressure favours the backwards reaction | 2\n | M2 because there are fewer moles/molecules (of gas) on the left | ALLOW particles\nREJECT atoms\nALLOW because there are fewer moles of $ \\mathrm{N_{2}O_{4}} $ (than $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $)\nALLOW because there are fewer moles of reactant (than product)\nACCEPT reverse argument | \n(ii) | the concentration of $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ has increased | ALLOW molecules/particles of $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ are closer together\nALLOW molecules/particles of $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ are in a smaller volume\nREJECT more $ \\mathrm{NO_{2}} $ produced | 1", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Additional guidance", "Marks"], ["7(c)(i)", "nitrogen/N2reacts with oxygen/O2(both from the air)", "IGNORE nitrogen burns/combusts in oxygen\nIGNORE nitrogen is oxidised", "1"], ["(ii)", "(they form) acid rain", "ACCEPT references to respiratory problems\nALLOW a specified harmful effect of acid rain\nALLOW references to smog\nALLOW references to greenhouse gases/global warming/climate change", "1"], ["(iii)", "2NO+2CO→N2+2CO2", "ACCEPT multiples and fractions", "1"], ["", "", "Total", "8"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Additional guidance | Marks\n7(c)(i) | nitrogen/N2reacts with oxygen/O2(both from the air) | IGNORE nitrogen burns/combusts in oxygen\nIGNORE nitrogen is oxidised | 1\n(ii) | (they form) acid rain | ACCEPT references to respiratory problems\nALLOW a specified harmful effect of acid rain\nALLOW references to smog\nALLOW references to greenhouse gases/global warming/climate change | 1\n(iii) | 2NO+2CO→N2+2CO2 | ACCEPT multiples and fractions | 1\n |  | Total | 8", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Additional guidance", "Marks"], ["8(a)", "An explanation using either of the following linked pairs:\nM1 use a fume cupboard\nM2 because chlorine is toxic/poisonous\nOR\nM1 wear goggles/safety glasses/gloves\nM2 because acid/bleach (may be) irritant/corrosive", "IGNORE chlorine is dangerous/harmful/irritant\nIGNORE laboratory coats", "2"], ["(b)(i)", "M1 60÷24000\nM2 0.0025(mol)", "0.0025 with no working scores 2 marks\nREJECT 0.003 for M2", "2"], ["(ii)", "0.0025 OR answer to M2 from(i)", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "M1(0.0025÷4.00)×1000", "Mark CSQ on(b)(ii)", "2"], ["M2 0.625(mol/dm3)", "ACCEPT any number of sig fig except1(unless ECF answer is exactly1 sig fig correct answer with no working throughout(b) scores2 marks", ""], ["", "", "Total", "7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Additional guidance | Marks\n8(a) | An explanation using either of the following linked pairs:\nM1 use a fume cupboard\nM2 because chlorine is toxic/poisonous\nOR\nM1 wear goggles/safety glasses/gloves\nM2 because acid/bleach (may be) irritant/corrosive | IGNORE chlorine is dangerous/harmful/irritant\nIGNORE laboratory coats | 2\n(b)(i) | M1 60÷24000\nM2 0.0025(mol) | 0.0025 with no working scores 2 marks\nREJECT 0.003 for M2 | 2\n(ii) | 0.0025 OR answer to M2 from(i) |  | 1\n(iii) | M1(0.0025÷4.00)×1000 | Mark CSQ on(b)(ii) | 2\nM2 0.625(mol/dm3) | ACCEPT any number of sig fig except1(unless ECF answer is exactly1 sig fig correct answer with no working throughout(b) scores2 marks | \n |  | Total | 7", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "c3ace227-3560-52cd-8427-ff529ed96620", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:00:20.452901501Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 89, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme FINAL", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2019", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2019 Publications Code 4CH1_2C_msc_20190822 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2019", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:00:40.768199+00');
