wn", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {a m o u n t o f C H _ {3} C O O H} =", "latex": "\\mathrm {a m o u n t o f C H _ {3} C O O H} =", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000138", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 138, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {m o l / d m ^ {3}}", "latex": "\\mathrm {m o l / d m ^ {3}}", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000141", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 141, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "(\\mathrm {T o t a l f o r Q u e s t i o n 6 = 1 5 m a r k s})", "latex": "(\\mathrm {T o t a l f o r Q u e s t i o n 6 = 1 5 m a r k s})", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000142", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 142, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {C H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm {C O} (\\mathrm {g}) + 3 \\mathrm {H} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) \\quad \\Delta H = + 2 0 6 \\mathrm {k J / m o l}", "latex": "\\mathrm {C H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm {C O} (\\mathrm {g}) + 3 \\mathrm {H} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) \\quad \\Delta H = + 2 0 6 \\mathrm {k J / m o l}", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000145", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 145, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "628fade2-c759-5a6a-829f-473f8ca0c149", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:00:21.053422298Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 206, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "Instructions", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Use black ink or ball-point pen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Fill in the boxes at the top of this page with your name, centre number and candidate number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer all questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer the questions in the spaces provided", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "there may be more space than you need.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Show all the steps in any calculations and state the units.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Some questions must be answered with a cross in a box . If you change your mind about an answer, put a line through the box and then mark your new answer with a cross.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Information", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The total mark for this paper is 70.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The marks for each question are shown in brackets", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "use this as a guide as to how much time to spend on each question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Write your answers neatly and in good English.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Advice", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Try to answer every question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Read each question carefully before you start to answer it.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Check your answers if you have time at the end.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Turn over", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The Periodic Table of the Elements", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ ^{*} $ The lanthanoids (atomic numbers 58-71) and the actinoids (atomic numbers 90-103) have been omitted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The relative atomic masses of copper and chlorine have not been rounded to the nearest whole number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Answer ALL questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "1 This question is about gases in the atmosphere.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The box gives the names of some gases in the atmosphere.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "argon carbon dioxide helium nitrogen oxygen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use gases from the box to answer the questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Each gas may be used once, more than once or not at all.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Identify the two noble gases.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Identify the gas that is a compound.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Identify the most abundant gas in the atmosphere.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) Identify the greenhouse gas.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Describe the test for oxygen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1 = 5 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "2 The diagram represents an atom of boron.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Use information from the diagram to complete the table.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The first row has been done for you.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(5)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Boron has two isotopes, boron-10 and boron-11.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A sample of boron contains 18.7% of boron-10 and 81.3% of boron-11.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the relative atomic mass of this sample of boron.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "relative atomic mass=", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "3 Crude oil is an important source of organic compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The diagram shows crude oil being separated into different fractions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Name the process used to separate crude oil into different fractions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000050", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 50, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000051", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 51, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) State what happens to the crude oil at X.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000052", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 52, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000053", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 53, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Describe the differences between fraction B and fraction E. In your answer, refer to", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000054", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 54, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "size of the molecules", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000055", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 55, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "boiling point", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000056", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 56, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "colour", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000057", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 57, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "viscosity", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000058", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 58, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Crude oil often contains sulfur as an impurity.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000059", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 59, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain why this is a problem when using crude oil fractions as fuels.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000060", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 60, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3 = 8 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000061", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 61, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "4 This question is about the halogens and their compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000062", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 62, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) The table gives the colour and physical state at room temperature of the halogens.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000063", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 63, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Complete the table by predicting the colour of astatine and the physical state of fluorine at room temperature.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000064", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 64, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Chlorine gas is bubbled into a colourless solution of potassium bromide. Explain why the solution turns orange.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000066", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 66, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Potassium bromide is an ionic compound.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000067", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 67, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Draw diagrams to show the outer electrons in a potassium ion and in a bromide ion Include the charges on the ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000068", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 68, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(3)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000069", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 69, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) A student sets up a circuit to test the electrical conductivity of water, solid sodium chloride and aqueous sodium chloride.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000071", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 71, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows the student''s results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000072", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 72, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain these results, with reference to the structure and bonding of the substances.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000074", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 74, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) A concentrated aqueous solution of sodium chloride is electrolysed using graphite electrodes.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000075", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 75, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Chlorine is formed at the positive electrode (anode).", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000076", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 76, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give an ionic half-equation for the formation of chlorine at the positive electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000077", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 77, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) State why this ionic half-equation represents an oxidation reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000078", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 78, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Which substance is formed at the negative electrode (cathode)?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000079", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 79, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A hydrogen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000080", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 80, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B oxygen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000081", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 81, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C sodium", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000082", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 82, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D water", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000083", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 83, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 15 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000084", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 84, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "5 This question is about the reactions of carboxylic acids.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000085", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 85, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Carboxylic acids react with solutions of metal carbonates.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000086", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 86, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Complete the chemical equation for the reaction of ethanoic acid, $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} C O O H} $ with potassium carbonate solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000087", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 87, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) State what you would see in this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000089", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 89, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The ester, ethyl ethanoate, can be prepared by reacting ethanol with ethanoic acid. This is the method for the preparation.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000090", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 90, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "mix equal amounts of ethanoic acid and ethanol in a boiling tube", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000091", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 91, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add a few drops of concentrated sulfuric acid", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000092", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 92, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "place the boiling tube in a hot water bath for several minutes", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000093", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 93, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State the role of concentrated sulfuric acid in this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000094", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 94, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Suggest why the mixture is heated in a water bath rather than directly with a Bunsen burner flame.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000095", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 95, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) State how you would know that ethyl ethanoate has formed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000096", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 96, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Another ester, methyl propanoate, can be prepared by reacting methanol with propanoic acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000097", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 97, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Draw the displayed formulae of methanol, propanoic acid and the ester, methyl propanoate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000098", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 98, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "methyl propanoate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000100", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 100, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give the name of the other product of this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000101", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 101, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Give one use of esters.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000102", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 102, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 11 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000103", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 103, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "6 When a bottle of wine is left open for several days, some of the ethanol in the wine turns to ethanoic acid, $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} C O O H} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000104", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 104, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) A scientist uses a titration method to investigate how much ethanoic acid is formed if a bottle of white wine is left open for one week.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000105", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 105, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "She uses this method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000106", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 106, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "fill a burette with the white wine and record the reading", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000107", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 107, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution to a conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000108", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 108, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add a few drops of phenolphthalein indicator to the flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000109", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 109, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "swirl the flask continuously while adding wine from the burette", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000110", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 110, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add the wine drop by drop near the end point", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000111", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 111, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "record the reading at the end point", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000112", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 112, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Name the piece of apparatus that would be most suitable for measuring the $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000113", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 113, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Suggest why red wine would not be suitable to use for this investigation.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000114", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 114, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) State why she swirls the flask continuously.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000115", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 115, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) State why she adds the wine drop by drop near the end point.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000116", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 116, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The diagram shows the burette readings at the start and end of one of the titrations.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000117", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 117, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use the readings to complete the table.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000120", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 120, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give your values to the nearest 0.05 $ cm^{3}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000121", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 121, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(3)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000122", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 122, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The scientist repeats the titration four more times.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000124", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 124, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows her results for these four titrations.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000125", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 125, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Concordant results are those within $ 0. 2 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of each other.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000127", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 127, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Add ticks ( $ \\surd $ ) to the table to show the concordant results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000128", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 128, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Use your ticked results to calculate the mean (average) volume of wine added.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000129", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 129, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Another scientist repeats the titration with a different bottle of white wine that has been left open for a week.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000130", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 130, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation for the reaction that occurs in this titration is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000131", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 131, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The mean volume of wine added is $ 1 9. 5 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000133", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 133, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) The concentration of the sodium hydroxide solution is $ 0. 0 5 0 0 \\mathrm{m o l} / \\mathrm{d m}^{3}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000134", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 134, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the amount, in moles, of NaOH in $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000135", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 135, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Deduce the amount, in moles, of $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} C O O H} $ in $ 1 9. 5 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of the wine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000137", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 137, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Calculate the concentration, in mol/dm $ ^{3} $ , of $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} C O O H} $ in the wine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000139", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 139, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "concentration of $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} C O O H}= $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000140", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 140, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "7 Hydrogen gas can be produced by reacting a mixture of methane and steam in the presence of a nickel catalyst.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000143", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 143, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The reaction conditions are a temperature of $ 7 0 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ and a pressure of 5 atmospheres. The equation for the reaction is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000144", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 144, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) What does the symbol $ \\rightleftharpoons $ represent?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000146", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 146, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) (i) The mixture of methane and steam is heated to a temperature greater than $ 7 0 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ but the pressure is kept at 5 atmospheres.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000147", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 147, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Predict the effect of this change on the yield of hydrogen at equilibrium, giving a reason for your answer.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000148", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 148, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) The mixture of methane and steam is kept at the same temperature of $ 7 0 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ but the pressure is increased to more than 5 atmospheres.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000149", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 149, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Predict the effect of this change on the yield of hydrogen at equilibrium, giving a reason for your answer.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000150", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 150, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Calculate the volume, in $ \\mathrm{d m}^{3} $ of hydrogen gas at rtp that is produced when 10 tonnes of methane gas completely react with steam.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000151", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 151, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:00:40.925981+00');
