"", "2"], ["", "M1 (when sulfur burns) sulfur dioxide/SO2 is formed", "ALLOW sulfur trioxide/SO3\nIGNORE sulfur oxides", ""], ["", "M2 causes acid rain", "ALLOW a specified harmful effect of acid rain\nACCEPT references to causing/acerbating respiratory problems", ""], ["", "", "ALLOW greenhouse gas/causes global warming/imate change", ""], ["", "", "", "Total 8"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3 | (a)(i) | fractional distillation | ALLOW fractionating/fractionation | 1\n(ii) | crude oil/it is heated/vapourised | ALLOW boiled\nIGNORE evaporates | 1\n(iii) | A description which refers to the following four points | ACCEPT reverse arguments for E | 4\n | M1 B contains larger/longer molecules |  | \n | M2 B has a higher boiling point | ALLOW E is more volatile\nIGNORE melting point | \n | M3 B has a darker colour | ALLOW arison giving specific colours e.g B is orange and E is pale yellow | \n | M4 B is more viscous/has greater viscosity | ALLOW E is more runny\nMAX 2 marks if no reference to fractions E or B in the answer? | \n(b) |  | An planation which links the following two points |  | 2\n | M1 (when sulfur burns) sulfur dioxide/SO2 is formed | ALLOW sulfur trioxide/SO3\nIGNORE sulfur oxides | \n | M2 causes acid rain | ALLOW a specified harmful effect of acid rain\nACCEPT references to causing/acerbating respiratory problems | \n |  | ALLOW greenhouse gas/causes global warming/imate change | \n |  |  | Total 8", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "M1fluorine- gasM2astatine- black", "ACCEPTvery dark grey", "2"], ["(b)", "An planation linking the following two pointsM1bromine/Br2is formed/displaced/producedM2as chlorine is more reactive(than bromine)", "REJECTbromide for bromineACCEPTbromine/Br2shown as the productin an equationIGNOREstate of bromineREJECTbromide/chloride", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | M1fluorine- gasM2astatine- black | ACCEPTvery dark grey | 2\n(b) | An planation linking the following two pointsM1bromine/Br2is formed/displaced/producedM2as chlorine is more reactive(than bromine) | REJECTbromide for bromineACCEPTbromine/Br2shown as the productin an equationIGNOREstate of bromineREJECTbromide/chloride | 2", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(c)", "M1 correct structure of potassium ion\nK+", "ACCEPT any combination of dots and crosses.\nIGNORE inner shells even if incorrect", "3"], ["", "M2 correct structure of bromide ion\nBr-", "", ""], ["", "M3 charges on both ions correct (with or without square brackets).", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(c) | M1 correct structure of potassium ion\nK+ | ACCEPT any combination of dots and crosses.\nIGNORE inner shells even if incorrect | 3\n | M2 correct structure of bromide ion\nBr- |  | \n | M3 charges on both ions correct (with or without square brackets). |  | ", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(d)", "An planation linking the following five points\nM1water is covalently bonded/has a simple molecular structure\nM2water does not contain any free (moving) charged parti es(so does not conduct electricity)\nM3sodium chloride has a giant ionic structure/has an ionic lattice structure/is ionically bonded\nM4the ions are in fixed positions/cannot move(so does not conduct electricity)\nM5in solution/aqueous sodium chloride the ions are free to flow/move(so the solution does conduct electricity)", "ALLOWwater is a covalent ound\nACCEPTwater does not contain any free ions/electrons or delocalised electrons\nALLOWsodium chloride is an ionic ound/contains ions\nREJECTmention of atoms/molecules/intermolecular forces in Na forM3only\nM4subsumesM3\nREJECTelectrons being unable to move forM4\nREJECTreference to electrons conducting electricity in aqueous sodium chloride forM5\nIGNOREreference to ions carrying charge/current", "5"], ["(e)(i)\n(ii)", "2-→2+2e(-)\nelectrons are lost(by chloride ions/-)", "ALLOW2-2e→2\nACCEPToxidation number of chlorine increases(by1)/changes from-1to0\nREJECTchlorine loses electrons\nIGNOREreferences to gain of oxygen", "1\n1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(d) | An planation linking the following five points\nM1water is covalently bonded/has a simple molecular structure\nM2water does not contain any free (moving) charged parti es(so does not conduct electricity)\nM3sodium chloride has a giant ionic structure/has an ionic lattice structure/is ionically bonded\nM4the ions are in fixed positions/cannot move(so does not conduct electricity)\nM5in solution/aqueous sodium chloride the ions are free to flow/move(so the solution does conduct electricity) | ALLOWwater is a covalent ound\nACCEPTwater does not contain any free ions/electrons or delocalised electrons\nALLOWsodium chloride is an ionic ound/contains ions\nREJECTmention of atoms/molecules/intermolecular forces in Na forM3only\nM4subsumesM3\nREJECTelectrons being unable to move forM4\nREJECTreference to electrons conducting electricity in aqueous sodium chloride forM5\nIGNOREreference to ions carrying charge/current | 5\n(e)(i)\n(ii) | 2-→2+2e(-)\nelectrons are lost(by chloride ions/-) | ALLOW2-2e→2\nACCEPToxidation number of chlorine increases(by1)/changes from-1to0\nREJECTchlorine loses electrons\nIGNOREreferences to gain of oxygen | 1\n1", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(iii)", "A hydrogen\nB is incorrect as oxygen is not formed at the cathode\nC is incorrect as sodium is not formed when graphite electrodes are used\nD is incorrect as water is not formed at the cathode", "", "1\nTotal 15"]], "text": "(iii) | A hydrogen\nB is incorrect as oxygen is not formed at the cathode\nC is incorrect as sodium is not formed when graphite electrodes are used\nD is incorrect as water is not formed at the cathode |  | 1\nTotal 15", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5", "(a)(i)", "$2\\text{CH}_{3}\\text{COOH}+\\text{K}_{2}\\text{CO}_{3}\\rightarrow 2\\text{CH}_{3}\\text{COOK}+\\text{CO}_{2}+\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}$", "ALLOW multiples", "2"], ["M1 2CH_{3}\\text{COOK}$", "ACCEPT 2CH_{3}\\text{COO}^{-}\\text{K}^{+}$", ""], ["M2 CO_{2}+\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}$", "ALLOW 2KCH_{3}\\text{COO}$", ""], ["(ii) effervescence / fizzing / bubbles", "If M1 not awarded any numbers before CO_{2}+\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O} can be ignored and M2 can be awarded.\nFor both marks to be awarded the equation must be correctly balanced", ""], ["(b)(i)", "(acts as a) catalyst", "IGNORE carbon dioxide/gas given off/evolved/formed /produced", "1"], ["(ii) ethanol is flammable / might catch fire / might ignite", "ACCEPT ethyl ethanoate /the mixture /it is flammable /might catch fire /might ignite", "1"], ["(iii) ester has) sweet / fruity / distinctive smell", "ALLOW liquid (ester) floats on top of mixture OWTTE", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5 | (a)(i) | $2\\text{CH}_{3}\\text{COOH}+\\text{K}_{2}\\text{CO}_{3}\\rightarrow 2\\text{CH}_{3}\\text{COOK}+\\text{CO}_{2}+\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}$ | ALLOW multiples | 2\nM1 2CH_{3}\\text{COOK}$ | ACCEPT 2CH_{3}\\text{COO}^{-}\\text{K}^{+}$ | \nM2 CO_{2}+\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}$ | ALLOW 2KCH_{3}\\text{COO}$ | \n(ii) effervescence / fizzing / bubbles | If M1 not awarded any numbers before CO_{2}+\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O} can be ignored and M2 can be awarded.\nFor both marks to be awarded the equation must be correctly balanced | \n(b)(i) | (acts as a) catalyst | IGNORE carbon dioxide/gas given off/evolved/formed /produced | 1\n(ii) ethanol is flammable / might catch fire / might ignite | ACCEPT ethyl ethanoate /the mixture /it is flammable /might catch fire /might ignite | 1\n(iii) ester has) sweet / fruity / distinctive smell | ALLOW liquid (ester) floats on top of mixture OWTTE | ", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(c)(i)", "H\nH-C-O-H\nH\nH-C-C-C\nH H O-H\nwater", "Penalise missing bond between O and H once only\nIf incorrect number of carbon atoms in alcohol and or acid allow ECF for structure of ester formed from their alcohol and acid\nACCEPT H2O", "3"], ["(ii)", "", "", "1"], ["(d)", "food flavourings/perfumes", "ACCEPT any correct use\ne.g. in cosmetics/making soaps/making detergents/solvents\n(for paints/varnishes)", "1"], ["", "", "", "Total 11"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(c)(i) | H\nH-C-O-H\nH\nH-C-C-C\nH H O-H\nwater | Penalise missing bond between O and H once only\nIf incorrect number of carbon atoms in alcohol and or acid allow ECF for structure of ester formed from their alcohol and acid\nACCEPT H2O