te reaction)/ so as not to overshoot the end point OWTTE | ACCEPT to find the act/precise point of neutralisation\nIGNORE to obtain an accurate reading | 1\n(b) |  |  |  | MAX2 if final and initial burette readings are reversed.\nMAX2 if readings not given to 2 decimal places.\nALLOW ECF for M3 on correct subtraction of M1-M2 | 3\n |  | M1 | final burette reading in cm3 | 22.70 |  | \n |  | M2 | initial burette reading in cm3 | 2.15 |  | \n |  | M3 | volume of wine added in cm3 | 20.55 |  | ", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(c)(i) ip(ii) ip", "Ticks in boxes 1,3 and 4\n• setting out of calculation\n• answer\nM120.40+20.35+20.453\nM220.40", "", "12"], ["", "", "20.40 without working scores2\n20.4 with or without working scores1\nIf no results ticked then only use of2 or3 concordant titres can score both marks in(ii)\nIf only one result ticked thenM2can be scored for averaging two or more titre values correctly\nM1CQ on results ticked\nM2CQ on correct calculation fromM1\nAnswer toM2must be correct to2dp", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(c)(i) ip(ii) ip | Ticks in boxes 1,3 and 4\n• setting out of calculation\n• answer\nM120.40+20.35+20.453\nM220.40 |  | 12\n |  | 20.40 without working scores2\n20.4 with or without working scores1\nIf no results ticked then only use of2 or3 concordant titres can score both marks in(ii)\nIf only one result ticked thenM2can be scored for averaging two or more titre values correctly\nM1CQ on results ticked\nM2CQ on correct calculation fromM1\nAnswer toM2must be correct to2dp | ", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(d)(i)", "setting out of calculation\nfinal answer\nM1 25.0 x 0.05(00)\n1000\nM2 0.00125\nIf no division by 1000 giving an answer of 1.25 award 1 mark\nCorrect answer without working scores 2\n(ii)\n0.00125 OR answer to (i)\n1\n(iii)\nsetting out of calculation\nfinal answer\nM1 0.00125 x 1000 OR answer to (ii) x 1000\n19.50\n19.5\nM2 0.0641 OR answer to M1\nACCEPT any number of sig fig cept 1\nCorrect answer without working scores 2\nanswer to (ii)\n19.5\ncorrectly evaluated to 2 or more sig figs. scores 1\nDo not penalise not multiplying by 1000 in (iii) if they have not divided by 1000 in (i)\nTotal 15"]], "text": "(d)(i) | setting out of calculation\nfinal answer\nM1 25.0 x 0.05(00)\n1000\nM2 0.00125\nIf no division by 1000 giving an answer of 1.25 award 1 mark\nCorrect answer without working scores 2\n(ii)\n0.00125 OR answer to (i)\n1\n(iii)\nsetting out of calculation\nfinal answer\nM1 0.00125 x 1000 OR answer to (ii) x 1000\n19.50\n19.5\nM2 0.0641 OR answer to M1\nACCEPT any number of sig fig cept 1\nCorrect answer without working scores 2\nanswer to (ii)\n19.5\ncorrectly evaluated to 2 or more sig figs. scores 1\nDo not penalise not multiplying by 1000 in (iii) if they have not divided by 1000 in (i)\nTotal 15", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 2, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7", "(a)", "reversible reaction", "IGNORE references to equilibrium", "1"], ["ALLOW the reaction goes both ways"], ["ALLOW the reaction can go forwards and backwards"], ["(b)", "(i)", "M1 yield increases", "ACCEPT more hydrogen produced", "2"], ["M2(equilibrium shifts to the right as the forward) reaction is endothermic", "IGNORE references to Le Chatelier e.g. an increase in temperature favours the forward reaction"], ["M2 dep on M1 correct or missing"], ["(ii)", "(ii)", "M1 yield decreases", "ACCEPT less hydrogen produced", "2"], ["M2(equilibrium shifts to the left as) fewer moles/molecules(of gas) on lhs/more moles/molecules(of gas) on rhs OWTTE", "ALLOW parti es"], ["IGNORE references to Le Chatelier e.g. an increase in pressure favours the side with fewer moles", "REJECT atoms"], ["M2 dep on M1 correct or missing"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7 | (a) | reversible reaction | IGNORE references to equilibrium | 1\nALLOW the reaction goes both ways\nALLOW the reaction can go forwards and backwards\n(b) | (i) | M1 yield increases | ACCEPT more hydrogen produced | 2\nM2(equilibrium shifts to the right as the forward) reaction is endothermic | IGNORE references to Le Chatelier e.g. an increase in temperature favours the forward reaction\nM2 dep on M1 correct or missing\n(ii) | (ii) | M1 yield decreases | ACCEPT less hydrogen produced | 2\nM2(equilibrium shifts to the left as) fewer moles/molecules(of gas) on lhs/more moles/molecules(of gas) on rhs OWTTE | ALLOW parti es\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier e.g. an increase in pressure favours the side with fewer moles | REJECT atoms\nM2 dep on M1 correct or missing", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(c)", "calculate the amount, in moles, of methane\nuse the equation to calculate the amount of hydrogen\nmultiply amount by 24 to find the volume of hydrogen\nfinal answer in standard form\nM110,000,000 OR 625,00016\nM2625,000 x 3 OR 1,875,000\nM31,875,000 x 24 OR 45,000,000(dm3)\nM44.5 x 107(dm3)", "Mark consequentially forM2,M3andM4.\n45,000,000 without working scores 3\nCorrect answer in standard form without working scores 4\nCommon answers4.5 x 104(3)45,000(2)\n4.5 x 101(3)45(2)\n1.5 x 107(3)15,000,000(2)\nNOTE even if working is incorrect e.g. division by 24 instead of multiplicationM4can still be awarded for correct conversion to standard form", "4"], ["", "", "", "Total 9"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(c) | calculate the amount, in moles, of methane\nuse the equation to calculate the amount of hydrogen\nmultiply amount by 24 to find the volume of hydrogen\nfinal answer in standard form\nM110,000,000 OR 625,00016\nM2625,000 x 3 OR 1,875,000\nM31,875,000 x 24 OR 45,000,000(dm3)\nM44.5 x 107(dm3) | Mark consequentially forM2,M3andM4.\n45,000,000 without working scores 3\nCorrect answer in standard form without working scores 4\nCommon answers4.5 x 104(3)45,000(2)\n4.5 x 101(3)45(2)\n1.5 x 107(3)15,000,000(2)\nNOTE even if working is incorrect e.g. division by 24 instead of multiplicationM4can still be awarded for correct conversion to standard form | 4\n |  |  | Total 9", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 1, "title": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000003", "e000004"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s004", "elementIds": ["e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000033"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "71e00b60-e568-55e2-b8c1-8b68f8f02787", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:00:21.104448683Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 139, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 1, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2019", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.Edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.Edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2019 Publications Code 4CH1_2CR_msc_20190822 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2019", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in actly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the e boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "TOTAL MARKS 70", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:00:40.939569+00');
