sion": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "M1(from) yellow", "", "2"], ["M2(to) orange", "ACCEPT red\nALLOW pink\n1 mark for two correct colours in the wrong order", ""], ["", "", ""], ["(b)", "A description that makes reference to any four of the following points", "", "4"], ["M1he should not rinse flask with sodium hydroxide solution or he should rinse flask with water", "ACCEPT he should use a pipette instead of a measuring cylinder", ""], ["M2he should use a pipette to measure out the sodium hydroxide solution", "", ""], ["M3he should not rinse the burette with water or he should rinse the burette with sulfuric acid", "", ""], ["M4he should record the initial burette reading", "", ""], ["M5he should place a white tile under the flask", "ALLOW white paper", ""], ["M6he should swirl the flask whilst adding the acid", "IGNORE stir", ""], ["M7he should add the acid dropwise near the end-point", "", ""], ["M8repeat the titration(to obtain an average/ concordant results)", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | M1(from) yellow |  | 2\nM2(to) orange | ACCEPT red\nALLOW pink\n1 mark for two correct colours in the wrong order | \n |  | \n(b) | A description that makes reference to any four of the following points |  | 4\nM1he should not rinse flask with sodium hydroxide solution or he should rinse flask with water | ACCEPT he should use a pipette instead of a measuring cylinder | \nM2he should use a pipette to measure out the sodium hydroxide solution |  | \nM3he should not rinse the burette with water or he should rinse the burette with sulfuric acid |  | \nM4he should record the initial burette reading |  | \nM5he should place a white tile under the flask | ALLOW white paper | \nM6he should swirl the flask whilst adding the acid | IGNORE stir | \nM7he should add the acid dropwise near the end-point |  | \nM8repeat the titration(to obtain an average/ concordant results) |  | ", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(c)", "calculate the amount, in moles, of sodium hydroxidecalculate the amount, in moles, of sulfuric acidcalculate the concentration of sulfuric acidExample calculationM1n(NaOH)=0.0250×0.200or0.005(mol)M2n(H2SO4)=0.005÷2or0.0025(mol)M3concn=(0.0025÷0.0167)=0.150(mol/dm3)", "answer to M1÷2answer to M2÷0.0167ALLOW0.1497or any number of sig fig except oneCorrect answer without working scores3ACCEPT alternative methods", "3"], ["", "", "", "Total 9"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(c) | calculate the amount, in moles, of sodium hydroxidecalculate the amount, in moles, of sulfuric acidcalculate the concentration of sulfuric acidExample calculationM1n(NaOH)=0.0250×0.200or0.005(mol)M2n(H2SO4)=0.005÷2or0.0025(mol)M3concn=(0.0025÷0.0167)=0.150(mol/dm3) | answer to M1÷2answer to M2÷0.0167ALLOW0.1497or any number of sig fig except oneCorrect answer without working scores3ACCEPT alternative methods | 3\n |  |  | Total 9", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)", "B it relights a glowing splintA is incorrect as this is the test for hydrogenC is incorrect as oxygen is not an acidic gasD is incorrect as this is the test for carbon dioxide", "", "1"], ["(b)", "An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 provides an alternative pathway OWTTEM2 with a lower activation energy OWTTE", "ACCEPT more collisions with energy greater than the activation energyALLOW lowers the energy needed to start the reaction", "2"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a) | B it relights a glowing splintA is incorrect as this is the test for hydrogenC is incorrect as oxygen is not an acidic gasD is incorrect as this is the test for carbon dioxide |  | 1\n(b) | An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 provides an alternative pathway OWTTEM2 with a lower activation energy OWTTE | ACCEPT more collisions with energy greater than the activation energyALLOW lowers the energy needed to start the reaction | 2", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(c)(i)", "find energy needed to break bonds\nfind energy released when bonds form\ncorrect subtraction to find ΔH\nExample calculation\nM1(4x463)+(2x143)OR2138(kJ)\nM2(4x463)+498OR2350(kJ)\nM3-212(kJ)ORM1-M2correctly evaluated\nEnergy\n2H2O2\nΔH\n2H2O+O2\nM1horizontal line to show products in correct position and correctly labelled\nM2vertical line in correct position and labelled ΔH", "ACCEPT(2x143)/286 for M1and498 for M2\nIGNORE any signs in M1andM2\n-212withorwithoutworkingscores3\n(+)212withorwithoutworkingscores2", "3"], ["", "", "MarkCQonsignin(i)\nACCEPTdoubleheadedarroworarrowpointingfromreactantsleveltoproductslevel\nREJECTarrowpointingfromproductsleveltoreactantslevel\nIGNOREanyattemptsatincludingactivationenergy", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total8"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(c)(i) | find energy needed to break bonds\nfind energy released when bonds form\ncorrect subtraction to find ΔH\nExample calculation\nM1(4x463)+(2x143)OR2138(kJ)\nM2(4x463)+498OR2350(kJ)\nM3-212(kJ)ORM1-M2correctly evaluated\nEnergy\n2H2O2\nΔH\n2H2O+O2\nM1horizontal line to show products in correct position and correctly labelled\nM2vertical line in correct position and labelled ΔH | ACCEPT(2x143)/286 for M1and498 for M2\nIGNORE any signs in M1andM2\n-212withorwithoutworkingscores3\n(+)212withorwithoutworkingscores2 | 3\n |  | MarkCQonsignin(i)\nACCEPTdoubleheadedarroworarrowpointingfromreactantsleveltoproductslevel\nREJECTarrowpointingfromproductsleveltoreactantslevel\nIGNOREanyattemptsatincludingactivationenergy | 2\n |  |  | Total8", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)(i)", "M1 300(℃)", "ACCEPT any temperature or range 250 to 350 inclusive.", "2"], ["M2 60 to 70(atm)", "ACCEPT any correct alternative unit and quantity", ""], ["C2H5OH+3O2→2CO2+3H2O", "ACCEPT any pressure or range 60 to 70 inclusive", "1"], ["All bonds including bond between O and H must be shown."], ["(b)(i)", "C2H5OH+3O2→2CO2+3H2O", "", "2"], ["M1 all formulae correct", "ALLOW C2H6O for ethanol", ""], ["M2 balancing of correct formulae", "ACCEPT multiples and fractions", ""], ["(ii) prevents blood from carrying oxygen/ reduces the capacity of blood to carry oxygen OWTTE", "IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", ""], ["", "ALLOW references to combining with haemoglobin in red blood cells or forming carboxyhaemoglobin", "1"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a)(i) | M1 300(℃) | ACCEPT any temperature or range 250 to 350 inclusive. | 2\nM2 60 to 70(atm) | ACCEPT any correct alternative unit and quantity | \nC2H5OH+3O2→2CO2+3H2O | ACCEPT any pressure or range 60 to 70 inclusive | 1\nAll bonds including bond between O and H must be shown.\n(b)(i) | C2H5OH+3O2→2CO2+3H2O |  | 2\nM1 all formulae correct | ALLOW C2H6O for ethanol | \nM2 balancing of correct formulae | ACCEPT multiples and fractions | \n(ii) prevents blood from carrying oxygen/ reduces the capacity of blood to carry oxygen OWTTE | IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | \n | ALLOW references to combining with haemoglobin in red blood cells or forming carboxyhaemoglobin | 1", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(c)", "ethyl ethanoate", "ALLOW ethyl acetate", "1"], ["(d)(i)(ii)", "condensation (polymerisation)\nC=C-CH2CH2-C-O-CH2CH2-O-+2H2O\nM1 correct ester link\nM2 rest of polymer structure correct with extension bonds\nM3 2H2O", "ACCEPT\nC=C-CH2CH2-C-O-CH2CH2-\nfor M1 and M2\nIf brackets and n present equation must be fully balanced with n in front of each reactant and 2nH2O for full marks, otherwise max 2\nIf dimer is drawn with OH at one end and COOH at the other a mark can be awarded for H2O without the 2 as this equation is then balanced, so M1 and M3 can be awarded.", "13"], ["", "", "", "Total 11"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(c) | ethyl ethanoate | ALLOW ethyl acetate | 1\n(d)(i)(ii) | condensation (polymerisation)\nC=C-CH2CH2-C-O-CH2CH2-O-+2H2O\nM1 correct ester link\nM2 rest of polymer structure correct with extension bonds\nM3 2H2O | ACCEPT\nC=C-CH2CH2-C-O-CH2CH2-\nfor M1 and M2\nIf brackets and n present equation must be fully balanced with n in front of each reactant and 2nH2O for full marks, otherwise max 2\nIf dimer is drawn with OH at one end and COOH at the other a mark can be awarded for H2O without the 2 as this equation is then balanced, so M1 and M3 can be awarded. | 13\n |  |  | Total 11", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)(i)", "calcium+water→calcium hydroxide+hydrogen", "ACCEPT fully correct balanced chemical equationCa+2H2O→Ca(OH)2+H2IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", "1"], ["Any two fromM1 effervescence/fizzing/bubbles", "IGNORE gas given off", "2"], ["M2 calcium/metal/solid disappears/becomes smaller OWTTEM3 test tube/beaker feels warm/hot", "ALLOW calcium/metal/solid dissolvesALLOW heat produced/temperature increases", ""], ["(b)(i)", "A description that makes reference to the following five points", "", "5"], ["M1 dissolve each of the solids in water/make a solution of each of the solids", "ALLOW M1 and M2 if just one of the solids is dissolved in water and then the other solid is added to it.", ""], ["M2 mix/add (the two solutions together)", "M2 dep on M1 or on reference to the solutions being mixed", ""], ["M3 filter (the mixture)", "If implication is that filtering is to obtain crystals from the solution no M3", ""], ["M4 wash the precipitate/solid/barium sulfate/salt/residue (with water)", "", ""], ["M5 suitable method of drying the solid", "e.g. dry in a (warm) oven/dry between filter papers", "", ""], ["ALLOW leave to dry", "", ""], ["REJECT hot oven or direct heating (with Bunsen burner)If evaporation of solution to form crystals do not award M4 but allow M5 for suitable drying method", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a)(i) | calcium+water→calcium hydroxide+hydrogen | ACCEPT fully correct balanced chemical equationCa+2H2O→Ca(OH)2+H2IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | 1\nAny two fromM1 effervescence/fizzing/bubbles | IGNORE gas given off | 2\nM2 calcium/metal/solid disappears/becomes smaller OWTTEM3 test tube/beaker feels warm/hot | ALLOW calcium/metal/solid dissolvesALLOW heat produced/temperature increases | \n(b)(i) | A description that makes reference to the following five points |  | 5\nM1 dissolve each of the solids in water/make a solution of each of the solids | ALLOW M1 and M2 if just one of the solids is dissolved in water and then the other solid is added to it. | \nM2 mix/add (the two solutions together) | M2 dep on M1 or on reference to the solutions being mixed | \nM3 filter (the mixture) | If implication is that filtering is to obtain crystals from the solution no M3 | \nM4 wash the precipitate/solid/barium sulfate/salt/residue (with water) |  | \nM5 suitable method of drying the solid | e.g. dry in a (warm) oven/dry between filter papers |  | \nALLOW leave to dry |  | \nREJECT hot oven or direct heating (with Bunsen burner)If evaporation of solution to form crystals do not award M4 but allow M5 for suitable drying method |  | ", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "$Ba^{2+}(aq)+SO_{4}^{2-}(aq)\\rightarrow BaSO_{4}(s)$\nM1 all formulae correct\nM2 state symbols correct", "If formulae incorrect or full equation given (even if incorrect) M2 can still be awarded for correct state symbols. If NaCl in equation must be (aq).", "2"]], "text": "(ii) | $Ba^{2+}(aq)+SO_{4}^{2-}(aq)\\rightarrow BaSO_{4}(s)$\nM1 all formulae correct\nM2 state symbols correct | If formulae incorrect or full equation given (even if incorrect) M2 can still be awarded for correct state symbols. If NaCl in equation must be (aq). | 2", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(c)(i)", "C decompositionA is incorrect as it is not an addition reactionB is incorrect as oxygen is not a reactantD is incorrect as nothing is neutralised here", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "calculate the amount, in moles, of magnesium nitrateuse the equation to find the total amount, in moles, of gas producedmultiply this amount by 24answer given to two significant figuresExample calculationM1 n(magnesium nitrate) = 7.7÷148 or 0.052(mol)M2 n(gas) = 5x0.052÷2or0.13(mol)M3 Total volume of gas = 0.13x24or3.12M4 3.1(dm3)", "5x answer toM1÷2answer toM2x24answer toM3to2 sig figAllow any number of sig fig forM1,M2andM33.1 without working scores43.12 without working scores3", "4"], ["", "", "", "Total 15"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(c)(i) | C decompositionA is incorrect as it is not an addition reactionB is incorrect as oxygen is not a reactantD is incorrect as nothing is neutralised here |  | 1\n(ii) | calculate the amount, in moles, of magnesium nitrateuse the equation to find the total amount, in moles, of gas producedmultiply this amount by 24answer given to two significant figuresExample calculationM1 n(magnesium nitrate) = 7.7÷148 or 0.052(mol)M2 n(gas) = 5x0.052÷2or0.13(mol)M3 Total volume of gas = 0.13x24or3.12M4 3.1(dm3) | 5x answer toM1÷2answer toM2x24answer toM3to2 sig figAllow any number of sig fig forM1,M2andM33.1 without working scores43.12 without working scores3 | 4\n |  |  | Total 15", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "General Marking Guidance", "sectionId": "s003", "elementIds": ["e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "520f4405-753d-5882-876e-e0f577befa8b", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:00:21.789851870Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 64, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE in Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2020 Publications Code 4CH1_2C_msc_20200305 All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "General Marking Guidance", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required, mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:00:41.118155+00');
