orrect measurement of distance moved by spot Y | ALLOW 5.7-6.1 | 3exp\nM2 correct measurement of distance moved by solvent | ALLOW 8.7-9.1 | \nM3 use and evaluation of |  | \n$R_{f}=\\underline{\\underline{distance moved by spot Y}}$ distance moved by solvent | ALLOW 1-4 sig fig ALLOW ECF from M1 M2 only if $R_{f}<1$ | \n(ii) | spot from yellow food dye/Y does not move as far as spot from red food dye/R OWTTE | ORA | 1exp", "row_count": 13, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(a)(i)", "magnesium", "ALLOW Mg", "1 cler"], ["(ii)", "explanation including the following pointsM1 silverM2 because it is the least reactive(of the metals)", "ALLOW it is very unreactive", "2 grad"], ["(b)", "explanation including the following pointsM1 Method 1/ heating the metal oxide/lead(II) oxide with carbonM2 (because) lead is less reactive than iron(and iron is obtained from iron oxide by carbon extraction)M3 2PbO+C→2Pb+CO2", "ALLOW carbon is more reactive than leadACCEPT reverse argumentsALLOW PbO+CO→Pb+CO2ALLOW PbO+C→Pb+CO", "3 exp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(a)(i) | magnesium | ALLOW Mg | 1 cler\n(ii) | explanation including the following pointsM1 silverM2 because it is the least reactive(of the metals) | ALLOW it is very unreactive | 2 grad\n(b) | explanation including the following pointsM1 Method 1/ heating the metal oxide/lead(II) oxide with carbonM2 (because) lead is less reactive than iron(and iron is obtained from iron oxide by carbon extraction)M3 2PbO+C→2Pb+CO2 | ALLOW carbon is more reactive than leadACCEPT reverse argumentsALLOW PbO+CO→Pb+CO2ALLOW PbO+C→Pb+CO | 3 exp", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(c)", "Explanation containing the following points\nPure metal:\nM1(particles/ions/atoms are same size in a regular arrangement so) layers can easily slide over each other\nAlloy:\nM2 diagram of alloy structure showing minimum of three layers with at least one different sized circle\nM3(having different sized particles/ions/atoms) disrupts/breaks up regular arrangement OWTTE\nM4so hard(er) for layers to slide over each other", "REJECT molecules once only\nALLOW disrupts the lattice / layers / rows(of particles/ions/atoms)\nALLOW layers cannot slide over each other\nIGNORE references to strength/breaking of forces/(metallic) bonds", "4exp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(c) | Explanation containing the following points\nPure metal:\nM1(particles/ions/atoms are same size in a regular arrangement so) layers can easily slide over each other\nAlloy:\nM2 diagram of alloy structure showing minimum of three layers with at least one different sized circle\nM3(having different sized particles/ions/atoms) disrupts/breaks up regular arrangement OWTTE\nM4so hard(er) for layers to slide over each other | REJECT molecules once only\nALLOW disrupts the lattice / layers / rows(of particles/ions/atoms)\nALLOW layers cannot slide over each other\nIGNORE references to strength/breaking of forces/(metallic) bonds | 4exp", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "CH3OH", "IGNORE displayed formula", "1grad"], ["(b)(i)", "fermentation", "", "1cler"], ["(ii)", "Explanation including four fromM1 fermentation/reaction/respiration needs to be anaerobicM2 because in air/aerobic conditions ethanol not producedM3 because in air/aerobic conditions CO2and H2Oare producedM4(if temperature above40℃/too high)enzymes(in yeast)become denatured/lose their structureOWTTEM5 causing fermentation/reaction to slow down/stop", "ALLOWM1 in air ethanol would react with oxygen/be oxidisedM2 in air ethanol would form ethanoic acid/carboxylic acid/vinegarALLOW reference to optimum temperature(between30℃and40℃)", "4exp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | CH3OH | IGNORE displayed formula | 1grad\n(b)(i) | fermentation |  | 1cler\n(ii) | Explanation including four fromM1 fermentation/reaction/respiration needs to be anaerobicM2 because in air/aerobic conditions ethanol not producedM3 because in air/aerobic conditions CO2and H2Oare producedM4(if temperature above40℃/too high)enzymes(in yeast)become denatured/lose their structureOWTTEM5 causing fermentation/reaction to slow down/stop | ALLOWM1 in air ethanol would react with oxygen/be oxidisedM2 in air ethanol would form ethanoic acid/carboxylic acid/vinegarALLOW reference to optimum temperature(between30℃and40℃) | 4exp", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(c)(i)", "M1M2C3H6O2M3 butanoic acidcarboxylic(acids)", "", "3grad1grad"], ["(d)(i)(ii)", "(acid acts as) a catalyst/to speed up reaction(ii)M1 ester linkageM2 rest of molecule fully correct", "IGNORE references to activation energy", "1grad2exp"], ["(iii)", "M1(Property:) distinctive/sweet/fruity smellM2 used in perfumes/flavourings", "ALLOW volatileALLOW any correct use eg in making soaps/in solvents(for paints/varnishes)", "2exp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(c)(i) | M1M2C3H6O2M3 butanoic acidcarboxylic(acids) |  | 3grad1