ivation energy correctly shown and labelledM4 $\\triangle H$ correctly shown and labelled", "4ExpALLOW double headed arrowREJECT arrow pointing downwardsALLOW double headed arrowREJECT arrow pointing upwardsALLOW -3446 for $\\triangle H$ labelan endothermic reaction profile can score M2 M3 M4 ECF"]], "text": "(c)(i) | $2\\text{C}_{4}\\text{H}_{6}+7\\text{O}_{2}\\rightarrow 2\\text{C}+4\\text{CO}+2\\text{CO}_{2}+6\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}$ | 1Exp\n(ii) | Explanation includingM1 CO/carbon monoxideM2 is poisonous/toxic/reduces capacity of blood to carry oxygenOWTTEORM1 CO_{2}/carbon dioxideM2 is a greenhouse gas/contributes to global warming/contributes to climate changeOWTTE | 2ExpACCEPT prevents blood from carrying oxygenOWTTEALLOW correct explanation in terms of haemoglobin eg prevents haemoglobin from carrying oxygen/forms carboxyhaemoglobin\n(iii) | M1 horizontal line below level of reactants with $8\\text{CO}_{2}+6\\text{H}_{2}\\text{O}$M2 profile curve rising from reactants level to form“hump” and then falling down to products levelM3 activation energy correctly shown and labelledM4 $\\triangle H$ correctly shown and labelled | 4ExpALLOW double headed arrowREJECT arrow pointing downwardsALLOW double headed arrowREJECT arrow pointing upwardsALLOW -3446 for $\\triangle H$ labelan endothermic reaction profile can score M2 M3 M4 ECF", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 3, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6", "(a)(i)", "zinc would react with sulfuric acid/solution X", "IGNORE zinc is too reactive", "1 grad"], ["(ii)", "bubbles", "ALLOW fizzing / effervescence\nIGNORE gas evolved\nIGNORE incorrectly named gas", "1 grad"], ["(iii)", "B a burning splint gives a squeaky pop is correct because this is the test for hydrogen\nA is incorrect because a glowing splint relights is not the test for hydrogen\nC is incorrect because a burning splint goes out is not the test for hydrogen\nD is incorrect because limewater turns cloudy is not the test for hydrogen", "", "1 comp"], ["(b)", "description including\nM1 add barium chloride/BaCl2", "ACCEPT barium nitrate/Ba(NO3)2\nIGNORE references to adding (dilute)\nHCl/HNO3\nREJECT add H2SO4", "2 Grad"], ["(c)(i)", "(graduated) pipette", "ALLOW burette", "1 Cler"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 | (a)(i) | zinc would react with sulfuric acid/solution X | IGNORE zinc is too reactive | 1 grad\n(ii) | bubbles | ALLOW fizzing / effervescence\nIGNORE gas evolved\nIGNORE incorrectly named gas | 1 grad\n(iii) | B a burning splint gives a squeaky pop is correct because this is the test for hydrogen\nA is incorrect because a glowing splint relights is not the test for hydrogen\nC is incorrect because a burning splint goes out is not the test for hydrogen\nD is incorrect because limewater turns cloudy is not the test for hydrogen |  | 1 comp\n(b) | description including\nM1 add barium chloride/BaCl2 | ACCEPT barium nitrate/Ba(NO3)2\nIGNORE references to adding (dilute)\nHCl/HNO3\nREJECT add H2SO4 | 2 Grad\n(c)(i) | (graduated) pipette | ALLOW burette | 1 Cler", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "calculation with following steps\nM1 setting out of how to calculate n(KOH)\nM2 evaluation\nExample calculation\nM1 n(KOH)=0.125x25÷1000\nM2=0.003125/3.125x10-3", "ALLOW any number of sig figs except one\nIf no division by 1000 giving answer of 3.125 award 1 mark\ncorrect answer with no working scores 2", "2Exp"]], "text": "(ii) | calculation with following steps\nM1 setting out of how to calculate n(KOH)\nM2 evaluation\nExample calculation\nM1 n(KOH)=0.125x25÷1000\nM2=0.003125/3.125x10-3 | ALLOW any number of sig figs except one\nIf no division by 1000 giving answer of 3.125 award 1 mark\ncorrect answer with no working scores 2 | 2Exp", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(iii)", "calculation with following steps\nM1 calculate n(H2SO4)=M2 from(i)÷2\nM2 calculate vol H2SO4=(M1x1000)÷0.10\nM3 evaluation of volume\nExample calculation\nM1 0.003125÷2=0.0015625/1.5625x10-3\nM2 0.0015625x1000÷0.10\nM3=15.625/15.63/15.6/16(cm3)", "Mark ECF from M1\nMark ECF from M2\nALLOW any number of sig figs except one\ncorrect answer with no working scores 3\nDo not penalise not multiplying by 1000 in(iii) if they have not divided by 1000 in(ii)\n31.25/31.3/31 scores 2\n62.5/63 scores 2", "3Exp"]], "text": "(iii) | calculation with following steps\nM1 calculate n(H2SO4)=M2 from(i)÷2\nM2 calculate vol H2SO4=(M1x1000)÷0.10\nM3 evaluation of volume\nExample calculation\nM1 0.003125÷2=0.0015625/1.5625x10-3\nM2 0.0015625x1000÷0.10\nM3=15.625/15.63/15.6/16(cm3) | Mark ECF from M1\nMark ECF from M2\nALLOW any number of sig figs except one\ncorrect answer with no working scores 3\nDo not penalise not multiplying by 1000 in(iii) if they have not divided by 1000 in(ii)\n31.25/31.3/31 scores 2\n62.5/63 scores 2 | 3Exp", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "calculation with following steps\nM1 calculation of n(K2CO3)\nM2 deduction of n(CO2)和\nvol(CO2) by multiplying by 24(dm3)\nM3 correct evaluation of volume in cm3\nExample calculation\nM1 n(K2CO3)=6.9÷138OR0.05\nM2 vol(CO2)=0.05x24(dm3)\nM3 1200(cm3)", "Mark ECF from M1\ncorrect answer with no working scores 3\n1.2 scores 2 marks", "3\nExp"], ["(b)(i)", "M1 higher yield of CO\nM2 because (equilibrium shifts to the right as the forward) reaction is endothermic", "ACCEPT more CO is produced\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s Principle eg increasing temperature favours the forward reaction\nM2 DEP M1 correct or missing", "2\nExp"], ["(ii)", "M1 no effect (on yield) OWTTE\nM2 because equal numbers of moles/molecules (of gas) on both sides", "M2 DEP M1 correct or missing", "2\nExp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | calculation with following steps\nM1 calculation of n(K2CO3)\nM2 deduction of n(CO2)和\nvol(CO2) by multiplying by 24(dm3)\nM3 correct evaluation of volume in cm3\nExample calculation\nM1 n(K2CO3)=6.9÷138OR0.05\nM2 vol(CO2)=0.05x24(dm3)\nM3 1200(cm3) | Mark ECF from M1\ncorrect answer with no working scores 3\n1.2 scores 2 marks | 3\nExp\n(b)(i) | M1 higher yield of CO\nM2 because (equilibrium shifts to the right as the forward) reaction is endothermic | ACCEPT more CO is produced\nIGNORE references to Le Chatelier''s Principle eg increasing temperature favours the forward reaction\nM2 DEP M1 correct or missing | 2\nExp\n(ii) | M1 no effect (on yield) OWTTE\nM2 because equal numbers of moles/molecules (of gas) on both sides | M2 DEP M1 correct or missing | 2\nExp", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000019", "e000021", "e000024", "e000027", "e000030", "e000034", "e000036"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "a7488398-a7d0-5837-8870-085a9992379e", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:01:05.366388265Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 92, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 2, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "November 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Autumn 2020 Publications Code 4CH1_2C_2011_MS All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Q1=5", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Q2=7", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Q3 = 10", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Q4=15", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Q5=15", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Q6 = 11", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for Q7=7", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:01:25.867404+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('2ad4d062-4bc3-4f0c-aed9-ddddd9b3b1b7', 'cb9f6de1-5273-543c-af09-ed31fe11d020', '1.0', 1, 'QUESTION_PAPER', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2020junr/QP.md', 'QP.md', 'text/markdown', '3f5b72af74212f3ebd6ecb7f327aadd820aaeced336183cfea12e6d41e3fac15', 'SHA-256', 1, 136, 129, 10, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 13:01:05.984986+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2020junr/QP.md", "checksum": "3f5b72af74212f3ebd6ecb7f327aadd820aaeced336183cfea12e6d41e3fac15", "fileName": "QP.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information"], ["Candidate surname", "Other names"], ["Centre Number Candidate Number"], ["Pearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)"], ["Wednesday 10 June 2020"], ["Afternoon (Time: 1 hour 15 minutes)", "Paper Reference 4CH1/2CR"], ["Chemistry\nUnit: 4CH1\nPaper: 2CR"], ["You must have:\nCalculator"], ["Total Marks"]], "text": "Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information\nCandidate surname | Other names\nCentre Number Candidate Number\nPearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)\nWednesday 10 June 2020\nAfternoon (Time: 1 hour 15 minutes) | Paper Reference 4CH1/2CR\nChemistry\nUnit: 4CH1\nPaper: 2CR\nYou must have:\nCalculator\nTotal Marks", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7Li lithium3", "9Be beryllium4", "Key", "4He helium2"], ["23Na sodium11", "24Mg magnesium12", "relative atomic mass atomic symbol atomic (proton) number", "20Ne neon10"], ["39K potassium19", "40Ca calcium20", "45Sc scandium21", "48Ti titanium22", "51V vanadium23", "52Cr chromium24", "55Mn manganese25", "56Fe iron26", "59Co cobalt27", "59Ni nickel28", "63.5Cu copper29", "65Zn zinc30", "70Ga gallium31", "73Ge germanium32", "75As arsenic33", "79Se selenium34", "80Br bromine35", "84Kr krypton36"], ["85Rb rubidium37", "88Sr strontium38", "89Y yttrium39", "91Zr zirconium40", "93Nb niobium41", "96Mo molybdenum42", "[98]Tc technetium43", "101Ru ruthenium44", "103Rh rhodium45", "106Pd palladium46", "108Ag silver47", "112Cd cadmium48", "115In indium49", "119Sn tin50", "122Sb antimony51", "128Te tellurium52", "127I iodine53", "131Xe xenon54"], ["133Cs caesium55", "137Ba barium56", "139La* lanthanum57", "178Hf hafnium72", "181Ta tantalum73", "184W tungsten74", "186Re rhenium75", "190Os osmium76", "192Ir iridium77", "195Pt platinum78", "197Au gold79", "201Hg mercury80", "204TI thallium81", "207Pb lead82", "209Bi bismuth83", "[209]Po polonium84", "[210]At astatine85", "[222]Rn radon86"], ["[223]Fr francium87", "[226]Ra radium88", "[227]Ac* actinium89", "[261]Rf rutherfordium104", "[262]Db dubnium105", "[266]Sg seaborgium106", "[264]Bh bohrium107", "[277]Hs hassium108", "[268]Mt meitnerium109", "[271]Ds darmstadium110", "[272]Rg roentgenium111", "Elements with atomic numbers 112-116 have been reported but not fully authenticated"]], "text": "7Li lithium3 | 9Be beryllium4 | Key | 4He helium2\n23Na sodium11 | 24Mg magnesium12 | relative atomic mass atomic symbol atomic (proton) number | 20Ne neon10\n39K potassium19 | 40Ca calcium20 | 45Sc scandium21 | 48Ti titanium22 | 51V vanadium23 | 52Cr chromium24 | 55Mn manganese25 | 56Fe iron26 | 59Co cobalt27 | 59Ni nickel28 | 63.5Cu copper29 | 65Zn zinc30 | 70Ga gallium31 | 73Ge germanium32 | 75As arsenic33 | 79Se selenium34 | 80Br bromine35 | 84Kr krypton36\n85Rb rubidium37 | 88Sr strontium38 | 89Y yttrium39 | 91Zr zirconium40 | 93Nb niobium41 | 96Mo molybdenum42 | [98]Tc technetium43 | 101Ru ruthenium44 | 103Rh rhodium45 | 106Pd palladium46 | 108Ag silver47 | 112Cd cadmium48 | 115In indium49 | 119Sn tin50 | 122Sb antimony51 | 128Te tellurium52 | 127I iodine53 | 131Xe xenon54\n133Cs caesium55 | 137Ba barium56 | 139La* lanthanum57 | 178Hf hafnium72 | 181Ta tantalum73 | 184W tungsten74 | 186Re rhenium75 | 190Os osmium76 | 192Ir iridium77 | 195Pt platinum78 | 197Au gold79 | 201Hg mercury80 | 204TI thallium81 | 207Pb lead82 | 209Bi bismuth83 | [209]Po polonium84 | [210]At astatine85 | [222]Rn radon86\n[223]Fr francium87 | [226]Ra radium88 | [227]Ac* actinium89 | [261]Rf rutherfordium104 | [262]Db dubnium105 | [266]Sg seaborgium106 | [264]Bh bohrium107 | [277]Hs hassium108 | [268]Mt meitnerium109 | [271]Ds darmstadium110 | [272]Rg roentgenium111 | Elements with atomic numbers 112-116 have been reported but not fully authenticated", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Letter", "Name"], ["A", ""], ["B", ""], ["C", ""], ["D", ""]], "text": "Letter | Name\nA | \nB | \nC | \nD | ", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 2, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Isotope", "Mass number", "Percentage abundance(%)"], ["thallium-203", "203", "30.80"], ["thallium-205", "205", "69.20"]], "text": "Isotope | Mass number | Percentage abundance(%)\nthallium-203 | 203 | 30.80\nthallium-205 | 205 | 69.20", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000052", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 3, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 52, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["lithium ion", "fluoride ion"], ["", ""]], "text": "lithium ion | fluoride ion\n | ", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000075", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 2, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 75, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Element", "Electronic configuration"], ["sodium", "2.8.1"], ["potassium", "2.8.8.1"]], "text": "Element | Electronic configuration\nsodium | 2.8.1\npotassium | 2.8.8.1", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000077", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 2, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 77, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Bond", "C-C", "C-H", "C-O", "O-H", "O=O", "C=O"], ["Bond energy in kJ/mol", "346", "412", "358", "463", "496", "743"]], "text": "Bond | C-C | C-H | C-O | O-H | O=O | C=O\nBond energy in kJ/mol | 346 | 412 | 358 | 463 | 496 | 743", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000129", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 7, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 129, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(i) Use values from the table to calculate the energy needed to break all the bonds in the reactants.", "(2)"], ["energy needed", "kJ"], ["(ii) Use values from the table to calculate the energy released when all the bonds in the products are formed.", "(2)"], ["energy released", "kJ"], ["(iii) Calculate the molar enthalpy change ($\\Delta H$) in kJ/mol, for the complete combustion of ethanol.", "Include a sign in your answer."], ["$\\Delta H = \\dots\\dots\n(c) Ethanol reacts with methanoic acid, HCOOH, in the presence of an acid catalyst to form an ester.\nThe equation for the reaction is\n$$\n\\mathrm {C} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {5} \\mathrm {O H} + \\mathrm {H C O O H} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm {H C O O C} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {5} + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O}\n$$\n(i) Give the name of the ester that forms.\n(ii) Draw the displayed formula for this ester.\n(iii) When this reaction takes place in a sealed container, the reaction can reach dynamic equilibrium.\nGive two characteristics of a reaction at dynamic equilibrium.\n(d) Methanoic acid reacts with sodium carbonate to form sodium methanoate, carbon dioxide and water.\nThe equation for the reaction is\n$$\n2 \\mathrm {H C O O H} + \\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \\mathrm {C O} _ {3} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm {H C O O N a} + \\mathrm {C O} _ {2} + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O}\n$$\nCalculate the volume, in $ cm^{3} $ , of carbon dioxide gas produced when 2.3 g of methanoic acid reacts completely with sodium carbonate.\n[M $ _{r} $ of HCOOH=46]\n[molar volume of carbon dioxide at rtp=24 dm $ ^{3} $]\nvolume of carbon dioxide =", "cm3"]], "text": "(i) Use values from the table to calculate the energy needed to break all the bonds in the reactants. | (2)\nenergy needed | kJ\n(ii) Use values from the table to calculate the energy released when all the bonds in the products are formed. | (2)\nenergy released | kJ\n(iii) Calculate the molar enthalpy change ($\\Delta H$) in kJ/mol, for the complete combustion of ethanol. | Include a sign in your answer.\n$\\Delta H = \\dots\\dots\n(c) Ethanol reacts with methanoic acid, HCOOH, in the presence of an acid catalyst to form an ester.\nThe equation for the reaction is\n$$\n\\mathrm {C} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {5} \\mathrm {O H} + \\mathrm {H C O O H} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm {H C O O C} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {5} + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O}\n$$\n(i) Give the name of the ester that forms.\n(ii) Draw the displayed formula for this ester.\n(iii) When this reaction takes place in a sealed container, the reaction can reach dynamic equilibrium.\nGive two characteristics of a reaction at dynamic equilibrium.\n(d) Methanoic acid reacts with sodium carbonate to form sodium methanoate, carbon dioxide and water.\nThe equation for the reaction is\n$$\n2 \\mathrm {H C O O H} + \\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \\mathrm {C O} _ {3} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm {H C O O N a} + \\mathrm {C O} _ {2} + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O}\n$$\nCalculate the volume, in $ cm^{3} $ , of carbon dioxide gas produced when 2.3 g of methanoic acid reacts completely with sodium carbonate.\n[M $ _{r} $ of HCOOH=46]\n[molar volume of carbon dioxide at rtp=24 dm $ ^{3} $]\nvolume of carbon dioxide = | cm3", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000130", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 2, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 130, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [{"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_1_1789069646062.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_1_1789069646062.png", "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "figure", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_2_1789069646072.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_2_1789069646072.png", "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "figure", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_3_1789069646076.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_3_1789069646076.png", "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "figure", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_4_1789069646082.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_4_1789069646082.png", "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "figure", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"alt": "OCR图片", "text": "assets/crop_1_1789069646102.png", "format": "png", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000058", "page_number": 1, "source_name": "assets/crop_1_1789069646102