kdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Use black ink or ball-point pen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Fill in the boxes at the top of this page with your name, centre number and candidate number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer all questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer the questions in the spaces provided", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "there may be more space than you need.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Show all the steps in any calculations and state units.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Some questions must be answered with a cross in a box. If you change your mind about an answer, put a line through the box and then mark your new answer with a cross.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Information", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The total mark for this paper is 70.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The marks for each question are shown in brackets", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "use this as a guide as to how much time to spend on each question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Advice", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Read each question carefully before you start to answer it.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Write your answers neatly and in good English.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Try to answer every question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Check your answers if you have time at the end.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Turn over", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The lanthanoids (atomic numbers 58-71) and the actinoids (atomic numbers 90-103) have been omitted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The relative atomic masses of copper and chlorine have not been rounded to the nearest whole number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Answer ALL questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "1 The diagram shows some pieces of apparatus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Complete the table by giving the name of each piece of apparatus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Which piece of apparatus can be used to measure the volume of a liquid?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1 = 5 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "2 Thallium, Tl, is an element in Group 3 and Period 6 of the Periodic Table. The atomic number of thallium is 81 (a) How many electrons are there in the outer shell of an atom of thallium?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A 3", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B 6", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C 13", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D 81", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) A thallium ion has a charge of 3+", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "How many electrons are there in this thallium ion?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A 3", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B 78", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C 81", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D 84", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000049", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 49, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) A sample of thallium contains two isotopes.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000050", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 50, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows the mass number and percentage abundance of each isotope in the sample.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000051", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 51, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give the number of protons and the number of neutrons in one atom of the thallium-205 isotope.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000053", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 53, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "number of protons", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000054", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 54, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "number of neutrons", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000055", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 55, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Calculate the relative atomic mass of this sample of thallium. Give your answer to one decimal place.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000056", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 56, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "3 (a) The diagram shows a fractionating column used to separate crude oil into fractions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000057", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 57, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give a use for bitumen and a use for gasoline.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000059", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 59, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "use for bitumen use for gasoline", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000060", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 60, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Explain why bitumen is collected at the bottom of the fractionating column and gasoline is collected near the top of the fractionating column.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000061", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 61, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) There is a low demand for some of the fractions obtained from crude oil. Cracking can be used to convert these fractions into more useful substances. (i) State the conditions needed for cracking.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000062", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 62, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Dodecane $ \\left( \\mathrm{C}_{1 2} \\mathrm{H}_{2 6} \\right) $ can be cracked to produce an alkane and two alkenes. Complete the equation by giving the formulae of the two alkenes.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000063", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 63, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 3 = 8 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000065", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 65, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000066", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 66, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "4 This question is about some of the alkali metals and their compounds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000067", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 67, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) When a teacher drops a small piece of sodium into a trough of cold water, she observes bubbles of gas.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000068", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 68, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give two other observations that would be made when sodium reacts with cold water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000069", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 69, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Lithium reacts with fluorine to form the compound lithium fluoride.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000070", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 70, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give a chemical equation for this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000071", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 71, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give a test to show that lithium fluoride contains lithium ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000072", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 72, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Draw diagrams to show the arrangement of the electrons in a lithium ion and in a fluoride ion.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000073", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 73, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Include the charge on each ion.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000074", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 74, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The table shows the electronic configurations of sodium and potassium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000076", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 76, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain, in terms of their electronic configurations, why potassium is more reactive than sodium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000078", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 78, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 11 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000079", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 79, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "5 This question is about the metal aluminium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000080", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 80, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) (i) Draw a labelled diagram to represent the structure and bonding in a metal.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000081", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 81, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Explain why a metal conducts electricity.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000082", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 82, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Aluminium is used to make cans for drinks.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000083", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 83, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give two properties of aluminium that make it suitable for this use.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000085", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 85, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Aluminium is extracted from aluminium oxide $ \\mathrm{(A l_{2} O_{3})} $ by electrolysis.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000086", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 86, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The electrolyte is aluminium oxide dissolved in molten cryolite.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000087", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 87, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State why aluminium cannot be extracted by heating aluminium oxide with carbon.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000088", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 88, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Aluminium is produced at the negative electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000089", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 89, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The ionic half-equation for the reaction is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000090", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 90, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "State why this is a reduction reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000092", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 92, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Complete the ionic half-equation for the reaction at the positive electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000093", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 93, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000095", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 95, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "6 A student wants to prepare sodium chloride crystals from sodium hydroxide solution and dilute hydrochloric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000096", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 96, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "He does a titration to find the volume of dilute hydrochloric acid needed to neutralise the sodium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000097", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 97, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is his method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000098", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 98, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution to a conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000099", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 99, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add a few drops of phenolphthalein indicator to the conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000100", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 100, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "titrate the solution with the hydrochloric acid", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000101", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 101, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Name a suitable piece of apparatus that the student should use to measure $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000102", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 102, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) (i) Give the colour of the phenolphthalein indicator in sodium hydroxide solution and in hydrochloric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000103", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 103, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "colour in sodium hydroxide solution", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000104", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 104, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "colour in hydrochloric acid...", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000105", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 105, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Suggest why universal indicator is never used in a titration.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000106", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 106, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The student finds that $ 2 1. 5 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of hydrochloric acid is needed to neutralise $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000107", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 107, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Describe what the student should do next to prepare a pure solution of sodium chloride.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000108", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 108, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Describe how the student could obtain dry crystals of sodium chloride from the pure sodium chloride solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000109", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 109, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) The student needs $ 2 1. 5 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of hydrochloric acid to neutralise $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution of concentration $ 0. 8 0 0 \\mathrm{m o l} / \\mathrm{d m}^{3}. $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000110", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 110, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation for the reaction is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000111", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 111, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the concentration, in mol/dm $ ^{3} $ , of the hydrochloric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000113", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 113, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6 = 13 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000115", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 115, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "7 (a) Ethanol, $ \\mathrm{C_{2} H_{5} O H} $ , can be oxidised to produce ethanoic acid, $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} C O O H} $ , by heating it with potassium dichromate(VI).", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000116", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 116, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Name one other reactant needed for this reaction to occur.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000117", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 117, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Which colour change occurs during this reaction?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000118", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 118, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A colourless to green", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000119", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 119, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B green to orange", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000120", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 120, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "orange to colourless", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000121", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 121, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D orange to green", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000122", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 122, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) When ethanol is burned in air, complete combustion can occur.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000123", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 123, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation for this reaction is", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000124", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 124, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This equation can also be written using displayed formulae to show all the covalent bonds in the molecules.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000126", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 126, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table gives the bond energies for these bonds.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000128", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 128, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7 = 16 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000131", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 131, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "TOTAL FOR PAPER = 70 MARKS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000132", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 132, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000133", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 133, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000134", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 134, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000135", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 135, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:01:26.018365+00');
