er | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(a)(i) | M1(bitumen)(surfacing) roads/(surfacing) roofs | ALLOW other suitable uses | 2Exp\nM2(gasoline) petrol/fuel for cars/vehicles | ALLOW other suitable uses e.g. fuel for cooking | \nAn explanation that links the following two points |  | 2Exp\nM1 column is cooler near the top than at the bottom ORA | ACCEPT column cool near the top and hot at the bottom | \n | ACCEPT temperature decreases up the column ORA | \nM2 gasoline has a lower boiling point than bitumen(so is collected nearer the top) ORA | ACCEPT gasoline has a low boiling point(so is collected near the top) and bitumen has a high boiling point(so is collected near the bottom) | \n(b)(i) | M1 alumina/silica(catalyst) | ACCEPT Al2O3/SiO2/aluminium oxide/silicon dioxide/aluminosilicate(s)/zeolite(s) | 2Exp\nM2600-700(℃) | ACCEPT range or any value within the range | \nC12H26-->C7H16+C2H4+C3H6 | ACCEPT correct temperatures in other units | \nM1C2H4M2C3H6 | ACCEPT answers in either order | 2Exp\n |  |  | Total8", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "Any two of the following observations.", "", "2Exp"], ["M1(sodium) floats/moves on surface(of water)", "", ""], ["M2(sodium) melts/forms a ball", "", ""], ["M3(sodium) gets smaller/disappears", "ALLOW dissolves", ""], ["M4(sodium forms) white trail", "IGNORE references to flame/heat released/temperature increasesIGNORE fizzing/effervescence", ""], ["(b)(i)", "2Li+F2→2LiF", "ALLOW multiples or fractionsIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", "1Exp"], ["M1 flame testM2 red(flame)", "ALLOW description of flame testALLOW crimson/scarletREJECT orange-red/brick red", "2Exp"], ["(iii)", "M1 correct electron arrangement of lithium ion", "ACCEPT any combination of dots and crossesIGNORE empty second shell", "3Exp"], ["M2 correct electron arrangement of fluoride ion", "Inner electron shell required to score M2", ""], ["M3 correct charges on both ions(with or without brackets)", "M3 not dep on M1 and M2 correct", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | Any two of the following observations. |  | 2Exp\nM1(sodium) floats/moves on surface(of water) |  | \nM2(sodium) melts/forms a ball |  | \nM3(sodium) gets smaller/disappears | ALLOW dissolves | \nM4(sodium forms) white trail | IGNORE references to flame/heat released/temperature increasesIGNORE fizzing/effervescence | \n(b)(i) | 2Li+F2→2LiF | ALLOW multiples or fractionsIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | 1Exp\nM1 flame testM2 red(flame) | ALLOW description of flame testALLOW crimson/scarletREJECT orange-red/brick red | 2Exp\n(iii) | M1 correct electron arrangement of lithium ion | ACCEPT any combination of dots and crossesIGNORE empty second shell | 3Exp\nM2 correct electron arrangement of fluoride ion | Inner electron shell required to score M2 | \nM3 correct charges on both ions(with or without brackets) | M3 not dep on M1 and M2 correct | ", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(c)", "An explanation that links three of the following four points", "", "3\nExp"], ["M1 the outer electron is further from the nucleus in potassium / potassium has more shells/ potassium has larger atomic radius ORA", "ALLOW potassium atom is bigger than a sodium atom", ""], ["M2 there is more shielding (by the inner shells) in potassium ORA", "", ""], ["M3 there is less attraction between the outer electron and the nucleus in potassium ORA", "outer electron needs to be mentioned at least once in the answer for full marks", ""], ["M4 (so outer) electron (in potassium) more easily lost ORA", "Max 2 if no mention of outer electron in the answer", ""], ["", "", "Total 11"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(c) | An explanation that links three of the following four points |  | 3\nExp\nM1 the outer electron is further from the nucleus in potassium / potassium has more shells/ potassium has larger atomic radius ORA | ALLOW potassium atom is bigger than a sodium atom | \nM2 there is more shielding (by the inner shells) in potassium ORA |  | \nM3 there is less attraction between the outer electron and the nucleus in potassium ORA | outer electron needs to be mentioned at least once in the answer for full marks | \nM4 (so outer) electron (in potassium) more easily lost ORA | Max 2 if no mention of outer electron in the answer | \n |  | Total 11", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)(i)", "A labelled diagram showingM1 at least three rows of at least three cations/atoms in a regular arrangementM2 surrounded by (delocalised) electronsExample of diagram", "Max 1 if no labelsMinimum requirement for 2 marks is + signs on atoms and electrons labelled or shown as e-", "2Exp"], ["An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 delocalised electronsM2 flow/are mobile/move/are free to move", "IGNORE free electrons/sea of electronsM2 dep on mention of electronsAny mention of ions/atoms moving scores 0", "2Exp"], ["Any two of the following propertiesM1 low densityM2 does not react with drinkM3 malleable", "ALLOW lightweightIGNORE lightIGNORE less denseALLOW does not corrode/non-toxicIGNORE does not rustALLOW easy to bend/easy to shapeIGNORE references to costIGNORE can be recycledIGNORE any irrelevant properties e.g. high melting/boiling point/good conductor/ductile", "2Exp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a)(i) | A labelled diagram showingM1 at least three rows of at least three cations/atoms in a regular arrangementM2 surrounded by (delocalised) electronsExample of diagram | Max 1 if no labelsMinimum requirement for 2 marks is + signs on atoms and electrons labelled or shown as e- | 2Exp\nAn explanation that links the following two pointsM1 delocalised electronsM2 flow/are mobile/move/are free to move | IGNORE free electrons/sea of electronsM2 dep on mention of electronsAny mention of ions/atoms moving scores 0 | 2Exp\nAny two of the following propertiesM1 low densityM2 does not react with drinkM3 malleable | ALLOW lightweightIGNORE lightIGNORE less denseALLOW does not corrode/non-toxicIGNORE does not rustALLOW easy to bend/easy to shapeIGNORE references to costIGNORE can be recycledIGNORE any irrelevant properties e.g. high melting/boiling point/good conductor/ductile | 2Exp", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(c)(i)", "aluminium/it is more reactive/higher in the reactivity series than carbon ORA", "ALLOW aluminium is too reactive/too high in the reactivity series", "1Grad"], ["(ii)", "electrons are gained (by aluminium ion/Al3+)", "ACCEPT oxidation state of aluminium/Al is decreased/changes from+3to0REJECT aluminium/Al gains electronsIGNORE references to loss of oxygen", "1Exp"], ["(iii)", "2O2-→O2+4e(-)M1 correct formulae of productsM2 balancing of correct formulae", "ACCEPT multiples and fractionsM2 dep on M1", "2Exp"], ["", "", "", "Total 10"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(c)(i) | aluminium/it is more reactive/higher in the reactivity series than carbon ORA | ALLOW aluminium is too reactive/too high in the reactivity series | 1Grad\n(ii) | electrons are gained (by aluminium ion/Al3+) | ACCEPT oxidation state of aluminium/Al is decreased/changes from+3to0REJECT aluminium/Al gains electronsIGNORE references to loss of oxygen | 1Exp\n(iii) | 2O2-→O2+4e(-)M1 correct formulae of productsM2 balancing of correct formulae | ACCEPT multiples and fractionsM2 dep on M1 | 2Exp\n |  |  | Total 10", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6", "(a)(i)", "pipette", "", "1Cl"], ["", "(b)(i)", "M1(colour in NaOH) pink", "ACCEPT magenta\nALLOW red", "2Grad"], ["M2(colour in HCl) colourless/no colour", "IGNORE clear\n1 mark for two correct colours in the wrong order", ""], ["There is no clear (colour change at the) end point/difficult to determine which shade of green is pH 7 OWTTE", "ALLOW it has a range of colours", "1Exp"], ["", "(ii)", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 | (a)(i) | pipette |  | 1Cl\n | (b)(i) | M1(colour in NaOH) pink | ACCEPT magenta\nALLOW red | 2Grad\nM2(colour in HCl) colourless/no colour | IGNORE clear\n1 mark for two correct colours in the wrong order | \nThere is no clear (colour change at the) end point/difficult to determine which shade of green is pH 7 OWTTE | ALLOW it has a range of colours | 1Exp\n | (ii) |  | ", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(c)(i)", "A description that makes reference to the following two pointsM1 add 21.5cm3of hydrochloric acidM2 to 25cm3of sodium hydroxide solution", "0 marks if mention of adding indicatorALLOW repeat the titration without indicator for1markALLOW the following alternative methodM1 add activated charcoal(to absorb the indicator)M2 filter(to remove the activated charcoal and indicator)M2 dep onM1", "2Exp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(c)(i) | A description that makes reference to the following two pointsM1 add 21.5cm3of hydrochloric acidM2 to 25cm3of sodium hydroxide solution | 0 marks if mention of adding indicatorALLOW repeat the titration without indicator for1markALLOW the following alternative methodM1 add activated charcoal(to absorb the indicator)M2 filter(to remove the activated charcoal and indicator)M2 dep onM1 | 2Exp", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "A description that makes reference to the following four points", "Max 1 mark if solution evaporated to dryness", "4 Exp"], ["M1 heat the solution to evaporate some of the water/ to form a saturated solution/ to crystallisation point", "If solution left to partially evaporate without heating only M3 and M4 can be awarded", ""], ["M2 leave the solution to cool /leave the solution for (more) crystals to form", "", ""], ["M3 filter off the crystals", "IGNORE references to washing", ""], ["M4 suitable method of drying the crystals", "e.g. dry between filter papers/dry in a warm oven/ leave to dry", ""], ["", "REJECT hot oven or direct heating with Bunsen burner", ""], ["", "No M4 if crystals are washed after drying", ""], ["6(d)", "calculate the amount, in moles, of NaOH\ndivide amount in moles by volume in dm3\nevaluation to obtain correct answer", "correct answer without working scores 3 marks", "3 Exp"], ["", "Example calculation\nM1 n(NaOH) = 0.0250 x 0.800 or 0.02(00)\nM2 conc = (0.02 ÷ 0.0215)\nM3 0.930", "answer to M1 ÷ 0.0215\nALLOW any number of sig fig except 1", ""], ["", "", "ALLOW ecf on M2", ""], ["", "", "", "Total 13"]], "text": "(ii) | A description that makes reference to the following four points | Max 1 mark if solution evaporated to dryness | 4 Exp\nM1 heat the solution to evaporate some of the water/ to form a saturated solution/ to crystallisation point | If solution left to partially evaporate without heating only M3 and M4 can be awarded | \nM2 leave the solution to cool /leave the solution for (more) crystals to form |  | \nM3 filter off the crystals | IGNORE references to washing | \nM4 suitable method of drying the crystals | e.g. dry between filter papers/dry in a warm oven/ leave to dry | \n | REJECT hot oven or direct heating with Bunsen burner | \n | No M4 if crystals are washed after drying | \n6(d) | calculate the amount, in moles, of NaOH\ndivide amount in moles by volume in dm3\nevaluation to obtain correct answer | correct answer without working scores 3 marks | 3 Exp\n | Example calculation\nM1 n(NaOH) = 0.0250 x 0.800 or 0.02(00)\nM2 conc = (0.02 ÷ 0.0215)\nM3 0.930 | answer to M1 ÷ 0.0215\nALLOW any number of sig fig except 1 | \n |  | ALLOW ecf on M2 | \n |  |  | Total 13", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7", "(a)(i)", "sulfuric acid", "IGNORE references to concentration\nALLOW H2SO4\nREJECT sulfurous acid", "1\nGrad"], ["(ii)", "D orange to green\nA is incorrect as the solution is not colourless at the start of the reaction\nB is incorrect as the solution is not green at the start or orange at the end of the reaction\nC is incorrect as the solution is not colourless at the end of the reaction", "", "1\nComp"], ["(b)(i)", "(ii)", "·show the expression for the sum of the bond energies for the breaking of bonds\n·evaluation to give answer in kJ", "correct answer without working scores 2", "2\nExp"], ["M1∑C-C+5C-H+C-O+O-H+3O=O\nOR∑346+(5x412)+358+463+(3x496)\nM24715(kJ)", "-1 mark for each error", ""], ["(ii)", "(ii)", "·show the expression for the sum of the bond energies for the forming of bonds\n·evaluation to give answer in kJ", "correct answer without working scores 2", "2\nExp"], ["M1∑4C=O+6O-H\nOR∑(4x743)+(6x463)\nM25750(kJ)", "-1 mark for each error\nIGNORE any signs in(i)and(ii)", ""], ["(iii)", "(iii)", "(4715-5750=)-1035(kJ/mol)", "minus sign must be included\nACCEPT-1040(kJ/mol)\nALLOW ecf on answers to(i)and(ii)\nIf answers to(i)and(ii)are reversed allow max3and ecf on(iii)", "1\nExp"], ["", "", ""], ["", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7 | (a)(i) | sulfuric acid | IGNORE references to concentration\nALLOW H2SO4\nREJECT sulfurous acid | 1\nGrad\n(ii) | D orange to green\nA is incorrect as the solution is not colourless at the start of the reaction\nB is incorrect as the solution is not green at the start or orange at the end of the reaction\nC is incorrect as the solution is not colourless at the end of the reaction |  | 1\nComp\n(b)(i) | (ii) | ·show the expression for the sum of the bond energies for the breaking of bonds\n·evaluation to give answer in kJ | correct answer without working scores 2 | 2\nExp\nM1∑C-C+5C-H+C-O+O-H+3O=O\nOR∑346+(5x412)+358+463+(3x496)\nM24715(kJ) | -1 mark for each error | \n(ii) | (ii) | ·show the expression for the sum of the bond energies for the forming of bonds\n·evaluation to give answer in kJ | correct answer without working scores 2 | 2\nExp\nM1∑4C=O+6O-H\nOR∑(4x743)+(6x463)\nM25750(kJ) | -1 mark for each error\nIGNORE any signs in(i)and(ii) | \n(iii) | (iii) | (4715-5750=)-1035(kJ/mol) | minus sign must be included\nACCEPT-1040(kJ/mol)\nALLOW ecf on answers to(i)and(ii)\nIf answers to(i)and(ii)are reversed allow max3and ecf on(iii) | 1\nExp\n |  | \n |  | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(c)(i)(ii)(iii)", "ethyl methanoate", "ALLOW ethyl formateALLOW words written without gap", "1Grad"], ["M1 ester linkageO-|-C-O-", "", "2Exp"], ["M2 rest of molecule correctStructural formula of ethyl formate or ethyl methanoate", "M2 dep on M1", ""], ["M1 forward and reverse reactions occur at the same rate OWTTEM2 concentrations of reactants and products remain constant", "", "2Exp"], ["(d)", "calculate amount in moles of HCOOHuse equation to find amount in moles of CO2multiply amount in moles of CO2 by molar volumeevaluation of answer in cm3Example calculationM1 n(HCOOH)=2.3÷46or0.05(0)M2 n(CO2)=0.05(0)÷2or0.025M3(volume of CO2)=0.025x24or0.025x24000M4600(cm3)", "correct answer without working scores4No ecf from M1 and M2 if mass or Mr multiplied by 24/24000ALLOW ecf from M30.6,1200 and 2400 score31.2 and 2.4 score2", "4Exp"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(c)(i)(ii)(iii) | ethyl methanoate | ALLOW ethyl formateALLOW words written without gap | 1Grad\nM1 ester linkageO-|-C-O- |  | 2Exp\nM2 rest of molecule correctStructural formula of ethyl formate or ethyl methanoate | M2 dep on M1 | \nM1 forward and reverse reactions occur at the same rate OWTTEM2 concentrations of reactants and products remain constant |  | 2Exp\n(d) | calculate amount in moles of HCOOHuse equation to find amount in moles of CO2multiply amount in moles of CO2 by molar volumeevaluation of answer in cm3Example calculationM1 n(HCOOH)=2.3÷46or0.05(0)M2 n(CO2)=0.05(0)÷2or0.025M3(volume of CO2)=0.025x24or0.025x24000M4600(cm3) | correct answer without working scores4No ecf from M1 and M2 if mass or Mr multiplied by 24/24000ALLOW ecf from M30.6,1200 and 2400 score31.2 and 2.4 score2 | 4Exp", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "", "", "Total\n16"]], "text": " |  |  | Total\n16", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "afea9828-beed-5934-ab5a-9d931a781d9e", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:01:06.055593944Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 66, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "November 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Autumn 2020 Publications Code 4CH1_2CR_2011_MS All the material in this publication is copyright $ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2020", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:01:26.067201+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('a0f7da10-1869-4442-be9c-2b82d2845952', '7e261528-c3e7-5b6d-9cde-a941a56e82d8', '1.0', 1, 'QUESTION_PAPER', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2021jan/QP.md', 'QP.md', 'text/markdown', '13b8cded84321a508bb84d6f9d28a305c83001b6c4b81721ef09741394f95329', 'SHA-256', 1, 141, 135, 10, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 13:01:06.63189+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2021jan/QP.md", "checksum": "13b8cded84321a508bb84d6f9d28a305c83001b6c4b81721ef09741394f95329", "fileName": "QP.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information"], ["Candidate surname", "Other names"], ["Centre Number"], ["Candidate Number"], ["Pearson Edexcel\nInternational GCSE (9-1)"], ["Thursday 14 January 2021"], ["Morning (Time: 1 hour 15 minutes)", "Paper Reference 4CH1/2C"], ["Chemistry\nUnit: 4CH1\nPaper 2C"], ["You must have:\nCalculator, ruler"], ["Total Marks"]], "text": "Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information\nCandidate surname | Other names\nCentre Number\nCandidate Number\nPearson Edexcel\nInternational GCSE (9-1)\nThursday 14 January 2021\nMorning (Time: 1 hour 15 minutes) | Paper Reference 4CH1/2C\nChemistry\nUnit: 4CH1\nPaper 2C\nYou must have:\nCalculator, ruler\nTotal Marks", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7Li lithium3", "9Be beryllium4", "Key", "4He helium2"], ["23Na sodium11", "24Mg magnesium12", "relative atomic mass atomic symbol atomic (proton) number", "20Ne neon10"], ["39K potassium19", "40Ca calcium20", "45Sc scandium21", "48Ti titanium22", "51V vanadium23", "52Cr chromium24