 "2"], ["M2 which reacts with/burns in oxygen", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a)(i) | M1 layers/rows(of atoms/ions) |  | 2\nM2 can slide over one another | M2 is dependent on mention of layers/rows in M1 | \nM1 delocalised electronsM2 can move/can flow/are free to move(throughout the structure) | IGNORE references to charge or currentIGNORE free electronsM2 dependent on mention of electrons in M1 | 2\n(b) | aluminium is more reactive than carbon | ALLOW references to position in reactivity series e.g. aluminium is higher in reactivity series than carbon.ALLOW carbon is less reactive than aluminium | 1\n(c)(i) | M1 aluminium/Al3+ions are attracted to the negative electrode/cathode(because they are positively charged) |  | 2\nM2 where they gain electrons(forming aluminium) | ALLOW Al3+ + 3e-→AlIGNORE references to reduction | \n(ii) | 2O2-→O2+4e- | ALLOW 2O2- - 4e-→O2 | 1\n(iii) | M1 electrodes are made of carbon |  | 2\nM2 which reacts with/burns in oxygen |  | ", "row_count": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(d)(i)", "iron oxide loses oxygen", "IGNORE references to electrons", "1"], ["(ii)", "aluminium+iron oxide\niron+aluminium oxide", "IGNORE horizontal axis drawn", "3"], ["", "M1 right hand line below left hand line", "", ""], ["", "M2 correct name/formula of both reactants", "", ""], ["", "M3 correct name/formula of both products", "If only use words reactants(on left)和 products(on right) award 1 mark from M2 and M3", ""], ["", "", "M2 and M3 can be scored from an endothermic diagram", ""], ["14 marks"]], "text": "(d)(i) | iron oxide loses oxygen | IGNORE references to electrons | 1\n(ii) | aluminium+iron oxide\niron+aluminium oxide | IGNORE horizontal axis drawn | 3\n | M1 right hand line below left hand line |  | \n | M2 correc