rom M1 and M2", ""], ["M32Cl-→Cl2+2e-", "2H2O→O2+4H++4e- or 4OH-→O2+2H2O+4e-", ""], ["", "", "M42H++2e-→H2", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4 | (c)(i) | hydroxide/OH- | ALLOW HO- | 1\n(ii) | K2O+H2O→2KOH | ALLOW multiples | 1\n(d) | (e) | M1(when molten or in aqueous solution)ions can move |  | 2\nM2(in solid)ions cannot move |  | \nM1Xis chlorine/Cl2 | ALLOW oxygen/O2 | 4\nM2Yis hydrogen/H2 | If both given but wrong way round or unclear which is which allow 1 mark from M1 and M2 | \nM32Cl-→Cl2+2e- | 2H2O→O2+4H++4e- or 4OH-→O2+2H2O+4e- | \n |  | M42H++2e-→H2 |  | ", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5", "(a)(i)", "ore(s)", "IGNORE minerals", "1"], ["(ii)", "gold/platinum", "ALLOW silver/copper ALLOW symbols", "1"], ["5", "(b)(i)", "(calcium from calcium chloride)\nM1 electrolysis\nM2(because) calcium is more reactive than carbon OR carbon cannot displace calcium", "ALLOW reverse argument M2 dep on M1", "2"], ["(ii)", "(lead from lead oxide)\nM1 carbon extraction\nM2(because) carbon is more reactive than lead OR carbon can displace lead", "ALLOW reverse argument M2 dep on M1", "2"], ["", "", "", ""], ["", "", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5 | (a)(i) | ore(s) | IGNORE minerals | 1\n(ii) | gold/platinum | ALLOW silver/copper ALLOW symbols | 1\n5 | (b)(i) | (calcium from calcium chloride)\nM1 electrolysis\nM2(because) calcium is more reactive than carbon OR carbon cannot displace calcium | ALLOW reverse argument M2 dep on M1 | 2\n(ii) | (lead from lead oxide)\nM1 carbon extraction\nM2(because) carbon is more reactive than lead OR carbon can displace lead | ALLOW reverse argument M2 dep on M1 | 2\n |  |  | \n |  |  | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.