 (dm3) | ALLOWecf onM2andM36x10^{6} scores33x10^{6} scores36000000 scores23000000 scores22.083x10^{4} scores3 | \n(b)An explanation that links the following two pointsM1argon is unreactive/inertM2(so argon) will not react with/oxidise the magnesiumOR oxygen(in air) will react with/oxidise the magnesium | ALLOWargon will not react with/oxidise titaniumOR oxygen(in air) will react with/oxidise the titanium | 2\n(c)An explanation that links the following three pointsM1in pure titanium all atoms are the same sizeOR layers/atoms can slide over each other(making it soft/malleable)M2the alloy has atoms of different sizesM3(which disrupts the structure so that) atoms/layers do not/harder to slide over each other(making it stronger)OWTTE | all marks can be awarded from labelled diagramsALLOWcations/ions/particles in place of atoms throughoutREJECTmention of molecules once only | 3\n |  |  | Total9", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "carbon", "ALLOW soot\nALLOW copper(II) oxide/copper oxide/CuO\nREJECT copper(I) oxide", "1"], ["(b)", "M1(amount of ethanol)=0.92÷46OR0.02(0)(mol)\nM2(-)18.2÷0.02(0)=(-)910(kJ/mol)", "ALLOW alternative methods", "2"], ["(c)", "Any 2 from\nM1heat(energy)/thermal energy was lost(to the surroundings/apparatus)\nM2incomplete combustion(of ethanol)\nM3the ethanol was impure/ethanol evaporates", "", "2"], ["(d)(i)", "M1∑bonds broken=4xC-H+2x498\nM2∑bonds formed=2x805+4x463OR3462\nM34xC-H+996-3462=-890\nM4C-H=1576÷4=394(kJ/mol)", "correct answer with or without working scores4\nALLOW2x498OR996seen\nALLOWecf throughout\n839 without working scores3\n616.5/617 without working scores3", "4"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | carbon | ALLOW soot\nALLOW copper(II) oxide/copper oxide/CuO\nREJECT copper(I) oxide | 1\n(b) | M1(amount of ethanol)=0.92÷46OR0.02(0)(mol)\nM2(-)18.2÷0.02(0)=(-)910(kJ/mol) | ALLOW alternative methods | 2\n(c) | Any 2 from\nM1heat(energy)/thermal energy was lost(to the surroundings/apparatus)\nM2incomplete combustion(of ethanol)\nM3the ethanol was impure/ethanol evaporates |  | 2\n(d)(i) | M1∑bonds broken=4xC-H+2x498\nM2∑bonds formed=2x805+4x463OR3462\nM34xC-H+996-3462=-890\nM4C-H=1576÷4=394(kJ/mol) | correct answer with or without working scores4\nALLOW2x498OR996seen\nALLOWecf throughout\n839 without working scores3\n616.5/617 without working scores3 | 4", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "Energy\nCH4+2O2\nΔH\nCO2+2H2O\nM1 horizontal line to show products in correct position and correctly labelled\nM2 vertical line in correct position and labelled ΔH/−890(kJ/mol)", "ACCEPT double headed arrow or arrow pointing from reactants level to products level\nREJECT arrow pointing from products level to reactants level\nIGNORE any attempts at including activation energy\nIf endothermic reaction shown M2 can be awarded for correct arrow/line labelled ΔH/+890(kJ/mol)", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total 11"]], "text": "(ii) | Energy\nCH4+2O2\nΔH\nCO2+2H2O\nM1 horizontal line to show products in correct position and correctly labelled\nM2 vertical line in correct position and labelled ΔH/−890(kJ/mol) | ACCEPT double headed arrow or arrow pointing from reactants level to products level\nREJECT arrow pointing from products level to reactants level\nIGNORE any attempts at including activation energy\nIf endothermic reaction shown M2 can be awarded for correct arrow/line labelled ΔH/+890(kJ/mol) | 2\n |  |  | Total 11", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000007"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021", "e000022"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "5ff5aef7-21db-5ed9-bfc3-c48add89d7db", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:02:35.031130864Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 88, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Question Paper Log Number P70947A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_2C_2206_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:02:54.165494+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('54473ad9-ddaf-4dc5-81f5-2752f14bca08', '35fdc8b0-ffff-5f0d-a81b-100139963e77', '1.0', 1, 'QUESTION_PAPER', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2022junr/QP.md', 'QP.md', 'text/markdown', '828b1bd177edbd473470f4e0f6a4c9a4ba7248a4ab9c12a625081d1e2a0d0eba', 'SHA-256', 1, 149, 143, 9, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 13:03:16.895878+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2022junr/QP.md", "checksum": "828b1bd177edbd473470f4e0f6a4c9a4ba7248a4ab9c12a625081d1e2a0d0eba", "fileName": "QP.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information"], ["Candidate surname", "Other names"], ["Centre Number", "Candidate Number"], ["Pearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)"], ["Time", "1 hour 15 minutes", "Paper reference 4CH1/2CR"], ["Chemistry\nUNIT: 4CH1\nPAPER: 2CR"], ["You must have:\nCalculator, ruler"], ["Total Marks"]], "text": "Please check the examination details below before entering your candidate information\nCandidate surname | Other names\nCentre Number | Candidate Number\nPearson Edexcel International GCSE (9-1)\nTime | 1 hour 15 minutes | Paper reference 4CH1/2CR\nChemistry\nUNIT: 4CH1\nPAPER: 2CR\nYou must have:\nCalculator, ruler\nTotal Marks", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 1, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7Li lithium3", "9Be beryllium4", "Key", "4He helium2"], ["23Na sodium11", "24Mg magnesium12", "relative atomic mass atomic symbol atomic (proton) number", "20Ne neon10"], ["39K potassium19", "40Ca calcium20", "45Sc scandium21", "48Ti titanium22", "51V vanadium23", "52Cr chromium24", "55Mn manganese25", "56Fe iron26", "59Co cobalt27", "59Ni nickel28