ct heating with Bunsen burner\nM5 DEP on crystals having been formed\nNo M5 if crystals are washed after drying", "Total 12"]], "text": "(d) | A description that refers to four of the following |  | 4\n | M1 heat the solution | ALLOW boil\nMax 1 mark if solution evaporated to dryness | \n | M2 to evaporate some of the water/ to form a saturated solution/ to crystallisation point | If solution left to partially evaporate without heating only M4 and M5 can be awarded | \n | M3 leave the solution to cool / leave the solution for (more) crystals to form | leave solution to cool and (then) filter off crystals scores M3 and M4 | \n | M4 filter off the crystals | ALLOW decant off solution\nIGNORE references to washing | \n | M5 suitable method of drying the crystals | e.g. dry between filter papers/dry in a warm oven/ leave to dry\nREJECT hot oven or direct heating with Bunsen burner\nM5 DEP on crystals having been formed\nNo M5 if crystals are washed after drying | Total 12", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7", "(a)(i)", "reversible (reaction)/reaction that goes both ways OWTTE", "IGNORE references to equilibrium", "1"], ["(ii)", "increases the rate of reaction/speeds up the reaction", "REJECT to increase yield\nALLOW to reach equilibrium faster\nIGNORE provides an alternative pathway with lower activation energy", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "(ii)", "M1 yield decreases", "IGNORE references to rate and Le Chatelier throughout", "2"], ["M2 (forward) reaction is exothermic/backward reaction is endothermic", "ACCEPT (when temperature increased equilibrium shifts in) endothermic direction which is (from right) to left", ""], ["M1 yield increases", "M2 DEP M1 correct or missing", "2"], ["(ii)", "M2 there are fewer moles (of gas) on the right-hand side/product side / there are more moles (of gas) on the left-hand side/there are 4 moles of reactants and 2 moles of product/ OWTTE", "ALLOW molecules for moles\nM2 DEP M1 correct or missing", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7 | (a)(i) | reversible (reaction)/reaction that goes both ways OWTTE | IGNORE references to equilibrium | 1\n(ii) | increases the rate of reaction/speeds up the reaction | REJECT to increase yield\nALLOW to reach equilibrium faster\nIGNORE provides an alternative pathway with lower activation energy | 1\n(b)(i) | (ii) | M1 yield decreases | IGNORE references to rate and Le Chatelier throughout | 2\nM2 (forward) reaction is exothermic/backward reaction is endothermic | ACCEPT (when temperature increased equilibrium shifts in) endothermic direction which is (from right) to left | \nM1 yield increases | M2 DEP M1 correct or missing | 2\n(ii) | M2 there are fewer moles (of gas) on the right-hand side/product side / there are more moles (of gas) on the left-hand side/there are 4 moles of reactants and 2 moles of product/ OWTTE | ALLOW molecules for moles\nM2 DEP M1 correct or missing | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "", "", ""], ["7(c)", "Energy N2+3H2ΔH2NH3", "IGNORE any horizontal axis/labelsIGNORE any attempts at including activation energy", "3"], ["", "M1 horizontal line labelled with N2+3H2", "ALLOW nitrogen and hydrogen", ""], ["", "M2 horizontal line showing 2NH3in correct position", "ALLOW ammoniaIf not balanced or words reactants and products on horizontal lines in correct position scores1 out of2", ""], ["", "M3 vertical line in correct position and labelled ΔH/-92(kJ/mol)", "ACCEPT double headed arrow or arrow pointing from reactants level to products levelREJECT arrow pointing from products level to reactants levelIf endothermic reaction can scoreM1 and M3", ""]], "text": " |  |  | \n7(c) | Energy N2+3H2ΔH2NH3 | IGNORE any horizontal axis/labelsIGNORE any attempts at including activation energy | 3\n | M1 horizontal line labelled with N2+3H2 | ALLOW nitrogen and hydrogen | \n | M2 horizontal line showing 2NH3in correct position | ALLOW ammoniaIf not balanced or words reactants and products on horizontal lines in correct position scores1 out of2 | \n | M3 vertical line in correct position and labelled ΔH/-92(kJ/mol) | ACCEPT double headed arrow or arrow pointing from reactants level to products levelREJECT arrow pointing from products level to reactants levelIf endothermic reaction can scoreM1 and M3 | ", "row_count": 5, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["7(d)(i)", "M1amount of nitrogen=(48÷24=)2(mol)\nM2amount of hydrogen=(120÷24=)5(mol)\nM32.5mol of hydrogen to1mol of nitrogen(which is less than3so nitrogen is in excess)OR2mol of nitrogen needs6mol of hydrogen(so not enough hydrogen to react with the nitrogen)", "ACCEPT alternative methods\ncorrect answer without working scores3\nALLOW ECF from(i)\nALLOW3.3\nuse of3.3gives79.2\nuse of79.2gives15.84\nALLOW ECF fromM2\nACCEPT120dm3of hydrogen gives2x120÷3OR80(dm3of ammonia)forM1andM2\nALLOWmax2for use of48dm3of nitrogen giving96dm3of ammonia and final answer of19.2(dm3)", "3"], ["(ii)", "M15mol of hydrogen gives3.33mol of ammonia\nM2volume of ammonia(if100%conversion)=3.33x24OR80(dm3)\nM3(volume of ammoniaif20%conversion)=\\frac{(20\\times80)}{100}=16.0(dm3)", "", "3"], ["", "", "", "Total15"]], "text": "7(d)(i) | M1amount of nitrogen=(48÷24=)2(mol)\nM2amount of hydrogen=(120÷24=)5(mol)\nM32.5mol of hydrogen to1mol of nitrogen(which is less than3so nitrogen is in excess)OR2mol of nitrogen needs6mol of hydrogen(so not enough hydrogen to react with the nitrogen) | ACCEPT alternative methods\ncorrect answer without working scores3\nALLOW ECF from(i)\nALLOW3.3\nuse of3.3gives79.2\nuse of79.2gives15.84\nALLOW ECF fromM2\nACCEPT120dm3of hydrogen gives2x120÷3OR80(dm3of ammonia)forM1andM2\nALLOWmax2for use of48dm3of nitrogen giving96dm3of ammonia and final answer of19.2(dm3) | 3\n(ii) | M15mol of hydrogen gives3.33mol of ammonia\nM2volume of ammonia(if100%conversion)=3.33x24OR80(dm3)\nM3(volume of ammoniaif20%conversion)=\\frac{(20\\times80)}{100}=16.0(dm3) |  | 3\n |  |  | Total15", "row_count": 3, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000007"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021", "e000022"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "dd78b694-8b04-536f-ab00-c2ad60c723dc", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:03:16.957447658Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 87, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2CR", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Question Paper Log Number XXXXX*", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_2CR_2206_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2022", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:03:37.778399+00');
