: [], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "BLANK PAGE", "sectionId": "s010", "elementIds": [], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [{"text": "\\mathrm {P b} \\left(\\mathrm {N O} _ {3}\\right) _ {2} (\\mathrm {a q}) + \\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \\mathrm {S O} _ {4} (\\mathrm {a q}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {P b S O} _ {4} (\\mathrm {s}) + 2 \\mathrm {N a N O} _ {3} (\\mathrm {a q})", "latex": "\\mathrm {P b} \\left(\\mathrm {N O} _ {3}\\right) _ {2} (\\mathrm {a q}) + \\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \\mathrm {S O} _ {4} (\\mathrm {a q}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {P b S O} _ {4} (\\mathrm {s}) + 2 \\mathrm {N a N O} _ {3} (\\mathrm {a q})", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000066", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 66, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "3 \\mathrm {N} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightarrow 4 \\mathrm {N H} _ {3} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {N} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g})", "latex": "3 \\mathrm {N} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightarrow 4 \\mathrm {N H} _ {3} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {N} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g})", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000130", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 130, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "3 \\mathrm {N} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightarrow 4 \\mathrm {N H} _ {3} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {N} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g})", "latex": "3 \\mathrm {N} _ {2} \\mathrm {H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightarrow 4 \\mathrm {N H} _ {3} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {N} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g})", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000141", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 141, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "50d1855f-e792-59ea-a218-7ec5a12be849", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:03:17.585170689Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 185, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "Instructions", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Use black ink or ball-point pen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "If pencil is used for diagrams/sketches/graphs it must be dark (HB or B).", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Fill in the boxes at the top of this page with your name, centre number and candidate number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer all questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer the questions in the spaces provided", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "there may be more space than you need.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Show all the steps in any calculations and state the units.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Information", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The total mark for this paper is 70.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The marks for each question are shown in brackets", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "use this as a guide as to how much time to spend on each question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Advice", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Read each question carefully before you start to answer it.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Write your answers neatly and in good English.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Try to answer every question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Check your answers if you have time at the end.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Turn over", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ ^{*} $ The lanthanoids (atomic numbers 58-71) and the actinoids (atomic numbers 90-103) have been omitted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The relative atomic masses of copper and chlorine have not been rounded to the nearest whole number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Answer ALL questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Some questions must be answered with a cross in a box. If you change your mind about an answer, put a line through the box and then mark your new answer with a cross.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "1 (a) The diagram shows the electronic configuration of an atom of an element.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Complete the table by giving the missing information.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(3)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The table gives information about four different species, W, X, Y and Z.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give the mass number of W.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give a reason why X has a 3+ charge.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Explain why Y and Z are isotopes of the same element.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 1 = 7 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "2 The table shows properties of four substances, A, B, C and D.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Use information from the table to identify these substances.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Which substance could be a metal?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Which substance could be diamond?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Which substance is a gas at 600 $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}? $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000049", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 49, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000050", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 50, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000051", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 51, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000052", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 52, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) One of the substances in the table is a compound with the formula $ \\mathrm{C_{10}H_{16}N_{2}O_{3}S} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000053", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 53, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give the number of different elements in $ C_{1 0} H_{1 6} N_{2} O_{3} S $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000054", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 54, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Determine the number of atoms in a molecule of $ C_{1 0} H_{1 6} N_{2} O_{3} S $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000055", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 55, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2 = 5 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000056", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 56, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000057", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 57, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "3 This question is about soluble salts and insoluble salts.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000058", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 58, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Which pair of solutions produces an insoluble salt when mixed?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000059", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 59, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A sodium sulfate and potassium nitrate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000060", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 60, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B potassium carbonate and calcium nitrate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000061", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 61, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C sodium chloride and ammonium nitrate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000062", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 62, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D sodium hydroxide and potassium sulfate", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000063", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 63, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) When solutions of lead nitrate and sodium sulfate are mixed, one product is solid lead sulfate.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000064", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 64, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000065", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 65, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Describe how a pure, dry sample of solid lead sulfate can be obtained from the mixture.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000067", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 67, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The table gives the solubility of a salt in water at six different temperatures.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000068", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 68, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Plot the points on the grid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000070", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 70, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Draw a curve of best fit.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000071", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 71, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) A saturated solution of the salt in 100g of water is cooled from $ 9 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ to $ 3 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ Use your graph to determine the mass of salt that will crystallise. Show your working on the graph.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000073", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 73, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "4 Fractional distillation is used to separate crude oil into fractions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000074", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 74, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The diagram shows a fractionating column and the fractions obtained from crude oil.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000075", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 75, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) (i) Describe how crude oil is separated into fractions in the fractionating column.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000077", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 77, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give a use for kerosene and a use for bitumen. kerosene", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000078", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 78, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "bitumen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000079", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 79, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Some fractions obtained from crude oil are cracked to form alkenes.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000080", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 80, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Describe what is meant by cracking.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000081", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 81, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Ethene is obtained by cracking.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000082", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 82, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the displayed formula of ethene.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000083", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 83, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain why ethene is described as an unsaturated hydrocarbon.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000085", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 85, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Describe a test to show that ethene is unsaturated.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000086", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 86, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 4 = 13 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000087", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 87, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000088", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 88, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "5 This question is about metals.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000089", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 89, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Explain why metals are malleable.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000090", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 90, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Sodium metal is extracted by the electrolysis of molten sodium chloride.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000091", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 91, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Sodium metal forms at the negative electrode and chlorine gas forms at the positive electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000092", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 92, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The diagram represents this electrolysis.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000093", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 93, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Explain why molten sodium chloride conducts electricity.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000095", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 95, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Explain how sodium metal forms at the negative electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000096", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 96, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Write an ionic half-equation for the formation of chlorine gas at the positive electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000097", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 97, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) Give a reason why sodium metal does not form in the electrolysis of an aqueous solution of sodium chloride.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000098", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 98, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Copper can be produced by reacting an oxide of copper with methane.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000099", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 99, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The diagram shows the apparatus used.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000100", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 100, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The oxide of copper is heated until the reaction is complete.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000102", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 102, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table shows the results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000103", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 103, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Use the results to show that this oxide has the empirical formula CuO [for Cu, $ A_{\\mathrm{r}}=6 3. 5 $ for O, $ A_{\\mathrm{r}}=1 6 $]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000105", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 105, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(3)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000106", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 106, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000108", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 108, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "6 When ethanoic acid reacts with ethanol in the presence of concentrated sulfuric acid, one of the products is ester A.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000109", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 109, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000110", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 110, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) (i) Draw a circle around the functional group in ethanoic acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000112", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 112, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Give the displayed formula of ester A.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000113", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 113, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Name ester A.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000114", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 114, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The reaction mixture is kept in a sealed container until dynamic equilibrium is reached.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000115", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 115, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "State what is meant by the term dynamic equilibrium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000116", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 116, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) During the reaction, the number of moles of ethanoic acid in the reaction mixture decreases, but the number of moles of concentrated sulfuric acid does not change.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000117", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 117, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give a reason why the number of moles of concentrated sulfuric acid does not change.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000118", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 118, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) A student does a titration to find the accurate volume of sodium hydroxide solution needed for complete neutralisation.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000119", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 119, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The student starts by using a pipette to transfer $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of the reaction mixture to a conical flask.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000120", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 120, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Describe how the student should complete the titration.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000121", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 121, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6 = 13 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000122", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 122, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000123", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 123, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "7 This question is about hydrazine, $ \\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{4} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000124", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 124, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) This is the displayed formula for a molecule of hydrazine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000125", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 125, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Complete the dot-and-cross diagram for hydrazine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000127", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 127, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) This is the equation for the decomposition of hydrazine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000129", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 129, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation can be shown using displayed formulae.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000131", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 131, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The table gives the relevant bond energies.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000133", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 133, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Use the data in the table to calculate the total energy needed to break all the bonds in the reactants.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000135", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 135, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Use the data in the table to calculate the total energy released when all the bonds in the products are made.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000136", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 136, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Calculate the enthalpy change, $ \\Delta H $ , in kJ/mol, for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000137", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 137, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) Explain, in terms of bonds broken and bonds made, why this reaction is exothermic.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000138", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 138, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) A sample of hydrazine is completely decomposed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000139", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 139, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for the decomposition of hydrazine.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000140", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 140, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The products of the decomposition are bubbled through $ 1 1 0 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000142", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 142, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The ammonia completely dissolves in the water, but nitrogen is insoluble in water.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000143", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 143, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The nitrogen has a volume of $ 1 5 7 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ at room temperature and pressure (rtp).", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000144", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 144, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the concentration, in mol/dm $ ^{3} $ , of the ammonia solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000145", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 145, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give your answer to 3 significant figures.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000146", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 146, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "[for a gas at rtp,molar volume = 24000 $ cm^{3} $]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000147", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 147, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7 = 13 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000148", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 148, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "TOTAL FOR PAPER = 70 MARKS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000149", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 149, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000150", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 150, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000151", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 151, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:03:38.078761+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('deab1aa5-b45a-4bf6-8cb3-3423c4cb5fe0', '36681d06-86ad-5e7d-9d9d-43c97e6d34e9', '1.0', 1, 'MARK_SCHEME', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2023jan/MS.md', 'MS.md', 'text/markdown', '2f480d71ce7d62d19789db0ab6a08fe3c7cadf0fc71584729f99b1fb6749bc77', 'SHA-256', 1, 31, 31, 11, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 13:03:17.639192+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2023jan/MS.md", "checksum": "2f480d71ce7d62d19789db0ab6a08fe3c7cadf0fc71584729f99b1fb6749bc77", "fileName": "MS.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["1", "(a)", "name of the part of this atom labelled A nucleus\nnumber of the group that contains this element2\nnumber of the period that contains this element3", "", "3"], ["", "(b)(i)", "4", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "(species X has) three more protons than electrons/three fewer electrons than protons", "ALLOW (the atom which formed species X has) lost three electrons\nIGNORE refs to Group 3", "1"], ["(iii)", "M1 same number of protons/both have 17 protons\nM2 different number of neutrons/one has two neutrons more/one has 18 neutrons and the other has 20 neutrons", "IGNORE all refs to electrons\nALLOW “same atomic number,different mass number” for(1)mark", "2"], ["Total for question=7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n1 | (a) | name of the part of this atom labelled A nucleus\nnumber of the group that contains this element2\nnumber of the period that contains this element3 |  | 3\n | (b)(i) | 4 |  | 1\n(ii) | (species X has) three more protons than electrons/three fewer electrons than protons | ALLOW (the atom which formed species X has) lost three electrons\nIGNORE refs to Group 3 | 1\n(iii) | M1 same number of protons/both have 17 protons\nM2 different number of neutrons/one has two neutrons more/one has 18 neutrons and the other has 20 neutrons | IGNORE all refs to electrons\nALLOW “same atomic number,different mass number” for(1)mark | 2\nTotal for question=7", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["2", "(a)(i)", "B", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "A, C and D are not the correct answers as metals conduct electricity when solid", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "A is not the correct answer because diamond will not conduct electricity when moltenB is not the correct answer because diamond will not conduct electricity when solid or moltenC is not the correct answer because diamond has a much higher melting and boiling point", "", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "A is not the correct answer as A is a solid at 600℃B is not the correct answer as B is a liquid at 600℃D is not the correct answer as D is a solid at 600℃", "", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "(ii)", "5/five", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "32/thirty two", "", "1"], ["Total for question=5"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n2 | (a)(i) | B |  | 1\n(ii) | A, C and D are not the correct answers as metals conduct electricity when solid |  | 1\n(iii) | A is not the correct answer because diamond will not conduct electricity when moltenB is not the correct answer because diamond will not conduct electricity when solid or moltenC is not the correct answer because diamond has a much higher melting and boiling point |  | 1\n(b)(i) | A is not the correct answer as A is a solid at 600℃B is not the correct answer as B is a liquid at 600℃D is not the correct answer as D is a solid at 600℃ |  | 1\n(b)(i) | (ii) | 5/five |  | 1\n(ii) | 32/thirty two |  | 1\nTotal for question=5", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(a)", "B\nA is not correct because mixing sodium sulfate and potassium nitrate does not produce an insoluble salt.\nC is not correct because mixing sodium chloride and ammonium nitrate does not produce an insoluble salt.\nD is not correct because mixing sodium hydroxide and potassium sulfate does not produce an insoluble salt.", "", "1"], ["(b)", "M1 filter (the solid lead sulfate)\nM2 wash / rinse (with deionised / distilled water)\nM3 leave (in a warm place) to dry", "If the method starts with crystallisation then, max (2)\nALLOW leave on a windowsill / dry using filter paper / dry in a (warm / drying) oven\nIf the reaction mixture is just heated to dryness, score M3 only", "3"], ["(c)(i)", "6 points plotted ± half a square", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "smooth curve of best fit through, or within a square, of all points", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "M1 working shown on graph\nM2 solubility at 90℃-solubility at 30℃", "ALLOW any evidence of temperatures marked on graph eg dots / lines\nExpected answer of 74-82 scores 2 provided some working is shown on graph\nIf no working shown, score M2 only\nMark ECF on (ii), even if a straight line is drawn", "2"], ["Total for question = 8"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(a) | B\nA is not correct because mixing sodium sulfate and potassium nitrate does not produce an insoluble salt.\nC is not correct because mixing sodium chloride and ammonium nitrate does not produce an insoluble salt.\nD is not correct because mixing sodium hydroxide and potassium sulfate does not produce an insoluble salt. |  | 1\n(b) | M1 filter (the solid lead sulfate)\nM2 wash / rinse (with deionised / distilled water)\nM3 leave (in a warm place) to dry | If the method starts with crystallisation then, max (2)\nALLOW leave on a windowsill / dry using filter paper / dry in a (warm / drying) oven\nIf the reaction mixture is just heated to dryness, score M3 only | 3\n(c)(i) | 6 points plotted ± half a square |  | 1\n(ii) | smooth curve of best fit through, or within a square, of all points |  | 1\n(iii) | M1 working shown on graph\nM2 solubility at 90℃-solubility at 30℃ | ALLOW any evidence of temperatures marked on graph eg dots / lines\nExpected answer of 74-82 scores 2 provided some working is shown on graph\nIf no working shown, score M2 only\nMark ECF on (ii), even if a straight line is drawn | 2\nTotal for question = 8", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)(i)", "M1 crude oil is heated/vapourised", "ALLOW boiled\nREJECT burned", "4"], ["M2 vapours/gases/compounds/hydrocarbons rise up the column", "", ""], ["M3 the column is hotter at the bottom than the top", "ALLOW temperature gradient of the column\nALLOW different temperatures at each level\nALLOW fractions with lowest boiling point rise to the top\nIGNORE refs to gradient in density of molecules", ""], ["M4 vapours/compounds/hydrocarbons condense at their boiling point", "ALLOW vapours/compounds/hydrocarbons/condense at different heights\nALLOW the vapours/compounds/hydrocarbons/fractions have different boiling points\nIGNORE melting point", ""], ["kerosene=aeroplane fuel/fuel for heating", "ALLOW fuel for lamps/fuel for cooking", "2"], ["bitumen=road tar/tarmac/(waterproofing) roofs", "ALLOW road surfacing/road making", ""], ["(b)(i)", "M1 breaking down long-chain hydrocarbons/long-chain molecules/long-chain alkanes", "REJECT polymers\nIGNORE refs to separation", "2"], ["M2 to form shorter chains(of alkanes/alkenes/hydrocarbons)", "ALLOW to break(C-C) bonds", ""], ["M1(ethene is unsaturated because it has a) double(C=C) bond", "", "3"], ["M2(ethene is a hydrocarbon as it contains) hydrogen and carbon(atoms)\nM3 only", "REJECT carbon and hydrogen molecules\nM3 dep on mention of carbon and hydrogen in M2", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a)(i) | M1 crude oil is heated/vapourised | ALLOW boiled\nREJECT burned | 4\nM2 vapours/gases/compounds/hydrocarbons rise up the column |  | \nM3 the column is hotter at the bottom than the top | ALLOW temperature gradient of the column\nALLOW different temperatures at each level\nALLOW fractions with lowest boiling point rise to the top\nIGNORE refs to gradient in density of molecules | \nM4 vapours/compounds/hydrocarbons condense at their boiling point | ALLOW vapours/compounds/hydrocarbons/condense at different heights\nALLOW the vapours/compounds/hydrocarbons/fractions have different boiling points\nIGNORE melting point | \nkerosene=aeroplane fuel/fuel for heating | ALLOW fuel for lamps/fuel for cooking | 2\nbitumen=road tar/tarmac/(waterproofing) roofs | ALLOW road surfacing/road making | \n(b)(i) | M1 breaking down long-chain hydrocarbons/long-chain molecules/long-chain alkanes | REJECT polymers\nIGNORE refs to separation | 2\nM2 to form shorter chains(of alkanes/alkenes/hydrocarbons) | ALLOW to break(C-C) bonds | \nM1(ethene is unsaturated because it has a) double(C=C) bond |  | 3\nM2(ethene is a hydrocarbon as it contains) hydrogen and carbon(atoms)\nM3 only | REJECT carbon and hydrogen molecules\nM3 dep on mention of carbon and hydrogen in M2 | ", "row_count": 11, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(iii)", "M1 add bromine water", "ALLOW bromine solution\nNOT just‘bromine’", "2"], ["M2 which decolourises/turns colourless", "M2 dep on mention of bromine in M1\nIGNORE starting colour of bromine\nIGNORE clear\nNOT just‘changes colour’"], ["", "If reaction takes place in presence of uv, then score M1 only"], ["Total for question=13"]], "text": "(iii) | M1 add bromine water | ALLOW bromine solution\nNOT just‘bromine’ | 2\nM2 which decolourises/turns colourless | M2 dep on mention of bromine in M1\nIGNORE starting colour of bromine\nIGNORE clear\nNOT just‘changes colour’\n | If reaction takes place in presence of uv, then score M1 only\nTotal for question=13", "row_count": 4, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)", "M1 layers/rows of atoms/(positive) ionsM2 can slide over one another", "REJECT moleculesIGNORE refs to electrons", "2"], ["(b)(i)", "M1 ionsM2 can move", "REJECT electronsM2 dep on ions in M1", "2"], ["(ii)", "M1 positive sodium ions/cations/Na+ (ions) are attracted(to the negative electrode)M2 where they gain electrons OR where they are reduced", "ALLOW moveREJECT atoms/metalALLOW balanced ionic equation(Na++e\\rightarrow Na)", "2"], ["(iii)", "2Cl-→Cl2+2e-", "ALLOW2Cl--2e-→Cl2", "1"], ["(iv)", "sodium is more reactive(than hydrogen)/higher in the reactivity series(than hydrogen)", "ALLOW(in aqueous solution) hydrogen ions are discharged/hydrogen is produced", "1"], ["(c)", "M1 mass of copper=3.81g and mass of oxygen=0.96gM2 moles of copper=0.06 and moles of oxygen=0.06M3 ratio=1:1", "M2 allow ECF from M1but only ifArfor copper and oxygen are usedM3 dep on M1 and M2but must be1:1 ratioIFAris divided by mass,then M1 only scores", "3"], ["Total for question=11"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a) | M1 layers/rows of atoms/(positive) ionsM2 can slide over one another | REJECT moleculesIGNORE refs to electrons | 2\n(b)(i) | M1 ionsM2 can move | REJECT electronsM2 dep on ions in M1 | 2\n(ii) | M1 positive sodium ions/cations/Na+ (ions) are attracted(to the negative electrode)M2 where they gain electrons OR where they are reduced | ALLOW moveREJECT atoms/metalALLOW balanced ionic equation(Na++e\\rightarrow Na) | 2\n(iii) | 2Cl-→Cl2+2e- | ALLOW2Cl--2e-→Cl2 | 1\n(iv) | sodium is more reactive(than hydrogen)/higher in the reactivity series(than hydrogen) | ALLOW(in aqueous solution) hydrogen ions are discharged/hydrogen is produced | 1\n(c) | M1 mass of copper=3.81g and mass of oxygen=0.96gM2 moles of copper=0.06 and moles of oxygen=0.06M3 ratio=1:1 | M2 allow ECF from M1but only ifArfor copper and oxygen are usedM3 dep on M1 and M2but must be1:1 ratioIFAris divided by mass,then M1 only scores | 3\nTotal for question=11", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)(i)(ii)(iii)", "M1 ester linkage(COO)correctly displayed", "REJECTmore than one molecule or group circled", "1"], ["M2 rest of the molecule correct", "M2 dep on M1", "2"], ["ethyl ethanoate", "", "1"], ["(b)", "M1 the forwards and the reverse reactions occur at the same rate", "", "2"], ["M2 the concentrations of reactants and products remain constant", "REJECT concentrations of reactants and products are the same ALLOW amounts", ""], ["(c)(i)(ii)", "(concentrated)sulfuric acid/it is a catalyst", "", "1"], ["Any 6 of the following:", "", "6"], ["M1 rinse the burette with sodium hydroxide", "", ""], ["M2 fill the burette with sodium hydroxide", "", ""], ["M3 make sure that the jet/space between tap and tip contains liquid", "ALLOW no bubbles in the burette", ""], ["M4 add(a few drops) of indicator(to the conical flask)", "ALLOW any named indicator except universal indicator", ""], ["M5 add(sodium hydroxide)from the burette until the indicator changes colour(permanently)", "ACCEPTany stated colour change", ""], ["M6 swirl the conical flask", "ACCEPT shake", ""], ["M7 add(sodium hydroxide)dropwise close to the endpoint", "", ""], ["M8 record initial and final volume on burette", "ALLOW record volume of solution added", ""], ["M9 repeat until concordant results", "ALLOW repeat until two results are $\\pm$0.2cm3", ""], ["Total for question=13"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a)(i)(ii)(iii) | M1 ester linkage(COO)correctly displayed | REJECTmore than one molecule or group circled | 1\nM2 rest of the molecule correct | M2 dep on M1 | 2\nethyl ethanoate |  | 1\n(b) | M1 the forwards and the reverse reactions occur at the same rate |  | 2\nM2 the concentrations of reactants and products remain constant | REJECT concentrations of reactants and products are the same ALLOW amounts | \n(c)(i)(ii) | (concentrated)sulfuric acid/it is a catalyst |  | 1\nAny 6 of the following: |  | 6\nM1 rinse the burette with sodium hydroxide |  | \nM2 fill the burette with sodium hydroxide |  | \nM3 make sure that the jet/space between tap and tip contains liquid | ALLOW no bubbles in the burette | \nM4 add(a few drops) of indicator(to the conical flask) | ALLOW any named indicator except universal indicator | \nM5 add(sodium hydroxide)from the burette until the indicator changes colour(permanently) | ACCEPTany stated colour change | \nM6 swirl the conical flask | ACCEPT shake | \nM7 add(sodium hydroxide)dropwise close to the endpoint |  | \nM8 record initial and final volume on burette | ALLOW record volume of solution added | \nM9 repeat until concordant results | ALLOW repeat until two results are $\\pm$0.2cm3 | \nTotal for question=13", "row_count": 18, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "M1 two electrons between nitrogen and each of the four hydrogen atoms", "ALLOW any symbols used for electrons", "2"], ["M2 two electrons between the two nitrogen atoms, and a non-bonding pair on each nitrogen", "ALLOW each non-bonding pair shown as two separate electrons", ""], ["(b)(i)", "M1(3×158)+(12×391)", "", "2"], ["M25166kJ", "5166kJ without working scores2IGNORE sign of final answer", ""], ["M1(12×391)+945", "", "2"], ["M25637kJ", "5637kJ without working scores2IGNORE sign of final answer", ""], ["(iii)", "-471(kJ/mol)", "ECF onb(i)&b(ii)If final answer is+ve do not penalise lack of sign", "1"], ["(iv)", "An explanation that links together the following two points:M1 bond breaking requires energy/is endothermic,bond formation releases energy/is exothermicM2 more energy released than taken in/making bonds involves more energy than breaking bonds", "“bonds” only needs mentioning once“more energy is given out when bonds are made than is taken in when bonds are broken” scores(2)", "2"], ["(c)", "M1amount of nitrogen gas=1570÷24000OR0.06542(mol)", "", "4"], ["M2amount of ammonia=0.0654×4OR0.2617(mol)", "ALLOWM1×4", ""], ["M3 concentration of ammonia=0.2617÷1100x1000=0.237878...", "ALLOWM3÷1.1", ""], ["M40.238(mol/dm3)*", "Must be 3 sig figs to scoreM4answer of0.238(mol/dm3) scores4marks with or without working", ""], ["Total for question=13"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | M1 two electrons between nitrogen and each of the four hydrogen atoms | ALLOW any symbols used for electrons | 2\nM2 two electrons between the two nitrogen atoms, and a non-bonding pair on each nitrogen | ALLOW each non-bonding pair shown as two separate electrons | \n(b)(i) | M1(3×158)+(12×391) |  | 2\nM25166kJ | 5166kJ without working scores2IGNORE sign of final answer | \nM1(12×391)+945 |  | 2\nM25637kJ | 5637kJ without working scores2IGNORE sign of final answer | \n(iii) | -471(kJ/mol) | ECF onb(i)&b(ii)If final answer is+ve do not penalise lack of sign | 1\n(iv) | An explanation that links together the following two points:M1 bond breaking requires energy/is endothermic,bond formation releases energy/is exothermicM2 more energy released than taken in/making bonds involves more energy than breaking bonds | “bonds” only needs mentioning once“more energy is given out when bonds are made than is taken in when bonds are broken” scores(2) | 2\n(c) | M1amount of nitrogen gas=1570÷24000OR0.06542(mol) |  | 4\nM2amount of ammonia=0.0654×4OR0.2617(mol) | ALLOWM1×4 | \nM3 concentration of ammonia=0.2617÷1100x1000=0.237878... | ALLOWM3÷1.1 | \nM40.238(mol/dm3)* | Must be 3 sig figs to scoreM4answer of0.238(mol/dm3) scores4marks with or without working | \nTotal for question=13", "row_count": 14, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021", "e000030"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "36681d06-86ad-5e7d-9d9d-43c97e6d34e9", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:03:17.639191830Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 61, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "January 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Question Paper Log Number P71894A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_2C_MS_2301", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Total for question = 13", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:03:38.097773+00');
