rm {a q}) + \\mathrm {O H} ^ {-} (\\mathrm {a q}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {I})", "latex": "\\mathrm {H} ^ {+} (\\mathrm {a q}) + \\mathrm {O H} ^ {-} (\\mathrm {a q}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {I})", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000102", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 102, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\begin{array}{l} \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {H} + \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {H} \\rightarrow \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {H} + \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {H} \\\\ \\mathrm {H} \\\\ \\end{array}", "latex": "\\begin{array}{l} \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {H} + \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {H} \\rightarrow \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {C} \\mathrm {H} + \\mathrm {H} \\mathrm {O} \\mathrm {H} \\\\ \\mathrm {H} \\\\ \\end{array}", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000117", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 117, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {C H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm {C O} (\\mathrm {g}) + 3 \\mathrm {H} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) \\quad \\Delta H = + 2 0 6 \\mathrm {k J / m o l}", "latex": "\\mathrm {C H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm {C O} (\\mathrm {g}) + 3 \\mathrm {H} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) \\quad \\Delta H = + 2 0 6 \\mathrm {k J / m o l}", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000128", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 128, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"text": "\\mathrm {d m} ^ {3}", "latex": "\\mathrm {d m} ^ {3}", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000139", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "equation", "reading_order": 139, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "d9f7c281-91c5-5cba-b2e3-49460138d3a7", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:03:18.958730027Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 184, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 0, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "heading", "text": "Instructions", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Use black ink or ball-point pen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "If pencil is used for diagrams/sketches/graphs it must be dark (HB or B).", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Fill in the boxes at the top of this page with your name, centre number and candidate number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer all questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Answer the questions in the spaces provided", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "there may be more space than you need.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Show all the steps in any calculations and state the units.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Information", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The total mark for this paper is 70.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The marks for each question are shown in brackets - use this as a guide as to how much time to spend on each question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Advice", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Read each question carefully before you start to answer it.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Write your answers neatly and in good English.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Try to answer every question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Check your answers if you have time at the end.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Turn over", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "The lanthanoids (atomic numbers 58-71) and the actinoids (atomic numbers 90-103) have been omitted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The relative atomic masses of copper and chlorine have not been rounded to the nearest whole number.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Answer ALL questions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Some questions must be answered with a cross in a box. If you change your mind about an answer, put a line through the box and then mark your new answer with a cross.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "1 Use the Periodic Table to help you answer this question.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) (i) Name the element with atomic number 14.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Name the element in Group 2 and Period 3.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Name an element that is a liquid at room temperature.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iv) Give the electronic configuration of an atom of phosphorus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(v) Give the formula of sodium sulfide.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Explain, in terms of electron configuration, why neon is unreactive.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "2 This question is about gases in the atmosphere.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Which of these gases has the lowest percentage by volume in the atmosphere?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A argon", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000032", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 32, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B carbon dioxide", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000033", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 33, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C nitrogen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000034", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 34, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D oxygen", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000035", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 35, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) When copper(II) carbonate is heated, copper(II) oxide and carbon dioxide form.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000036", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 36, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) What is the name of this type of reaction?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000037", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 37, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A addition", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000038", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 38, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B decomposition", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000039", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 39, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "oxidation", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000040", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 40, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D substitution", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000041", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 41, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Which colour change occurs when copper(II) carbonate is heated?", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000042", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 42, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A blue to black", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000043", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 43, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "B blue to orange", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000044", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 44, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "C green to black", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000045", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 45, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "D green to orange", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000046", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 46, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Give the chemical equation for this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000047", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 47, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(1)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000048", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 48, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) A student uses this apparatus to find the percentage of oxygen in a sample of air.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000049", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 49, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The student leaves the apparatus until there is no further change in volume of gas in the syringe.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000051", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 51, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "These are the student''s results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000052", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 52, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the percentage of oxygen in the sample of air.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000054", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 54, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give your answer to two significant figures.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000055", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 55, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Explain why an increasing amount of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere is likely to cause a problem for the environment.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000056", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 56, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 2 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000057", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 57, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000058", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 58, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "3 This question is about alcohols.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000059", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 59, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Ethanol can be manufactured using two different methods.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000060", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 60, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "hydration of ethene", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000061", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 61, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "fermentation of glucose", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000062", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 62, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for hydration.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000063", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 63, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Complete the equation for fermentation.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000065", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 65, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The table gives some information about the two methods.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000067", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 67, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Complete the table by giving the missing information.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000069", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 69, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Explain one advantage and one disadvantage of using fermentation rather than hydration to produce ethanol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000070", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 70, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "You should use information from the table to help your answer.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000071", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 71, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "advantage", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000072", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 72, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "disadvantage", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000073", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 73, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) Explain why fermentation needs to occur in the absence of air.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000074", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 74, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Propanol has this percentage composition by mass.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000075", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 75, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Show by calculation that the empirical formula of propanol is $ \\mathrm{C_{3} H_{8}O}。 $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000077", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 77, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Draw the displayed formula of propanol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000078", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 78, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000079", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 79, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "4 A student does a titration to find the concentration of potassium hydroxide solution. This is the student''s method.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000080", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 80, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of the potassium hydroxide solution to a conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000081", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 81, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add a few drops of methyl orange indicator to the conical flask", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000082", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 82, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "fill a burette with dilute sulfuric acid and record the initial burette reading", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000083", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 83, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "place the conical flask on a white tile", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000084", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 84, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "add the acid from the burette to the mixture in the conical flask, swirling the flask continuously", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000085", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 85, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "when the indicator changes colour at the end point, record the final burette reading", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000086", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 86, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Repeat the titration to obtain concordant results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000087", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 87, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Give the name of the most suitable piece of apparatus to measure out $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of potassium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000088", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 88, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Give the colour of methyl orange in potassium hydroxide solution and in dilute sulfuric acid.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000089", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 89, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "colour in potassium hydroxide solution", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000090", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 90, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "colour in dilute sulfuric acid", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000091", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 91, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) State why the student places the conical flask on a white tile.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000092", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 92, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) State why the student swirls the flask continuously.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000093", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 93, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(e) State what is meant by the term concordant results.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000094", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 94, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(f) The student finds that $ 1 5. 0 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sulfuric acid of concentration $ 0. 1 8 0 \\mathrm{m o l} / \\mathrm{d m}^{3} $ neutralises $ 2 5. 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of potassium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000095", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 95, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000096", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 96, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Calculate the concentration of the potassium hydroxide solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000098", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 98, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(g) This is the ionic equation for the reaction between an acid and an alkali.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000101", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 101, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain why the $ \\mathrm{O H}^{-} $ ion is a proton acceptor in this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000103", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 103, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "5 When copper(II) sulfate solution is electrolysed, copper forms at the negative electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000104", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 104, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "A student uses this apparatus to investigate the electrolysis of copper(II) sulfate solution.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000105", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 105, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) Describe how the student could test a sample of copper(II) sulfate solution to show that it contains copper(II) ions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000107", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 107, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Describe how copper metal forms at the negative electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000108", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 108, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) State the appearance of the copper that forms on the negative electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000109", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 109, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Oxygen forms at the positive electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000110", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 110, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) Give a test for oxygen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000111", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 111, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Complete the half-equation for the formation of oxygen at the positive electrode.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000112", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 112, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) State why the formation of oxygen at the positive electrode is an oxidation reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000113", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 113, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 5 = 10 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000114", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 114, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "6 Ethanoic acid reacts with methanol to form an ester.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000115", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 115, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "The equation shows the displayed formulae for the reactants and products.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000116", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 116, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) (i) Give the name of a suitable catalyst to increase the rate of this reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000118", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 118, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) State how you would know that an ester has formed.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000119", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 119, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(iii) Give the name of this ester.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000120", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 120, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) The table shows the number of bonds in the reactants and the number of bonds in the products.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000121", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 121, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) Explain why the enthalpy change in this reaction is approximately 0 kJ/mol.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000123", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 123, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) State which two bonds need to be broken in the reactants.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000124", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 124, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 6 = 6 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000125", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 125, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "7 Methane reacts with steam to form carbon monoxide and hydrogen.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000126", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 126, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "This is the equation for the reaction.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000127", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 127, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(a) State why carbon monoxide is poisonous to humans.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000129", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 129, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(b) Explain the effect, if any, on the yield of hydrogen at equilibrium when a nickel catalyst is used.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000130", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 130, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(c) The reaction conditions for this reaction are a temperature of $ 7 0 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ and a pressure of 5 atmospheres.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000131", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 131, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(i) The temperature of the reaction mixture is reduced to $ 6 0 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ , but the pressure is kept at 5 atmospheres.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000132", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 132, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain the effect on the yield of hydrogen at equilibrium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000133", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 133, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(ii) The pressure of the reaction mixture is reduced to 4 atmospheres, but the temperature is kept at $ 7 0 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000134", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 134, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Explain the effect on the yield of hydrogen at equilibrium.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000135", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 135, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(d) Calculate the volume, in $ \\mathrm{d m}^{3} $ of methane gas at rtp needed to produce 6.6 tonnes of hydrogen gas.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000136", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 136, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "[at rtp,molar volume=24 dm $ ^{3} $ 1 tonne= $ 1 0^{6} \\mathrm{~ g} $ ]", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000137", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 137, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Give your answer in standard form.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000138", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 138, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "(Total for Question 7 = 11 marks)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000140", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 140, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "BLANK PAGE", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000141", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 141, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:03:38.464477+00');
INSERT INTO public.documents VALUES ('9dffbd66-6af0-4035-9c62-174308abfb85', '3126f938-f14e-58cd-b68e-7b38a5840ce5', '1.0', 1, 'MARK_SCHEME', 'corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2023jun/MS.md', 'MS.md', 'text/markdown', '4c3cb10ab21c228322bc6043ff7a7c5c276df799d98f9a1f4804892ac87ffe4e', 'SHA-256', 1, 32, 32, 12, 'glm-ocr-markdown', '1.1.0', '2026-09-13 13:03:19.009349+00', '{"pages": [{"width": null, "height": null, "pageNumber": 1}], "source": {"uri": "corpus/igcse-chemistry-4ch0-2c-2023jun/MS.md", "checksum": "4c3cb10ab21c228322bc6043ff7a7c5c276df799d98f9a1f4804892ac87ffe4e", "fileName": "MS.md", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "checksumAlgorithm": "SHA-256"}, "tables": [{"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["1", "(a)(i)", "silicon", "ALLOW Si", "1"], ["(ii)", "magnesium", "ALLOW Mg", "1"], ["(iii)", "bromine", "ALLOW mercury/Hg\nALLOW Br/Br2\nREJECT bromide/Br-", "1"], ["(iv)", "2,8,5/2.8.5", "ACCEPT diagram showing electron configuration", "1"], ["(v)", "Na2S", "ALLOW Na+2S2-", "1"], ["(b)", "An explanation that links the following two points\nM1 full outer shell/8 electrons in outer shell/(electron configuration)2.8\nM2(so) does not need to lose or gain(or share) electrons/e(-)", "", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total 7"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n1 | (a)(i) | silicon | ALLOW Si | 1\n(ii) | magnesium | ALLOW Mg | 1\n(iii) | bromine | ALLOW mercury/Hg\nALLOW Br/Br2\nREJECT bromide/Br- | 1\n(iv) | 2,8,5/2.8.5 | ACCEPT diagram showing electron configuration | 1\n(v) | Na2S | ALLOW Na+2S2- | 1\n(b) | An explanation that links the following two points\nM1 full outer shell/8 electrons in outer shell/(electron configuration)2.8\nM2(so) does not need to lose or gain(or share) electrons/e(-) |  | 2\n |  |  | Total 7", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000022", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 22, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["2(a)", "B(carbon dioxide)\nA is incorrect as there is more argon in the atmosphere than carbon dioxide\nC is incorrect as there is more nitrogen in the atmosphere than carbon dioxide\nD is incorrect as there is more oxygen in the atmosphere than carbon dioxide", "", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "B(decomposition)\nA is incorrect as this is not an addition reaction\nC is incorrect as this is not an oxidation reaction\nD is incorrect as this is not a substitution reaction", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "C(green to black)\nA is incorrect as copper(II) carbonate is not blue\nB is incorrect as copper(II) carbonate is not blue and copper(II) oxide is not orange\nD is incorrect as copper(II) oxide is not orange", "", "1"], ["(iii)", "CuCO3→CuO+CO2", "ALLOW multiples\nIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", "1"], ["(c)", "M1(volume of oxygen=)100-27OR73(cm3)\nM2(volume of air at start=)280+100OR380(cm3)\nM373÷380×100OR19.2(%)M419(%)", "correct answer with or without working scores4\nALLOW ECF throughout\nUse of 280 gives an answer of 26 scores3\nAlternative method\nM1(volume of air left=)280+27OR307(cm3)\nM2307÷380×100OR80.8(%)M3100-80.8OR19.2M419(%)", "4"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n2(a) | B(carbon dioxide)\nA is incorrect as there is more argon in the atmosphere than carbon dioxide\nC is incorrect as there is more nitrogen in the atmosphere than carbon dioxide\nD is incorrect as there is more oxygen in the atmosphere than carbon dioxide |  | 1\n(b)(i) | B(decomposition)\nA is incorrect as this is not an addition reaction\nC is incorrect as this is not an oxidation reaction\nD is incorrect as this is not a substitution reaction |  | 1\n(ii) | C(green to black)\nA is incorrect as copper(II) carbonate is not blue\nB is incorrect as copper(II) carbonate is not blue and copper(II) oxide is not orange\nD is incorrect as copper(II) oxide is not orange |  | 1\n(iii) | CuCO3→CuO+CO2 | ALLOW multiples\nIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | 1\n(c) | M1(volume of oxygen=)100-27OR73(cm3)\nM2(volume of air at start=)280+100OR380(cm3)\nM373÷380×100OR19.2(%)M419(%) | correct answer with or without working scores4\nALLOW ECF throughout\nUse of 280 gives an answer of 26 scores3\nAlternative method\nM1(volume of air left=)280+27OR307(cm3)\nM2307÷380×100OR80.8(%)M3100-80.8OR19.2M419(%) | 4", "row_count": 6, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000023", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 23, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(d)", "An explanation that links two of the following three points\nM1 carbon dioxide is a greenhouse gas\nAND\nM2 (that causes) climate change / global warming / global temperature rise\nOR\nM3 melting of polar icecaps / flooding / wildfires / sea levels rising", "ACCEPT description of greenhouse effect e.g. carbon dioxide traps heat / infra-red rays in the atmosphere\nALLOW oceans becoming more acidic / less basic /pH decreasing\nREJECT reference to the ozone layer for M2 or M3\nIGNORE reference to acid rain", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total 10"]], "text": "(d) | An explanation that links two of the following three points\nM1 carbon dioxide is a greenhouse gas\nAND\nM2 (that causes) climate change / global warming / global temperature rise\nOR\nM3 melting of polar icecaps / flooding / wildfires / sea levels rising | ACCEPT description of greenhouse effect e.g. carbon dioxide traps heat / infra-red rays in the atmosphere\nALLOW oceans becoming more acidic / less basic /pH decreasing\nREJECT reference to the ozone layer for M2 or M3\nIGNORE reference to acid rain | 2\n |  |  | Total 10", "row_count": 2, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["3(a)", "C6H12O6→2C2H5OH+2CO2M1 both formulae correctM2 balancing of correct formulae", "ACCEPT CH3CH2OHM2 dep on M1 but ifC2H6O given no M1 but allow M2 for correct balancingIGNORE state symbols even if incorrectALLOW multiples and fractions", "2"], ["(b)(i)", "", "Hydration", "Fermentation", "ACCEPT H3PO4If formula alone must be correct, but if name given and formula incorrect ignore formulaALLOW sulphuric acid/H2SO4ACCEPT any temperature between20and40inclusiveACCEPT any pressure between60and70inclusive", "3"], ["", "Reagents", "ethene and steam", "aqueous glucose", ""], ["", "Catalyst", "phosphoric acid", "enzymes in yeast", ""], ["", "Temperature in℃", "300", "30", ""], ["", "Pressure in atmospheres", "60-70", "1", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n3(a) | C6H12O6→2C2H5OH+2CO2M1 both formulae correctM2 balancing of correct formulae | ACCEPT CH3CH2OHM2 dep on M1 but ifC2H6O given no M1 but allow M2 for correct balancingIGNORE state symbols even if incorrectALLOW multiples and fractions | 2\n(b)(i) |  | Hydration | Fermentation | ACCEPT H3PO4If formula alone must be correct, but if name given and formula incorrect ignore formulaALLOW sulphuric acid/H2SO4ACCEPT any temperature between20and40inclusiveACCEPT any pressure between60and70inclusive | 3\n | Reagents | ethene and steam | aqueous glucose | \n | Catalyst | phosphoric acid | enzymes in yeast | \n | Temperature in℃ | 300 | 30 | \n | Pressure in atmospheres | 60-70 | 1 | ", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "An explanation that links one advantage and one disadvantage\nadvantage:\nM1 uses low(er) pressure / atmospheric pressure / 1 atm\nM2 so less energy needed / less costly equipment / safer\nOR\nM1 uses low(er) temperature\nM2 so less energy / heat needed\nOR\nM1 glucose / sugar cane is a natural resource / is renewable\nM2 whereas ethene obtained from crude oil / ethene is non-renewable / ethene is a finite resource\nOR\nM1 yeast is a natural resource\nM2 whereas phosphoric acid is a manufactured catalyst\ndisadvantage:\nM3 fermentation is slow(er)\nM4 fermentation is less efficient / so hydration is more efficient\nOR\nM3 ethanol is impure\nM4 so ethanol needs to be purified ORA\nOR\nM3 growing sugar cane takes up land\nM4 that can be used to grow food crops", "IGNORE cheaper / less costly alone\nIGNORE cheaper / less costly", "4"]], "text": "(ii) | An explanation that links one advantage and one disadvantage\nadvantage:\nM1 uses low(er) pressure / atmospheric pressure / 1 atm\nM2 so less energy needed / less costly equipment / safer\nOR\nM1 uses low(er) temperature\nM2 so less energy / heat needed\nOR\nM1 glucose / sugar cane is a natural resource / is renewable\nM2 whereas ethene obtained from crude oil / ethene is non-renewable / ethene is a finite resource\nOR\nM1 yeast is a natural resource\nM2 whereas phosphoric acid is a manufactured catalyst\ndisadvantage:\nM3 fermentation is slow(er)\nM4 fermentation is less efficient / so hydration is more efficient\nOR\nM3 ethanol is impure\nM4 so ethanol needs to be purified ORA\nOR\nM3 growing sugar cane takes up land\nM4 that can be used to grow food crops | IGNORE cheaper / less costly alone\nIGNORE cheaper / less costly | 4", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(c)", "An explanation that links the following two points\nM1 oxygen would oxidise / react with ethanol / alcohol\nM2 which would produce ethanoic acid / CH3COOH\nOR\nM1 fermentation needs to be anaerobic\nM2 so ethanol / alcohol will be formed / otherwise only carbon dioxide and water would form", "2"], ["(d)(i)", "M1 $\\frac{60.0}{12}$", "$\\frac{13.3}{1}$", "$\\frac{26.7}{16}$", "0 marks for division by atomic numbers or upside-down calculation", "3"], ["", "M2 5.0", "13.3", "1.67", "ALLOW any number of sig figs except 1 apart from 5 in M2 and M3", ""], ["", "M3 $\\frac{5.0}{1.67}$", "$\\frac{13.3}{1.67}$", "$\\frac{1.67}{1.67}$", "", ""], ["", "OR 2.99", "7.96", "1", "ACCEPT alternative methods", ""], ["(ii)", "H H H\nI I I\nH C C C O H\nI I I\nH H H", "Bond between O and H must be shown", "1"], ["", "", "ACCEPT structure of propan-2-ol", ""], ["", "", "", "Total 15"]], "text": "(c) | An explanation that links the following two points\nM1 oxygen would oxidise / react with ethanol / alcohol\nM2 which would produce ethanoic acid / CH3COOH\nOR\nM1 fermentation needs to be anaerobic\nM2 so ethanol / alcohol will be formed / otherwise only carbon dioxide and water would form | 2\n(d)(i) | M1 $\\frac{60.0}{12}$ | $\\frac{13.3}{1}$ | $\\frac{26.7}{16}$ | 0 marks for division by atomic numbers or upside-down calculation | 3\n | M2 5.0 | 13.3 | 1.67 | ALLOW any number of sig figs except 1 apart from 5 in M2 and M3 | \n | M3 $\\frac{5.0}{1.67}$ | $\\frac{13.3}{1.67}$ | $\\frac{1.67}{1.67}$ |  | \n | OR 2.99 | 7.96 | 1 | ACCEPT alternative methods | \n(ii) | H H H\nI I I\nH C C C O H\nI I I\nH H H | Bond between O and H must be shown | 1\n |  | ACCEPT structure of propan-2-ol | \n |  |  | Total 15", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 3, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)", "pipette", "", "1"], ["(b)", "M1(colour in potassium hydroxide) yellowM2(colour in sulfuric acid) red", "ALLOW pink", "2"], ["(c)", "to see the colour(change more) clearly(at the end-point) OWTTE", "", "1"], ["(d)", "to mix the solutions(more thoroughly) OWTTE", "ALLOW to speed up the reaction between the acid and alkali OWTTE", "1"], ["(e)", "titres/results within(+or-)0.2(cm3of each other)", "ALLOW within0.1REJECT>0.2or<0.1", "1"], ["(f)", "M1n(H2SO4)=0.0150×0.180or0.0027(0)(mol)M2n(KOH)=0.0027(0)×2or0.0054(0)(mol)M3concn=(0.0054(0)÷0.0250)=0.216(mol/dm3)", "correct answer with or without working scores3answer toM1×2answer toM2÷0.0250ALLOW any number of sig figs except1common answers:0.108and0.054scores2", "3"], ["(g)", "An explanation that links the following two pointsM1anH+ion is a protonM2the OH-ion) reacts / bonds with theH+ion)(to form water)", "ALLOW donates a proton/H+ion)to theOH-IGNORE accepts a proton", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total11"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a) | pipette |  | 1\n(b) | M1(colour in potassium hydroxide) yellowM2(colour in sulfuric acid) red | ALLOW pink | 2\n(c) | to see the colour(change more) clearly(at the end-point) OWTTE |  | 1\n(d) | to mix the solutions(more thoroughly) OWTTE | ALLOW to speed up the reaction between the acid and alkali OWTTE | 1\n(e) | titres/results within(+or-)0.2(cm3of each other) | ALLOW within0.1REJECT>0.2or<0.1 | 1\n(f) | M1n(H2SO4)=0.0150×0.180or0.0027(0)(mol)M2n(KOH)=0.0027(0)×2or0.0054(0)(mol)M3concn=(0.0054(0)÷0.0250)=0.216(mol/dm3) | correct answer with or without working scores3answer toM1×2answer toM2÷0.0250ALLOW any number of sig figs except1common answers:0.108and0.054scores2 | 3\n(g) | An explanation that links the following two pointsM1anH+ion is a protonM2the OH-ion) reacts / bonds with theH+ion)(to form water) | ALLOW donates a proton/H+ion)to theOH-IGNORE accepts a proton | 2\n |  |  | Total11", "row_count": 9, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)", "M1 add sodium hydroxide(to the copper(II) sulfate solution)", "ALLOW potassium hydroxide or aqueous ammonia", "2"], ["M2 blue precipitate(forms)", "No M1 if any incorrect reagent added", ""], ["OR", "IGNORE qualifiers e.g. pale/dark etc.", ""], ["M1 flame test", "M2 dep on addition of a correct alkali", ""], ["M2 blue-green(flame)", "ACCEPT description of flame test", ""], ["", "ALLOW green", ""], ["", "M2 dep on flame", ""], ["(b)", "An description that refers to any three from", "", "3"], ["M1 copper ions are positively charged/cations/Cu2+ions", "ALLOW M1 and M3 for a fully correct half equation", ""], ["M2 and are attracted to/travel to the negative electrode/cathode", "i.e. Cu2++2e→Cu", ""], ["M3 where they accept electrons", "", ""], ["M4 and become(copper)atoms", "", ""], ["(c)", "pink solid/deposit/coating/metal", "ACCEPT pink-brown/orange-brown/brown/orange/red-brown", "1"], ["", "REJECT red", ""], ["", "REJECT precipitate", ""], ["(d)(i)(ii)(iii)", "relights a glowing splint", "", "1"], ["2H2O→4H++O2+4e(-)", "4OH-→2H2O+O2+4e(-) scores 1", "2"], ["M1O2+e(-)", "IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", ""], ["M2 equation fully correct electrons are lost", "IGNORE any numbers in front ofO2+e(-)and any other species", ""], ["", "", "ALLOW H2O/water loses electrons", "1"], ["", "", "", "Total 10"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a) | M1 add sodium hydroxide(to the copper(II) sulfate solution) | ALLOW potassium hydroxide or aqueous ammonia | 2\nM2 blue precipitate(forms) | No M1 if any incorrect reagent added | \nOR | IGNORE qualifiers e.g. pale/dark etc. | \nM1 flame test | M2 dep on addition of a correct alkali | \nM2 blue-green(flame) | ACCEPT description of flame test | \n | ALLOW green | \n | M2 dep on flame | \n(b) | An description that refers to any three from |  | 3\nM1 copper ions are positively charged/cations/Cu2+ions | ALLOW M1 and M3 for a fully correct half equation | \nM2 and are attracted to/travel to the negative electrode/cathode | i.e. Cu2++2e→Cu | \nM3 where they accept electrons |  | \nM4 and become(copper)atoms |  | \n(c) | pink solid/deposit/coating/metal | ACCEPT pink-brown/orange-brown/brown/orange/red-brown | 1\n | REJECT red | \n | REJECT precipitate | \n(d)(i)(ii)(iii) | relights a glowing splint |  | 1\n2H2O→4H++O2+4e(-) | 4OH-→2H2O+O2+4e(-) scores 1 | 2\nM1O2+e(-) | IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | \nM2 equation fully correct electrons are lost | IGNORE any numbers in front ofO2+e(-)and any other species | \n |  | ALLOW H2O/water loses electrons | 1\n |  |  | Total 10", "row_count": 22, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6", "(a)(i)", "sulfuric acid/H2SO4", "ACCEPT hydrochloric acid/HCl and nitric acid/HNO3/phosphoric acid/H3PO4", "1"], ["(ii)", "distinctive sweet fruity smell", "ACCEPT an oily layer forms(on the surface)", "1"], ["(iii)", "methyl ethanoate", "spelling must be correct", "1"], ["(b)(i)", "(i)", "C-O and O-H", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 the same(two)bonds/C-O and O-H are broken and formedM2 energy needed to break bonds equals energy released when bonds form(so overall enthalpy change is0)", "ALLOW ecf if wrong bonds in(i)IGNORE the same number of bonds are broken and formed", "2"], ["", "", "", "Total 6"], ["", "", "", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6 | (a)(i) | sulfuric acid/H2SO4 | ACCEPT hydrochloric acid/HCl and nitric acid/HNO3/phosphoric acid/H3PO4 | 1\n(ii) | distinctive sweet fruity smell | ACCEPT an oily layer forms(on the surface) | 1\n(iii) | methyl ethanoate | spelling must be correct | 1\n(b)(i) | (i) | C-O and O-H |  | 1\n(ii) | An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 the same(two)bonds/C-O and O-H are broken and formedM2 energy needed to break bonds equals energy released when bonds form(so overall enthalpy change is0) | ALLOW ecf if wrong bonds in(i)IGNORE the same number of bonds are broken and formed | 2\n |  |  | Total 6\n |  |  | ", "row_count": 8, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "reduces the capacity of blood to transport oxygen round the body OWTTE", "ALLOW carbon monoxide /it binds with haemoglobin", "1"], ["(b)", "An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 no effectM2 as increases rate of forward reaction and rate of backward reaction equally", "M2 dep on M1 or missing", "2"], ["(c)(i)", "An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 yield decreasesM2 as (forward) reaction is endothermic (so equilibrium shifts to the LHS / reactants side)", "ALLOW backward /reverse reaction is exothermicM2 dep on M1 or missingIGNORE references to Le Chatelier", "2"], ["(ii)", "An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 yield increasesM2 as there are fewer moles / molecules (of gas) on the left-hand side / there are 2 mol on LHS and 4 mol on RHS (so equilibrium shifts to the RHS / products side) ORA", "M2 dep on M1 or missingIGNORE references to Le Chatelier", "2"], ["(d)", "M1 n(H2)=6.6×106÷2 OR 3.3×106(mol)M2 n(CH4)=3.3×106÷3 OR 1.1×106(mol)M3 vol(CH4)=1.1×106×24 OR 2640000(dm3)M4 2.6×107", "correct answer with or without working scores4ACCEPT 3300000ACCEPT 1100000M2×24ACCEPT 2.64×107ALLOW ECF throughoutcommon answers:7.9(2)×107scores 35.28×107scores 31.584×108scores 2", "4"], ["", "", "", "Total 11"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | reduces the capacity of blood to transport oxygen round the body OWTTE | ALLOW carbon monoxide /it binds with haemoglobin | 1\n(b) | An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 no effectM2 as increases rate of forward reaction and rate of backward reaction equally | M2 dep on M1 or missing | 2\n(c)(i) | An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 yield decreasesM2 as (forward) reaction is endothermic (so equilibrium shifts to the LHS / reactants side) | ALLOW backward /reverse reaction is exothermicM2 dep on M1 or missingIGNORE references to Le Chatelier | 2\n(ii) | An explanation that links the following two pointsM1 yield increasesM2 as there are fewer moles / molecules (of gas) on the left-hand side / there are 2 mol on LHS and 4 mol on RHS (so equilibrium shifts to the RHS / products side) ORA | M2 dep on M1 or missingIGNORE references to Le Chatelier | 2\n(d) | M1 n(H2)=6.6×106÷2 OR 3.3×106(mol)M2 n(CH4)=3.3×106÷3 OR 1.1×106(mol)M3 vol(CH4)=1.1×106×24 OR 2640000(dm3)M4 2.6×107 | correct answer with or without working scores4ACCEPT 3300000ACCEPT 1100000M2×24ACCEPT 2.64×107ALLOW ECF throughoutcommon answers:7.9(2)×107scores 35.28×107scores 31.584×108scores 2 | 4\n |  |  | Total 11", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000031", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 31, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "3126f938-f14e-58cd-b68e-7b38a5840ce5", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:03:19.009349322Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 92, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Question Paper Log Number P71952A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_2C_2306_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2023", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:03:38.480031+00');
