oints |  | 3\nM1 there is a surplus supply of/less demand for larger fractions/molecules/hydrocarbons |  | \nORthere is not enough supply/greater demand for smaller fractions/molecules/hydrocarbons |  | \nM2 alkenes are produced which are needed to make polymers | ALLOW plastics/to make ethanol | \nM3 smaller fractions/alkanes/molecules/hydrocarbons are needed for petrol | ALLOW gasoline/fuel for cars | \n |  | Total 11 | ", "row_count": 16, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000024", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 24, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["4(a)(i)(ii)(b)", "M1 all points plotted correctly to the nearest+or-half a small square forKNO3M2 all points plotted correctly to the nearest+or-half a small square forNaNO3", "", "2"], ["M1 smooth curve of best fit forKNO3M2 smooth curve of best fit forNaNO3", "IfKNO3andNaNO3are not labelled or labelled incorrectly lose1mark if curves are correct but allowECF for(c)和(d)if the curves are the wrong way round", "2"], ["temperature where their lines cross(expected value approximately68℃)", "", "1"], ["(c)(d)", "M1 mass at30℃read from graph(expected value approximately24g)M24x answer toM1(expected value approximately96g)", "", "2"], ["M1 mass at50℃read from graph(expected value approximately21g)M2 mass at20℃read from graph(expected value approximately8g)M3M1-M2(expected value approximately13g)", "Need to show working on the graph forM1andM2to score but allowM3forM1-M2", "3"], ["", "", "", "Total10"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n4(a)(i)(ii)(b) | M1 all points plotted correctly to the nearest+or-half a small square forKNO3M2 all points plotted correctly to the nearest+or-half a small square forNaNO3 |  | 2\nM1 smooth curve of best fit forKNO3M2 smooth curve of best fit forNaNO3 | IfKNO3andNaNO3are not labelled or labelled incorrectly lose1mark if curves are correct but allowECF for(c)和(d)if the curves are the wrong way round | 2\ntemperature where their lines cross(expected value approximately68℃) |  | 1\n(c)(d) | M1 mass at30℃read from graph(expected value approximately24g)M24x answer toM1(expected value approximately96g) |  | 2\nM1 mass at50℃read from graph(expected value approximately21g)M2 mass at20℃read from graph(expected value approximately8g)M3M1-M2(expected value approximately13g) | Need to show working on the graph forM1andM2to score but allowM3forM1-M2 | 3\n |  |  | Total10", "row_count": 7, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000025", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 25, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["5(a)", "Any two from", "", "2"], ["M1 same general formula", "", ""], ["M2 same functional group", "", ""], ["M3 similar chemical properties/characteristics", "IGNORE same chemical properties", ""], ["M4 trend in physical properties/characteristics", "accept any trend in specified physical property", ""], ["(b)(i)", "H2SO4", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "M1(from) orange", "must be in the correct order", "2"], ["M2(to) green", "", ""], ["(iii)", "M1(methanol) H\nI\nH-C-O-H\nI\nH", "Penalise once only if O-H bond not shown and both structures correct", "2"], ["M2(methanoic acid) O\nII\nH-C-O-H", "", ""], ["(c)", "CH3OH+HCOOH→HCOOCH3+H2O", "ALLOW multiples\nALLOW CH3OOCH\nIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect\nREJECT CH3COOH and C2H4O2", "1"], ["(d)(i)", "A(butyl ethanoate)\nBbutyl methanoate is not the correct name of the ester CH3COOCH2CH2CH3\nCethyl butanoate is not the correct name of the ester CH3COOCH2CH2CH3\nDmethyl butanoate is not the correct name of the ester CH3COOCH2CH2CH3", "", "1"], ["(ii)", "C6H12O2", "ALLOW symbols in any order", "1"], ["", "", "", "Total 10"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n5(a) | Any two from |  | 2\nM1 same general formula |  | \nM2 same functional group |  | \nM3 similar chemical properties/characteristics | IGNORE same chemical properties | \nM4 trend in physical properties/characteristics | accept any trend in specified physical property | \n(b)(i) | H2SO4 |  | 1\n(ii) | M1(from) orange | must be in the correct order | 2\nM2(to) green |  | \n(iii) | M1(methanol) H\nI\nH-C-O-H\nI\nH | Penalise once only if O-H bond not shown and both structures correct | 2\nM2(methanoic acid) O\nII\nH-C-O-H |  | \n(c) | CH3OH+HCOOH→HCOOCH3+H2O | ALLOW multiples\nALLOW CH3OOCH\nIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect\nREJECT CH3COOH and C2H4O2 | 1\n(d)(i) | A(butyl ethanoate)\nBbutyl methanoate is not the correct name of the ester CH3COOCH2CH2CH3\nCethyl butanoate is not the correct name of the ester CH3COOCH2CH2CH3\nDmethyl butanoate is not the correct name of the ester CH3COOCH2CH2CH3 |  | 1\n(ii) | C6H12O2 | ALLOW symbols in any order | 1\n |  |  | Total 10", "row_count": 15, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000026", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 26, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["6(a)", "A description that refers to the following three points", "", "3"], ["M1 filter (the mixture)", "", ""], ["M2 wash (the precipitate/solid/lead(II) bromide with distilled water)", "", ""], ["M3 suitable drying method", "e.g. dry with filter paper/leave to dry/dry in a desiccator/dry in an oven", ""], ["REJECT M3 if they attempt to crystallise the filtrate", ""], ["", "If any attempt to evaporate the solution allow MAX 1", ""], ["(b)(i)", "2(.0)x0.025=0.05(0)(mol)", "ACCEPT25÷1000=0.0250.05÷0.025=2", "1"], ["OR2(.0)x25=0.05(0)(mol)1000", "All working must be shown to gain full marks", ""], ["(ii)", "M1(nPbBr2)=0.05(0)÷2=0.025", "ALLOW2:1=0.05:0.025", "2"], ["M20.025x367=9.175(g)", "ACCEPT9.18/9.2/9(g)", ""], ["ORM10.05x367=18.35(g)", "", ""], ["M218.35÷2=9.175(g)", "ACCEPT9.18/9.2/9(g)All working must be shown to gain full marks", ""], ["(c)(i)", "An explanation that links the following three points", "", "3"], ["M1when solid the ions are in fixed positions/in a lattice", "", ""], ["M2so there are no ions/electrons/charged particles free to move", "", ""], ["M3(when molten)the ions are free to move so can conduct electricity/carry a current", "IGNORE carry charge", ""], ["REJECT solution for M3", ""], ["", "REJECT electrons moving/delocalised electrons for M3", ""]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n6(a) | A description that refers to the following three points |  | 3\nM1 filter (the mixture) |  | \nM2 wash (the precipitate/solid/lead(II) bromide with distilled water) |  | \nM3 suitable drying method | e.g. dry with filter paper/leave to dry/dry in a desiccator/dry in an oven | \nREJECT M3 if they attempt to crystallise the filtrate | \n | If any attempt to evaporate the solution allow MAX 1 | \n(b)(i) | 2(.0)x0.025=0.05(0)(mol) | ACCEPT25÷1000=0.0250.05÷0.025=2 | 1\nOR2(.0)x25=0.05(0)(mol)1000 | All working must be shown to gain full marks | \n(ii) | M1(nPbBr2)=0.05(0)÷2=0.025 | ALLOW2:1=0.05:0.025 | 2\nM20.025x367=9.175(g) | ACCEPT9.18/9.2/9(g) | \nORM10.05x367=18.35(g) |  | \nM218.35÷2=9.175(g) | ACCEPT9.18/9.2/9(g)All working must be shown to gain full marks | \n(c)(i) | An explanation that links the following three points |  | 3\nM1when solid the ions are in fixed positions/in a lattice |  | \nM2so there are no ions/electrons/charged particles free to move |  | \nM3(when molten)the ions are free to move so can conduct electricity/carry a current | IGNORE carry charge | \nREJECT solution for M3 | \n | REJECT electrons moving/delocalised electrons for M3 | ", "row_count": 19, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000027", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 27, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["(ii)", "An explanation that links the following two points", "", "2"], ["M1 graphite", "IGNORE carbon", ""], ["M2 resistance to high temperature /has a high melting point", "ALLOW platinum", ""], ["ALLOW conducts electricity /doesn''t react with product /is inert", ""], ["M2 dependent on graphite /carbon /a transition metal", ""], ["(iii)", "Pb$^{2+}$ + 2e$^{-}$ → Pb", "ACCEPT multiples", "1"], ["IGNORE state symbols even if incorrect", ""], ["(d)", "(i) brown vapour/gas/fumes", "ALLOW red-brown vapour/gas/fumes", "1"], ["REJECT orange/orange-brown/red alone", ""], ["(ii)", "bromide (ions)/Br$^{-}$ loses electrons", "ALLOW electrons are lost", "1"], ["REJECT bromine loses electrons", ""], ["", "", "", "Total 14"]], "text": "(ii) | An explanation that links the following two points |  | 2\nM1 graphite | IGNORE carbon | \nM2 resistance to high temperature /has a high melting point | ALLOW platinum | \nALLOW conducts electricity /doesn''t react with product /is inert | \nM2 dependent on graphite /carbon /a transition metal | \n(iii) | Pb$^{2+}$ + 2e$^{-}$ → Pb | ACCEPT multiples | 1\nIGNORE state symbols even if incorrect | \n(d) | (i) brown vapour/gas/fumes | ALLOW red-brown vapour/gas/fumes | 1\nREJECT orange/orange-brown/red alone | \n(ii) | bromide (ions)/Br$^{-}$ loses electrons | ALLOW electrons are lost | 1\nREJECT bromine loses electrons | \n |  |  | Total 14", "row_count": 12, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000028", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 28, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["Question number", "Answer", "Notes", "Marks"], ["7(a)", "M1(electrostatic) attraction between nuclei(of both atoms)", "nuclei must be plural", "2"], ["M2 and a shared/bonding pair of electrons"], ["OR"], ["M1(electrostatic) attraction between a shared/bonding pair of electrons"], ["(b)", "M2 and nuclei(of both atoms)", "nuclei must be plural", "4"], ["An explanation that links the following four points"], ["M1(in the organic solvent) litmus paper stays blue/has no change"], ["M2 because there are no(H+)ions/the solution is not acidic/does not dissociate in an organic solvent"], ["M3(in the aqueous solution) litmus paper turns red"], ["M4 because H+ions are formed/hydrochloric acid forms", "REJECT M3 if litmus is bleached or turns white"], ["(c)(i)", "", "correct answer-184 with or without working scores3", "3"], ["M1 reactants bond energy=436+242 OR 678(kJ)", "(+)184 scores2"], ["M2 products bond energy=2x431 OR 862(kJ)", "ALLOW ecf on incorrect values onM1 and/or M2"], ["(ii)", "M1 show correct positions of horizontal lines and activation energy hump", "ALLOW ecf if positive answer in(i)", "4"], ["M2 correct labelling of(reactants)H2+Cl2and(products)2HCl", "M3 REJECT arrow pointing down"], ["M3 vertical line in correct position labelledΔH", "ACCEPT arrow pointing down or double headed arrow"], ["", "REJECT arrow pointing up"]], "text": "Question number | Answer | Notes | Marks\n7(a) | M1(electrostatic) attraction between nuclei(of both atoms) | nuclei must be plural | 2\nM2 and a shared/bonding pair of electrons\nOR\nM1(electrostatic) attraction between a shared/bonding pair of electrons\n(b) | M2 and nuclei(of both atoms) | nuclei must be plural | 4\nAn explanation that links the following four points\nM1(in the organic solvent) litmus paper stays blue/has no change\nM2 because there are no(H+)ions/the solution is not acidic/does not dissociate in an organic solvent\nM3(in the aqueous solution) litmus paper turns red\nM4 because H+ions are formed/hydrochloric acid forms | REJECT M3 if litmus is bleached or turns white\n(c)(i) |  | correct answer-184 with or without working scores3 | 3\nM1 reactants bond energy=436+242 OR 678(kJ) | (+)184 scores2\nM2 products bond energy=2x431 OR 862(kJ) | ALLOW ecf on incorrect values onM1 and/or M2\n(ii) | M1 show correct positions of horizontal lines and activation energy hump | ALLOW ecf if positive answer in(i) | 4\nM2 correct labelling of(reactants)H2+Cl2and(products)2HCl | M3 REJECT arrow pointing down\nM3 vertical line in correct position labelledΔH | ACCEPT arrow pointing down or double headed arrow\n | REJECT arrow pointing up", "row_count": 18, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000029", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 29, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"rows": [["", "M4 vertical line in correct position labelled Ea or activation energy", "ACCEPT arrow pointing up or double headed arrow\nREJECT arrow pointing down", "Total 13"]], "text": " | M4 vertical line in correct position labelled Ea or activation energy | ACCEPT arrow pointing up or double headed arrow\nREJECT arrow pointing down | Total 13", "row_count": 1, "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000030", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "column_count": 4, "element_type": "table", "reading_order": 30, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "figures": [], "version": 1, "sections": [{"level": 2, "title": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "sectionId": "s001", "elementIds": ["e000006"], "pageNumber": 1}, {"level": 2, "title": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "sectionId": "s002", "elementIds": ["e000008", "e000009", "e000010", "e000011", "e000012", "e000013", "e000014", "e000015", "e000016", "e000017", "e000018", "e000019", "e000020", "e000021"], "pageNumber": 1}], "equations": [], "pageCount": 1, "documentId": "8fe25072-6546-5de3-808d-6f21d3a9e309", "provenance": {"engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "application": "syllabai-parser", "extractedAt": "2026-09-13T13:04:01.570524032Z", "engineVersion": "1.1.0", "schemaVersion": "1.0", "extractionParams": {"pageBoundaries": "none-in-source", "sourceLineCount": 44, "upstreamConverter": "zai-glm-ocr", "entityDecodedLines": 1, "signedUrlFigureRefs": 0, "normalizedHtmlEntities": true}}, "textBlocks": [{"role": "paragraph", "text": "PMT", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000000", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 0, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000001", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 1, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Mark Scheme (Results)", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000002", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 2, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2024", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000003", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 3, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson Edexcel International GCSE In Chemistry (4CH1) Paper 2C", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000004", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 4, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC Qualifications", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000005", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 5, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Edexcel and BTEC qualifications are awarded by Pearson, the UK''s largest awarding body. We provide a wide range of qualifications including academic, vocational, occupational and specific programmes for employers. For further information visit our qualifications websites at www.edexcel.com or www.btec.co.uk. Alternatively, you can get in touch with us using the details on our contact us page at www.edexcel.com/contactus.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000006", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 6, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "heading", "text": "Pearson: helping people progress, everywhere", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000007", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": 2, "reading_order": 7, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Pearson aspires to be the world''s leading learning company. Our aim is to help everyone progress in their lives through education. We believe in every kind of learning, for all kinds of people, wherever they are in the world. We''ve been involved in education for over 150 years, and by working across 70 countries, in 100 languages, we have built an international reputation for our commitment to high standards and raising achievement through innovation in education. Find out more about how we can help you and your students at: www.pearson.com/uk", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000008", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 8, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Summer 2024", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000009", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 9, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Question Paper Log Number P75822A", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000010", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 10, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "Publications Code 4CH1_2C_2406_MS", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000011", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 11, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "All the material in this publication is copyright", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000012", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 12, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "paragraph", "text": "$ \\textcircled{c} $ Pearson Education Ltd 2024", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000013", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 13, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All candidates must receive the same treatment. Examiners must mark the first candidate in exactly the same way as they mark the last.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000014", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 14, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Mark schemes should be applied positively. Candidates must be rewarded for what they have shown they can do rather than penalised for omissions.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000015", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 15, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "There is no ceiling on achievement. All marks on the mark scheme should be used appropriately.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000016", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 16, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Examiners should mark according to the mark scheme not according to their perception of where the grade boundaries may lie.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000017", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 17, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "All the marks on the mark scheme are designed to be awarded. Examiners should always award full marks if deserved, i.e. if the answer matches the mark scheme. Examiners should also be prepared to award zero marks if the candidate''s response is not worthy of credit according to the mark scheme.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000018", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 18, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Where some judgement is required,mark schemes will provide the principles by which marks will be awarded and exemplification may be limited.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000019", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 19, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "When examiners are in doubt regarding the application of the mark scheme to a candidate''s response, the team leader must be consulted.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000020", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 20, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}, {"role": "list_item", "text": "Crossed out work should be marked UNLESS the candidate has replaced it with an alternative response.", "confidence": 1.0, "element_id": "e000021", "page_number": 1, "bounding_box": null, "element_type": "text_block", "heading_level": null, "reading_order": 21, "source_engine": "glm-ocr-markdown", "source_engine_version": "1.1.0"}], "schemaVersion": "1.0"}', NULL, '2026-09-13 13:04:20.967384+00');
