(Total for Question 13 = 9 marks)
14 Carbon monoxide and hydrogen are used in the manufacture of methanol （ $ \mathrm{C H_{3} O H} $ ）.
The reaction is reversible and can reach a position of dynamic equilibrium.
\mathrm {C O (g)} + 2 \mathrm {H} _ {2} (\mathrm {g}) \rightleftharpoons \mathrm {C H} _ {3} \mathrm {O H} (\mathrm {g}) \quad \Delta H = - 9 1 \mathrm {k J / m o l}
The reaction is carried out at a pressure of about 100 atmospheres and a temperature of $ 2 5 0^{\circ} \mathrm{C} $
(a) State two features of a reaction that is in dynamic equilibrium.', 1, 1, '["e000244", "e000245", "e000246", "e000247", "e000248", "e000249", "e000250", "e000251", "e000252", "e000253", "e000254", "e000255"]', 271, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:52:25.716012+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('726d0feb-d970-4253-bcb0-7e3f3754f710', '16d31134-6baa-4001-abdf-7957ac2c0ba6', 17, '(b) (i) How would a decrease in temperature at constant pressure affect the amount of methanol in the equilibrium mixture?
