12 Titanium is a metal that can be extracted from its ore in a three-stage process.
stage 1 titanium ore is converted into titanium dioxide, $ \mathrm{T i O}_{2} $
stage 2 titanium dioxide is then converted into titanium chloride, $ \mathrm{T i C l}_{4} $
stage 3 titanium chloride is converted into titanium, Ti
(a) A titanium ore contains the composition by mass
\mathrm {F e} = 3 6. 8 \% \quad \mathrm {T i} = 3 1. 6 \% \quad \mathrm {O} = 3 1. 6 \%
Show by calculation that the empirical formula of this ore is $ \mathrm{F e T i O}_{3} $', 1, 1, '["e000182", "e000183", "e000184", "e000185", "e000186", "e000187", "e000188", "e000189", "e000190", "e000191", "e000192", "e000193", "e000194", "e000195", "e000196", "e000197", "e000198", "e000199"]', 287, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:11.715411+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('56ff649c-d392-4dd7-8cad-6f145b089a5b', '7d73db06-aceb-4fb9-afe9-f3b2c3322a0c', 11, '(b) The equation for the conversion of titanium dioxide into titanium chloride is
\mathrm {T i O} _ {2} + 2 \mathrm {C l} _ {2} + \mathrm {C} \rightarrow \mathrm {T i C l} _ {4} + \mathrm {C O} _ {2}
Explain which element has been oxidised in this reaction.
(c) In stage 3
titanium chloride vapour is passed through molten magnesium in an atmosphere of argon
the products are allowed to cool to form a solid mixture of titanium and magnesium chloride
this mixture is crushed into a powder and then added to water to dissolve the magnesium chloride
(i) Write a chemical equation for the reaction between titanium chloride and magnesium.
(ii) Suggest why this reaction cannot be successfully carried out in an atmosphere of air.
(iii) Suggest why the mixture is crushed into a powder before it is added to water.
(d) (i) Describe the bonding in titanium metal.
(ii) Explain why titanium conducts electricity.
(Total for Question 12 = 12 marks)
