14 Potassium hydrogencarbonate （ $ \mathrm{KHCO}_{3} $ ）decomposes on heating.
Three possible equations for the decomposition are
\mathrm {e q u a t i o n 1} \quad 2 \mathrm {K H C O} _ {3} (\mathrm {s}) \rightarrow \mathrm {K} _ {2} \mathrm {O} (\mathrm {s}) + 2 \mathrm {C O} _ {2} (\mathrm {g}) + \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} (\mathrm {g})
