K2CO3 | 138 | 5.52 |
(b) Use the information in the table to explain which equation, 1, 2 or 3, represents the decomposition of potassium hydrogencarbonate.
(Total for Question 14 = 4 marks)
15 Butane $ \left( \mathrm{C}_{4} \mathrm{H}_{1 0} \right) $ is a gas at room temperature and pressure.
The equation for the complete combustion of butane is
C _ {4} H _ {1 0} (g) + 6 \frac {1}{2} O _ {2} (g) \rightarrow 4 C O _ {2} (g) + 5 H _ {2} O (l)
Butane is used in an experiment to determine its $ \Delta H $ of combustion.
(a) State what the symbol $ \Delta H $ represents.
(b) The table shows the results of the experiment.', 1, 1, '["e000226", "e000227", "e000228", "e000229", "e000230", "e000231", "e000232", "e000233", "e000234", "e000235", "e000237", "e000238"]', 291, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:11.715804+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('1401e0ce-8aef-4282-ae78-bce90a088932', '7d73db06-aceb-4fb9-afe9-f3b2c3322a0c', 14, 'mass of water heated | 200g
mass of butane burned | 0.725g
initial temperature of water | 20.2℃
final temperature of water | 43.7℃
Use this equation to calculate the heat produced when 0.725 g of butane is burned in this experiment.
heat produced = mass of water $ \times $ 4.2 $ \times $ temperature rise of water (in J) (in g) (in $ ^{\circ} C $)
(c) A student uses the value from part (b) to calculate $ \Delta H $ for the combustion of butane. He calculates it as $ -1580 \mathrm{kJ} / \mathrm{mol} $ . He has not made a mistake in his calculation. A data book value is $ -2887 \mathrm{kJ} / \mathrm{mol} $ (i) What is the significance of the negative sign for $ \Delta H? $ (1)
(ii) The student notices that at the end of the experiment the bottom of the beaker is covered in black soot (carbon) Suggest how this soot is formed.
(iii) Explain how the formation of the soot may account for the difference between the value of $ \Delta H $ from the experiment and the value of $ \Delta H $ in the data book.
(iv) Suggest one other reason why the two $ \Delta H $ values are different.
(Total for Question 15 = 8 marks)', 1, 1, '["e000239", "e000240", "e000241", "e000242", "e000243", "e000244", "e000245", "e000246"]', 282, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:11.715917+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('5cbddddb-25c4-45cc-8464-eca1e9df79d5', '7d73db06-aceb-4fb9-afe9-f3b2c3322a0c', 15, '16 The diagram shows the apparatus used to investigate the rate of reaction between calcium carbonate and an excess of dilute hydrochloric acid.
