(Total for Question 9 = 15 marks)
10 This question is about magnesium and its compounds.
(a) A student draws this labelled diagram to show the particles in magnesium metal.
He makes two mistakes.
State the two corrections he should make to his labelled diagram.
(b) Explain why magnesium metal is malleable and a good conductor of electricity.
(c) Magnesium is a reactive metal. Its reactivity can be seen in its reactions with oxygen and dilute sulfuric acid.
The chemical equations for these reactions are
reaction 1
2 \mathrm {M g} + \mathrm {O} _ {2} \rightarrow 2 \mathrm {M g O}
reaction 2', 1, 1, '["e000217", "e000218", "e000219", "e000220", "e000221", "e000222", "e000223", "e000224", "e000226", "e000227", "e000228", "e000229", "e000230", "e000231", "e000232", "e000233"]', 276, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.854903+00');
