B it relights a glowing splint
D it turns limewater milky
C it turns damp blue litmus paper red
(d) The student used this method to obtain a sample of magnesium sulfate crystals from the solution formed in reaction 2.
heat the solution in a beaker for several minutes
dip a glass rod into the hot solution for a few seconds and then remove it
allow the solution to cool to room temperature
filter off the crystals and then dry them
