(ii) Explain why the student dips a glass rod into the heated solution.
(iii) Give the formulae of the two compounds that pass through the filter paper.
(e) After drying the crystals, the student weighs them and then heats them until they reach a constant mass.
This equation represents the change that occurs during heating.', 1, 1, '["e000234", "e000235", "e000236", "e000237", "e000238", "e000239", "e000240", "e000241", "e000242", "e000243", "e000244", "e000245", "e000246", "e000247", "e000248", "e000249", "e000250"]', 295, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:53:55.855276+00');
