INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('8aac6441-db3e-46d8-a4a4-453fe1df5f95', 'a7713333-d184-443d-a8d0-f8de214c35dd', 14, '(ii) The teacher wears safety glasses and a lab coat during the demonstration. Give one other safety precaution that she should take.
(c) Iron forms when iron(III) oxide is heated with carbon.
The equation for the reaction is
\mathrm {F e} _ {2} \mathrm {O} _ {3} + 3 \mathrm {C} \rightarrow 2 \mathrm {F e} + 3 \mathrm {C O}
(i) State how the equation shows that iron(III) oxide is reduced.
(ii) State why carbon monoxide should not be released into the atmosphere.
(iii) Calculate the maximum mass, in tonnes, of iron that can be produced when 30.0 tonnes of iron(III) oxide are reacted with an excess of carbon.
[ 1 \mathrm {t o n n e} = 1. 0 \times 1 0 ^ {6} \mathrm {g} ]
(iv) A mixture of 25 000 mol of iron(III) oxide and 840 000 g of carbon is heated.
Use this equation to show that the iron(III) oxide is in excess.
\mathrm {F e} _ {2} \mathrm {O} _ {3} + 3 \mathrm {C} \rightarrow 2 \mathrm {F e} + 3 \mathrm {C O}
\text{Total for Question 11 = 15 marks}
TOTAL FOR PAPER = 110 MARKS
