(Total for Question 5 = 10 marks)
BLANK PAGE
6 This question is about organic compounds.
(a) The diagram shows the displayed formulae of five compounds, U, V, W, X and Y.
(i) Give the letter of the compound that is not a hydrocarbon.
(1)
(ii) Give the letter of the compound that is a saturated hydrocarbon with the empirical formula $ \mathrm{C H_{2}} $
(iii) Give the letter of the compound that reacts with bromine in the presence of ultraviolet radiation to form this structure.
(1)
(iv) Give the letter of the compound that forms an addition polymer with this repeat unit.
(v) Give the displayed formula of an alkene that is an isomer of compound X.
(vi) Compounds U and X are members of the same homologous series Members of the same homologous series have the same functional group. Give two other characteristics of compounds in the same homologous series.
(b) Compound Z contains 38.7% carbon, 9.7% hydrogen and 51.6% oxygen by mass.
(i) Show by calculation that the empirical formula of compound Z is $ \mathrm{C H_{3} O} $', 1, 1, '["e000114", "e000115", "e000116", "e000117", "e000118", "e000120", "e000121", "e000122", "e000123", "e000124", "e000126", "e000128", "e000129", "e000130", "e000131"]', 273, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:56:09.168641+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('a104471c-6627-4a37-b44d-c713ceb72de6', '64b6a80a-a61f-4cff-9538-04dbcc03952c', 7, '(ii) The relative formula mass $ ( M_{\mathrm{r}}) $ of compound Z is 62 Deduce the molecular formula of compound Z.
