7 This question is about nitrogen and some of its compounds.
(a) Nitrogen and oxygen do not react together at room temperature.
At the high temperatures in a car engine, nitrogen and oxygen react to form nitrogen monoxide, NO
(i) Give a chemical equation for this reaction.
(ii) Give a reason why this reaction only occurs at high temperatures.
(iii) State why it is important that oxides of nitrogen are not released into the atmosphere.
(b) Nitrogen monoxide gas can be removed from car exhaust fumes when it reacts with carbon monoxide gas.
(i) The rate of the reaction is increased by passing the gases over a catalyst. Explain how a catalyst increases the rate of a reaction.
(ii) Explain how increasing the pressure of gases increases the rate of reaction.
(c) Ammonia is a simple molecule with the formula $ \mathrm{N H}_{3} $
(i) Complete the diagram to show the outer shell electrons in ammonia.
(ii) The bonds in ammonia are covalent.
Describe the forces of attraction in a covalent bond.
(iii) Explain why ammonia has a low boiling point.', 1, 1, '["e000132", "e000133", "e000134", "e000135", "e000136", "e000137", "e000138", "e000139", "e000140", "e000141", "e000142", "e000143", "e000144", "e000146", "e000147", "e000148"]', 297, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:56:09.170182+00');
