INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('f84923f5-d7f2-461d-a8fd-78f88d4f2eed', '1bb8029a-7b6b-4f15-b473-da7ad8fc706f', 7, '(iv) One mole of magnesium has a mass of 24.32 g. There are $ 6.022\times10^{23} $ atoms in one mole. Calculate the mass, in grams, of one atom of magnesium. Give your answer to 4 significant figures.
(c) The equation for the reaction between magnesium and oxygen is
2 \mathrm {M g} + \mathrm {O} _ {2} \rightarrow 2 \mathrm {M g O}
Determine the maximum amount, in moles, of magnesium oxide that can be produced from 0.50 mol of magnesium and 0.20 mol of oxygen.
(Total for Question 5 = 11 marks)
6 This question is about sodium oxide, $ \mathrm{N a_{2} O} $
(a) The diagram shows the electronic configuration of atoms of sodium and oxygen.
Sodium
Oxygen
Describe the changes in the electronic configuration of the atoms of sodium and oxygen to form the ions in sodium oxide.
(b) Calculate the relative formula mass $ ( M_{r} ) $ of sodium oxide, $ \mathrm{N a_{2} O} $ , using information from the Periodic Table.
(c) Explain why solid sodium oxide does not conduct electricity.
(d) Give a test to show that sodium oxide contains sodium ions.
(e) When sodium oxide is heated it reacts to form sodium metal and sodium peroxide, $ \mathrm{N a_{2} O_{2}} $', 1, 1, '["e000106", "e000107", "e000108", "e000109", "e000110", "e000111", "e000112", "e000114", "e000116", "e000117", "e000118", "e000119", "e000120", "e000121"]', 292, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:56:09.755076+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('2618ef4e-7358-4ece-bc87-0e127eed545c', '1bb8029a-7b6b-4f15-b473-da7ad8fc706f', 8, 'Complete the equation for this reaction.
\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \mathrm {O} \rightarrow
(Total for Question 6 = 9 marks)
7 This question is about soluble and insoluble compounds.
A precipitate is an insoluble compound formed when solutions of soluble compounds react after mixing.
(a) Different solutions are mixed in separate test tubes.
Tube 1 copper(II) sulfate solution and calcium chloride solution
Tube 2 magnesium nitrate solution and potassium sulfate solution
Tube 3 sodium carbonate solution and copper(II) sulfate solution In which of the tubes will a precipitate form?
A 1 and 2 only
B 2 and 3 only
C 1 and 3 only
D 1,2 and 3
(b) A student mixes solutions, containing equal amounts in moles, of silver nitrate and sodium chloride.
The equation for the reaction between silver nitrate solution and sodium chloride solution is
\mathrm {A g N O} _ {3} (\mathrm {a q}) + \mathrm {N a C l} (\mathrm {a q}) \rightarrow \mathrm {A g C l} (\mathrm {s}) + \mathrm {N a N O} _ {3} (\mathrm {a q})
(i) State the colour of the precipitate of silver chloride.
