Number of neutrons ...
Number of electrons ...
(ii) What is meant by the term isotopes?
(c) Bromine has two naturally-occurring isotopes with mass numbers 79 and 81. A sample of bromine contained the two isotopes in the following proportions:
bromine-79=50.7% and bromine-81=49.3%
Use this information to calculate the relative atomic mass of bromine. Give your answer to two decimal places.
