INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('9eb6a46a-52d4-4f30-b97d-f79b53ec1ecd', '0cd9f7fd-1fcb-4880-b246-e0b945f01812', 8, '(i) Give two advantages of making ethanol from ethene, rather than by fermentation.
(ii) Suggest two reasons why ethanol is sometimes made by fermentation,rather than from ethene.
(Total for Question 7 = 8 marks)
TURN OVER FOR QUESTION 8
8 Sulfur dioxide, $ \mathrm{S O_{2}} $ , is used as a preservative in wine.
The sulfur dioxide content of a wine can be found by titration. A chemist found that $ 2 5. 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of a sample of wine reacted with exactly $ 1 5. 0 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of 0.0010 mol/dm $ ^{3} $ aqueous iodine, $ \mathrm{I}_{2} $ (aq).
The equation for the reaction is
\mathrm {S O} _ {2} (\mathrm {a q}) + \mathrm {I} _ {2} (\mathrm {a q}) + 2 \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} (\mathrm {l}) \rightarrow \mathrm {S O} _ {4} ^ {2 -} (\mathrm {a q}) + 2 \mathrm {I} ^ {-} (\mathrm {a q}) + 4 \mathrm {H} ^ {+} (\mathrm {a q})
(a) Calculate the amount, in moles, of iodine in $ 1 5. 0 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of a 0.0010 mol/dm $ ^{3} $ solution.
(b) Deduce the amount, in moles, of sulfur dioxide in $ 2 5. 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of the wine.
(c) Calculate the concentration, in mol/dm $ ^{3} $ , of sulfur dioxide in the wine.', 1, 1, '["e000122", "e000123", "e000124", "e000125", "e000126", "e000127", "e000128", "e000129", "e000130", "e000131", "e000132"]', 286, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:57:41.871728+00');
