INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('2d566050-34d4-4a7c-b3e7-51b29510a125', '5cabf8fa-9227-4c90-aca6-416b54eeb726', 1, '1 Use the Periodic Table on page 2 to help you answer this question. Give the name or symbol of
(a) the element in group 3 and period 4.
(b) an element in period 3 that is a good conductor of electricity.
(c) the element in group 7 that is the most reactive.
(d) the element in group 5 that is present in a molecule of ammonia.
(e) an element with an atom containing 8 electrons in its outer shell.
(Total for Question 1 = 5 marks)
2 (a) The list shows some techniques used to separate mixtures.
A crystallisation
B filtration
C fractional distillation
D paper chromatography
E simple distillation
Complete the table to show the best method of obtaining each substance from the mixture.
In each case, choose one of the letters A, B, C, D or E. Each letter may be used once more than once or not at all.
Substance | Mixture | Letter
sand | sand and water | 
solid copper(II) sulfate | aqueous copper(II) sulfate | 
red food dye | mixture of food dyes | 
kerosene | crude oil |
(b) Gold occurs in ores, which are mixtures of gold and other substances. Several elements and compounds are used in the extraction of gold from its ores.', 1, 1, '["e000020", "e000021", "e000022", "e000023", "e000024", "e000025", "e000026", "e000027", "e000028", "e000029", "e000030", "e000031", "e000032", "e000033", "e000034", "e000035", "e000036"]', 284, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:58:26.455628+00');
