(i) Balance the equation to show the complete combustion of ethene $ \left( \mathrm{C}_{2} \mathrm{H}_{4} \right) $
\mathrm {C} _ {2} \mathrm {H} _ {4} + \dots \dots \dots \mathrm {O} _ {2} \rightarrow \dots \dots \dots \mathrm {C O} _ {2} + \dots \dots \dots \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {O}
(ii) Draw a dot and cross diagram to show the bonding in an ethene molecule. Show only the outer electrons in each atom.
(d) Ethanol can be manufactured by the hydration of ethene. The equation for this reaction is', 1, 1, '["e000072", "e000073", "e000074", "e000075", "e000076", "e000077", "e000078", "e000079", "e000080"]', 206, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 12:58:26.456464+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('6d230295-cb26-42fa-aac0-e7ff9dbd88e2', '5cabf8fa-9227-4c90-aca6-416b54eeb726', 6, 'reaction is
C2H4(g)+H2O(g)→C2H5OH(g)
(i) Identify the catalyst and state the temperature used in this process.
(2)
Catalyst
Temperature
(ii) A 20 mol sample of ethanol was produced using this reaction.
Deduce the amount, in moles, of ethene needed and the volume, in dm3, that this amount of ethene would occupy at room temperature and pressure.
Assume that all of the ethene is converted into ethanol and that the molar volume of ethene is 24 dm3 at rtp.
