INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('a999aaf3-baf0-40d6-8279-c8421a4be2de', 'e75587a8-9de5-4d5e-b74e-9e37e7b322ef', 4, '4 Bromine, chlorine, fluorine and iodine are elements in Group 7 of the Periodic Table.
(a) Which element is the most reactive?
A bromine
(1)
B chlorine
D iodine
C fluorine
(b) Which element is a solid at room temperature?
A bromine
B chlorine
C fluorine
D iodine
(1)
(c) Which element has the darkest colour at room temperature?
A bromine
(1)
B chlorine
C fluorine
D iodine
(d) Bromine reacts with hydrogen to form hydrogen bromide.
The equation for the reaction is
\mathrm {H} _ {2} (\mathrm {g}) + \mathrm {B r} _ {2} (\mathrm {g}) \rightarrow 2 \mathrm {H B r} (\mathrm {g})
The table shows some average bond energies.
Bond | H—H | Br—Br | H—Br
Average bond energy in kJ/mol | 436 | 193 | 366
Use the values in the table to calculate the enthalpy change for the reaction between hydrogen and bromine.
enthalpy change = | kJ/mol
(Total for Question 4 = 6 marks)
