5 Sodium sulfate can be prepared by the reaction between sodium hydroxide solution and sodium hydrogensulfate $ \mathrm{(N a H S O_{4})} $ solution.
This is the equation for the reaction.
\mathrm {N a O H} (\mathrm {a q}) + \mathrm {N a H S O} _ {4} (\mathrm {a q}) \rightarrow \mathrm {N a} _ {2} \mathrm {S O} _ {4} (\mathrm {a q}) + \mathrm {H} _ {2} \mathrm {O} (\mathrm {I})
Sodium hydrogensulfate solution is acidic.
A student adds $ 2 5. 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution to a conical flask and adds two drops of indicator.
The student does a titration.
(a) (i) Name a piece of apparatus that should be used to add $ 2 5. 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution to the conical flask.
(ii) Describe the method the student should use to find the accurate volume of sodium hydrogensulfate solution needed to neutralise the $ 2 5. 0 \mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of sodium hydroxide solution.
(b) The student repeats the titration without the indicator and forms a solution of sodium sulfate.', 1, 1, '["e000086", "e000087", "e000088", "e000089", "e000090", "e000091", "e000092", "e000093", "e000094", "e000095", "e000096", "e000097", "e000098", "e000099"]', 297, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 13:04:21.224057+00');
