8 Polymers can be classified as addition polymers or condensation polymers.
(a) An addition polymer can be formed from the monomer $ \mathrm{C H_{2}=C H C l} $
(i) Name this monomer.
(ii) Name the addition polymer formed from this monomer.
(b) The diagram shows the repeat unit of a different addition polymer.
Draw the displayed formula of the monomer used to make this polymer.
(c) Polyesters are condensation polymers.
The structures of two monomers that are used to make a polyester are:
HO—CH $ _{2} $ CH $ _{2} $ —OH
(i) Draw the structure of the repeat unit of the polyester formed from these two monomers.', 1, 1, '["e000134", "e000135", "e000136", "e000137", "e000138", "e000139", "e000140", "e000141", "e000142", "e000144", "e000145", "e000146", "e000148", "e000149"]', 285, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 13:04:21.457568+00');
INSERT INTO public.document_chunks VALUES ('002f394a-110a-4891-9a6d-d3e829ce7ca6', 'ec852bc6-8839-42a6-8aad-7e3ec729395e', 11, '(ii) Identify the small molecule formed when these two monomers form the polyester.
9 Grapes contain glucose that can be fermented to make ethanol.
(a) The grapes are collected and crushed to produce an aqueous solution containing glucose. Yeast is added to the solution and the mixture is left to ferment at a temperature of about $ 3 0^{\circ} \mathrm{C} $ in the absence of air.
(i) State why yeast is added.
(ii) Explain why another organic compound may also be formed if fermentation is carried out in the presence of air.
(iii) Explain why $ 3 0^{\circ} \mathrm{C} $ is considered to be an optimum temperature for this reaction.
(b) Ethanol can also be manufactured by reacting ethene with steam.
(i) Write the chemical equation for this reaction.
(ii) Name the type of reaction that occurs.
(iii) State two conditions used for this reaction in industry.
(c) Grapes also contain esters.
The formula of an ester is shown.
Deduce the name of the carboxylic acid and the alcohol that can react together to make this ester.
carboxylic acid
alcohol..
