(a): bare integer cell \"1\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "16(a): bare integer cell \"1\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "16(a): bare integer cell \"2\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "16(a): bare integer cell \"3\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}]', '{"paper": {"board": "Edexcel", "session": "June 2016", "subject": null, "duration": null, "examDate": "Thursday 19 May 2016 – Morning", "logNumber": null, "qualification": null, "paperReference": "4CH0/1C", "publicationCode": null, "canonicalDocumentId": "f4948ec0-cbe0-5f7e-982e-278246156fda"}, "warnings": ["unclassified heading: Experiment 2", "unclassified heading: (c) In stage 3"], "questions": [{"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "The diagram shows a kettle of boiling water. As the water vapour cools it turns into droplets of liquid water.", "marks": 4, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "The change of state when water vapour changes into liquid water is described as A boiling B condensation C evaporation D sublimation", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q01-f4948ec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Describe what happens when water vapour cools to form liquid water. Your answer should include the change in the energy, arrangement and movement of the particles. change in energy change in arrangement change in movement", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q01-f4948ec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 1, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789048899616.png", "width": 1026, "format": "png", "height": 300, "sha256": "285c21b151355a009d93a74bcdd9d471a3c67bae9d26ebf6602010c78269224b", "assetId": "img:285c21b151355a009d93a74bcdd9d471a3c67bae9d26ebf6602010c78269224b", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000022", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789048899616.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q01-f4948ec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": []}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "Air is a mixture of gases. The two main gases present are the elements nitrogen and oxygen.", "marks": 0, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "Another element that is present in air is A argon B carbon dioxide C hydrogen D sulfur dioxide", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-f4948ec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Give the formula of a compound that is found in unpolluted air.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-f4948ec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "This apparatus in the diagram is used to find the percentage of oxygen in air. The large pile of copper powder is heated, and the air in the syringe is passed several times from one gas syringe to the other. The large pile of copper powder turns black. The remaining gas is allowed to cool and its volume is measured.", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-f4948ec0-pc", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789048899632.png", "width": 1397, "format": "png", "height": 495, "sha256": "cd9d55729cae93531f085cb06c63aa5cc90bbc33b17c1e0706f3bea1441acddb", "assetId": "img:cd9d55729cae93531f085cb06c63aa5cc90bbc33b17c1e0706f3bea1441acddb", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000043", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789048899632.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Explain why the large pile of copper turns black.", "label": "c-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-f4948ec0-pc-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Why is the gas allowed to cool before its volume is measured?", "label": "c-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-f4948ec0-pc-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The small pile of copper powder is then heated and the remaining gas is passed several times over the hot copper. The copper does not turn black. Suggest why the small pile of copper does not turn black.", "label": "c-iii", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-f4948ec0-pc-iii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "In another experiment, the total volume of air in the apparatus before heating is $ 1 5 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3}. $ At the end of the experiment the volume of gas remaining is $ 1 2 5 \\mathrm{c m}^{3}. $ Use this information to calculate the percentage of oxygen in this sample of air.", "label": "d", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-f4948ec0-pd", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 2, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789048899632.png", "width": 1397, "format": "png", "height": 495, "sha256": "cd9d55729cae93531f085cb06c63aa5cc90bbc33b17c1e0706f3bea1441acddb", "assetId": "img:cd9d55729cae93531f085cb06c63aa5cc90bbc33b17c1e0706f3bea1441acddb", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000043", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789048899632.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.45, "marksKnown": false, "questionId": "q02-f4948ec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": []}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "A student wants to find out if the green colouring in grass is a mixture of dyes. He uses a solvent to dissolve the green colouring from some grass. He then separates the solution of the green colouring from the remaining grass.", "marks": 0, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "Which of these methods is used to separate the solution of the green colouring from the remaining grass? A boiling B condensation evaporation D filtration", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-f4948ec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The student uses a dropping pipette to place a drop of the green solution onto a piece of chromatography paper and produces a chromatogram. The diagram shows his results.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-f4948ec0-pb", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789048899652.png", "width": 683, "format": "png", "height": 501, "sha256": "cd8f9136e58b8550714e287cf32616082a9c0bc43849caad850406df54231f7c", "assetId": "img:cd8f9136e58b8550714e287cf32616082a9c0bc43849caad850406df54231f7c", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000057", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789048899652.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Add three more labels to the diagram to show the solvent the chromatography paper the original position of the spot of the green solution", "label": "b-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-f4948ec0-pb-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Explain how many different dyes are present in the green colouring.", "label": "b-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-f4948ec0-pb-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 3, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789048899652.png", "width": 683, "format": "png", "height": 501, "sha256": "cd8f9136e58b8550714e287cf32616082a9c0bc43849caad850406df54231f7c", "assetId": "img:cd8f9136e58b8550714e287cf32616082a9c0bc43849caad850406df54231f7c", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000057", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789048899652.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.45, "marksKnown": false, "questionId": "q03-f4948ec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": []}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "The diagram shows the electronic configurations of six different atoms.", "marks": 9, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "You may use the Periodic Table on page 2 to help you answer this question. Answer each part by writing one of the letters A,B,C,D,E or F in the box provided. You may use each letter once, more than once or not at all. Give the letter that represents an atom", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "of a noble gas", "label": "a-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pa-i", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_7_1789048899712.png", "width": 109, "format": "png", "height": 108, "sha256": "41919f63c45449a125c4a7302a441d2008ac4d54e23b8b7a5426ccc9a7572bf3", "assetId": "img:41919f63c45449a125c4a7302a441d2008ac4d54e23b8b7a5426ccc9a7572bf3", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000073", "sourceName": "assets/crop_7_1789048899712.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "that contains three protons", "label": "a-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pa-ii", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_8_1789048899719.png", "width": 108, "format": "png", "height": 108, "sha256": "a308f2d9deb8ef1e0d0fd7f03b0fcdc3263e4069c40285099dbf832446f0c8a0", "assetId": "img:a308f2d9deb8ef1e0d0fd7f03b0fcdc3263e4069c40285099dbf832446f0c8a0", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000075", "sourceName": "assets/crop_8_1789048899719.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "of phosphorus", "label": "a-iii", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pa-iii", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_9_1789048899722.png", "width": 110, "format": "png", "height": 109, "sha256": "b766f3a42ee52f920c410a7832897f4191777da7235afad5e7d2202be7e17576", "assetId": "img:b766f3a42ee52f920c410a7832897f4191777da7235afad5e7d2202be7e17576", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000077", "sourceName": "assets/crop_9_1789048899722.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "of an element in Group 4 of the Periodic Table", "label": "a-iv", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pa-iv", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_10_1789048899752.png", "width": 107, "format": "png", "height": 101, "sha256": "df212a3d03369cc1406f14537c17a9f51179878d8dc678e917b12c68776b7a27", "assetId": "img:df212a3d03369cc1406f14537c17a9f51179878d8dc678e917b12c68776b7a27", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000079", "sourceName": "assets/crop_10_1789048899752.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "of an element in Period 3 of the Periodic Table", "label": "a-v", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pa-v", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_11_1789048899760.png", "width": 108, "format": "png", "height": 102, "sha256": "7f3bfabcd39ef42cd76dfe7fd62ee249f133170191382811c80228040d628a7f", "assetId": "img:7f3bfabcd39ef42cd76dfe7fd62ee249f133170191382811c80228040d628a7f", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000081", "sourceName": "assets/crop_11_1789048899760.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "with a full outer shell of electrons", "label": "a-vi", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pa-vi", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_12_1789048899764.png", "width": 109, "format": "png", "height": 107, "sha256": "5f7164c41cb4ef6653dafda3922dd4fc4e058d1a16792150198b4554fe5491e5", "assetId": "img:5f7164c41cb4ef6653dafda3922dd4fc4e058d1a16792150198b4554fe5491e5", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000083", "sourceName": "assets/crop_12_1789048899764.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Atoms of A and D combine to form a compound containing covalent bonds.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Complete the sentence to describe a covalent bond. A covalent bond is the electrostatic attraction between a pair of and the ... of two atoms.", "label": "b-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pb-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Suggest, with reference to electronic configurations, the most likely formula of the compound formed between atoms of A and D.", "label": "b-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-f4948ec0-pb-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 4, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789048899662.png", "width": 88, "format": "png", "height": 95, "sha256": "66b8a3b6a7d6f9b00a7470a6d00f4471efefa9f03d21896f69887ed3000841c0", "assetId": "img:66b8a3b6a7d6f9b00a7470a6d00f4471efefa9f03d21896f69887ed3000841c0", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000064", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789048899662.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_2_1789048899667.png", "width": 141, "format": "png", "height": 143, "sha256": "5c8e72c5aa1b2fa0e5f1b11570876c783aff544021c3e7018f2ad80a7c13537f", "assetId": "img:5c8e72c5aa1b2fa0e5f1b11570876c783aff544021c3e7018f2ad80a7c13537f", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000065", "sourceName": "assets/crop_2_1789048899667.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_3_1789048899680.png", "width": 154, "format": "png", "height": 152, "sha256": "002db671f0cb3183a8b468be4b450ffaf08b94550b0257278c11a607d6cbff55", "assetId": "img:002db