ium moves (up and down)"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNORE floats"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT refs to moving on the surface"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M5 water/solution/liquid gets warm"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT temperature of water/solution/liquid rises"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNORE refs to heat released"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 any value greater than 7"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT “greater than 7”"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 hydroxide ions/OH- are present / calcium hydroxide/Ca(OH)2 is an alkali / calcium hydroxide/Ca(OH)2 is a base"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT metal hydroxides are alkalis/bases"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNORE hydroxides are alkalis/bases"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 dep on correct or missing M1"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNORE calcium is an alkali metal"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 (Solid X) - CaO / calcium oxide"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "if both formula and name given both must be correct"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 (Solution Y) - CaCl2 / calcium chloride"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3 (Solid Z) - CaCO3 / calcium carbonate"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT Ca(HCO3)2 / calcium hydrogencarbonate"}], "answerText": "Any two from:\nM1 calcium/solid/it disappears", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "8(a)", "marks": 1, "number": 8, "entryId": "ms-d5191851-q8a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT a flame"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "if >1 arrow drawn, all must be correct"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "to condense the (water) vapour / steam"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT to cool the water vapour"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT to cool/condense the gas (given off)"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNORE to condense the water"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNORE t