water"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept H2OAllow moistureIgnore vapour"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept answers in either orderIf name and formulae given both must be correct"}], "answerText": "galvanising/galvanisation", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "4(a)", "marks": 3, "number": 4, "entryId": "ms-9e53afca-q4a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C(copper(II) sulfate)The only correct answer is CA is not correct because the name of CuSO4 is not copper(I) sulfateB is not correct because the name of CuSO4 is not copper(I) sulfiteD is not correct because the name of CuSO4 is not copper(II) sulphite"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(c)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C(white AND colourless)The only correct answer is CA is not correct because NH4Cl(s) is not colourlessB is not correct because NH4Cl(s) is not colourlessD is not correct because NH4Cl(aq) is not white"}], "answerText": "M1(top row)CuCl2M2(middle row)(NH4)2SO4M3(bottom row)Fe2(CO3)3", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "6(a)", "marks": 4, "number": 6, "entryId": "ms-9e53afca-q6a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "the molecules that are cracked are hydrocarbons"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "√"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Award 1 mark for each correct tickIf more than 3 ticks then subtract 1 mark for each extra tick"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "catalytic cracking uses iron as the catalyst"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "cracking is used because of different requirements for hydrocarbons"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "√"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "cracking reactions are examples of addition reactions"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "cracking produces molecules with shorter chains"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "√"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "CH4+2O2→CO2+2H2O is an equation for a cracking reaction"}], "answerText": "M1 vaporisation\nM2 temperature\nM3 condensation\nM4 boiling point", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "7(a)", "marks": 1, "number": 7, "entryId": "ms-9e53afca-q7a", "guidance": [{"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to larger surface area"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Reject references to dissolving"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "reaction very slow/too slow without water"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept rusting needs water/ moisture"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "Allow so that iron can rust"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept reference to increasing rate of reaction/rusting"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(c)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1(at start)71"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore trailing .0(0) in all answers"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore units"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3 CQ M1-M2"}], "answerText": "reaction faster/takes less time\nM2(at end)16\nM3(change)(-)55", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "9(a)", "marks": 3, "number": 9, "entryId": "ms-9e53afca-q9a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "√"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Award 1 mark for each correct tickIf more than 3 ticks then subtract 1 mark for each extra tick"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "√"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "√"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "2K+I2→2KI"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept fractions/multiplesIgnore state symbols"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(c)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(hydrogen chloride) g(hydrochloric acid)aq"}], "answerText": "the elements can be obtained by electrolysing molten metal halides\nthe elements with paler colours are lower down the group\nthe boiling points decrease down the group\nthe elements form covalent compounds with other non-metals\ntheir molecules contain two atoms\nall are gases at room temperature", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "9(e)(i)", "marks": 2, "number": 9, "entryId": "ms-9e53afca-q9ei", "guidance": [{"kind": "allow", "text": "Allow description of test"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept chlorine does not displace itself"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C(solution becomes darker)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "The only correct answer is C"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "A is not correct because original sodium iodide solution is colourless but in Test 1 iodine is formed in the solution so the solution becomes darker(red/brown)-no effervescence is seen as no gas being formed"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "B is not correct because original sodium iodide solution is colourless but in Test 1 iodine is formed in the solution so the solution becomes darker(red/brown)-no iodine vapour produced so no purple fumes produced"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "D is not correct because original sodium iodide solution is colourless but in Test 1 iodine is formed in the solution so the solution becomes darker(red/brown)-no white precipitate formed"}], "answerText": "M1 test 2\nM2 chlorine does not react with chloride(ions)\nAllow chlorine does not react with itself\nAccept reference to halogen/halide in place of chlorine/chloride\nIgnore chlorine does not displace chloride", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "10(a)", "marks": 2, "number": 10, "entryId": "ms-9e53afca-q10a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "Accept all ions should be cations/positive Reject if state/imply these particles are protons/nuclei"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 replace protons (label) by electrons"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "Allow electrons (not protons) are delocalised"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1(magnesium) ions in layers/rows/sheets/planes/OWTTE"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept atoms/cations/particles for ions Reject molecules"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 slip/slide(over each other)"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "Allow OWTTE eg shift/roll/flow"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 DEP on mention of EITHER layers or equivalent OR mention of ions or equivalent"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Do not award M2 if molecules/protons/electrons/nuclei in place of ions etc."}, {"kind": "note", "text": "If reference to ionic bonding/covalent bonding/molecules/intermolecular forces,M1 and M2 cannot be scored"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3 delocalised electrons"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept sea of electrons Ignore free electrons"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M4 can flow/move(through the magnesium/metal/structure)/are mobile(when voltage/p.d.is applied)"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore carry the charge M4 DEP on mention of electrons"}], "answerText": "M1 replace signs by + signs/OWTTE", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "10(e)", "marks": 4, "number": 10, "entryId": "ms-9e53afca-q10e", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "calculation of mass of water"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "m(H2O)=(17.2-8.3)=8.9(g)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "calculation of amounts of MgSO4 AND H2O"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "n(MgSO4)=8.3÷120 OR 0.069(mol)Allow any sig. fig e.g.0.07ANDn(H2O)=8.9÷18 OR 0.49(mol)Allow any sig. fig e.g.0.5"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "calculation of MgSO4:H2O ratio"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "0.069:0.49 OR 1:7.101449275..allow any sig. fig."}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M4"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "x=7"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "OR 0.49/0.069 OR 7.101449275..allow any sig. fig.accept MgSO4.7H2OCorrect final answer with or without working scores 