dd dilute sulfuric acid to the malachite(in a beaker)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPTmix the powder with dilute sulfuric acid(in a beaker)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3 filter(using filter funnel and paper)"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOWdecant"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M4 add magnesium powder to the filtrate/solution/copper sulfate"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M5 method to collect/obtain/remove the residue/copper(using filter funnel and paper)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M6 reference to appropriate useof at least two pieces of apparatus"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNOREany latersteps e.g. washing/evaporation"}], "answerText": "M1 powder/crush the malachite(using the pestle and mortar)", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "11", "marks": null, "number": 11, "entryId": "ms-696bac95-q11", "guidance": [], "answerText": "OR\nIf malachite and magnesium are both added to the acid at the same time, then:\nM1 powder/crush the malachite\n(using the pestle and mortar)\nM2 add the malachite/powder to dilute sulfuric acid and add the magnesium (in a beaker)\nM3 filter and collect/obtain the residue/copper (using filter funnel and paper)\nM4 reference to appropriate use of at least two pieces of apparatus", "confidence": 0.5, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": null}, {"mcq": true, "qwc": false, "label": "12(a)", "marks": 1, "number": 12, "entryId": "ms-696bac95-q12a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "(b)(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "camping gas/bottled gas/calor gas"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW(fuel for) stoves/(fuel for) cooking/(fuel for) heating"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNOREfuel by itself"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "fuel for(aero)planes"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPTfuel forjets/jet engines"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPTfuel forheating/lamps"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "