"label": "1(a)", "marks": 1, "number": 1, "entryId": "ms-12ba157b-q1a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "(b)(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "A(all of the liquid is purple)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "B is not correct as the crystal will remain dissolved"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C is not correct as the particles will have diffused throughout the whole of the liquid"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "D is not correct as the particles will have diffused throughout the whole of the liquid"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C(diffusion)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "A is not correct as condensation describes the process of a gas changing into a liquid"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "B is not correct as crystallisation describes the process of a soluble solid forming from a solution"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C is not correct as evaporation describes the process of a liquid changing into a gas"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(c)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "A(3)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "B is not correct as there are only 3 elements present not 4"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C is not correct as there are only 3 elements present not 6"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "D is not correct as there are only 3 elements present not 7"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Total"}], "answerText": "B(the crystal dissolves in water)\nA is not correct as the crystal does not condense\nC is not correct as the crystal does not evaporate\nD is not correct as the crystal does not melt", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "13", "marks": 2, "number": 13, "entryId": "ms-12ba157b-q13", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "M1 curve Y starting at origin and below original curve"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 levelling off at $42\\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ to + or - half a square"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ii"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 curve Z starting at origin and above original cu