.18g"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "3.78g"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "calculation with following steps"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1calculate moles ofNa2CO3"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2calculate moles ofH2O"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3divide each by smaller to obtain ratio1:7"}, {"kind": "example-calculation", "text": "example calculation:"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1$\\frac{3.18}{106}$=0.03"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOWECFfrom(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2$\\frac{3.78}{18}$=0.21"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOWECFfrom(ii)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3$\\frac{0.03}{0.03}$:$\\frac{0.21}{0.03}$=1:7"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(c)(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Alternative method:"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1(If formula isNa2CO3.7H2O products will form in ratio)106gNa2CO3:126gH2O"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2so mass of water that forms with3.18gNa2CO3should=$\\frac{(126\\times3.18)}{106}$"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3=3.78g so formula is correct"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "explanation including"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1not heated crystals(for long) enough"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2so not all water removed/evaporated OWTTE"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1repeat heating(and cooling)"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOWheat for longer"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2until constant mass OWTTE"}], "answerText": "contain water of crystallisation /are hydrated", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "11(a)", "marks": 6, "number": 11, "entryId": "ms-965200a3-q11a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "Method 1"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 polystyrene (insulator so) reduces/prevents heat loss (to atmosphere) OWTTE"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 no lid so heat/thermal energy will be lost (to atmosphere)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3 stirring will ensure even temperature / more accurate (highest) temper