-a44d-596a7434ed70"}, "warnings": ["unclassified heading: TOTAL FOR PAPER = 60 MARKS"], "questions": [{"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "A student investigates some food colourings, each of which is made up of one or more dyes. She produces a chromatogram using the safe colourings red (SR), blue (SB) and green (SG) and food colourings red (FR), blue (FB) and green (FG). The diagram shows her chromatogram. reference line", "marks": 3, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "How many dyes are there in SR? A1 B2 C3 D4", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q01-3815dec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Complete the table by placing ticks ( $ \\checkmark $ ) next to the two food colourings that are definitely safe to use. Explain your answer. explanation", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q01-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 1, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789069398151.png", "width": 686, "format": "png", "height": 661, "sha256": "25d47d637f345b431f60591922387aa646ac4a716a93eb1be7dd5b5105bb0648", "assetId": "img:25d47d637f345b431f60591922387aa646ac4a716a93eb1be7dd5b5105bb0648", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000024", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789069398151.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q01-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": ["e000030"]}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "This apparatus is used to separate a mixture of ethanol (boiling point 78 $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $) and water (boiling point 100 $ ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $).", "marks": 4, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "What is the name of this method of separation?", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-3815dec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Why can ethanol and water be separated by this method?", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Suggest why water should enter the condenser at A rather than B.", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-3815dec0-pc", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Explain why the first liquid to be collected in the beaker is mostly ethanol.", "label": "d", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-3815dec0-pd", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 2, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789069398165.png", "width": 1320, "format": "png", "height": 879, "sha256": "45f3c3d232c91d0e90b2bf7fe08e50a604fc0d3d211aaac15433c4c705144c5e", "assetId": "img:45f3c3d232c91d0e90b2bf7fe08e50a604fc0d3d211aaac15433c4c705144c5e", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000034", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789069398165.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q02-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": []}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "The diagram shows a section of the Periodic Table and the symbols for the first 20 elements.", "marks": 0, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "What name is given to a horizontal row of elements such as Na to Ar?", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3815dec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Name two metals in the row Na to Ar.", "label": "a-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3815dec0-pa-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Which is the least reactive element in the row Na to Ar? Explain your answer. least reactive element. explanation ...", "label": "a-iii", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3815dec0-pa-iii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "State, in terms of electronic configurations, why the elements in the column Li to K have similar chemical properties.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Which element has atomic number 6?", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3815dec0-pc", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Which element has atoms with an electronic configuration of 2.8.6?", "label": "c-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3815dec0-pc-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 3, "figures": [], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.45, "marksKnown": false, "questionId": "q03-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": ["e000041", "e000051"]}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "A student investigates the rate of reaction between sodium thiosulfate and hydrochloric acid at $ 2 5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ The equation for the reaction is $\\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \\mathrm {S} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} _ {3} (\\mathrm {a q}) + 2 \\mathrm {H C l} (\\mathrm {a q}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm {N a C l} (\\mathrm {a q}) + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {I}) + \\mathrm {S O} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {S} (\\mathrm {s})$ She uses this method. pour 50 $ cm^{3} $ of sodium thiosulfate solution into a conical flask place the conical flask on top of a sheet of paper with a cross drawn on it add 10 $ cm^{3} $ of hydrochloric acid and start the timer stop the timer when the cross can no longer be seen and record the time taken The student repeats the experiment five times with different volumes of sodium thiosulfate solution. She adds water as necessary to keep the total volume of reaction mixture constant.", "marks": 10, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "Why can the student no longer see the cross at the end of each experiment?", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3815dec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The student keeps the total volume of the reaction mixture constant in each experiment. Explain how this makes each experiment a fair test.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The table shows the student''s results. Why is it important for the student to add the water before the acid in experiments 2 to 6?", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3815dec0-pc", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Sulfur dioxide gas is given off in the reaction. Suggest a safety precaution that the student should take when doing this experiment. Explain your answer. precaution. explanation", "label": "d", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3815dec0-pd", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Plot the student''s results on the grid and draw a curve of best fit.", "label": "e", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3815dec0-pe", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789069398250.png", "width": 1312, "format": "png", "height": 1366, "sha256": "814a94f7008198944792545d419b4e86cc9533a4d6530a00bc4b1e21f6d3fbf6", "assetId": "img:814a94f7008198944792545d419b4e86cc9533a4d6530a00bc4b1e21f6d3fbf6", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000074", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789069398250.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "On the grid, sketch the curve that you would expect if the investigation were repeated at $ 4 0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} $ Assume all other factors remain constant.", "label": "e-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3815dec0-pe-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 4, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789069398201.png", "width": 270, "format": "png", "height": 110, "sha256": "3b048191b6c53a914f5c305e06026d933b10cab27854f2102e619dc6a7081cf0", "assetId": "img:3b048191b6c53a914f5c305e06026d933b10cab27854f2102e619dc6a7081cf0", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000062", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789069398201.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_2_1789069398212.png", "width": 1019, "format": "png", "height": 410, "sha256": "c7a4973633ba3e6d7af26c0c49e4c91d0a9a06ebec97ac44a1e88c68bcbb78a3", "assetId": "img:c7a4973633ba3e6d7af26c0c49e4c91d0a9a06ebec97ac44a1e88c68bcbb78a3", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000063", "sourceName": "assets/crop_2_1789069398212.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_1_1789069398250.png", "width": 1312, "format": "png", "height": 1366, "sha256": "814a94f7008198944792545d419b4e86cc9533a4d6530a00bc4b1e21f6d3fbf6", "assetId": "img:814a94f7008198944792545d419b4e86cc9533a4d6530a00bc4b1e21f6d3fbf6", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000074", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789069398250.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q04-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": ["e000067"]}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "The diagram shows the diaphragm cell used in the electrolysis of concentrated sodium chloride solution, NaCl(aq).", "marks": 8, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "Explain what is meant by the term electrolysis.", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q05-3815dec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Identify gas A, gas B and solution C. gas A. gas B. solution C.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q05-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Sodium is manufactured by the electrolysis of molten sodium chloride, NaCl(l). Sodium is produced at the negative electrode and chlorine is produced at the positive electrode.", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q05-3815dec0-pc", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Why does the sodium chloride have to be molten before it will conduct electricity?", "label": "c-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q05-3815dec0-pc-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The ionic half-equation for the formation of sodium is $\\mathrm {N a} ^ {+} + \\mathrm {e} ^ {-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm {N a}$ Write the ionic half-equation for the formation of chlorine from chloride ions.", "label": "c-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q05-3815dec0-pc-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 5, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789069398265.png", "width": 1517, "format": "png", "height": 853, "sha256": "5851024cd92bf57c55b512d003215caf0ab184c15fffedee0b697b5dc7cb33fc", "assetId": "img:5851024cd92bf57c55b512d003215caf0ab184c15fffedee0b697b5dc7cb33fc", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000079", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789069398265.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q05-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": []}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "Solid X contains two cations (positive ions) and one anion (negative ion). One of the cations is $ \\mathrm{F e}^{3+} $", "marks": 6, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "The table describes the tests carried out on an aqueous solution of X and some of the observations made. Complete the table by giving the missing observation.", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q06-3815dec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Which cation, other than $ \\mathrm{F e}^{3+} $ , is present in X? Explain your answer. cation. explanation", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q06-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Identify the anion present in X.", "label": "b-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q06-3815dec0-pb-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "When zinc is added to a solution containing $ \\mathrm{F e}^{3+} $ ions, a reaction occurs. The ionic equation for this reaction is $\\mathrm {Z n} (\\mathrm {s}) + 2 \\mathrm {F e} ^ {3 +} (\\mathrm {a q}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {Z n} ^ {2 +} (\\mathrm {a q}) + 2 \\mathrm {F e} ^ {2 +} (\\mathrm {a q})$ Identify the reducing agent in this reaction and explain your choice. reducing agent. explanation", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q06-3815dec0-pc", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 6, "figures": [], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q06-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": ["e000096"]}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "(a) The first two members of the homologous series of alcohols are methanol and ethanol. (i) Give two characteristics of the compounds in a homologous series. (ii) The displayed formula for methanol is Suggest a displayed formula for ethanol, $ \\mathrm{C H_{3} C H_{2} O H} $", "marks": 0, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "The table shows the two different processes for making ethanol on a large scale. Compare the two processes in terms of the rate at which the ethanol can be produced the purity of the product the use of finite resources", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q07-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The equation for the fermentation of glucose is $C _ {6} H _ {1 2} O _ {6} \\rightarrow 2 C H _ {3} C H _ {2} O H + 2 C O _ {2}$ A mass of 3600 kg of glucose was completely fermented.", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q07-3815dec0-pc", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Calculate the amount, in moles, of glucose that was fermented. $ ( M_{r} $ of glucose=180)", "label": "c-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q07-3815dec0-pc-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Deduce the amount, in moles, of ethanol produced in this reaction.", "label": "c-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q07-3815dec0-pc-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Calculate the volume, in $ \\mathrm{d m^{3}} $ at rtp, of carbon dioxide produced in this reaction. (1 mol of carbon dioxide occupies $ 2 4 \\mathrm{d m^{3}} $ at rtp)", "label": "c-iii", "marks": null, "partId": "q07-3815dec0-pc-iii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 7, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789069398291.png", "width": 240, "format": "png", "height": 217, "sha256": "b6f0f9583f7fd48bba56882a211b342323462868de2494e0424187ff592b0867", "assetId": "img:b6f0f9583f7fd48bba56882a211b342323462868de2494e0424187ff592b0867", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000111", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789069398291.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.45, "marksKnown": false, "questionId": "q07-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": ["(1)"], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": ["e000115", "e000126"]}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "The hydrogen needed for the manufacture of ammonia is made by a process called steam reforming. In this process, a mixture of methane and steam is passed over a nickel catalyst. The equation for the reaction is $\\mathrm {C H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm {C O} (\\mathrm {g}) + 3 \\mathrm {H} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) \\quad \\Delta H = + 2 1 0 \\mathrm {k J / m o l}$", "marks": 9, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "In this part of the question, assume that the reaction reaches a position of equilibrium.", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Predict whether a high or low temperature would produce the highest yield of hydrogen. Give a reason for your choice. prediction reason ...", "label": "a-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pa-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Predict whether a high or low pressure would produce the highest yield of hydrogen. Give a reason for your choice. prediction reason ...", "label": "a-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pa-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Explain how a catalyst increases the rate of a reaction.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Some of the carbon monoxide produced is removed in another reaction. In this reaction, carbon monoxide is mixed with steam and passed over a heated catalyst. The reaction is reversible and the carbon monoxide is oxidised to carbon dioxide.", "label": "c", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pc", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Write a chemical equation for this reaction.", "label": "c-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pc-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Explain why the carbon in carbon monoxide is oxidised in this reaction.", "label": "c-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pc-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The carbon dioxide produced can be removed by passing the gas through a solution of potassium carbonate, $ \\mathrm{K_{2} C O_{3}} $ The potassium carbonate reacts with carbon dioxide and water to form potassium hydrogencarbonate, $ \\mathrm{KHCO}_{3} $ Write a chemical equation for this reaction.", "label": "c-iii", "marks": null, "partId": "q08-3815dec0-pc-iii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 8, "figures": [], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q08-3815dec0", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": []}], "paperTotal": 60, "schemaVersion": "1.0", "sectionTotals": {}, "questionTotals": {"1": 3, "2": 4, "4": 10, "5": 8, "6": 6, "8": 9}, "reviewRequired": true, "extractionMethod": "glm-ocr-qp-v1", "frontMatterFigures": []}', '{"paper": {"board": "Edexcel", "session": "June 2014", "subject": null, "duration": null, "examDate": null, "logNumber": null, "qualification": null, "paperReference": null, "publicationCode": "UG038305", "canonicalDocumentId": "b27e3724-c846-5220-b8d7-52376dca347c"}, "entries": [{"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "1", "marks": 1, "number": 1, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q1", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "i"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "B(2)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "b"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "FR AND FG"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "FR and FG/they/colourings/dyes/spots/OWTTE"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "AND"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "line up/match/correspond with/travel same distance(s) as/ have sameRfvalues as"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "AND"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "SR and SG/safe colourings/red and green colourings"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Choice can be indicated by ticks or other marks or Yes"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 DEP on M1 correct or missing"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to FB unless incorrect"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to FR and FG containing/being the same as SR and SG"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "1"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "1"}], "answerText": "a", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "2", "marks": 1, "number": 2, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q2", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "fractional distillation / fractionation"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore just distillation"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Reject simple distillation"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "b"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(they have) different boiling points/boiling temperatures / boil at different temperatures"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "OR ethanol has a lower boiling point (than water)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "/water has a higher boiling point (than ethanol))"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to melting point"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to condensing"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept one boils at 78(℃), the other at 100(℃)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept ethanol boils/evaporates first"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore boils/evaporates faster"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "c"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "to keep the jacket full of water"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "/to make sure there is no air in the jacket"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "/to surround the whole tube"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "OR"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(for B) not enough water in the condenser"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "/water not in contact with tube for long enough"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "/water runs straight out"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept tube/condenser in place of jacket"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept reverse arguments relating to B"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to rate of cooling or condensing"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore so that more ethanol/vapour/gas condenses / to make sure all the ethanol/vapour/gas condenses"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to glass breaking"}], "answerText": "a", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "2", "marks": 1, "number": 2, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q2", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "(ethanol/it) has a lower boiling point/is more volatile (than water)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "OR"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "boils/evaporates first/before water"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept weaker forces of attraction between ethanol molecules"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept reverse arguments for water"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept boiling point (of ethanol) reached first"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore incorrect difference eg 12℃ lower"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore boils/evaporates faster"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to rate of evaporation/boiling/condensation"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore ethanol condenses first"}], "answerText": "d", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "3", "marks": 1, "number": 3, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q3", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "i"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "period"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore number of period"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ii"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Any two of sodium/magnesium/aluminium"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore symbols Na,Mg,Al"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "iii"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Ar/argon(it does) not easily gain/lose electronsORhas 8 electrons in outer shell"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "If name and symbol both given,then both must be correctAccept(it has)a full outer shellIgnore 2.8.8Ignore inert/noble gasIgnore references to Group numberIgnore stableM2 DEP on M1"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "b"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "one electron/same number of electronsANDreference to outer/valence(shell/energylevel/orbit)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Reject incorrect number of electronsIgnore similar electronic configurationsIgnore actual electronic configurations"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "c"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "i"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "C/ carbon"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ii"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "S/ sulfur"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "d"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "8 for both protons AND electrons10 neutrons"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept wordsAccept words"}], "answerText": "a", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "4", "marks": 1, "number": 4, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q4", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "sulfur/precipitate forms"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept usual precipitate alternatives"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore precipitate colour"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept cloudy/ opaque"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Reject wrongly identified precipitate (eg sodium chloride)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "b"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "to keep the depth/height/shallowness of liquid(in the conical flask) the same/OWTTE"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "OR"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "the same mass of sulfur(needed to obscure the cross)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept reverse argument"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Reject to keep the concentration the same"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "c"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "reaction would start before the correct depth/concentration of liquid was obtained"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "OR"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "the reaction starts when the acid is added/straight away/before the water is added"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to keeping the total volume constant"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to fair test/accuracy/safety"}], "answerText": "a", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "4", "marks": 1, "number": 4, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q4", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "fume cupboard / well-ventilated room /open windows / extractor fan OR wear eye protection / safety goggles / OWTTE OR (gas) mask / respirator (SO2/it is) poisonous/toxic OR reference to specific harmful effect on humans (eg affects breathing/respiratory irritant /eye irritant/triggers asthma attack/makes bronchitis or emphysema worse) OR to prevent gas reaching eyes/lungs/OWTTE"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore references to pollution / acid rain / greenhouse effect Ignore just harmful Mark independently To score M1 and M2, explanation must match precaution: fume cupboard etc can link with all explanations eye protection etc. can link with all explanations except those involving breathing etc. mask etc. can link with all explanations except those involving eyes etc."}], "answerText": "d", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "4", "marks": null, "number": 4, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q4", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "i"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "all points correctly plotted to nearest gridline"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "suitable curve of best fit based on plotted points"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "curve completely below original curve"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "starts at vol=10cm3, finishes at vol=50cm3"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Deduct 1 mark for each incorrect plot"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Do not penalise continuation of line above 255s unless incorrect(eg straight line to 300s)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Do not award mark if curve starts from(10,255)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "DEP on point plotted for experiment1"}], "answerText": "e", "confidence": 0.5, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": null}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "5", "marks": 2, "number": 5, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q5", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "decomposition / breakdown / breakup / splitting / chemical changeby electricity / (electric) current/ (flow of) electrons"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore specific examples that do notinclude key words (eg obtainingaluminium from its ore)Ignore separation / movement of ionsMark independently"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "b"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "A=chlorine/Cl2B=hydrogen/H2C=sodium hydroxide/NaOH"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore ClIgnore HIgnore references to sodium chlorideIf both name and formula given,bothmust be correct,but ignore Cl and HAward 1 mark for chlorine and hydrogenthe wrong way round"}], "answerText": "a", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "5", "marks": 1, "number": 5, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q5", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "i"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "so that ions are mobile/can flow/free to move(in liquid)ORions not mobile/cannot flow/not free to move in solid"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept Na+/Cl- in place of ionsIgnore references to charged species and particlesReject references to moving electronsReject no ions in solidReference to solid can be implied(eg if not molten...)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ii"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "2Cl-→Cl2+2e(-)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 for Cl- on left and Cl2 on rightM2 for balancing, DEP on M1 correctAccept-2e(-)on LHSIf neither M1 nor M2 awarded, then award1 mark for Cl-→Cl+e(-)or 2Cl-→2Cl+2e(-)"}], "answerText": "c", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "6", "marks": 1, "number": 6, "entryId": "ms-b27e3724-q6", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "brown precipitate"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Accept usual alternatives for precipitate"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore qualifiers such as dark/light"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore red(dish)/orange/rust(y)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Reject other colours"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "Ignore all names and formulae"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "b"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "i"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ammonium/NH4+gas given off is ammonia/NH3"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "If name and formula