s": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: M2because there are more moles/molecules(of gas) on the left/ORA", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: REJECTatoms", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: ACCEPTthere are more moles/molecules of reactants", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: IGNOREreaction moves to the side with the larger number of moles/molecules", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: IGNOREreferences to rate", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: IGNOREreferences to Le Chatelier''s principle, eg lower pressure favours the reaction that produces the larger number of moles(of gas)/equilibrium position shifts to increase the pressure", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: M2DEP M1", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: (c)(i)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: (ii)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "10(a)(i): bare integer cell \"1\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}, {"detail": "orphan row before first entry: (b)", "source": "MS_WARNING", "msMarks": null, "qpMarks": null, "severity": "warning", "questionNumber": null}]', '{"paper": {"board": "Edexcel", "session": "January 2019", "subject": null, "duration": null, "examDate": "Wednesday 16 January 2019", "logNumber": null, "qualification": null, "paperReference": "4CH0/2C", "publicationCode": null, "canonicalDocumentId": "3097a144-271a-522d-ab0e-3ee70ce778f6"}, "warnings": ["unclassified heading: TOTAL FOR PAPER = 60 MARKS", "Q1: detached option letters without option text", "Q2: incomplete MCQ option set folded into stem"], "questions": [{"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "The diagram shows six pieces of apparatus that are used in the laboratory. E F The table lists the names of four pieces of apparatus. Complete the table by giving a letter, A, B, C, D, E or F, to identify each piece of apparatus listed.", "marks": 0, "parts": [], "number": 1, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789064067407.png", "width": 83, "format": "png", "height": 779, "sha256": "91ffdc9ecc0c106f5701cb0466c4c4eb28ed16c4a84495742b2d19ff337171c8", "assetId": "img:91ffdc9ecc0c106f5701cb0466c4c4eb28ed16c4a84495742b2d19ff337171c8", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000023", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789064067407.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_2_1789064067414.png", "width": 276, "format": "png", "height": 392, "sha256": "aee67ef9e9197cbfcfaff925d016aece733776b22a99a85f9137dd5c09dcb45b", "assetId": "img:aee67ef9e9197cbfcfaff925d016aece733776b22a99a85f9137dd5c09dcb45b", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000025", "sourceName": "assets/crop_2_1789064067414.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_3_1789064067419.png", "width": 158, "format": "png", "height": 474, "sha256": "58da14e59b01d5463920aa7e3f0f2e0246ca352730e86afe0a30f4c9d3d36600", "assetId": "img:58da14e59b01d5463920aa7e3f0f2e0246ca352730e86afe0a30f4c9d3d36600", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000027", "sourceName": "assets/crop_3_1789064067419.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_4_1789064067423.png", "width": 215, "format": "png", "height": 256, "sha256": "d8993c84db04bdeea01937e7a7e36b763f638ed66a2c72b73d01ea3a98b0d676", "assetId": "img:d8993c84db04bdeea01937e7a7e36b763f638ed66a2c72b73d01ea3a98b0d676", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000029", "sourceName": "assets/crop_4_1789064067423.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_5_1789064067429.png", "width": 207, "format": "png", "height": 296, "sha256": "e5949859de05f53358f4bdf98269505899a4e049cb8443d86caba5e3c8611edc", "assetId": "img:e5949859de05f53358f4bdf98269505899a4e049cb8443d86caba5e3c8611edc", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000031", "sourceName": "assets/crop_5_1789064067429.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_6_1789064067436.png", "width": 57, "format": "png", "height": 519, "sha256": "a2f6d40a87c73514430e125efab5de5bc666a1845ada0c7b8475f6d10504aabc", "assetId": "img:a2f6d40a87c73514430e125efab5de5bc666a1845ada0c7b8475f6d10504aabc", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000033", "sourceName": "assets/crop_6_1789064067436.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.45, "marksKnown": false, "questionId": "q01-3097a144", "answerPrompts": ["(4)"], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": ["e000038"]}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "Rubidium is an element in Group 1 of the Periodic Table. 85 87 A sample of rubidium contains two isotopes, $ _{37}Rb $ and $ _{37}Rb $ (a) (i) State how the nuclei of the two isotopes are similar. (ii) State how the nuclei of the two isotopes are different. (iii) How many electrons are in the outer shell of a rubidium atom? A 1 B 3 C 9 D 37", "marks": 5, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "The relative abundances of the two isotopes in the sample of rubidium are $ _{37}^{85} $ Rb 72.2 % $ _{37}^{87} $ Rb 27.8 % Calculate the relative atomic mass of rubidium Give your answer to one decimal place.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q02-3097a144-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": ["relative atomic mass"]}], "number": 2, "figures": [], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q02-3097a144", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": []}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "A student uses this apparatus to investigate the action of heat on sodium hydrogencarbonate $ \\mathrm{(N a H C O_{3})}. $ The equation for the reaction is $2 \\mathrm {N a H C O} _ {3} (\\mathrm {s}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {N a} _ {2} \\mathrm {C O} _ {3} (\\mathrm {s}) + \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {g}) + \\mathrm {C O} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g})$", "marks": 5, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "State the type of reaction taking place.", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3097a144-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Describe a test to show that the gas given off is carbon dioxide.", "label": "a-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3097a144-pa-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The student heats a 1.00g sample of sodium hydrogencarbonate for one minute. He then measures the mass of solid left in the test tube. He repeats the experiment four times, heating separate samples of mass 1.00 g for a different number of minutes each time. The table shows the student''s results.", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3097a144-pb", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "State why the mass of solid in each test tube decreases.", "label": "b-i", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3097a144-pb-i", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "Suggest why the mass of solid stops decreasing after four minutes.", "label": "b-ii", "marks": null, "partId": "q03-3097a144-pb-ii", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}], "number": 3, "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789064067457.png", "width": 665, "format": "png", "height": 390, "sha256": "f0599751ae5a87b61170ad654196651f1c6bf85e9fcf9410e69c1166128dc910", "assetId": "img:f0599751ae5a87b61170ad654196651f1c6bf85e9fcf9410e69c1166128dc910", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000052", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789064067457.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}], "options": [], "section": null, "confidence": 0.6, "marksKnown": true, "questionId": "q03-3097a144", "answerPrompts": [], "numberingStyle": "space", "tableElementIds": ["e000060"]}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "stem": "Sodium reacts with fluorine to form sodium fluoride. The reaction is very exothermic.", "marks": 0, "parts": [{"qwc": false, "text": "State what is meant by the term exothermic.", "label": "a", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3097a144-pa", "figures": [], "confidence": 0.55, "answerPrompts": []}, {"qwc": false, "text": "The diagram shows the electronic configuration of a sodium atom. Which of these diagrams shows the electronic configuration of a fluorine atom? A B C D", "label": "b", "marks": null, "partId": "q04-3097a144-pb", "figures": [{"url": "assets/crop_1_1789064067471.png", "width": 478, "format": "png", "height": 447, "sha256": "0f1718b29248398f6a05c1d1ff57adddba867b8ee2611036f8a2602a3f631ca5", "assetId": "img:0f1718b29248398f6a05c1d1ff57adddba867b8ee2611036f8a2602a3f631ca5", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "elementId": "e000067", "sourceName": "assets/crop_1_1789064067471.png", "availability": "available", "formatMismatch": true}, {"url": "assets/crop_2_1789064067481.png", "width": 268, "format": "png", "height": 268, "sha256": "333c26219a1b4666dac52402e83d