{"kind": "note", "text": "penalise 1 sig fig in M1ALLOW M1÷2ALLOW 2 or more sig figs in answers to M1 and M2ALLOW 2 or more sig figs if all working showncorrect answers in the range 23,707 to 24,910 cm3 to 3 or more significant figures, without working scores4 marks."}], "answerText": "Any two from:\nTotal for question = 11", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "5(a)", "marks": 5, "number": 5, "entryId": "ms-9047f3ba-q5a", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "M1 add hydrogen peroxide to the conical flask and add catalyst"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 start the timer"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3 record volume of gas produced in a given time/record the time for certain volume of gas to be produced"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M4 repeat with same mass of a different catalyst"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M5 and with same volume of hydrogen peroxide"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M6 plot the results on a graph and calculate gradient (for each catalyst)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M7 the most effective catalyst gives the fastest rate of reaction OWTTE"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 a vertical line from the level of the hydrogen peroxide to the top of the curve labelled activation energy or $E_{\\mathrm{a}}$"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "the line does not need an arrow head"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 a vertical line from the level of the hydrogen peroxide to the level of the water and oxygen labelled enthalpy change or $\\Delta H$"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW double headed arrow"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT arrow pointing down"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "curve starting from hydrogen peroxide level, below the peak of the original curve, and ending at water and oxygen level"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW double headed arrow"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT arrow pointing up"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}], 