correct formulae\nM1 delocalised electrons\nTotal for question = 12", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "7(a)(i)", "marks": 1, "number": 7, "entryId": "ms-9047f3ba-q7ai", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT any other atoms in the ring."}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii) ethyl ethanoate"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW ethylethanoate"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(iii) M1 add a metal such as magnesium, aluminium, zinc or ironM2 effervescence/bubbles/fizzing"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "must be a named metal REJECT Group 1 metals"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT any named carbonateACCEPT test gas with limewater which goes cloudy/milkyM2 dep on M1"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 C-O and one/two O-H bonds are broken and formedM2 so the same amount of energy is needed to break the bonds in the reactants as is given off when the bonds in the products are formed"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW the same bonds are broken and formed"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(c)(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 the rate of the forward reaction equals the rate of the backward reactionM2 the concentrations of reactants and products remain constant"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)M1 a catalyst increases the rate of forward and backward reactionsM2 equally"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 dep on M1"}], "answerText": "Chemical structure of ethyl ethanoate\nALLOW ethyl acetate\nACCEPT test gas with lighted splint which pops\nM2 dep on reference to adding a metal\nORM1 add a carbonateM2 effervescence/bubbles/fizzing\nALLOW energy of bonds formed equals energy of bonds broken\nREJECT concentration of the reactants and products are the same", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "7(d)", "marks": 3, "number": 7, "entryId": "ms-9047f3ba-q7d", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "M1 needs to be given to at least 3 sig figs"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW M1×2"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW answer to M2 to 3 significant figures."}, {"kind": "note", "text": "correct answer of0.00683 moles with or without working scores3 marks"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT answer in standard form"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT 0.00682 if M1 given to 3 sig figs"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "6.83 with or without working scores2 marks"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(e)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "correct answer scores2 marks"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Chemical structure"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 three carbons from the dicarboxylic acid and two from the diol and the ester linkage"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 -OH lost from the dicarboxylic acid and -H lost from the diol"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW structure without extension bonds"}, {"kind": "ignore", "text": "IGNORE brackets and n and +H2O"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW -OH lost from diol and -H lost from dicarboxylic acid"}], "answerText": "example calculation\nM1 moles barium hydroxide=(0.150×22.75)÷1000\nOR0.0034125\nM2 moles ethanoic acid=0.006825\nM3 moles ethanoic acid to 3 significant figures=0.00683\nTotal for question=15", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}], "icTable": null, "warnings": ["orphan row before first entry: 1(a)(i)(ii)", "orphan row before first entry: M2 only", "orphan row before first entry: ethene has a double bond", "orphan row before first entry: (b)", "orphan row before first entry: (c)(i)", "orphan row before first entry: (ii)", "orphan row before first entry: Total for question=7", "2(a)(i): bare integer cell \"1\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "2(a)(i): bare integer cell \"2\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "2(a)(i): bare integer cell \"1\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "2(a)(i): bare integer cell \"1\" skipped (rubric/rowspan ambiguity)", "2(