ECT white precipitate"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(b)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "A description that refers to the following two points"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 magnesium/Mg loses two electrons/becomes 2.8"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 oxygen/O gains two electrons/becomes 2.8"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ACCEPT magnesium gives two electrons to oxygen for M1 and M2"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "Both marks can be scored from diagrams showing correct electronic configurations of the ions."}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(c)(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "magnesium is more reactive/higher in the reactivity series (than carbon)/magnesium is a better reducing agent (than carbon) ORA"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW carbon cannot displace magnesium"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "An explanation that links the following four points"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M1 (magnesium) has delocalised electrons"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT reference to ions or atoms moving for M2"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "ions are free to move when (magnesium chloride) is molten/in solution OR (magnesium chloride) cannot conduct when solid"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M2 electrons can move"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M3 (magnesium chloride) can only conduct when molten/in solution OR (magnesium chloride) cannot conduct when solid"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "M4 ions are free to move"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT reference to electrons moving for M4"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(d)(i)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "magnesium ions/Mg2+ gains electrons"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW electrons are gained"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "2Cl-→Cl2+2e(-)"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT magnesium/Mg gains electrons"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "REJECT reference to loss or gain of oxygen"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "(ii)"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW 2Cl-→2e(-)→Cl2"}, {"kind": "allow", "text": "ALLOW multiples or fractions"}, {"kind": "ignore",