lse, "dependentOn": [], "alternatives": []}], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "7(a)(i)", "marks": 4, "number": 7, "entryId": "ms-30157e99-q7ai", "guidance": [{"kind": "ignore", "text": "ignore any references to or arguments based on Le Chatelier''s principle"}, {"kind": "note", "text": "accept the (forward) reaction is exothermic"}], "answerText": "Graph A\nAn explanation that links the following two points:\n• the backward/reverse reaction is endothermic(1)\n• so an increase in temperature shifts the equilibrium to the left(hence the percentage of NO decreases)(1)\nGraph B\nAn explanation that links the following two points:\n• there are fewer molecules/moles of gas on the left(1)\n• so an increase in pressure shifts the equilibrium to the left(hence the percentage of NO decreases)(1)", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [{"ecf": false, "text": "Graph A\nAn explanation that links the following two points:\n• the backward/reverse reaction is endothermic", "marks": 1, "reject": false, "ordinal": 1, "rawText": "Graph A\nAn explanation that links the following two points:\n• the backward/reverse reaction is endothermic", "anyTwoFrom": false, "dependentOn": [], "alternatives": []}, {"ecf": false, "text": "• so an increase in temperature shifts the equilibrium to the left(hence the percentage of NO decreases)", "marks": 1, "reject": false, "ordinal": 2, "rawText": "• so an increase in temperature shifts the equilibrium to the left(hence the percentage of NO decreases)", "anyTwoFrom": false, "dependentOn": [], "alternatives": []}, {"ecf": false, "text": "Graph B\nAn explanation that links the following two points:\n• there are fewer molecules/moles of gas on the left", "marks": 1, "reject": false, "ordinal": 3, "rawText": "Graph B\nAn explanation that links the following two points:\n• there are fewer molecules/moles of gas on the left", "anyTwoFrom": false, "dependentOn": [], "alternatives": []}, {"ecf": false, "text": "• so an increase in pressure shifts the equilibrium to the left(hence the percentage of NO decreases)", "marks": 1, "reject": false, "ordinal": 4, "rawText": "• so an increase in pressure shifts the equilibrium to the left(hence the percentage of NO decreases)", "anyTwoFrom": false, "dependentOn": [], "alternatives": []}], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "7(a)(ii)", "marks": 2, "number": 7, "entryId": "ms-30157e99-q7aii", "guidance": [{"kind": "note", "text": "second mark is dependent on the first"}], "answerText": "•(The catalyst/it) increases the rate of both the forward and reverse reactions(1)\n•To the same extent(1)", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [{"ecf": false, "text": "•(The catalyst/it) increases the rate of both the forward and reverse reactions", "marks": 1, "reject": false, "ordinal": 1, "rawText": "•(The catalyst/it) increases the rate of both the forward and reverse reactions", "anyTwoFrom": false, "dependentOn": [], "alternatives": []}, {"ecf": false, "text": "•To the same extent", "marks": 1, "reject": false, "ordinal": 2, "rawText": "•To the same extent", "anyTwoFrom": false, "dependentOn": [], "alternatives": []}], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "7(b)(i)", "marks": 1, "number": 7, "entryId": "ms-30157e99-q7bi", "guidance": [], "answerText": "Because a proton is transferred from HNO3to NH3", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [], "correctOption": null, "marksCellSource": "label row"}, {"mcq": false, "qwc": false, "label": "7(b)(ii)", "marks": 2, "number": 7, "entryId": "ms-30157e99-q7bii", "guidance": [], "answerText": "•Calculate the amount of nitric acid\n•Calculate the volume of aqueous ammonia\nExample calculation:\n$n(\\mathrm{HNO}_{3})=15.8\\times150\\text{mol}(=2370\\text{mol})(1)$\n$\\mathrm{vol(NH_{3})}$ required $=(2370\\div14.8)=160(\\mathrm{dm}^{3})(1)$", "confidence": 0.75, "markPoints": [{"ecf": fals